declare
  v_items constant jsonb := $satx$[{"gid":"sw-command_of_evidence_text-m-002","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Command of Evidence (Textual)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"command_of_evidence_text","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"The following text is adapted from a short story. Every weekday, the island children eat breakfast together in the cabin of the ferry that carries them to the mainland school.\n\nFor years the meal had followed its own quiet order: Pell poured the tea, the twins split the bread, and no one spoke until the engine changed pitch at the harbor mouth. Then, one gray morning in March, Miss Arden, the new schoolteacher, stepped aboard with a tin of oranges and sat down among them. The cabin seemed brighter, as though she had carried a lamp inside, yet the children hardly knew where to put their hands.\n\nA literary critic argues that the story presents Miss Arden's arrival as making the children's breakfast both more vivid and less settled than before.","question":"Which finding from the story, if true, would most directly support the critic's claim?","options":["Pell, peeling one of Miss Arden's oranges, notices that its scent fills the cabin, and he decides to bring fruit of his own to the next morning's meal so that the breakfast will stay just as it was.","Pell, noticing Miss Arden's tin of oranges, remembers that his mother once packed fruit for him, and he quietly pours the tea at the usual moment while the twins split the bread as always.","Pell, holding one of Miss Arden's oranges up to the window light, laughs aloud before the engine changes pitch, then stops, unsure whether he has broken a rule no one ever stated.","Pell, watching Miss Arden take a seat among them, wishes the cabin were brighter, and he resolves to ask the captain for a lamp before the next morning's crossing."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"비평가는 선생님의 등장으로 아침 식사가 '더 생생해지는 동시에 덜 안정된다'고 주장하므로 두 측면이 함께 드러나는 발견이 필요하다. C에서 Pell은 빛에 비친 오렌지를 보고 엔진 소리가 바뀌기 전에 웃는데, 이는 생생함이자 침묵 규칙을 깬 것이며, 이어지는 망설임은 불확실함을 보여 준다. A는 생생함은 있지만 식사를 그대로 유지하려 하므로 '덜 안정됨'이 없다. B는 기억이 떠오를 뿐 의식이 평소대로 진행되어 변화가 드러나지 않는다. D는 오히려 선실이 밝아지지 않았다고 느끼는 것이라 지문 속 '더 밝아짐'과도 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The critic claims the breakfast becomes both more vivid and less settled, so you need a finding that shows both at once. In C, Pell laughs at the orange glowing in the window light, which is vivid, and he does it before the engine changes pitch, breaking the silence rule; his hesitation afterward shows uncertainty. A has vividness, but Pell wants the breakfast to stay the same, so nothing is less settled. B gives Pell a memory, but the ritual goes on exactly as usual, so no change appears. D has Pell wishing the cabin were brighter, which actually contradicts the text's point that the cabin seemed brighter.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.585Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — A schoolteacher's unexpected arrival at the island boat's morning meal transforms the children's quiet ritual into something luminous and uncertain.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"비평가 주장은 '더 생생함 + 덜 안정됨' 두 요소. C만이 빛에 비친 오렌지·웃음(생생함)과 엔진 소리 전 침묵 규칙 위반 후 망설임(불안정)을 동시에 충족. A는 생생함만 있고 현상 유지를 택해 '덜 안정됨' 결여, B는 의식이 평소대로 진행되어 변화 없음, D는 '선실이 더 밝아 보였다'는 지문과 모순. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 정답과 선택지 참조가 일치하고 논리 정확. 두 조건을 모두 확인해야 하므로 medium 적합. 지문은 창작물로 저작권 문제 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"C만 '더 생생함'(빛·웃음)과 '덜 안정됨'(엔진 소리 전 침묵 규칙 위반·망설임)을 함께 충족한다. A는 생생함만 있고 안정 유지를 추구하며, B는 변화가 없다. D는 지문 내용과 모순되어 비교적 쉽게 배제된다. 부분 근거를 가진 오답이 A와 B 두 개라 medium 기준에 부합한다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-command_of_evidence_text-m-002","intendedSkill":"command_of_evidence_text","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-cross_text_connections-m-003","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Cross-Text Connections","difficulty":"medium","skill":"cross_text_connections","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Text 1\nIn Ilse Varga's novel The Tidewright, young Maren steers her uncle's skiff in the island's annual ferry-crossing regatta. She misreads the current, drifts far east of the course, and sees Corran Bank, her family's ancestral fishing ground, from the mainland side for the first time. From there the bank looks small and ordinary, just a pale patch of water among many others. Maren says nothing for the rest of the race, and that silence marks a break: she has outgrown the legends her family built around the place.\n\nText 2\nVarga makes sure the reader sees Corran Bank shrink under Maren's unexpected view; the narration even compares it to \"a thumbprint on glass.\" But reading Maren's quiet as a rejection overlooks what comes next. On the ferry home, she traces the bank's outline from memory on the back of her ticket and gets every shoal right. The strange angle has not cut her off from the grounds. It has shown her that her bond with them is something she will have to keep up by remembering, not something she simply inherits.","question":"Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the claim in Text 1 about what Maren's silence reveals?","options":["By accepting that Maren's silence shows she has outgrown her family's legends, while arguing that her drift off course is an accident rather than a meaningful event in the novel","By disputing that Corran Bank appears small from the mainland side, while agreeing that Maren's silence signals a break with her family","By accepting both that the bank appears diminished and that Maren is withdrawing, while citing her sketch on the ticket as further proof of her detachment","By accepting that the bank appears diminished from Maren's new angle, while arguing that a later moment shows her silence reflects a changed but continuing attachment"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"Text 2의 저자는 \"a thumbprint on glass\"라는 비유를 들어 둑이 작아 보인다는 점은 인정한다. 그러나 귀항하는 페리에서 Maren이 기억만으로 둑의 윤곽을 그리는 장면을 근거로, 그녀의 침묵이 거부가 아니라 형태가 바뀐 애착이라고 주장한다. 따라서 D가 정답이다. A는 Text 2가 반박하는 '침묵=단절'이라는 해석을 오히려 받아들이고 있다. B는 Text 2가 인정한 '둑이 작아 보인다'는 점을 부정하므로 틀렸고, C는 스케치 장면을 정반대 의미(애착이 아닌 거리 두기)로 읽었다.","explanationEn":"The author of Text 2 agrees that the bank looks smaller and quotes the \"thumbprint on glass\" comparison as support. However, the author points to the later scene in which Maren draws the bank accurately from memory and argues that her silence reflects a changed, ongoing attachment rather than a rejection. That makes D the answer. A is wrong because it accepts the \"silence equals break\" reading that Text 2 rejects. B is wrong because it denies the shrinking that Text 2 actually accepts, and C is wrong because it treats the sketch as a sign of detachment, when Text 2 uses it to show the opposite.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.589Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — During the ferry crossing's annual regatta, a miscalculated route causes an islander to witness her family's ancestral fishing ground from an angle she never imagined.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"Text 2 explicitly concedes the bank's diminished appearance (\"thumbprint on glass\") and then rebuts the \"silence = rejection\" reading via the ticket-sketch scene, framing the bond as changed but continuing — exactly D. A wrongly has Text 2 accepting the \"outgrown\" claim (and invents an \"accident\" argument); B contradicts Text 2's concession about the bank shrinking; C inverts the meaning Text 2 assigns to the sketch. Korean and English explanations align with each other and with the letter references; English explanation contains no Hangul. Fictional novel/critic, no copyright concern. Two-step (identify concession + identify rebuttal) with distractors each half-right fits medium."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"정답 D가 옳다. 오답 A·B·C는 각각 일부만 맞는 근거를 가지고 있어 두 텍스트를 비교해야 배제된다. 따라서 medium 난이도에 적합하다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-cross_text_connections-m-003","intendedSkill":"cross_text_connections","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-m-004","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"The letter from the Halvorsen Academy had been folded and refolded so many times that its creases had gone soft as cloth. Katrina, sitting at the stern of the school boat while the island's gray cliffs shrank into the mist behind ______ understood that if she signed it, every return to the harbor would be a visit rather than a homecoming.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["her,","her—","her;","her"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"주어 Katrina 뒤의 \"sitting at the stern ... behind her\"는 쉼표로 시작한 비필수 삽입구이므로, 같은 쉼표로 닫아야 동사 understood와 이어진다. 따라서 A가 정답이다. B의 대시는 삽입구를 닫는다는 점은 맞지만, 쉼표로 연 삽입구를 대시로 닫으면 부호가 서로 짝이 맞지 않는다. C의 세미콜론은 앞뒤에 독립절이 있어야 쓸 수 있는데, 앞부분 \"Katrina, sitting ...\"에는 본동사가 없어서 독립절이 아니다. D처럼 아무 부호도 쓰지 않으면 삽입구가 닫히지 않아 문장 구조가 흐트러진다.","explanationEn":"The phrase \"sitting at the stern ... behind her\" is a nonessential modifier that opens with a comma right after the subject Katrina, so you need a matching comma to close it before the verb \"understood.\" That makes A correct. B is right that the phrase needs to be closed at this point, but a dash can't close a phrase that started with a comma, because the two marks have to match. C fails because a semicolon has to join two independent clauses, and \"Katrina, sitting ...\" has no main verb, so it isn't one. D leaves the phrase open, which muddles the structure of the sentence.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.589Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On the school boat heading home, Katrina must decide whether to accept the scholarship that would carry her away from the island forever.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"Comma-opened nonessential participial phrase (\"sitting at the stern ... behind her\") between subject Katrina and verb understood must be closed with a matching comma; A is correct. B (dash) mismatches the opening comma, C (semicolon) lacks an independent clause before it, D leaves the modifier unclosed. Korean and English explanations agree, reference the correct letters, and contain no errors. Long interrupting phrase plus matching-punctuation rule makes this standard medium difficulty."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"삽입구 안에 while절이 끼어 있어 여는 쉼표를 놓치기 쉽다. 그래서 짝 맞추기 판단이 필요하고 medium 난이도에 맞는다. 대시 오답도 그럴듯하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-boundaries-m-004","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-m-005","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Thorvald had walked for two frozen days along the coast road, sleet stinging his face and the harbor lights of the next port nowhere in sight. When he finally pushed open the door of the pawn shop, the owner, a thin man with ink-stained cuffs who squinted at every stranger, looked up from his ledger______ in a velvet tray behind the counter lay the small garnet ring his daughter had lost.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":[", there,",". There,"," there,"," and there,"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"긴 동격구 뒤의 주절 'the owner ... looked up from his ledger'는 독립절이고, 'there ... lay the ... ring'도 도치된 독립절이다. 두 독립절은 마침표로 나누어야 하므로 B가 정답이다. A는 쉼표만으로 두 독립절을 이어 쉼표 오용(comma splice)이 된다. C는 구두점 없이 두 절을 붙여 무종지문(run-on)이 된다. D는 접속사 and를 썼지만 두 독립절 사이 and 앞에 필요한 쉼표가 없다.","explanationEn":"After the long appositive, the main clause \"the owner ... looked up from his ledger\" is a complete independent clause, and \"there ... lay the ... ring\" is another independent clause with inverted word order. Two independent clauses like these can be split with a period, so B is correct. A joins the two clauses with only a comma, which makes a comma splice. C puts the clauses together with no punctuation at all, which makes a run-on sentence. D adds \"and\" but leaves out the comma that has to come before a coordinating conjunction joining two independent clauses.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.589Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Thorvald, an Icelandic fisherman, travels two frozen days through winter storms to retrieve his daughter's lost wedding ring from a pawn shop in the next port.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B는 명확히 정답이며 A(쉼표 오용), C(무종지문)는 확실한 오답. 그러나 D(\"ledger and there, in a velvet tray ... lay the ring\")는 두 독립절을 등위접속사 and로 연결한 문장으로, 쉼표 누락만을 근거로 배제하는 것은 논쟁의 여지가 있어(짧은 절 사이에서는 쉼표 생략이 널리 허용됨) 정답 유일성이 다소 취약하다. 실제 SAT에서는 보통 이런 거리로는 변별하지 않으므로 D를 다른 명백한 오류(예: 세미콜론 오용, 'and' 없이 접속부사 사용 등)로 교체하는 것이 바람직하다. 난이도는 긴 동격구가 삽입되어 주절 경계를 파악해야 하므로 medium에 부합한다."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B가 유일한 정답이다. D(쉼표 없이 'and'를 쓴 경우)는 SAT 관례로 보면 오답이 맞지만, 짧은 절에서는 쉼표 생략을 허용하는 견해도 있어 다소 논쟁의 여지가 있다. 다만 이 문장에서는 두 절이 길기 때문에 배제가 타당하다. 동격구가 길어서 주어와 동사를 추적하는 단계가 필요하므로 medium 난이도에 적합하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-boundaries-m-005","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-m-006","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"For eleven autumns, Ramón and Diego had carried their squash to the village plaza, each certain the judges would finally favor his. This year a late frost forced them to share a single greenhouse, and on the third cold night Diego broke the silence. His father, a stubborn man who had trusted no neighbor ______ taught him to pinch off the first blossoms so that the vines would send their strength into the roots. Ramón listened, then knelt and showed Diego the crushed eggshells his own father had buried beneath every seedling.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["; had","— had",", had"," had"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"\"a stubborn man who had trusted no neighbor\"는 주어 \"His father\"를 설명하는 비필수 동격어구로, 앞에 쉼표가 열렸으므로 같은 쉼표로 닫아야 하고 그 뒤에 동사 \"had taught\"가 이어진다. 그래서 C가 정답이다. A는 세미콜론을 써서 주어와 동사를 갈라놓고, 세미콜론 앞부분은 독립절이 아니다. B는 대시로 닫아 쉼표로 연 동격어구와 문장부호가 맞지 않는다. D는 닫는 문장부호가 없어서 삽입 어구가 어디서 끝나는지 표시되지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The phrase \"a stubborn man who had trusted no neighbor\" is a nonessential appositive describing the subject \"His father.\" It opens with a comma, so it has to close with a comma before the verb \"had taught\" continues the sentence. That makes C correct. A uses a semicolon, which cuts the subject off from its verb, and the words before the semicolon don't form an independent clause. B closes with a dash, which doesn't match the comma that opened the appositive. D leaves out the closing punctuation entirely, so the reader can't tell where the inserted phrase ends.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.590Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — In a harvest village, Ramón and Diego, rival farmers competing for the year's best crop, end up teaching each other techniques their fathers had kept secret.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"검산: \"His father, a stubborn man who had trusted no neighbor, had taught him...\" — 쉼표로 연 비필수 동격어구를 쉼표로 닫는 C가 유일하게 정확. A는 세미콜론 앞이 독립절이 아니고 주어-동사 분리, B는 쉼표/대시 짝 불일치, D는 닫는 구두점 누락. 해설(한/영) 모두 C를 일관되게 뒷받침하며 글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 난이도: 여는 쉼표를 찾아 짝을 맞추는 두 단계 판단이 필요하고, B(대시)·D(무구두점)가 훑어 읽으면 그럴듯한 오답으로 기능해 medium 적합. 지문은 독창적 서사로 저작권 의심 없음. 사소한 형식 참고: D 선택지가 \" had\"로 앞 공백만 있어 '구두점 없음' 의도는 전달되나 시각적으로 다소 어색함(감점 수준 아님)."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"C는 쉼표로 연 동격어구를 쉼표로 닫는다. 그러면 \"His father, a stubborn man who had trusted no neighbor, had taught him...\"이 된다. 학생은 먼저 동격어구가 어디서 끝나는지 찾고, 이어서 연 부호와 닫는 부호가 같은지 확인해야 한다. 이 두 단계 판단이 medium 난이도에 맞다. D는 \"had trusted ... had taught\"처럼 had가 이어져 훑어 읽으면 고르기 쉽다. B는 대시도 삽입 부호라서 그럴듯해 보이므로 함정으로 잘 작동한다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-boundaries-m-006","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-m-008","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"From the back seat of the swaying matatu, Kamau watched the old leather worker guide the teenager's fingers along the edge of a stiff brown hide, pressing the awl through it with a patience that seemed older than Nairobi itself______ earbuds in, stared past him at the traffic crawling along Thika Road. Kamau wondered who, years from now, would remember the old man's hands.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["; the boy,",", the boy,","; the boy"," the boy,"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"빈칸 앞은 \"Kamau watched ... itself\"까지 완전한 독립절이고, 뒤의 \"the boy ... stared past him\"도 독립절이므로 두 절 사이에 세미콜론이 필요하다. 또한 \"earbuds in\"은 비필수 삽입구라서 \"the boy\" 뒤에 쉼표가 있어야 뒤 쉼표와 짝을 이룬다. 따라서 A가 정답이다. B는 삽입구 쉼표는 맞지만 두 독립절을 쉼표로만 이어 쉼표 오류(comma splice)가 된다. C는 세미콜론은 맞지만 삽입구 앞 쉼표가 빠져 쉼표 짝이 맞지 않고, D는 구두점 없이 두 절을 이어 붙인 run-on 문장이다.","explanationEn":"The text before the blank, \"Kamau watched ... Nairobi itself,\" is a complete independent clause, and \"the boy ... stared past him at the traffic\" is also an independent clause, so you need a semicolon between them. \"Earbuds in\" is a nonessential interrupting phrase, so it needs a comma after \"the boy\" to pair with the comma that follows \"in.\" That makes A correct. B sets off the interrupter correctly, but it joins two independent clauses with only a comma, which is a comma splice. C uses the semicolon correctly but leaves out the opening comma of the interrupter, so the commas don't pair up. D runs the two clauses together with no punctuation at all.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.590Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On a Nairobi matatu, Kamau watches an elderly leather worker train a disinterested teenager in a dying craft, wondering who will remember the old man's hands.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"검산: 빈칸 앞 \"Kamau watched ... Nairobi itself\"는 완전한 독립절, 뒤 \"the boy, earbuds in, stared past him...\"도 독립절 → 세미콜론 필요. \"earbuds in\"은 절대구(삽입구)로 앞뒤 쉼표 짝이 필요하므로 \"the boy,\" 형태가 맞음. A 정답 확인. B는 comma splice, C는 삽입구 앞 쉼표 누락, D는 run-on으로 모두 배제됨. 해설(한/영) 모두 동일 결론·글자 참조이며 모순 없음. 영어 해설 자연스럽고 한글 없음. matatu·Thika Road 등 배경 사실 문제 없음. 난이도: 독립절 판별 + 삽입구 쉼표 짝 확인의 두 단계 판단이 필요하고, B·C가 각각 부분적으로 맞는 근거를 가져 medium에 적합. 사소한 점: 선택지 D 앞 공백이 두 칸으로 표기된 것은 표기 정리 수준의 문제로 판정에 영향 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 A가 맞다. 앞은 독립절이고 뒤도 독립절이며 earbuds in은 쉼표 짝으로 감싼 삽입구다. 'the teenager'를 'the boy'로 받는 지시 관계도 자연스럽다. 경계 판단과 삽입구 판단의 두 단계가 필요해 medium 난이도에 맞다. 다만 D(구두점 없음)는 비교적 쉽게 배제된다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-boundaries-m-008","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-m-009","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Rashid had worked beside the stranger at the tannery vats for three mornings before she spoke of the merchant. Her name was Fadela, and the story she told, a rambling account of a leather trader who had once bartered a saddle for a bride's silver anklet______ the very tale Rashid's grandfather had recited every winter, decades earlier, to a room full of cousins.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":[", and was",", was","; was"," was"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"\"the story she told\" 뒤의 \"a rambling account ... anklet\"은 쉼표로 시작된 비필수 동격어구이므로 같은 쉼표로 닫아야 하고, 그 뒤에 주어 story의 동사 was가 와야 한다. 따라서 B가 정답이다. A는 and가 등위절을 만드는 것처럼 보이지만 앞에 동사가 없어 주어 story와 동사 was를 부적절하게 끊는다. C의 세미콜론은 주어와 동사 사이에 쓸 수 없으며, 앞부분은 독립절도 아니다. D는 동격어구를 여는 쉼표만 있고 닫는 쉼표가 없어 삽입구의 경계가 불완전하다.","explanationEn":"The phrase \"a rambling account ... anklet\" is a nonessential appositive. It opens with a comma after \"the story she told,\" so it must close with a matching comma before the verb \"was,\" which goes with the subject \"story.\" That makes B correct. A adds \"and\" as if it were joining two predicates, but the subject \"story\" has no verb earlier in the sentence, so \"and\" breaks the sentence apart. C puts a semicolon between the subject and its verb, and a semicolon can only join independent clauses. D leaves the appositive open because the closing comma is missing.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.590Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Rashid and Fadela, strangers at the tannery vats, discover they once knew each other's families through a leather merchant's tale told decades ago.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"검산: 주어 \"the story she told\" + 긴 비필수 동격어구(쉼표로 열림) + 동사 \"was\". 닫는 쉼표가 필요하므로 B가 유일하게 옳다. A는 선행 동사 없이 and로 술어를 접속하는 오류, C는 주어–동사 사이 세미콜론(앞부분이 독립절 아님), D는 동격어구를 닫지 않음. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 결론과 글자 참조가 일치하고 정확하다. 긴 삽입구 때문에 훑어 읽으면 D(쉼표 생략)나 A를 고르기 쉬워 medium에 적합. 창작 지문으로 저작권 우려 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"긴 동격어구 안에 관계절(who had once bartered...)이 들어 있어 주어와 동사가 멀리 떨어져 있다. 그래서 동격어구가 쉼표로 열린 지점을 찾고, 닫는 쉼표를 확인하는 두 단계 판단이 필요해 medium 난이도에 맞다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-boundaries-m-009","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-m-010","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"By the time Mara reached the shelter again, her headlamp had dimmed to a weak yellow circle. She had walked three miles in darkness to retrieve the envelope she had glimpsed that afternoon. The letter, creased along its folds and weighted beneath a dented tin cup on the shelter's back ______ been addressed to someone named Eli, and its first line, \"I should have said this at the trailhead,\" was not meant for her at all.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["bench had","bench—had","bench, had","bench; had"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"\"creased along its folds and weighted beneath ... bench\"는 주어 \"The letter\"와 동사 \"had been addressed\" 사이에 끼어든 비필수 수식어이고, 앞에서 쉼표로 열렸으므로 같은 쉼표로 닫아야 한다. 그래서 C가 정답이다. A는 닫는 쉼표가 없어 \"bench\"가 동사 \"had\"의 주어처럼 읽힌다. B는 대시를 쓰는데, 쉼표로 연 삽입구를 대시로 닫으면 짝이 맞지 않는다. D는 세미콜론으로 주어와 동사를 떼어 놓아 앞부분이 독립절이 되지 못한다.","explanationEn":"The phrase \"creased along its folds and weighted beneath ... bench\" is a nonessential modifier that sits between the subject \"The letter\" and its verb \"had been addressed.\" It opens with a comma, so it has to close with a comma too, which makes C correct. A leaves out the closing comma, so \"bench\" looks like the subject of \"had.\" B closes the phrase with a dash, but a phrase that opens with a comma can't close with a dash, because the punctuation has to match. D puts a semicolon between the subject and its verb, and the words before it can't stand alone as an independent clause.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.590Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — A hiker at a shelter walks three miles in darkness to retrieve a forgotten love letter someone else left behind, only to realize it wasn't meant for them.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"주어 \"The letter\"와 동사 \"had been addressed\" 사이 쉼표로 열린 비필수 분사구를 쉼표로 닫는 C가 유일하게 옳음. A는 닫는 쉼표 누락, B는 쉼표-대시 불일치, D는 주어·동사 사이 세미콜론. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 정답과 선택지 참조가 일치하며 오류 없음. 삽입구 범위 파악 + 짝 맞추기의 두 단계 판단이 필요하고 오답들이 그럴듯해 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"긴 삽입구 때문에 여는 쉼표를 확인해야 하는 2단계 판단이 필요하다. 그래서 medium에 맞다. 오답 B와 A가 그럴듯하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-boundaries-m-010","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-m-013","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Elias had paid forty dollars for the desk mostly out of pity: its legs had been splinted with mismatched pine, and a crack ran the length of its top. Back at the truck, he worked the swollen bottom drawer loose and found a bundle of envelopes tied with baling twine, each addressed in his grandfather's slanted hand to a woman named Ruth Avila ______ of them had ever been stamped.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":[", none","; none","none","and, none"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"빈칸 앞 \"he worked ... Ruth Avila\"는 긴 수식어(tied with..., each addressed...)를 포함하지만 그 자체로 완전한 독립절이고, 빈칸 뒤 \"none of them had ever been stamped\"도 주어와 동사를 갖춘 독립절이다. 두 독립절은 세미콜론으로 연결할 수 있으므로 B가 정답이다. A는 쉼표만으로 두 독립절을 이어 comma splice가 된다. 앞의 쉼표 수식어들 때문에 쉼표가 자연스러워 보이지만 접속사가 없다. C는 아무 부호 없이 두 절을 붙인 run-on 문장이다. D는 접속사 and 뒤에 쉼표를 두어 and와 그것이 연결하는 절을 부당하게 분리한다.","explanationEn":"Even with its long modifiers (\"tied with baling twine,\" \"each addressed...\"), the part before the blank is still a complete independent clause, and \"none of them had ever been stamped\" is also an independent clause. A semicolon can join two independent clauses, so B is correct. A joins the two clauses with only a comma, which makes a comma splice. The commas earlier in the sentence can make a comma look right here, but there's no conjunction. C puts no punctuation between the clauses, so it's a run-on sentence. D places a comma after \"and,\" which wrongly cuts the conjunction off from the clause it introduces.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.590Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — At a ranch auction, Elias buys a repaired wooden desk and discovers love letters his grandfather wrote but never mailed still tucked in a drawer.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"빈칸 앞은 긴 분사·동격 수식어를 포함하지만 \"he worked ... and found a bundle of envelopes ...\"로 완결된 독립절이고, 뒤 \"none of them had ever been stamped\"도 독립절이므로 세미콜론(B)이 유일하게 옳다. A는 comma splice, C는 run-on, D는 \"and,\" 로 접속사와 절을 분리하여 오답. 앞의 쉼표 수식어들이 A를 그럴듯하게 만들고 D도 접속사 사용이라는 부분적 근거를 가지므로 medium 적합. 한·영 해설 모두 정답·글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 원작 지문으로 저작권 우려 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"빈칸 앞은 긴 수식어가 붙어 있어도 독립절이고, 뒤의 \"none of them had ever been stamped\"는 정형동사 had가 있는 독립절이다. 따라서 B의 세미콜론만 맞다. A는 앞에 나오는 쉼표 수식어(each addressed...) 때문에 분사구문처럼 보여 강한 오답 유인이 되므로, 훑어 읽으면 틀리는 medium 설계에 맞다. C(run-on)와 D(and 뒤 쉼표)는 상대적으로 약한 오답이지만 그럴듯은 하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-boundaries-m-013","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-m-015","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Soren left the sauna on the point with heat still rising from his shoulders, and he carried that warmth like a lantern through the frozen dark toward the next fjord. His son had gone home hours earlier, unaware of what he had left behind. The knife his son had forgotten on the ice—a bone-handled blade once owned by Soren's own father______ half-buried in snow beside the abandoned fishing hole, its edge catching the faint blue light.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":[", lay","; lay"," lay","—lay"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"대시로 시작한 비필수 동격어구(a bone-handled blade once owned by Soren's own father)는 같은 대시로 닫아야 주어 The knife와 동사 lay가 이어지므로 D가 정답이다. A는 쉼표가 동격어구 뒤에 와서 그럴듯해 보이지만, 대시로 연 삽입구를 쉼표로 닫아 부호가 서로 맞지 않는다. B의 세미콜론은 독립절 두 개를 나눌 때 쓰는데, 여기서는 주어와 동사 lay 사이를 끊어 버린다. C는 삽입구를 닫는 부호가 아예 없어서 대시로 연 삽입구가 끝나지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The dash before \"a bone-handled blade\" opens a nonessential appositive, so a second dash has to close it. That lets the subject \"The knife\" connect to the verb \"lay,\" which is why D is correct. A looks reasonable because a comma comes after the appositive, but you can't close a dash-opened interruption with a comma, since the pair has to match. B uses a semicolon, which belongs between two independent clauses, and here it would cut the subject off from its verb \"lay.\" C leaves out the closing punctuation entirely, so the interruption that started with the dash never ends.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.592Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Soren travels from his coastal sauna to a neighboring fjord to retrieve his son's forgotten fishing knife, carrying warmth through the frozen dark.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"주어 \"The knife ... on the ice\"와 동사 \"lay\" 사이에 대시로 연 동격어구가 삽입되어 있으므로 짝이 맞는 대시로 닫는 D가 유일하게 옳음. A(쉼표)는 부호 불일치, B(세미콜론)는 주어-동사 분리, C는 삽입구 미종결로 배제됨. 해설(한/영) 모두 정답·선택지 참조 일치, 영어 해설 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 난이도는 대시 짝 맞추기+주어-동사 연결 확인의 두 단계 판단이 필요해 medium에 적합. 사소한 점: 선택지 C의 앞 공백이 두 칸으로 표기됨(내용상 문제 없음)."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"대시 짝 맞추기를 묻는 전형적인 문항이다. 삽입구가 길고 앞에 내용 문장이 있어서 쉼표 오답이 그럴듯하다. 중간 난이도에 맞다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-boundaries-m-015","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-m-016","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"When the first thunderclap rolled over the dyeing vats, Amira set down her scraping knife and ran for the drying shed, where Zahra, the rival whose hides had won the guild's praise three seasons running, was already pulling the last skins from the racks. For a long while the two women stood at opposite ends of the shed, listening to the rain drum on the tin ______ finally Zahra, without looking up, asked how Amira kept her indigo from streaking.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["roof, and","roof,","roof and,","roof: and"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"빈칸 앞 \"the two women stood ... roof\"와 뒤 \"Zahra ... asked ...\"는 각각 독립절이므로 둘을 잇는 올바른 경계가 필요하다. A는 쉼표+등위접속사 and로 두 독립절을 적절히 연결한다. B는 쉼표만으로 두 독립절을 이어 comma splice가 된다. C는 and 뒤에 쉼표를 두어 \"finally\"를 삽입구처럼 시작하지만 짝이 되는 쉼표가 없고, 절 사이에도 구두점이 없어 어색하다. D의 콜론은 뒤 내용이 앞 절을 설명·부연할 때 쓰는데, 여기서는 시간 순서의 사건이므로 맞지 않고 콜론 뒤 and도 부적절하다.","explanationEn":"The words before the blank (\"the two women stood ... on the tin roof\") and the words after it (\"Zahra ... asked how ...\") are both independent clauses, so you need a proper boundary between them. A joins them correctly with a comma plus the coordinating conjunction \"and.\" B links the two independent clauses with only a comma, which creates a comma splice. C puts a comma after \"and,\" as if \"finally\" began an interrupting phrase, but there's no matching comma, and there's still no punctuation between the clauses. D uses a colon, but a colon introduces something that explains or expands on the first clause. Here the second clause is just the next event in time, and \"and\" after a colon is inappropriate.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.592Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — At the tannery, a sudden storm forces Amira and her rival Zahra to shelter together, their routine work halted by weather that demands conversation.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"검산: 빈칸 앞 \"the two women stood ... on the tin roof\"(독립절, 분사구 수식 포함)와 뒤 \"finally Zahra ... asked ...\"(독립절)를 잇는 자리. A(쉼표+and) 정확. B는 comma splice, C는 and 앞 쉼표 없음·and 뒤 불필요한 쉼표, D는 콜론 뒤 등위접속사로 부적절. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 A 정답을 일관되게 뒷받침하고 글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 긴 수식어구(listening..., without looking up) 속에서 절의 경계를 찾아야 하고 B가 훑어 읽으면 그럴듯해 medium에 적합. 다만 C·D가 비교적 쉽게 배제되어 medium 하한에 가까움."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"긴 문장과 삽입구 때문에 절의 경계를 찾는 데 정독이 필요하다. 오답 B(comma splice)와 D(콜론)는 그럴듯하므로 medium 난이도에 맞다. C 해설의 '절 사이 구두점 부재' 설명은 다소 단순하지만 결론에는 문제가 없다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-boundaries-m-016","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-m-017","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"For three weeks Florian had practiced the opening bars of the march until his lips ached, and still the low F cracked every time. Mr. Albrecht, the band's conductor for nearly forty years and a man who rarely lifted his baton above his shoulder, listened from the back of the rehearsal hall without comment. When the last note finally sputtered out, he walked forward and rested a hand on the bell of the tuba______ problem, he explained gently, was not Florian's fingering but his fear of being heard.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":[", the","; the"," the",": and the"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"빈칸 앞 \"he walked forward and rested a hand on the bell of the tuba\"와 빈칸 뒤 \"the problem ... was not Florian's fingering ...\"는 각각 독립절이며, 뒤 절 안의 삽입구 \"he explained gently\"를 걷어내야 주어 the problem과 동사 was가 보인다. 두 독립절을 연결하려면 세미콜론이 적절하므로 B가 정답이다. A는 쉼표만으로 두 독립절을 이어 쉼표 오용(comma splice)이 된다. C는 아무 문장부호 없이 두 절을 붙인 무종지문이다. D는 콜론 뒤에 등위접속사 and를 덧붙여 콜론의 쓰임에 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The text before the blank, \"he walked forward and rested a hand on the bell of the tuba,\" is an independent clause. The text after it is one too: once you set aside the interrupting phrase \"he explained gently,\" you can see the subject \"the problem\" and the verb \"was.\" A semicolon correctly joins two independent clauses, so B is correct. A joins the clauses with only a comma, which makes a comma splice. C uses no punctuation at all, which makes a run-on sentence. D puts the conjunction \"and\" right after a colon, and that isn't how a colon is used.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.592Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Young Florian struggles to master the tuba while his mentor, the band's aging conductor, gently insists that precision is less important than presence.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"빈칸 앞 \"he walked forward and rested a hand on the bell of the tuba\"와 뒤 \"the problem ... was not ... but ...\"가 모두 독립절임을 직접 확인했으며, 삽입구 \"he explained gently\"를 걷어내면 주어·동사가 드러난다. 세미콜론(B)이 유일하게 적법. A는 comma splice, C는 run-on, D는 콜론+and 조합으로 부적절. 삽입구로 인해 두 번째 절의 독립성을 파악해야 하는 두 단계 판단이 필요하고, A·D가 부분적 근거를 가진 오답이므로 medium에 적합. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 B를 일관되게 뒷받침하며 글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 지문은 창작 서사로 저작권 의심 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"삽입구 'he explained gently'를 걷어내야 독립절이 보이므로 판단이 두 단계로 이루어져 medium 수준에 맞음. 다만 D(': and')는 쉽게 배제되는 편임.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-boundaries-m-017","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-m-021","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"For three seasons, Priya and Anita had measured each other in kilograms of leaf, each woman weighing her basket at dusk and glancing sideways at the other's tally. Then, on a rain-slick slope above the factory, Anita slipped and fell, her basket spilling green across the mud. Priya, the rival who had once hidden a pair of pruning shears just to slow Anita ______ beside her without a word. Their hands, blistered at the very same knuckles, met over the scattered leaves.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["down; knelt","down, knelt","down knelt","down—knelt"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"\"the rival who had once hidden ... down\"은 주어 Priya를 설명하는 비필수 동격 표현이고, Priya 바로 뒤 쉼표로 시작된다. 따라서 이 표현은 쉼표로 닫아야 주어 Priya와 동사 knelt가 바르게 이어지므로 B가 정답이다. A의 세미콜론은 두 독립절 사이에 쓰는 부호인데, 여기서는 주어와 동사를 갈라 놓아 앞뒤 어느 쪽도 완전한 절이 되지 못한다. C는 닫는 부호가 없어서 동격 표현이 문장의 나머지 부분과 뒤섞인다. D의 대시도 삽입 요소를 끊을 수는 있지만, 쉼표로 연 삽입구를 대시로 닫으면 부호의 짝이 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The phrase \"the rival who had once hidden ... down\" is a nonessential appositive describing the subject, Priya. It opens with the comma right after \"Priya.\" You have to close it with a matching comma so that the subject \"Priya\" connects cleanly to its verb \"knelt,\" which makes B correct. A uses a semicolon, which belongs between two independent clauses, but here it would cut the subject off from its verb and leave neither side a complete clause. C leaves out the closing punctuation, so the appositive blurs into the rest of the sentence. D's dash can set off an interruption, but an interruption that opens with a comma can't close with a dash, because the marks have to match.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.592Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On the tea estate, rival harvesters Priya and Anita compete mercilessly until an accident makes them realize they've been fighting the same exhaustion.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"검산: \"Priya, [the rival who had once hidden ... to slow Anita down], knelt beside her\" — 쉼표로 연 비필수 동격구는 쉼표로 닫아야 하므로 B가 유일한 정답. A(세미콜론)는 주어와 동사를 분리해 양쪽 모두 독립절이 아님, C는 닫는 부호 누락, D는 쉼표–대시 짝 불일치. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 B를 일관되게 뒷받침하며 글자 참조 정확, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 긴 동격구(관계절 포함) 속에서 여는 쉼표를 찾아 짝을 맞춰야 하므로 두 단계 판단이 필요하고, D는 부분적 타당성을 가진 매력적 오답 — medium 적합. 지문은 창작 서사로 저작권 의심 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"동격 삽입구가 길어서 여는 쉼표를 찾아야 하는 2단계 판단이 필요하다. 표준적인 medium 문항이다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-boundaries-m-021","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-m-023","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"By noon the bronze mirror borrowed from the neighboring shrine was gone, packed by mistake into a tour group's luggage and now somewhere on the coastal highway. Father Ishida, who had performed the harvest rite for thirty years without once altering its order, did not cancel the ceremony ______ placed a paper lantern on the altar where the mirror should have stood and began the chant as if nothing were missing.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":[", he","and, he",", instead, he","; instead, he"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"긴 비필수 관계절 뒤에 있는 'Father Ishida ... did not cancel the ceremony'는 독립절이고, 'he placed ...'도 독립절이다. 두 독립절은 세미콜론으로 이을 수 있으며, 접속부사 instead 뒤에는 쉼표를 찍으므로 D가 정답이다. A는 쉼표만으로 두 독립절을 이어 쉼표 오용(comma splice)이 된다. C는 instead가 들어가 있어도 접속부사는 접속사가 아니므로 역시 comma splice이다. B는 and로 두 절을 잇긴 했지만 and와 he 사이의 쉼표가 불필요하다.","explanationEn":"Look past the long nonessential clause and you'll see that \"Father Ishida ... did not cancel the ceremony\" is an independent clause, and \"he placed ...\" is another one. A semicolon can join two independent clauses, and the conjunctive adverb \"instead\" takes a comma after it, so D is correct. A joins the two independent clauses with only a comma, which makes a comma splice. C is still a comma splice even with \"instead,\" because a conjunctive adverb is not a conjunction. B does join the clauses with \"and,\" but the comma between \"and\" and \"he\" doesn't belong there.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.592Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — During the village festival, a borrowed shrine decoration gets mixed with tourists' luggage, forcing a priest to improvise a ceremony without its centerpiece.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"검산: 'Father Ishida ... did not cancel the ceremony'와 'he placed ... and began ...'은 모두 독립절. A·C는 comma splice(C는 접속부사 instead만으로 연결 불가), B는 'and, he'의 쉼표 위치 오류. D(세미콜론 + instead + 쉼표)만 적법. 해설 한·영 모두 정답 및 오답 근거가 일치하고 선택지 글자 참조가 정확함. 긴 비필수 관계절 뒤에서 독립절 경계를 식별해야 하고, B·C가 부분적으로 그럴듯한 오답이므로 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"긴 비필수 관계절 때문에 주절 구조를 파악해야 하고, C(쉼표+instead)가 그럴듯한 오답이어서 medium에 맞음. B는 'and, he'의 쉼표가 불필요하므로 배제가 타당함.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-boundaries-m-023","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-m-024","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"For three years, Morag had watched Miss Fraser chalk the date onto the blackboard each morning, and she knew the looping shape of every numeral by heart. Today the chalk skittered, leaving a seven that wavered like marram grass in the wind off the Sound. No one in the cramped schoolroom, not even the minister's son, who noticed everything and repeated most of ______ said a word about it. Morag, however, slid her own hands beneath the desk and began, very quietly, to count the tremors.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["it,","it","it;","it—"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장의 주어는 \"No one\"이고 본동사는 \"said\"이다. 그 사이에 쉼표로 시작하는 비필수 삽입 요소 \"not even the minister's son\"과 \"who noticed everything and repeated most of it\"이 들어가 있으므로, 여는 쉼표에 맞춰 쉼표로 닫아야 한다. 따라서 A가 정답이다. B는 닫는 쉼표가 없어서 \"it said\"가 하나로 붙어 읽히고, 그 결과 주어와 동사의 연결이 흐려진다. C의 세미콜론은 앞뒤에 독립절이 와야 하는데, 앞부분에는 본동사가 없어 독립절이 아니다. D의 대시는 쉼표로 연 삽입구를 닫을 수 없으므로 부호의 짝이 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this sentence is \"No one,\" and its main verb is \"said.\" Between them are two nonessential elements, \"not even the minister's son\" and \"who noticed everything and repeated most of it.\" Both open with commas, so they have to close with a comma before the verb. That makes A correct. B leaves out the closing comma, so \"it said\" runs together and the subject–verb link gets blurred. C uses a semicolon, which needs an independent clause on both sides, but the part before the blank has no main verb yet. D uses a dash, which can't close an interruption that opened with a comma, so the punctuation doesn't match.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.592Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On the Scottish island, young Morag notices the schoolteacher's trembling hands before anyone speaks the word \"illness\" aloud.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"주어 \"No one\"과 본동사 \"said\" 사이에 쉼표로 연 두 개의 비필수 삽입 요소(동격 \"not even the minister's son\" + 관계절)가 들어가 있으므로 쉼표로 닫는 A가 유일하게 옳다. B는 닫는 부호 누락, C는 앞부분이 독립절이 아니므로 세미콜론 불가, D는 쉼표로 연 삽입구를 대시로 닫아 짝이 맞지 않는다. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 정답 A와 선택지 참조가 일치하고 논리가 정확하다. 긴 삽입 구조 속에서 주어-동사를 찾아야 하므로 medium에 적합하며, B·D가 그럴듯한 오답으로 기능한다. 지문은 자체 창작으로 보여 저작권 우려 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"삽입구가 길고 관계절과 중첩되어 있어 정답을 고르려면 주어와 동사를 추적해야 한다. 그래서 중간 난이도에 맞다. 대시와 쉼표를 짝짓는 오답도 그럴듯하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-boundaries-m-024","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-m-025","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Bjorn worked beside the old man on the cold planks of the Húsavík pier, and neither of them spoke as they mended the torn net. Gunnar, who had fished these waters for fifty-one years and would sell his boat on Monday, tied each knot slowly, pulling it tight with a small grunt of ______ watched his mentor's hands and copied every motion, as if memorizing them were the only farewell he was allowed.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["satisfaction, Bjorn","satisfaction; Bjorn","satisfaction, and Bjorn,","satisfaction Bjorn"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"빈칸 앞 \"Gunnar ... tied each knot ... satisfaction\"은 완전한 독립절이고, 뒤의 \"Bjorn watched ... allowed\"도 독립절이다. 두 독립절은 세미콜론으로 연결할 수 있으므로 B가 정답이다. A는 쉼표만으로 두 독립절을 이어 comma splice가 된다. C는 쉼표+and는 맞지만 주어 Bjorn과 동사 watched 사이에 불필요한 쉼표를 넣었다. D는 문장부호 없이 두 절을 이어 run-on 문장이 된다.","explanationEn":"The text before the blank, \"Gunnar ... tied each knot ... satisfaction,\" is a complete independent clause, and \"Bjorn watched ... allowed\" is another one. You can join two independent clauses with a semicolon, so B is correct. A joins them with only a comma, which makes a comma splice. C correctly uses a comma plus \"and,\" but it puts an unnecessary comma between the subject \"Bjorn\" and its verb \"watched.\" D has no punctuation at all, so it's a run-on sentence.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.592Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — An Icelandic port fisherman, Bjorn, helps his mentor salvage one last net before the old man retires, each knot a wordless goodbye.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"빈칸 앞 \"Gunnar ... tied each knot ... satisfaction\"(분사구 포함)과 뒤 \"Bjorn watched ... allowed\"는 모두 독립절이며, 세미콜론(B)으로 연결하는 것이 적절함을 직접 확인. A는 comma splice, C는 주어-동사 사이 불필요한 쉼표, D는 run-on. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 B를 일관되게 뒷받침하고 선택지 참조가 정확하며 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 긴 삽입절(who ... Monday)과 분사구가 첫 절의 독립성 판단을 요구하고, C가 '쉼표+and'로 부분적으로 맞는 근거를 가져 비교가 필요하므로 medium에 적합. 원작 창작 지문으로 저작권 의심 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"긴 삽입절(who had fished... Monday)과 분사구(pulling...) 때문에 주절 범위를 찾는 데 두 단계 판단이 필요하다. C는 쉼표+and라는 부분적으로 맞는 근거를 갖춘 매력적인 오답이다. 중간 난이도로 적절하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-boundaries-m-025","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-m-026","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"The northbound train shuddered into the station, and Diane stepped aboard without looking at the other passengers on the El platform. Only when the doors closed did she notice him. The stranger in the gray overcoat, a man she had last seen as the boy who read Neruda aloud on her aunt's lakeside dock every evening during the summer of 1924______ lifted his eyes from his newspaper and quietly said her name.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":[";","—",",",":"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장의 주어는 \"The stranger in the gray overcoat\"이고 동사는 \"lifted\"이다. 그 사이에 쉼표로 시작하는 긴 동격어구 \"a man she had last seen ... 1924\"가 끼어 있다. 비필수 동격어구는 앞뒤를 같은 부호로 닫아야 하므로 쉼표가 필요하고, 따라서 정답은 C이다. A의 세미콜론은 앞뒤에 독립절이 와야 하는데, 이 문장에서는 주어와 동사를 갈라놓을 뿐이다. B의 대시는 동격어구를 닫을 수는 있지만 여는 부호가 쉼표여서 짝이 맞지 않고, D의 콜론은 앞부분이 완전한 절이 아니며 주어와 동사 사이에 올 수 없다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this sentence is \"The stranger in the gray overcoat,\" and its verb is \"lifted.\" Between them is a long appositive that starts with a comma: \"a man she had last seen ... 1924.\" A nonessential appositive has to be closed with the same mark that opened it, so a comma is needed, and C is correct. A is wrong because a semicolon needs an independent clause on each side, and here it would just split the subject from its verb. B is wrong because a dash could close an appositive, but this one opens with a comma, so the marks don't match. D is wrong because a colon has to follow a complete clause, and it can't go between a subject and its verb.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.592Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On the 1960s El platform, strangers Diane and Robert board the same northbound train and recognize each other from a brief, transformative summer forty years prior.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"주어 \"The stranger in the gray overcoat\"와 동사 \"lifted\" 사이에 쉼표로 열린 긴 동격어구가 끼어 있으므로 쉼표로 닫아야 함(C). 세미콜론·콜론은 주어-동사 사이에 올 수 없고, 대시는 여는 부호와 짝이 맞지 않음. 해설(한/영) 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스러움. 긴 동격어구 때문에 여는 쉼표를 찾아야 하고 대시(B)가 그럴듯한 오답으로 기능하므로 medium 적합. 창작 지문으로 저작권 우려 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"긴 동격어구 때문에 여는 쉼표를 놓치기 쉽고, 대시가 그럴듯한 오답이라 비교가 필요하다. 표준 medium 수준의 쉼표 짝 맞추기 문항이다. 네루다의 1924년 시집 출간 시기와도 맞는다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-boundaries-m-026","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-028","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Kipchoge leaned forward from the back bench of the matatu as it idled near the Kencom stage. The driver, his fingers blackened with engine grease and a toothpick rolling slowly between his lips, ______ a coil of copper wire salvaged from an old doorbell through the radio's cracked faceplate and fastened it in place with a strip torn from a faded football scarf. Every part, Kipchoge realized, carried some earlier life of the van.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["threaded","threading","who threaded","having threaded"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"주어 \"The driver\" 뒤에 긴 독립 분사구문(his fingers ... his lips)이 삽입되어 있어 문장의 본동사가 빈칸에 와야 한다. 또한 빈칸 뒤의 \"and fastened\"와 병렬을 이루려면 과거형 정동사가 필요하므로 A가 정답이다. B와 D는 분사 형태여서 문장에 본동사가 없게 되고 \"fastened\"와 병렬도 맞지 않는다. C는 관계절을 만들어 \"threaded\"와 \"fastened\"를 모두 관계절 안에 넣어 버리므로 주어 \"The driver\"의 본동사가 없는 불완전한 문장이 된다.","explanationEn":"The subject \"The driver\" is followed by a long interrupting phrase (his fingers ... his lips), so the blank has to supply the sentence's main verb. It also needs to be parallel with \"and fastened\" after the blank, and that calls for a past-tense finite verb, so A is correct. B and D are participles, so with either one the sentence has no main verb, and neither lines up with \"fastened.\" C makes a relative clause that pulls both \"threaded\" and \"fastened\" inside it, which leaves \"The driver\" without a main verb and turns the sentence into a fragment.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.592Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On a Nairobi matatu, Kipchoge watches a driver reassemble his broken dashboard radio with found parts, each piece telling the van's secret history.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"검산: 주어 \"The driver\" 뒤 긴 절대구문(his fingers ... his lips) 삽입 후 빈칸이 본동사 자리이며 \"and fastened\"와 병렬이므로 과거형 정동사 \"threaded\"(A)만 완전한 문장을 만든다. B·D는 분사라 본동사 부재, C는 관계절이 \"threaded ... and fastened\"를 모두 흡수해 주절 동사가 사라져 단편이 된다. 한·영 해설 모두 동일 결론과 글자 참조로 정확하고 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 난이도: 긴 삽입구로 주어-동사 추적 + \"and fastened\" 병렬 확인의 두 단계 판단이 필요하고, B·C가 훑어 읽으면 그럴듯해 medium에 적합. Kencom stage(나이로비 마타투 정류장)는 실제 지명으로 사실 오류 없음. 창작 지문으로 저작권 의심 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"긴 절대구문이 주어와 동사 사이에 끼어 있어 훑어 읽으면 B나 C를 고르기 쉬움. 병렬 구조까지 확인해야 하는 두 단계 판단이 필요해 medium 난이도에 적합함.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-028","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-029","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"The smoke from the roasting beans drifted toward the low ceiling as their host poured the first round, called abol. Tekla and Abeba, who had undercut each other's prices at the Merkato spice stalls for nearly a decade, sat stiffly on opposite cushions. Only when Abeba mentioned her mother's village near Adwa did Tekla set down her cup. The story her own mother had told, of two girls separated during the war and never reunited, ______ the same river, the same burned church, the same name.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["having contained","contained","were containing","containing"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장의 주어는 단수 명사 \"The story\"이고, \"her own mother had told\"와 \"of two girls ... never reunited\"는 그 주어를 꾸미는 수식어이므로 빈칸에는 단수 주어에 맞는 정동사가 들어가야 한다. B의 \"contained\"는 정동사이고 단수 주어와도 맞아 문장을 완성하므로 정답이다. C는 정동사이긴 하지만 복수형 \"were\"를 쓰는데, 바로 앞의 복수 명사 \"girls\"에 끌려 고르기 쉬운 오답이다. A와 D는 분사라서 문장에 본동사가 없게 되어 완전한 문장이 되지 못한다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this sentence is the singular noun \"The story.\" The phrases \"her own mother had told\" and \"of two girls ... never reunited\" only describe it, so the blank needs a finite verb that agrees with a singular subject. Choice B, \"contained,\" is a finite verb that agrees with \"story,\" so it completes the sentence correctly. Choice C is also a finite verb, but it uses the plural \"were.\" It's tempting because the plural noun \"girls\" sits right before the blank. Choices A and D are participles, which would leave the sentence without a main verb, so the sentence wouldn't be complete.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.592Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — At an Ethiopian coffee ceremony, rival merchants Tekla and Abeba meet in a stranger's home and discover their mothers were sisters separated by war.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"주어 \"The story\"(단수)와 빈칸 사이에 관계절·전치사구가 길게 끼어 있어 두 단계 판단(정동사 필요 + 단수 일치)이 요구됨. B \"contained\"만 정동사이면서 단수 일치. C는 \"girls\"에 끌리는 그럴듯한 오답, A/D는 비정형 동사. 해설 결론·선택지 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 난이도 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"긴 수식구로 주어-동사 분리, 분사 함정 2개, 수일치 함정 1개. 중간 난이도에 적합.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-029","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-030","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"As Abebe shook the green coffee beans over the charcoal brazier, smoke curling toward the low ceiling, his neighbors settled onto the woven grass mat and began to whisper about his cousin Tsehay. The rumors, carried up from the market by two women who claimed to have seen her stepping off the Addis Ababa bus in a tailored wool coat, ______ that she had spent her years of exile becoming a celebrated schoolteacher. Abebe poured the first cup slowly, wondering whether the story was true or merely a kindness the village had invented for her.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["insisting","insists","insisted","having insisted"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"문장의 주어는 'The rumors'이고, 'carried up from ... coat'는 주어를 꾸미는 긴 분사구일 뿐이므로 빈칸에는 본동사가 와야 한다. 또 지문 전체가 과거 시제로 서술되므로 복수 주어에 맞는 과거형 C가 정답이다. A와 D는 분사 형태여서 문장에 본동사가 없게 되어 불완전한 문장이 된다. B는 동사 형태이긴 하지만 바로 앞의 단수 명사 'bus'나 'coat'에 끌린 단수형이라 복수 주어 'rumors'와 일치하지 않고, 과거 서술과 시제도 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The subject of the sentence is \"The rumors,\" and the long phrase \"carried up from ... coat\" only modifies that subject, so the blank has to be filled by the main verb. The whole passage is told in the past tense, so C, a past-tense verb that works with the plural subject, is correct. A and D are participle forms, which would leave the sentence with no main verb and make it incomplete. B is a verb, but it is singular because it is pulled toward the nearby singular nouns \"bus\" and \"coat,\" so it doesn't agree with the plural subject \"rumors.\" It also breaks the past-tense narration.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.592Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Abebe hosts the coffee ceremony when whispers arrive that his distant cousin has returned from exile, and he wonders if the rumors of her transformed life are true or kind invention.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"주어 'The rumors'(복수) + 긴 분사 수식구 뒤 본동사 자리. 과거 서술과 복수 일치 모두 충족하는 C가 유일한 정답. A·D는 분사형으로 문장 파편, B는 인접 단수 명사(bus, coat)에 끌린 오답으로 설계되어 비교 판단 요구. 한·영 해설 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 긴 수식구 사이에 본동사 판단 + 수·시제 확인의 두 단계 → medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"긴 분사구로 주어와 동사를 떼어 놓았고, 단수 명사 bus/coat가 끌림 오답을 만든다. 시제와 수 일치를 함께 판단해야 하므로 medium 난이도에 맞다. 정답은 C 하나로 정해진다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-030","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-031","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Amara had worked her father's tannery vats since she was twelve, and she knew the sour smell of the lime pits better than her own name. On the morning the offer arrived, she could not bring herself to open it again. The letter from the master leatherworkers of Florence, with its two neat folds and its wax seal of crossed awls, ______ on the bench beside the dye vats all day while she scraped hides and tried not to look at it.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["lie","lying","have lain","lay"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장의 주어는 단수 명사 'The letter'이고, 'from the master leatherworkers of Florence'와 'with its two neat folds...' 같은 수식어구가 주어와 동사 사이에 끼어 있다. 그래서 문장에는 단수 주어와 일치하면서 과거 시제 서술('had worked', 'arrived', 'scraped')과도 맞는 정동사가 필요하다. 'lie'의 과거형인 D가 두 조건을 모두 충족한다. A는 정동사이긴 하지만 복수형 현재 시제여서 단수 주어와도, 과거 서술과도 맞지 않는다. B는 분사라서 문장에 정동사가 없게 된다. C는 완료 시제이긴 하지만 'have'가 복수형이라 단수 주어 'letter'와 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this sentence is the singular noun \"The letter.\" Two modifying phrases, \"from the master leatherworkers of Florence\" and \"with its two neat folds...,\" come between it and the verb. That means you need a finite verb that agrees with a singular subject and also fits the past-tense narration (\"had worked,\" \"arrived,\" \"scraped\"). Choice D, the past tense of \"lie,\" meets both requirements. Choice A is a finite verb, but it's a plural present-tense form, so it doesn't match a singular subject or the past-tense story. Choice B is a participle, so the sentence would have no main verb. Choice C is a perfect tense, but \"have\" is plural and doesn't agree with \"letter.\"","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.592Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Amara works the tannery vats and receives a letter offering apprenticeship abroad, forcing her to choose between honoring her father's legacy and claiming her own path.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"주어 'The letter'(단수)와 동사 사이에 두 개의 전치사구가 삽입되어 있고, 서술은 과거 시제('had worked', 'arrived', 'scraped'). 'lay'는 자동사 'lie'의 과거형으로 단수 일치·과거 시제 모두 충족하여 D가 정답. A 'lie'는 현재형(복수/원형)으로 수·시제 불일치, B 'lying'은 분사로 정동사 부재, C 'have lain'은 'have'가 단수 주어와 불일치. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 동일한 결론과 글자 참조를 가지며 정확함. 삽입 수식어구 건너뛰기 + 시제 확인의 두 단계 판단이 필요하고, A·C가 정동사로서 부분적 타당성을 가져 비교 배제가 요구되므로 medium에 적합. 독창적 지문으로 저작권 문제 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"수식어구가 주어와 동사 사이에 끼어 있고, lie/lay 혼동과 수 일치·시제를 함께 판단해야 해서 medium 수준에 맞다. 'lay'가 'lie'의 과거형이라는 점을 알아야 하므로 오답 선택지들도 그럴듯하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-031","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-036","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"By the third week of the grain elevator shutdown, the Macleods had run out of ways to fill their evenings. When a thin coyote began circling the empty machine shed, Della left scraps by the fence, and her brother Ross quietly loaded the rifle. The argument between them, along with the long silences that followed each of their father's attempts to settle it, ______ into every room of the farmhouse, even the kitchen, where no one had raised a voice in years.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["was seeping","were seeping","seeping","having seeped"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장의 주어는 단수 명사 'The argument'이고, 'along with ... settle it'는 주어 수에 영향을 주지 않는 삽입 수식어구이다. 따라서 문장에는 단수 정동사가 필요하므로 A가 정답이다. B는 정동사이긴 하지만 바로 앞의 복수 명사 'silences'나 'attempts'에 끌린 복수형이라 주어와 수가 맞지 않는다. C와 D는 분사 형태여서 문장에 정동사가 없게 되므로 문장이 불완전해진다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this sentence is the singular noun \"The argument.\" The phrase \"along with ... settle it\" is an interrupting modifier, and it doesn't change the subject's number. That means the sentence needs a singular finite verb, so A is correct. B is a finite verb, but it's plural, which happens when you match it to the nearby plural nouns \"silences\" or \"attempts\" instead of the real subject. C and D are participles, so with either one the sentence has no main verb and is incomplete.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.592Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — A stray coyote wanders onto the Macleods' property during the grain elevator shutdown, and their quiet household fractures into arguments about mercy and practicality.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"주어 'The argument'(단수) + 'along with ...' 삽입구(수에 영향 없음) → 단수 정동사 'was seeping'이 정답임을 직접 확인. 삽입구 내 복수 명사 'silences', 'attempts'가 B로 유인하는 구조이며, C·D는 정동사 부재로 문장 불완전. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 동일 결론과 글자 참조를 가지며 오류 없음. 긴 삽입구 속 복수 명사 간섭 + 정동사/비정동사 판별의 2단계 판단이 요구되어 medium에 적합. 다만 C·D는 모두 '정동사 없음'으로 배제 근거가 동일해 오답 간 변별은 B에 집중되는 전형적 SAT 구조."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"'along with' 삽입구를 넘어 주어와 동사의 수를 일치시키는 문항이다. 주어가 단수인 'argument'이고, 복수 명사인 'silences'와 'attempts'가 오답 B를 고르도록 유도한다. C와 D는 비정동사형 오답이다. 판단이 두 단계로 이루어지므로 중간 난이도에 맞다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-036","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-037","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"When the power failed, Danny lit a stub of candle and set the old checkerboard on the kitchen table. His grandson, Eli, wanted to know how miners had found their way underground before electric lamps, and Danny answered between jumps of his red kings. The questions that the boy asked between moves, whispered as though the dark itself might be listening, ______ gradually from the candle's flicker to whether the mine would still be open by the time he grew up.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["drifts","drifted","was drifting","drifting"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장의 주어는 복수 명사 'The questions'이고, 'that the boy asked between moves'와 'whispered as though...listening'은 주어를 꾸미는 수식어일 뿐이다. 그래서 빈칸에는 복수 주어와 맞는 정동사가 와야 하고, 지문 전체가 과거 시제(failed, lit, wanted)이므로 과거형 B 'drifted'가 정답이다. A 'drifts'는 바로 앞의 단수 명사 'dark'에 맞춘 단수 현재형이라 수도 시제도 맞지 않는다. C 'was drifting'은 과거 시제는 맞지만 단수 동사라서 복수 주어와 일치하지 않는다. D 'drifting'은 분사라서 문장에 정동사가 없게 된다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this sentence is the plural noun \"The questions.\" The phrases \"that the boy asked between moves\" and \"whispered as though the dark itself might be listening\" only modify that subject. So the blank needs a finite verb that agrees with a plural subject, and since the passage is told in the past tense (failed, lit, wanted), B, \"drifted,\" is correct. A, \"drifts,\" agrees with the nearby singular noun \"dark\" instead of the real subject, and it's also in the wrong tense. C, \"was drifting,\" gets the past tense right, but it's singular, so it doesn't agree with the plural subject. D, \"drifting,\" is a participle, which would leave the sentence with no main verb.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.593Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Old coal miner Danny plays checkers with his grandson during the power outage, and the boy's questions about the dark become questions about the future.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"주어 'The questions'(복수)와 과거 시제 서사에 맞는 정동사는 B 'drifted'뿐임을 직접 확인. A는 수·시제 불일치, C는 시제는 맞으나 단수(were drifting이어야 함), D는 비정형으로 정동사 부재. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 정답과 선택지 글자 참조가 일치하고 모순 없음. 영어 해설에 한글 없음, 자연스러움. 주어 식별(수식어 'dark' 함정)과 시제 판단의 두 단계가 요구되고, C·A가 부분적 근거를 가지므로 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"주어와 동사 사이에 관계절과 분사구가 길게 끼어 있어 수 일치를 판단해야 하고, 시제도 확인해야 함. 오답 A와 C는 각각 부분적으로 그럴듯해 보이고 D는 정동사가 없는 문장을 만듦. 정답은 하나로 명확함.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-037","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-038","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"All summer the two men had circled the date without naming it. Now, on the last Saturday before the mine sealed its shafts for good, Clarence stood at the stake behind Eugene's garage, the iron shoe cool against his palm. The pit, which the two neighbors had dug together nineteen years earlier and had raked smooth every spring since, ______ a shallow crater of packed clay. Eugene said nothing as Clarence swung his arm back, and neither of them looked toward the headframe on the ridge.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["having worn into","were worn into","had worn into","wearing into"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장의 주어는 단수 명사 'The pit'이고, which로 시작하는 관계절은 'since'에서 끝나므로 빈칸에는 주절의 정동사가 와야 한다. C의 'had worn'은 단수 주어와 맞는 정동사이므로 문장이 완성된다. A와 D는 분사 형태라 주절에 정동사가 없게 되어 문장이 성립하지 않는다. B는 정동사이지만 복수형 'were'가 관계절 안의 'neighbors'에 이끌린 형태여서 단수 주어 'pit'과 일치하지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this sentence is the singular noun \"The pit,\" and the relative clause starting with \"which\" ends at \"since,\" so the blank needs the main verb of the sentence. Choice C, \"had worn,\" is a finite verb that works with a singular subject, so it completes the sentence. Choices A and D are participles, which would leave the main clause with no finite verb. Choice B is a finite verb, but the plural \"were\" seems to be pulled in by \"neighbors\" inside the relative clause, and it doesn't agree with the singular subject \"pit.\"","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.593Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Neighbors Clarence and Eugene finally play their long-deferred horseshoe championship the summer before the mine closes forever, each throw weighted with unspoken farewell.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"주어 'The pit'(단수)와 긴 관계절(which ... since) 뒤에 주절 정동사가 필요. C 'had worn into'는 단수 주어와 일치하는 정동사이며 과거완료 시제도 주변 과거 서술과 조화됨. A·D는 분사형으로 정동사 부재, B는 관계절 내 'neighbors'에 이끌린 복수형으로 불일치. 해설(한/영) 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 오답 B가 부분적 타당성(정동사·수동태 가능)을 가져 비교 필요, A/D는 관계절 길이 때문에 훑어 읽으면 그럴듯함 — medium 적합. 지문은 창작으로 보이며 저작권 의심 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"주어와 동사 사이에 긴 관계절이 끼어 있어 정동사 필요 여부와 수 일치를 함께 판단해야 하므로 medium 수준에 맞음. 'had worn into'는 자동사 용법(점차 ~이 되다)으로 문법상 문제없음. 영어 해설의 'seems to be pulled in'은 표현이 조금 모호하지만 받아들일 만함.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-038","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-039","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Alem roasted the green beans in the shallow pan as she had every Sunday for thirty years, and the smoke drifted toward Dereje, who sat with his hands folded and his eyes on the window. The three small cups, each one chipped along the rim from decades of mornings like this one, ______ on the tray between them, and neither of the old friends reached for the first. Each knew exactly what grief the other carried; neither could remember the last time they had spoken of it.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["was waiting","waits","have waited","waited"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장의 주어는 복수 명사 'cups'이고, 삽입구 'each one chipped ... this one'은 주어를 꾸미는 수식어일 뿐이다. 또 지문은 roasted, drifted, reached 같은 과거 시제로 서술되므로 동사도 과거여야 한다. D(waited)는 복수 주어와 맞고 과거 서술과도 일치한다. A는 과거 시제지만 단수형이라 'each one'에 이끌린 오류이고, B는 단수이면서 현재 시제이다. C는 복수형이지만 현재완료라 뒤의 'reached'와 과거 서술의 흐름이 어긋난다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this sentence is the plural noun \"cups.\" The phrase \"each one chipped ... this one\" just describes the cups, so it doesn't change the subject. The passage is also told in the past tense (roasted, drifted, reached), so the verb needs to be past tense too. D, \"waited,\" agrees with the plural subject and fits the past-tense narration. A is past tense but singular, which is the mistake you'd make if \"each one\" pulled you off track. B is singular and present tense. C is plural, but its present perfect tense clashes with \"reached\" and the past-tense narration around it.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.593Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Alem and Dereje have shared coffee ceremonies for thirty years, but today's silence reveals they've become strangers who still know each other's sorrow.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"주어 'cups'(복수) + 과거 서술(roasted, drifted, reached) → 'waited'(D)만 수·시제 모두 충족. A는 시제만 맞고 단수, C는 수만 맞고 현재완료, B는 둘 다 불일치. 삽입구 'each one ...'이 단수 유인 역할을 해 두 단계 판단이 필요하므로 medium 적합. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 정답 및 선택지 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"이 문항은 두 가지를 함께 판단해야 합니다. 하나는 삽입된 독립 분사구 'each one chipped…'를 건너뛰고 복수 주어 'cups'와 수를 일치시키는 것이고, 다른 하나는 과거 시제 서술에 맞추는 것입니다. 오답 중 A는 과거 시제라는 점에서, C는 복수형이라는 점에서 일부 근거를 갖고 있어 비교해야만 배제됩니다. B도 그럴듯한 오답으로 기능합니다. 따라서 medium 난이도에 적합합니다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-039","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-041","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"When the third round of coffee had been poured, Alemayehu leaned across the low table and placed a small object in front of Yohannes. The cup, with its rim of carved acacia leaves and the three tiny birds pressed into its base, ______ heavier in the boy's hands than any cup his mother owned. Yohannes did not hear the old man say the word \"bride\"; he heard only the silence of his own family's chipped tin mugs.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["were feeling","felt","feeling","have felt"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장의 주어는 단수 명사 \"The cup\"이고, \"with its rim ... base\"는 주어와 동사 사이에 끼어든 수식어구일 뿐이므로 빈칸에는 단수 주어와 일치하는 정동사가 와야 한다. 또 이 장면은 과거 시제로 서술되므로 B \"felt\"가 수와 시제를 모두 충족한다. A는 과거 시제이긴 하지만 바로 앞의 복수 명사 \"birds\"에 맞춘 복수형이라 주어와 일치하지 않는다. C는 분사이므로 문장에 정동사가 없게 된다. D는 복수형인 데다 현재완료여서 과거 서술과도 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this sentence is the singular noun \"The cup.\" The phrase \"with its rim ... base\" just sits between the subject and the verb, so the blank needs a finite verb that agrees with a singular subject. The scene is also told in the past tense, and B, \"felt,\" fits both the number and the tense. A is in the past tense, but it is plural, matching the nearby noun \"birds\" instead of the real subject. C is a participle, so it would leave the sentence with no main verb. D is plural and in the present perfect, which also clashes with the past-tense narration.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.593Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — At the coffee ceremony, elder Alemayehu gives Yohannes a carved cup meant for his bride, but the boy misunderstands it as an insult to his family's poverty.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"주어 \"The cup\"(단수)과 동사 사이에 \"with its rim ... birds pressed into its base\"라는 긴 수식어구가 끼어 있고, 서술이 과거 시제이므로 B \"felt\"가 유일한 정답임을 직접 검산함. A는 시제는 맞으나 가까운 복수 명사 \"birds\"에 이끌린 복수형, D는 정동사이긴 하나 복수·현재완료, C는 비정형 분사로 정동사 부재. 수 일치(수식어구 건너뛰기)+시제 확인의 두 단계 판단이 필요하고 오답 중 A·D가 부분적 타당성을 가지므로 medium에 부합. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 지정 정답과 글자 참조가 일치하고 모순 없음. 영어 해설에 한글 없음, 자연스러움. 지문은 창작으로 보이며 저작권 의심 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"주어와 동사 사이에 끼어든 수식구(birds가 유인 요소)와 시제를 함께 판단해야 하므로 medium 수준에 맞는다. 다만 'were feeling'은 진행형이라 상태동사 feel과 어울리지 않는다는 점도 약하게 작용한다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-041","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-042","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"The residents of the boarding house on Gumpendorfer Strasse had settled on no single story about Herr Kessler, the new tenant in the attic room. His habit of folding the morning newspaper into precise thirds, along with the faded regimental crest stitched inside a coat he never wore, ______ the widow on the second floor that he had once been an officer, though the porter insisted that before the war the quiet man had merely bound books.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["were convincing","convincing","had convinced","have convinced"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장의 주어는 단수 명사 'His habit'이고, 'along with ~ never wore' 구는 삽입된 수식어일 뿐 주어의 수를 바꾸지 않는다. 또 이 문장에는 아직 본동사가 없으므로 빈칸에는 정동사가 들어가야 한다. C의 'had convinced'는 정동사이고 수와 관계없이 쓸 수 있으며, 과거 시제의 서술 흐름과도 맞는다. A와 D는 정동사이지만 'crest'까지 주어로 착각해 복수형을 썼으므로 단수 주어와 일치하지 않는다. B의 'convincing'은 분사여서 문장에 본동사가 없게 된다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this sentence is the singular noun \"His habit.\" The phrase \"along with ... never wore\" is just an interrupting modifier, so it doesn't make the subject plural. The sentence also has no main verb yet, so the blank needs a finite verb. C, \"had convinced,\" is a finite verb that works with a singular subject and fits the story's past-tense narration. A and D are finite verbs, but they're plural, as if \"crest\" were part of the subject, so they don't agree with \"habit.\" B, \"convincing,\" is a participle, which would leave the sentence without a main verb.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.593Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — In the Vienna boarding house, new tenant Herr Kessler's quiet background sparks theories among residents about who he was before the war changed everything.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"주어 'His habit'(단수)과 'along with ... never wore' 삽입구를 분리해 수 일치 판단 + 본동사 필요 여부 확인의 두 단계 문항. C 'had convinced'만 단수 주어와 일치하는 정동사이며 과거 서술과 부합. A·D는 'crest' 근접 복수 함정, B는 비정동사 함정으로 오답 설계 적절. 한·영 해설 모두 정답 및 선택지 참조가 일치하고 모순 없음. 지문은 창작으로 저작권 문제 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"'along with' 삽입구가 복수 주어로 착각하게 만드는 함정이고, 정동사 여부까지 함께 판단해야 하므로 두 단계 판단이 필요한 중간 난이도에 맞는다. 정답은 C 하나뿐이다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-042","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-043","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"When Prospector James pressed the golden locket into Mara's palm, she did not thank him. The locket, its delicate chain and engraved lid gleaming like the very ore her husband had failed to find in three successive claims, ______ to her less a gift than a reminder of the debts piling up at the general store.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["seem","seeming","were seeming","seemed"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장의 주어는 단수 명사 'The locket'이고, 그 뒤의 'its delicate chain ... claims'는 삽입된 독립 분사구이므로 빈칸에는 주어와 수가 일치하는 정동사가 필요하다. D는 단수 주어와 맞고 앞 문장의 과거 시제 서술(pressed, did not thank)과도 맞으므로 정답이다. A와 C는 정동사이지만 복수형이어서 삽입구 속 'chain and lid'나 'claims'에 끌린 오답이다. B는 분사여서 문장에 정동사가 없게 된다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this sentence is the singular noun \"The locket.\" The phrase \"its delicate chain ... three successive claims\" is an absolute phrase inserted between the subject and the verb. That means the blank needs a main verb that agrees with a singular subject. D works because it is singular and keeps the past tense of the narration (\"pressed,\" \"did not thank\"). A and C are main verbs, but they're plural forms that agree with \"chain and lid\" or \"claims\" from the inserted phrase, not with the real subject. B is a participle, so choosing it would leave the sentence without a main verb.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.593Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Prospector James gifts a young miner's wife a golden locket, but she interprets it as mockery of her husband's failed claims and their mounting debt.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"주어 'The locket'(단수) 뒤에 긴 독립 분사구('its delicate chain and engraved lid gleaming ... claims')가 삽입되어 있고, 빈칸은 주절의 정동사 자리. D 'seemed'는 단수 주어와 일치하고 앞 문장의 과거 시제(pressed, did not thank)와도 일치하므로 정답 확인. A 'seem'은 현재 복수형, C 'were seeming'은 복수형이자 상태동사의 어색한 진행형, B는 분사라 정동사 부재. 한·영 해설 모두 같은 결론과 글자 참조를 가지며 모순 없음. 영어 해설은 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 난이도: 삽입구를 건너뛰어 진짜 주어를 찾는 것과 시제 확인의 두 단계가 필요하며, A·C가 삽입구의 복수 명사에 끌리는 오답으로 기능하므로 medium에 적합. 저작권 의심 없음, 사실 오류 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"긴 독립 분사구가 단수 주어와 동사 사이에 끼어 있어 수 일치와 정동사 여부를 두 단계로 판단해야 한다. 복수 명사(chain and lid, claims)가 주의를 흩뜨리는 장치로 들어가 있어 medium 난이도에 맞다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-043","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-044","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"When Karim appeared unannounced in the doorway of the tannery's back room, Yusuf was halfway through his bowl of lentils and did not rise. The smell of lime and soaking hides, which had clung to both boys' clothes through every summer of their childhood, ______ the moment Karim set down his bag and said he had sold his share of his father's workshop and come home for good.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["seemed to thicken","seem to thicken","seeming to thicken","to have seemed to thicken"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장의 주어는 단수 명사 'The smell'이고, 'which ... childhood' 관계절은 주어와 동사 사이에 끼어든 삽입절이므로 빈칸에는 단수 주어와 일치하는 정동사가 들어가야 한다. 또한 이 이야기는 과거 시제(appeared, was, set, said)로 서술되므로 A의 'seemed'가 수와 시제 모두 맞는다. B의 'seem'은 정동사이긴 하지만 바로 앞의 복수 명사 'hides'나 'clothes'에 잘못 일치한 복수형이고 현재 시제라 시제도 어긋난다. C의 분사와 D의 부정사는 정동사가 아니어서 문장에 본동사가 없게 된다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this sentence is the singular noun \"The smell.\" The clause \"which had clung ... childhood\" just interrupts the sentence between the subject and its verb, so the blank needs a finite verb that agrees with a singular subject. The story is also told in the past tense (appeared, was, set, said), so choice A, \"seemed,\" fits in both number and tense. Choice B is a finite verb, but it's plural: it agrees with nearby nouns like \"hides\" or \"clothes\" instead of the real subject, and it's in the present tense. Choice C (a participle) and choice D (an infinitive) aren't finite verbs, so either one would leave the sentence without a main verb.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.593Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Karim arrives unannounced at his childhood friend's tannery meal, carrying news that forces Yusuf to confront whether they can return to who they were.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"주어 'The smell'(단수)과 동사 사이에 'which had clung ... childhood' 관계절이 삽입된 구조. 빈칸에는 과거 시제 단수 정동사가 필요하므로 A 'seemed to thicken'이 유일하게 적합함. B는 인접 복수 명사(hides/clothes)에 끌린 수 불일치+현재 시제, C·D는 비정형 동사라 본동사 부재. 한·영 해설 모두 정답과 선택지 참조가 일치하며 모순 없음. 삽입절 너머 주어 찾기 + 시제 확인의 두 단계 판단이 요구되고 B가 근접 일치 함정으로 작동하므로 medium에 부합. 지문은 창작 서사로 저작권 우려 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"이 문항은 단수 주어와 동사 사이에 긴 삽입절과 복수 명사(hides, clothes)를 넣어 주어-동사 일치와 과거 시제를 묻는 전형적인 medium 문항이다. B는 그럴듯한 함정이지만, 정동사가 아닌 C와 D는 비교적 쉽게 배제된다. 그래도 표준 SAT medium 범위 안에 든다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-044","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-046","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Michael had borrowed the rake from Mr. Kowalski one October afternoon, carrying it down the stoop's worn boards with a promise to bring it back by Saturday. Six winters later, the rake, along with the apologies he had rehearsed each time he passed the old man's door, ______ untouched in the corner of the shed, its tines rusted the color of dried leaves.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["were left","have stayed","stayed","stay"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장의 주어는 단수 명사 'the rake'이고, 'along with the apologies...'는 삽입된 수식어구라서 동사의 수에 영향을 주지 않는다. 또 지문 전체가 과거 시제(had borrowed, passed)로 서술되므로 동사도 과거형이어야 한다. 단수 주어와 과거 시제를 모두 만족하는 것은 C 'stayed'이다. A는 과거 시제지만 복수형 'were'이므로 틀리고, B는 복수형이면서 현재완료라 과거 서술과 맞지 않는다. D는 복수 현재형이라 수와 시제가 모두 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this sentence is the singular noun \"the rake.\" The phrase \"along with the apologies...\" is just an interrupting modifier, so it doesn't change the number of the verb. The passage is also told in the past tense (had borrowed, passed), so the verb needs to be in the past tense too. Choice C, \"stayed,\" is the only option that fits both a singular subject and the past-tense narration. A is past tense, but \"were\" is plural; B is a plural present perfect that clashes with the past-tense narration; and D is a plural present-tense form, so it's wrong on both number and tense.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.593Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Across the stoop's worn boards, young Michael borrows a rake from aging Mr. Kowalski and keeps it through six winters, never finding the courage to return it.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"주어 'the rake'(단수) + 'along with...' 삽입구 처리 + 과거 시제 서술이라는 두 단계 판단 구조. A/B/D는 모두 복수형이라 C만 단수 주어와 일치하며, 과거 시제 서술과도 부합한다. 해설(한·영)은 정답과 글자 참조가 일치하고 모순이 없으며 영어 해설에 한글이 없다. 다만 오답 3개가 모두 수 불일치로 한 번에 배제되어 '시제' 판단은 보조적 단서에 그친다는 점에서 상위 medium보다는 전형적 medium 수준이다."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"주어-동사 수 일치(along with 삽입구 함정)와 과거 시제 확인을 모두 거쳐야 하는 두 단계 판단 문항이다. A는 시제 근거가, B·D는 각각 부분적인 근거가 있어 오답 설계가 적절하다. 'stayed'는 수에 따라 형태가 바뀌지 않는 형태이지만, 해설의 설명은 그래도 타당하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-046","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-047","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"The matatu lurched away from the stage on Moi Avenue, its speakers thumping, and Kamau recognized the man climbing aboard before he recognized the reason his chest had tightened. It was Otieno, who had shared his desk at the insurance office for six years, and beside him was a woman in a green headscarf, her hand resting lightly on his arm in the way Kamau's own wife once rested hers on his. Pressing his shoulder against the cold window and pretending to study the traffic outside, ______ while the woman laughed at something Otieno said and neither of them glanced toward the back row.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["the face of his former colleague was something Kamau watched in the smudged glass,","Kamau's eyes followed his former colleague's reflection in the smudged glass,","the smudged glass held a reflection of his former colleague for Kamau to watch,","Kamau watched his former colleague's reflection in the smudged glass,"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"문장 앞의 분사구 'Pressing his shoulder ... and pretending to study the traffic'은 어깨를 창문에 기대고 바깥 교통을 보는 척하는 사람, 즉 Kamau를 수식하므로 쉼표 바로 뒤에는 주어 Kamau가 와야 한다. D는 Kamau를 주어로 두어 수식 관계가 정확하다. B는 Kamau를 언급하지만 주어가 'Kamau's eyes'라서 눈이 어깨를 기대고 척하는 것이 되어 어색하다. A는 동료의 얼굴이, C는 유리창이 그 행동을 하는 것처럼 되어 수식어가 잘못 연결된다.","explanationEn":"The introductory phrase \"Pressing his shoulder against the cold window and pretending to study the traffic outside\" describes someone who leans and pretends, which is Kamau, so the subject right after the comma has to be Kamau himself. D does this, so the modifier attaches correctly. B is tempting because it mentions Kamau, but its subject is \"Kamau's eyes,\" and eyes can't press a shoulder or pretend. A makes the colleague's face the one doing the action, and C makes the glass do it, so both leave the modifier dangling.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.593Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On the matatu, Kamau's former colleague boards with a woman who could be his wife from the life he abandoned, and neither acknowledges the other's existence.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"Dangling-modifier item. Only D places Kamau as the subject after the participial phrase; B (\"Kamau's eyes\") is the classic possessive trap, A and C make the face/glass the agent. Korean and English explanations agree, reference correct letters, and are accurate. Original-looking prose, no copyright concern. Medium-appropriate."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"현수 수식어 문항. 정답 D 맞음. B(소유격 함정)가 그럴듯한 오답이고, A와 C는 수동적·우회적 구문이라 배제하기 쉽다. 중간 난이도로 적절하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-047","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-048","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"The depot sat so high in the pass that snow lingered on the tracks well into April. Javier had come there with his mother and two younger sisters intending to stay only until the road below reopened. Limping across the platform with one paw held off the frozen boards, ______ That night the family made room for it beside the stove, and by the time the road cleared, no one spoke of leaving.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["the stray dog caught Javier's eye just as the last train of the evening pulled away.","Javier noticed the stray dog just as the last train of the evening pulled away.","the stray dog, catching Javier's eye just as the last train of the evening pulled away.","the stray dog's thin frame caught Javier's eye just as the last train of the evening pulled away."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"도입 분사구 \"Limping ... boards\"의 의미상 주어는 다리를 저는 개여야 하므로 주절 주어는 'the stray dog'여야 하며, 동시에 문장에는 정동사가 있어야 한다. A는 주어 'the stray dog'와 정동사 'caught'를 모두 갖추어 정답이다. B는 정동사가 있지만 절뚝이는 주체가 Javier가 되어 수식어가 잘못 연결된다. C는 주어는 맞지만 'catching'이 분사여서 정동사가 없는 불완전한 문장이 된다. D는 정동사는 있으나 주어가 'thin frame'(마른 몸)이 되어 몸이 앞발을 들고 절뚝인다는 비논리적 수식이 된다.","explanationEn":"The opening phrase \"Limping across the platform with one paw held off the frozen boards\" has to describe the limping dog, so the main clause needs \"the stray dog\" as its subject. The sentence also needs a finite verb. Choice A has both: the subject \"the stray dog\" and the verb \"caught,\" so it's correct. Choice B has a proper verb, but it makes Javier the one limping, which is a dangling modifier. Choice C has the right subject, but \"catching\" is a participle, so the sentence has no main verb and becomes a fragment. Choice D has a finite verb, but its subject is the dog's \"thin frame,\" which illogically says the frame was limping with a paw held up.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.593Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — At the mountain depot, Javier adopts a dog limping through the station, and his family's temporary shelter becomes permanent in ways no one anticipated.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"도입 분사구 \"Limping ... with one paw held off\" 의 의미상 주어는 개여야 하고 주절에 정동사가 필요함. A만 'the stray dog' + 'caught'를 갖춤. B는 현수수식어, C는 정동사 없는 단편, D는 소유격 'thin frame'이 주어가 되어 비논리적. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 선택지 글자와 결론이 일치하며 정확함. 두 단계 판단(수식어 논리 + 문장 완결성)과 그럴듯한 오답 구성으로 medium에 적합. 지문은 창작물로 저작권 우려 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"현수 수식어 문제와 정동사 유무 판단을 함께 요구한다. B와 D는 각각 그럴듯한 근거가 있어 비교해야 배제된다. 표준 medium 수준이다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-048","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-049","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"On the rooftop, where the monsoon rain drummed against the tin awning, Priya kept the vigil her mother had asked of her. The promise to wait, whispered to her mother and her two aunts over the sputtering wicks of the oil lamps, ______ heavier now that the letter from her estranged father lay damp in her lap, its final line insisting that she choose before the rains ended.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["seem","seemed","were seeming","seeming"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장의 주어는 단수 명사 'The promise'이고, 'whispered ... oil lamps'는 주어를 꾸미는 분사구이므로 빈칸에는 단수 주어와 일치하는 정동사가 필요하다. 지문 전체가 과거 시제(drummed, kept, lay)로 서술되므로 B의 'seemed'가 수와 시제 모두 맞다. A의 'seem'은 바로 앞의 복수 명사(aunts, lamps)에 끌린 복수형이자 현재형이라 틀린다. C의 'were seeming'은 과거 시제지만 복수 동사라 단수 주어와 맞지 않는다. D의 'seeming'은 분사여서 문장에 정동사가 없게 된다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this sentence is the singular noun \"The promise.\" The phrase \"whispered ... oil lamps\" is a participial modifier describing that subject, so the blank needs a finite verb that agrees with a singular subject. The whole passage is told in the past tense (drummed, kept, lay), so B, \"seemed,\" fits in both number and tense. A, \"seem,\" is plural and present tense; it agrees with the nearby plural nouns (aunts, lamps) instead of the real subject. C, \"were seeming,\" is past tense, but it's plural, so it doesn't agree with \"promise.\" D, \"seeming,\" is a participle, which would leave the sentence without a main verb.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.593Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — During the monsoon vigil on the rooftop, Priya's mother makes her promise to wait, but the letter from her estranged father arrives now demanding she decide.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"주어 'The promise'(단수) + 긴 분사 수식구(복수 명사 aunts, lamps로 끝남) 뒤 정동사 자리. 과거 서술(drummed, kept, lay)이므로 'seemed'가 수·시제 모두 적합. A는 근접 명사 끌림 오답, C는 시제는 맞지만 복수, D는 비정형으로 정동사 부재. 수 일치 + 시제 확인의 두 단계 판단이 필요하고 오답 구성도 기준에 부합하여 medium 적합. 해설 한·영 결론 및 글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"주어와 동사 사이에 긴 분사구가 끼어 있고 그 안에 복수 명사(aunts, lamps)가 있어 수 일치 판단이 흐려진다. 여기에 과거 시제 문맥까지 확인해야 하므로 두 단계 판단이 필요하다. A와 C는 각각 수나 시제 중 하나에서만 걸러지므로 medium 난이도에 맞다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-m-049","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-051","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"medium","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- The Breaker Room is a 2019 novel by South Korean writer Han Ji-woo.\n- Its main character, Min, is a 28-year-old accountant who labels every drawer and shelf in her Seoul apartment.\n- In the novel's central scene, a citywide blackout leaves Min's apartment complex dark for six hours.\n- Searching for candles by touch, Min opens an unlabeled box that she had taped shut years earlier.\n- The box holds letters from an older brother whom Min has told her coworkers she never had.\n- Reviewers have praised Han's spare, precise prose.","question":"The student wants to explain how the novel's central scene upsets the main character's carefully arranged life. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["In The Breaker Room, a 2019 novel by South Korean writer Han Ji-woo, Min is a 28-year-old accountant living in Seoul, and reviewers have praised the novel's spare, precise prose.","In The Breaker Room, Min is an accountant who labels every drawer and shelf in her Seoul apartment, a habit that Han Ji-woo describes in spare, precise prose.","In The Breaker Room, Min keeps a taped box of letters from an older brother, though she has told her coworkers that she never had a brother.","In The Breaker Room, Min, who labels every drawer and shelf she owns, must search by touch during a blackout and ends up opening a long-sealed, unlabeled box of letters from a brother she has denied having."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"목표는 중심 장면이 Min의 정돈된 삶을 어떻게 흔드는지 설명하는 것이므로, Min의 정돈 습관(라벨)과 정전 장면, 그리고 그 결과 드러나는 숨긴 과거를 함께 연결해야 한다. D는 이 세 요소를 모두 결합해 정답이다. A는 작품 기본 정보와 문체 평가만 제시하고 중심 장면은 다루지 않는다. B는 Min의 정돈 습관은 언급하지만 그것이 흔들리는 장면이 없다. C는 숨긴 과거(편지)는 언급하지만 정전 장면과 정돈된 삶과의 대비가 빠져 있다.","explanationEn":"Your goal is to explain how the central scene upsets Min's carefully arranged life, so you need to connect three things: her orderly habits (the labels), the blackout scene, and the hidden past it exposes. D combines all three, so it's the correct answer. A gives only basic facts about the novel and a comment on its prose; it never mentions the central scene. B describes Min's labeling habit but leaves out the scene that disrupts it. C mentions the hidden letters but not the blackout, and it doesn't contrast them with her orderly life.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.593Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — In the Seoul apartment complex, young Min's carefully organized life erupts when the power fails and she discovers her carefully hidden past in the darkness.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"D만이 정돈 습관(라벨)–정전 장면(촉각 탐색)–숨긴 과거(형제 편지) 세 요소를 연결해 '중심 장면이 정돈된 삶을 흔든다'는 목표를 충족한다. B(정돈 습관만)·C(숨긴 과거만)는 부분적으로 관련 있어 비교가 필요하고, A는 기본 정보·문체 평가로 그럴듯한 오답이다. 노트와 선택지 간 사실 불일치 없음(D의 \"every drawer and shelf she owns\"는 노트의 아파트 서술과 사실상 일치). 한국어·영어 해설 모두 D를 일관되게 뒷받침하며 글자 참조 정확, 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 소설·작가는 허구적 설정으로 저작권 문제 없음. 난이도 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"가상의 소설로 보이며 저작권 문제는 없음. D만 중심 장면(정전), 정돈 습관, 숨겨온 과거가 드러나는 일을 모두 담고 있음. B와 C는 일부 요소만 갖춘 그럴듯한 오답이고 A는 비교적 쉽게 배제됨. 중간 난이도로 적절함. D가 다른 선택지보다 눈에 띄게 길어서 길이만 보고 정답을 고를 여지가 조금 있음.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-051","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-052","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"medium","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- \"The Upriver Letter\" is a 2019 short story by novelist Clara Vesey.\n- In the story, a steamboat clerk named Samuel travels upriver for three days to mail a single letter for his employer, Mr. Hollis.\n- Samuel guards the sealed envelope carefully, sleeping with it under his pillow.\n- When he reaches the post office, he learns that Mr. Hollis had sent a telegram instructing the postmaster to return the letter unsent.\n- Vesey has said the story explores how loyalty can be exploited by those who receive it.","question":"The student wants to emphasize the contrast between Samuel's devotion to his task and the outcome of his journey. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Although Samuel guards Mr. Hollis's letter so closely that he sleeps with it under his pillow, he arrives at the post office to find that Mr. Hollis had already arranged for it to be returned unsent.","Although Samuel is only a steamboat clerk, he travels upriver for three days to mail a single letter for Mr. Hollis, sleeping with the sealed envelope under his pillow.","Although Clara Vesey is known as a novelist, her 2019 short story \"The Upriver Letter\" follows a clerk who learns at a post office that his employer's letter will be returned unsent.","Although \"The Upriver Letter\" centers on a clerk's three-day journey to mail a letter, Vesey has said the story explores how loyalty can be exploited by those who receive it."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"목표는 Samuel이 임무에 보인 헌신과 여정의 결과를 대조하는 것이다. A는 편지를 베개 밑에 두고 잘 만큼 지켰다는 헌신과, 고용주가 이미 반송을 지시해 두었다는 결과를 함께 제시하므로 정답이다. B는 헌신만 보여 주고 여정의 결과가 빠져 있다. C는 결과는 언급하지만 대조의 축이 작가의 경력(소설가 대 단편)이라 Samuel의 헌신이 드러나지 않는다. D는 줄거리와 작가의 주제 의도를 대조할 뿐, Samuel의 헌신과 실제 결과를 구체적으로 맞세우지 않는다.","explanationEn":"Your goal is to contrast Samuel's devotion to his task with how his journey turns out. A does both: it shows his devotion (he sleeps with the letter under his pillow) and the outcome (Mr. Hollis had already arranged for the letter to be returned unsent), so A is correct. B shows only his devotion and leaves out the outcome. C mentions the outcome, but its contrast is about Vesey's career (novelist vs. short story), so Samuel's devotion never shows up. D contrasts the plot with the author's stated theme instead of setting Samuel's devotion against what actually happens.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.593Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Steamboat clerk Samuel journeys upriver for three days to mail a single letter, only to learn his employer never intended to send it.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"A alone pairs Samuel's devotion (sleeping with the letter under his pillow) with the outcome (letter returned unsent). B gives devotion only; D gives theme vs. plot without the outcome; C shifts the contrast to the author's career. Distractors require comparison; difficulty appropriate for medium. Fictional source, no copyright concern."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"A만 헌신과 결과를 모두 담음. B는 헌신만, C·D는 대조 축이 다름. 오답 각각에 부분 근거가 있어 medium 난이도에 적합.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-052","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-053","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"medium","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- \"The Quiet Shaft\" is a 1998 short story by American writer Maren Holloway.\n- The story is set in a Colorado coal-mining camp in the 1910s.\n- Miners of that era carried canaries underground; a bird that fell silent or sick warned of dangerous gas.\n- In the story's central scene, ten-year-old Billy asks his father why the camp's canaries no longer sing.\n- By this point in the story, the camp's adults have stopped talking openly about the mine's worsening conditions.","question":"The student wants to explain to an audience unfamiliar with the story why the central scene matters. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["In Maren Holloway's 1998 short story \"The Quiet Shaft,\" ten-year-old Billy asks his father a question in a Colorado coal-mining camp of the 1910s.","In Maren Holloway's \"The Quiet Shaft,\" ten-year-old Billy's question about the camp's silent canaries puts into words a danger that the adults around him have stopped discussing openly.","In Maren Holloway's \"The Quiet Shaft,\" the canaries that Billy asks about were carried underground by miners because a silent or sick bird warned of dangerous gas.","In Maren Holloway's \"The Quiet Shaft,\" Billy asks why the canaries no longer sing, and the adults of the camp have stopped talking about the mine."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"목표는 소설을 모르는 독자에게 핵심 장면의 의미를 설명하는 것이다. B는 카나리아가 노래하지 않는다는 Billy의 질문(장면)과 어른들이 말하지 않게 된 위험(맥락)을 연결해 장면의 의미를 드러낸다. A는 작품 정보와 배경만 제시할 뿐 질문의 내용이나 의미가 없다. C는 카나리아의 역사적 기능을 정확히 설명하지만 어른들의 침묵과 연결하지 않아 장면의 의미를 설명하지 못한다. D는 두 사실을 나열만 하고 둘의 관계(아이가 금기된 진실을 말함)를 밝히지 않는다.","explanationEn":"Your goal is to show an unfamiliar audience why the central scene matters. B does this by connecting Billy's question about the silent canaries to the danger the adults no longer speak about, which reveals the scene's significance. A gives only publication and setting details and never says what Billy asks or why it matters. C accurately explains what canaries did in mines, but it doesn't tie that to the adults' silence, so the scene's meaning is still missing. D puts the two facts side by side without explaining how they relate, so it never shows that the child is saying out loud a truth the adults avoid.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.593Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — In the mining camp, ten-year-old Billy asks his father why the canaries no longer sing, noticing the truth adults have stopped speaking aloud.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 B 검산 확인: 장면(카나리아에 대한 질문)과 맥락(어른들의 침묵)을 연결해 '왜 중요한가'를 설명하는 유일한 선택지. C(카나리아의 기능만 설명)와 D(두 사실을 병렬 나열만 함)는 노트 내용상 정확하지만 의미 연결이 없어 비교를 통해서만 배제되고, A는 배경 정보만 제시해 말은 되지만 목표 미달 — medium 기준 충족. 작품·작가는 가상이나 SAT 관행상 허용되며, 카나리아 관련 역사적 사실은 정확함. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 선택지 글자 참조와 결론이 일치하고 영어 해설에 한글 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B만 장면(카나리아에 대한 질문)과 맥락(어른들의 침묵·위험)을 연결해 장면이 왜 중요한지 보여 준다. C와 D는 관련 정보를 일부 담고 있어서 비교해야만 배제되고, A는 질문 내용이 없어 비교적 쉽게 배제된다. medium 기준(오답 중 최소 2개가 부분 근거를 가짐)을 충족한다. 작품은 가상으로 보이며, 메모 안에서 완결되므로 문제없다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-053","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-054","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"medium","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- \"The Last Ledger\" is a 2019 short story by novelist Inès Marchand.\n- In the story, two collectors, Simone and Christiane, compete to buy an unpublished manuscript in Monsieur Leclerc's Paris bookshop.\n- Simone wants the manuscript because she believes it proves the author, Léon Duret, plagiarized his most famous novel.\n- Christiane wants the manuscript because she believes it proves Duret wrote that novel entirely alone.\n- By the story's end, the two women read the manuscript together and discover that both of their theories were wrong: Duret had secretly co-written the novel with his sister.","question":"The student wants to emphasize how the collectors' reasons for pursuing the manuscript differed. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["In Inès Marchand's \"The Last Ledger,\" Simone and Christiane compete in Monsieur Leclerc's bookshop for a manuscript that, they eventually learn, reveals Duret co-wrote his novel with his sister.","In Inès Marchand's \"The Last Ledger,\" Simone and Christiane both seek a manuscript by Léon Duret, and both of their theories about his famous novel turn out to be wrong.","In Inès Marchand's \"The Last Ledger,\" Simone seeks the manuscript to show that Duret plagiarized his famous novel, whereas Christiane seeks it to show that he wrote the novel alone.","In Inès Marchand's \"The Last Ledger,\" Simone and Christiane stop competing for Duret's manuscript and read it together, discovering a secret about his famous novel."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"목표는 두 수집가가 원고를 찾는 이유가 어떻게 달랐는지 강조하는 것이다. C는 Simone의 동기(표절 입증)와 Christiane의 동기(단독 집필 입증)를 'whereas'로 대조해 목표를 정확히 달성한다. A는 경쟁과 결말만 언급하고 각자의 이유는 없다. B는 두 사람이 이론을 가졌다는 점을 암시하지만 차이 대신 공통점(둘 다 틀림)을 강조한다. D는 둘이 화해해 함께 원고를 읽는 결말에 초점을 맞추어 동기의 차이를 보여 주지 않는다.","explanationEn":"Your goal is to emphasize how the collectors' reasons for wanting the manuscript differed. C does this by setting Simone's motive (proving plagiarism) against Christiane's motive (proving sole authorship) with \"whereas.\" A mentions the competition and the ending but never gives either woman's reason. B hints that each had a theory, but it stresses what they share (both were wrong) instead of how they differ. D focuses on the two women reconciling and reading together, so it doesn't show their contrasting motives.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.594Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — In Monsieur Leclerc's bookshop, rival collectors Simone and Christiane battle over a rare manuscript until they realize they've been hunting for the same author's truth.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 C는 노트의 3·4번 항목을 'whereas'로 대조하여 목표(이유의 차이 강조)를 정확히 달성함. B는 '두 이론'을 언급해 부분적으로 그럴듯하고, A는 '경쟁'을 언급해 훑어 읽으면 혼동 가능하며, D는 결말 중심으로 오답임이 명확함. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 글자 참조와 결론이 일치하고 사실 오류 없음. 가상의 작품으로 저작권 문제 없음. 난이도는 medium 하한에 가까우나(정답이 비교적 명확), 오답 B·A의 부분적 근거가 있어 적합 판정."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"C만 두 동기를 whereas로 대조함. B는 '이론'을 언급해 부분 근거를 가진 매력적 오답이고, A·D도 노트 내용을 정확히 반영해 그럴듯함. 해설에서 D를 '화해'로 표현한 것은 약간의 해석이지만 결론에는 영향이 없음. 전형적인 중간 난이도이며, 쉬운 쪽에 가까움.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-054","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-055","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"medium","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- \"The Ferry Term\" is a short story by novelist Mairi Calder, published in 2019.\n- In the story, a teacher named Ailsa arrives to run the one-room school on a remote Scottish island.\n- On her first day, the island's young children whisper that she must be running from something on the mainland.\n- The children's rumors are a way of testing whether Ailsa will stay longer than the three teachers before her.\n- Calder has said she wanted the story to show how small communities protect themselves from loss.","question":"The student wants to explain the purpose behind the children's behavior toward the new teacher. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["In Mairi Calder's 2019 short story \"The Ferry Term,\" Ailsa arrives to run the one-room school on a remote Scottish island, where the young children whisper about her.","In Mairi Calder's short story \"The Ferry Term,\" the children whisper that Ailsa, who has come from the mainland, must be running from something there.","In Mairi Calder's short story \"The Ferry Term,\" which the author says shows how small communities protect themselves, a teacher named Ailsa comes to an island school.","In Mairi Calder's short story \"The Ferry Term,\" the island children spread rumors about Ailsa to find out whether she, unlike the three teachers before her, will remain."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"목표는 아이들이 왜 그렇게 행동하는지, 즉 행동의 목적을 설명하는 것입니다. D는 아이들이 소문을 퍼뜨린 사실과, 그 목적이 Ailsa가 이전 교사 세 명과 달리 섬에 남을지 알아보려는 데 있다는 점을 함께 제시하므로 목표를 이룹니다. B는 소문의 내용만 전할 뿐 왜 소문을 퍼뜨리는지는 말하지 않습니다. C는 공동체가 스스로를 지킨다는 작가의 말을 쓰지만 아이들의 행동과 연결하지 않고, A는 배경과 아이들이 수군거린다는 사실만 소개합니다.","explanationEn":"Your goal is to explain why the children behave the way they do, meaning the purpose of their behavior. D accomplishes this because it states both that the children spread rumors and that their purpose is to find out whether Ailsa will stay, unlike the three teachers before her. B gives only what the rumor says and never explains why the children spread it. C uses the author's comment about communities protecting themselves but doesn't connect it to the children's behavior, and A only sets the scene and mentions that the children whisper.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.594Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — When teacher Ailsa introduces herself to the island school, young children spread rumors that she's running from something, testing whether she'll stay.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 D 검증: 아이들의 소문(행동)과 '남을지 알아보려는' 목적(4번째 노트)을 함께 제시하므로 목표에 부합. B는 소문의 내용만, C는 작가의 주제 언급만(아이들 행동과 미연결), A는 배경 소개만으로 목적 설명 없음. B와 C가 부분적으로 관련 있어 비교가 필요한 medium 수준에 적합. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 D를 일관되게 뒷받침하고 글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 가상의 작가·작품으로 저작권 우려 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"D만 노트 4(목적)를 담고 있다. C는 '보호'라는 주제를 넣어 그럴듯하게 유인하고 B는 행동 자체만 담고 있어, 둘을 비교해야 배제할 수 있으므로 medium에 맞다. 다만 목적 표지(\"to find out\")가 꽤 눈에 띄어 medium 중에서는 쉬운 편이다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-055","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-056","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"medium","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- \"The Dyer's Morning\" is a 2019 short story by Moroccan writer Nadia Fassi.\n- The story is set in a centuries-old tannery in Fez, where workers soak animal hides in stone vats of dye.\n- In one scene, a goat wanders into the vats during the busy morning rush.\n- Larbi, a veteran tanner, at first shouts at the goat and swings his wooden pole to drive it out.\n- Watching the goat stand calmly in a vat, its legs stained saffron yellow, Larbi lowers his pole and laughs quietly.\n- Critics have praised the story's vivid descriptions of color.","question":"The student wants to show how Larbi's attitude toward the goat develops over the course of the scene. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["In Fassi's story, Larbi shouts and swings his pole at a goat that has strayed into the vats, yet as he watches it stand calmly with saffron-stained legs, he lowers the pole and laughs quietly.","In Fassi's story, set in a centuries-old Fez tannery, Larbi shouts and swings his pole at a goat that has strayed into the vats during the busy morning rush.","In Fassi's story, Larbi watches a goat stand calmly with saffron-stained legs, a scene that reflects the vivid descriptions of color that critics have praised.","In Fassi's story, a goat strays into the stone vats of a centuries-old Fez tannery, where workers soak animal hides in dye during the busy morning rush."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문제의 목표는 장면 전체에서 Larbi의 태도가 어떻게 변하는지 보여 주는 것이므로, 처음 반응과 나중 반응이 함께 들어가야 합니다. A는 처음에 소리치며 막대를 휘두르던 모습과, 나중에 막대를 내리고 조용히 웃는 모습을 'yet'으로 이어 그 변화를 분명히 보여 주므로 정답입니다. B는 처음의 화난 반응만 담고 있어서 태도가 어떻게 바뀌는지는 드러나지 않습니다. C는 차분한 염소를 바라보는 장면과 색채에 대한 비평가들의 평가를 언급할 뿐, Larbi가 처음에 화를 냈다는 점도 나중에 웃었다는 점도 빠져 있습니다. D는 배경과 사건만 설명하고 Larbi의 반응은 전혀 다루지 않습니다.","explanationEn":"Your goal is to show how Larbi's attitude develops over the whole scene, so you need both his first reaction and his later one. Choice A is correct because it pairs his shouting and pole-swinging with his later choice to lower the pole and laugh quietly, and the word \"yet\" makes the shift clear. Choice B gives only his first, angry reaction, so you can't see his attitude change. Choice C mentions him watching the calm goat and the critics' praise for color, but it leaves out both his early anger and his later laugh. Choice D describes only the setting and the event and never mentions how Larbi reacts.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.594Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — At the tannery, a goat wanders into Larbi's vats during the morning rush, and his exasperated response softens into something like wonder.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"정답 A 검증: 노트의 '처음 소리치며 막대 휘두름'과 '막대를 내리고 조용히 웃음'을 모두 포함하고 'yet'으로 변화를 연결해 목표(태도 발전)를 유일하게 충족. B는 초기 반응만(부분 근거), C는 후반 장면만(부분 근거) 담아 비교 배제가 필요하고, D는 배경 설명으로 말은 되나 목표 불충족. 해설 한·영 모두 글자 참조·결론 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 가공 작가·작품이라 저작권 문제 없음. 난이도는 표준 rhetorical synthesis 중간 수준으로 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"B와 C가 각각 장면의 절반씩만 담고 있어 비교가 필요하다. D는 쉽게 배제된다. 다만 정답 A만 눈에 띄게 길고 'yet'이 들어 있어 단서가 될 수 있지만, 중간 난이도로는 허용 범위다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-056","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-057","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"medium","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- \"The Fourth-Floor Kitchen\" is a 2019 short story by Korean writer Han Mi-rae.\n- It is set in a crowded apartment complex in Seoul.\n- In the opening scene, neighbor Soo-jin whispers in the hallway that a newly arrived resident is \"hiding something.\"\n- By evening, the rumor has passed from door to door, spreading through the building like the smell of the newcomer's unfamiliar cooking.\n- Critics have noted that Han uses the image of drifting kitchen smells to show how gossip moves without anyone deciding to carry it.","question":"The student wants to explain the significance of a sensory image in the story to an audience unfamiliar with it. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["In Han Mi-rae's 2019 short story \"The Fourth-Floor Kitchen,\" set in a crowded Seoul apartment complex, a neighbor named Soo-jin whispers that a new resident is \"hiding something.\"","In Han Mi-rae's 2019 short story \"The Fourth-Floor Kitchen,\" a rumor spreads through a Seoul apartment building like the smell of a newcomer's cooking, an image critics say shows gossip moving without anyone choosing to carry it.","In Han Mi-rae's 2019 short story \"The Fourth-Floor Kitchen,\" a rumor started by Soo-jin passes from door to door by evening, reaching nearly every resident of a crowded Seoul apartment complex.","In Han Mi-rae's 2019 short story \"The Fourth-Floor Kitchen,\" critics have paid attention to how the opening scene takes place in the hallway of a crowded Seoul apartment complex."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"목표는 작품을 모르는 독자에게 감각적 이미지의 의미를 설명하는 것이므로, 소문이 요리 냄새처럼 퍼진다는 이미지와 그 이미지가 갖는 의미(누구도 의도하지 않아도 소문이 퍼짐)를 둘 다 담아야 한다. B는 작품 소개와 함께 이 두 요소를 모두 담고 있다. A는 수진의 속삭임만 전할 뿐 감각적 이미지가 없다. C는 소문이 퍼지는 과정은 말하지만 냄새 이미지와 그 의미가 빠져 있다. D는 비평가를 언급하지만 이미지가 아니라 배경에 대한 이야기를 한다.","explanationEn":"Your goal is to explain what a sensory image means, so the right sentence needs both the image (the rumor spreading like cooking smells) and what it means (gossip moves without anyone choosing to carry it). B gives both, and it also introduces the story for readers who don't know it. A only tells you about Soo-jin's whisper and never mentions any sensory image. C describes the rumor spreading, but it leaves out the smell image and what it means. D mentions critics, but it talks about the setting instead of the image.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.594Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — In the Seoul complex hallway, neighbor Soo-jin whispers that the new resident is hiding something, and the rumor spreads like the scent of unfamiliar cooking.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B만이 감각적 이미지(요리 냄새처럼 퍼지는 소문)와 그 의미(의도 없이 퍼지는 가십)를 함께 담고 작품 소개까지 포함하므로 정답 타당. A는 작품 소개·배경은 있으나 이미지 없음, C는 소문 확산 과정만 있고 냄새 이미지·의미 누락(또한 '거의 모든 주민'은 노트에 없는 확장), D는 비평가 언급만 있고 배경 이야기. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 결론·글자 참조 일치, 한글 혼입 없음. 가상 작품으로 사실 오류·저작권 문제 없음. 오답 중 A·C가 부분적 근거를 가져 비교가 필요하며 D도 말이 되므로 medium 적합(다소 평이한 편이나 표준 범위)."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["too_easy","eliminated:2"],"note":"냄새라는 감각적 이미지를 언급하는 선택지가 B 하나뿐이라, 'sensory image'라는 키워드만 찾아도 바로 답이 나온다. 오답들이 냄새 이미지는 넣고 그 의미를 빠뜨리거나, 의미만 넣고 이미지는 빠뜨리는 식으로 부분적인 근거를 갖고 있지 않아 비교할 필요가 없다. 그래서 medium 기준(두 단계 판단)에 미치지 못한다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-057","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-058","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"medium","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- Southern Wind is a 2019 novel by Argentine author Lucía Marín Ortega.\n- The novel is set on an isolated sheep ranch in Patagonia.\n- Its protagonist, Elena, is a shepherd who has never traveled beyond the ranch.\n- During lambing season, Elena meets Tomás, a traveling veterinarian who tells her about the cities where he has worked.\n- After Tomás leaves the ranch, Elena begins setting aside her wages for a bus ticket to Buenos Aires.","question":"The student wants to describe how a particular encounter in the novel affects the protagonist. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["In Marín Ortega's Southern Wind, shepherd Elena meets a traveling veterinarian named Tomás during lambing season on an isolated Patagonian sheep ranch.","In Marín Ortega's Southern Wind, shepherd Elena, who has never traveled beyond the ranch, spends lambing season on an isolated sheep ranch in Patagonia.","In Marín Ortega's Southern Wind, after a traveling veterinarian describes the cities where he has worked, shepherd Elena starts saving her wages for a bus ticket to Buenos Aires.","In Marín Ortega's 2019 novel Southern Wind, Tomás is a traveling veterinarian who has worked in several cities before arriving at a Patagonian ranch."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"목표는 만남이 주인공에게 미친 영향을 설명하는 것이므로, 만남(수의사가 도시 이야기를 함)과 그 결과(엘레나가 버스표를 위해 돈을 모음)를 연결해야 한다. C가 두 메모를 결합해 이를 보여 준다. A는 만남 자체만 서술하고 엘레나에게 생긴 변화는 빠져 있다. B는 엘레나의 배경과 장소만 제시해 만남이 아예 등장하지 않는다. D는 토마스에 초점을 맞춰 주인공에게 미친 영향을 말하지 않는다.","explanationEn":"Your goal is to show how an encounter affects the protagonist, so you need to connect the meeting (Tomás describing cities) with its result (Elena saving for a bus ticket). Choice C combines those two notes and does exactly that. Choice A describes the meeting itself but never says how Elena changes. Choice B gives Elena's background and the setting but leaves out the encounter entirely. Choice D is about Tomás, not about any effect on Elena.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.594Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On the Patagonian ranch, shepherd Elena meets a traveling veterinarian in the lambing season, and their brief connection reshapes what she imagines possible.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"C는 만남(토마스의 도시 이야기)과 결과(버스표를 위해 임금 저축)를 인과적으로 연결한 유일한 선택지로 정답이 명확하다. A는 만남 자체를 서술해 부분적으로 목표에 부합하고, D는 토마스·도시 정보를 담아 그럴듯하며, B는 배경만 제시해 가장 약한 오답이다. 해설(한·영)은 결론과 선택지 참조가 일치하고 모순 없음. D의 \"several cities\"는 메모의 \"cities\"에서 나온 가벼운 추론 수준으로 문제 없음. 난이도는 표준 SAT rhetorical synthesis 중간 수준에 해당하나, 결과를 담은 선택지가 하나뿐이어서 다소 쉬운 쪽 경계에 있음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"가상의 소설로 보이며 저작권 문제는 없다. 오답 A와 D는 만남을 다루고 B는 주인공을 다루므로 각각 부분적인 근거를 가진다. 정답인 C만 만남과 그 영향을 연결한다. 전형적인 중간 난이도 문항이다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-058","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-059","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"medium","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- \"The Third Pour\" is a 2019 short story by Ethiopian writer Hiwot Alemu.\n- The story takes place during a coffee ceremony, in which coffee is traditionally served in three rounds: abol, tona, and baraka.\n- During the first round, Semira is handed a letter from her eldest son, Dawit, who disappeared three seasons earlier.\n- Dawit wrote the letter the week before he vanished, but a cousin forgot it in a coat pocket for months.\n- Semira does not open the letter until baraka, the ceremony's final round, whose name means \"blessing.\"\n- Critics argue that the story's central idea is that love can arrive late and still be fully received.","question":"The student wants to explain how the way the scene's events are arranged supports the story's central idea. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["In Hiwot Alemu's 2019 short story \"The Third Pour,\" Semira is handed a letter from her eldest son, Dawit, who disappeared three seasons earlier, during the first round of a coffee ceremony.","In \"The Third Pour,\" the letter Semira receives was written by Dawit the week before he vanished, but it was delayed for months because a cousin forgot it in a coat pocket.","In \"The Third Pour,\" a story set during a three-round coffee ceremony of abol, tona, and baraka, critics find the central idea that love can arrive late and still be fully received.","In \"The Third Pour,\" Semira holds her son's long-delayed letter unopened until baraka, the ceremony's final \"blessing\" round, suggesting that love arriving late can still be fully received."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"정답은 D이다. D는 Semira가 편지를 마지막 라운드인 baraka('축복')까지 열지 않는다는 사건 배치를 '늦게 도착한 사랑도 온전히 받아들여질 수 있다'는 중심 주제와 직접 연결한다. A는 작가·작품과 편지를 받는 장면만 소개할 뿐 주제와 연결하지 않는다. B는 편지가 늦어진 이유를 설명하지만 그 지연이 어떻게 주제를 뒷받침하는지는 말하지 않는다. C는 주제와 의식의 세 라운드를 모두 언급하지만, 사건의 배치(편지를 언제 여는지)가 주제를 어떻게 뒷받침하는지는 설명하지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The answer is D. D links how the scene is arranged, with Semira waiting until baraka, the final \"blessing\" round, to open the letter, to the story's central idea that late-arriving love can still be fully received. A introduces the author and the moment Semira gets the letter, but it never connects anything to the theme. B explains why the letter was delayed, but it doesn't say how that delay supports the central idea. C mentions both the theme and the ceremony's three rounds, but it doesn't show how the order of events, especially when Semira opens the letter, supports that theme.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.594Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — At the coffee ceremony, Semira receives a letter from her eldest son, written before he disappeared three seasons ago, and must decide what to do with delayed love.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 D 검산: 과제는 '사건 배치(편지를 언제 여는지)가 중심 주제를 어떻게 뒷받침하는가'를 설명하는 것. D만이 '마지막 라운드 baraka(축복)까지 열지 않음'이라는 배치를 '늦게 온 사랑도 온전히 받아들여짐'이라는 주제와 명시적으로 연결함. A는 사건만 서술(주제 없음), B는 지연 원인만 서술(주제 없음), C는 주제와 세 라운드를 모두 언급하지만 사건 배치와의 연결이 없어 가장 강한 오답으로 기능. 오답 중 B·C가 부분적 근거를 가지며 A도 말이 됨 → medium 적합. 한국어·영어 해설 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 가상의 작품이지만 노트의 커피 의식 3라운드(abol, tona, baraka) 및 baraka='축복' 의미는 실제와 부합하여 사실 오류 없음. 저작권 우려 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답은 D뿐이다. 오답 B와 C는 각각 지연과 주제·의식 구조를 다뤄 부분적으로 맞는 근거를 갖고 있어, medium 난이도로 적절하다. 다만 C는 문장 구조가 약간 어색하다(\"a story set during..., critics find\"). 가상의 작품으로 보인다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-059","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-060","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"medium","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- \"The Second Horn\" is a short story by the fictional author Mira Hollenbeck, published in 2019.\n- In the story, Dietrich is the reserved French horn player in a village brass band.\n- A newcomer named Klaus joins the band and plays the tuba without ever mentioning his past.\n- Band members whisper that Klaus once performed professionally with an orchestra in Berlin.\n- Dietrich begins to wonder what silence or loss led Klaus to leave the city for a small village.\n- Hollenbeck has said the story explores how people carry unspoken histories.","question":"The student wants to present the central mystery that occupies Dietrich's thoughts in the story. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["In Hollenbeck's \"The Second Horn,\" Dietrich, hearing rumors that newcomer Klaus once played professionally in Berlin, wonders what silence drove Klaus to a small village.","In Hollenbeck's \"The Second Horn,\" Dietrich, a reserved French horn player, plays in a village brass band that newcomer Klaus joins on tuba.","In Hollenbeck's \"The Second Horn,\" band members whisper that newcomer Klaus once performed with an orchestra in Berlin.","In Hollenbeck's \"The Second Horn,\" published in 2019, the author explores how people carry unspoken histories."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"목표는 Dietrich가 마음속에 품은 '수수께끼'를 제시하는 것이므로, 소문(베를린 경력)과 그에 따른 Dietrich의 의문(왜 마을로 왔는가)을 결합해야 한다. A는 두 메모를 연결해 Dietrich가 궁금해하는 내용을 정확히 제시한다. B는 인물과 배경만 소개할 뿐 의문이 없다. C는 소문은 담았지만 Dietrich의 의문이 빠져 수수께끼가 그의 생각임을 보여주지 못한다. D는 작가의 주제 의도로, 구체적 수수께끼를 제시하지 않는다.","explanationEn":"Your goal is to present the mystery in Dietrich's mind, so you need both the rumor about Klaus's Berlin career and Dietrich's question about why Klaus came to the village. A connects these two notes and states exactly what Dietrich wonders. B only introduces the characters and setting, with no mystery. C includes the rumor but leaves out Dietrich's wondering, so it never shows the mystery as his thought. D gives the author's general theme rather than the specific mystery.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.594Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Dietrich, the brass band's reserved French horn player, hears whispers that newcomer Klaus once played professionally in Berlin, and wonders what silence brought him to this small village.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"A alone combines the Berlin rumor with Dietrich's wondering, satisfying the goal of presenting the mystery occupying his thoughts. C (rumor only) and D (theme only) are partially relevant distractors requiring comparison; B is coherent but lacks any mystery. Explanations are consistent, accurate, and English is natural with no Hangul."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"C는 소문, D는 주제를 담고 있어 부분적으로 맞는 근거가 있음. 다만 정답만 'wonders'를 명시해 다소 쉬운 편이지만 medium 범위 안에 듦.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-060","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-transitions-m-063","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"medium","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"The other boarders had an easy explanation for why Frau Steinberg turned away whenever the radio in the parlor played Mahler: she was old, they said, and old people found loud music tiresome. ______ six-year-old Rainer had watched her sit contentedly through the brass band that thundered past the boarding house every Sunday, her teacup perfectly steady in her hand. It was only the slow Mahler symphonies that made her rise, face the window, and stand very still until they ended.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["In fact,","For instance,","Therefore,","However,"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"첫 문장은 하숙인들이 \"노인은 시끄러운 음악을 싫어한다\"고 설명하는 내용이고, 다음 문장은 프라우 슈타인베르크가 요란한 브라스 밴드는 편안히 견딘다는 라이너의 관찰이다. 이 관찰은 앞의 설명을 반박하므로 대조를 나타내는 D가 정답이다. A는 앞의 주장을 강화하거나 더 구체화하는 전환어인데, 뒤 문장은 그 주장을 약화한다. B는 뒤 문장이 구체적 장면이라 그럴듯해 보이지만, 이 장면은 앞 주장의 예시가 아니라 반례이다. C는 앞 문장의 결과를 나타내지만, 라이너의 관찰은 하숙인들의 설명에서 나온 결과가 아니다.","explanationEn":"The first sentence gives the boarders' explanation: Frau Steinberg is old, so loud music tires her. The next sentence describes Rainer seeing her sit calmly through a loud brass band, which contradicts that explanation. A contrast transition is needed, so D is correct. A would mean the second sentence strengthens or adds to the claim, but it actually undermines it. B seems tempting because the sentence describes a specific scene, but that scene is a counterexample, not an example. C would mean Rainer's observation follows from the boarders' explanation, and it does not.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.594Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Six-year-old Rainer notices that Frau Steinberg always turns away when the boarding house radio plays Mahler, sensing a grief no adult has named.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"앞 문장(하숙인들의 설명)과 뒤 문장(시끄러운 브라스 밴드를 편안히 듣는 반례)의 관계를 파악해야 하며, 세 번째 문장이 이를 재확인한다. D(However) 정답 확실. A(In fact)는 '실은'으로 읽으면 다소 그럴듯하고 B(For instance)는 구체적 장면이라 유인력이 있어 비교 판단이 필요하므로 medium에 적합. 해설 한/영 일치, 선택지 참조 정확, 영어 해설에 한글 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"D(However)가 가장 적절함. 다만 'In fact'는 앞서 말한 잘못된 통념을 바로잡을 때도 쓰일 수 있어(“they said X. In fact, Y”) 약간의 복수정답 시비가 생길 수 있음. 해설은 A를 '강화' 기능으로만 설명하므로 이 점이 약하다. 그래도 SAT 관례로는 However가 명확히 최선임. B는 그럴듯한 오답이고 C는 쉽게 배제되어 medium 수준에 맞음.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-transitions-m-063","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-transitions-m-064","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"medium","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"On the No. 28 tram climbing toward Alfama, Fernanda recognized the man by the crooked set of his left ear, the same as his sister Inês's. Thirty-one years earlier, at Inês's bedside, Fernanda had promised to find him and tell him he was forgiven, and in the decades since, she had rehearsed the sentence so often that she could recite it without thinking. ______ when he glanced up and met her eyes, the words would not come; she stared at her shopping bag until the tram lurched to a stop at her street.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Even so,","As a result,","In other words,","Likewise,"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"앞 문장은 페르난다가 그 문장을 수없이 연습해 생각 없이도 말할 수 있었다고 하고, 뒷문장은 정작 그를 마주하자 말이 나오지 않았다고 한다. 준비가 충분했는데도 예상과 반대 결과가 나왔으므로 양보 후 반전을 나타내는 A가 정답이다. B는 연습이 말문이 막힌 원인인 것처럼 만드는데, 지문에서 연습은 오히려 쉽게 말할 수 있게 해 줄 근거로 제시되어 인과 방향이 맞지 않는다. C는 뒷문장이 앞문장을 바꿔 말한 것으로 보게 하지만 두 문장의 내용은 서로 반대이다. D는 비슷한 내용을 덧붙일 때 쓰지만, 말이 나오지 않은 것은 술술 외울 수 있었다는 사실과 비슷하지 않다.","explanationEn":"The earlier sentence says Fernanda practiced the sentence so many times that she could recite it without thinking. The next sentence says that when she actually faced the man, the words would not come. She was well prepared, yet the opposite of what you'd expect happened, so this is a concession followed by a reversal, and A fits. B treats the practice as the cause of her silence, but the passage presents the practice as something that should have made speaking easy, so the cause and effect run the wrong way. C would make the second sentence a restatement of the first, but the two sentences say opposite things. D adds a similar point, but freezing up is not similar to being able to recite the words easily.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.594Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On the Lisbon tram, Fernanda encounters a man and remembers she promised his dying sister decades ago that she would find him and tell him he was forgiven.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 A(양보/반전) 검산 일치: 수없이 연습해 생각 없이 암송 가능 → 실제 마주치자 말이 안 나옴. B는 '연습했으니 그 결과'라는 표면적 연결로 부분적 유인력이 있으나 인과 방향이 어긋나고, C·D는 내용 관계상 배제됨. 한·영 해설 결론·글자 참조 동일, 영어 해설에 한글 없음, 자연스러움. 창작 지문으로 저작권 우려 없음. 난이도는 medium 범위이나 C·D의 유인력이 약해 다소 쉬운 쪽에 가까움."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"대조 신호가 분명함. B는 '너무 연습해서 오히려 막혔다'로 읽힐 여지가 있어 오답 매력도가 어느 정도 있음. medium 수준으로 적절.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-transitions-m-064","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-transitions-m-066","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"medium","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"For most of the winter, Nino had looked at Giorgi as though he were a polite stranger who had wandered into her kitchen in the mountain village; she thanked him for the bread he baked and asked when her husband would come back from the high pastures. Giorgi had learned not to correct her. ______ on the evening the first snow slid from the slate roofs, she took his hand beside the stove and quietly repeated the words he had spoken at their wedding fifty years earlier: that he would love her even through her forgetting.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Consequently,","Indeed,","Still,","Likewise,"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"앞 문장들은 Nino가 겨울 내내 Giorgi를 알아보지 못했다는 상황을 말하고, 빈칸 뒤 문장은 그녀가 50년 전 약속을 기억해 낸 반대되는 순간을 그린다. 그러므로 예상과 반대되는 일을 이끄는 C가 정답이다. A는 Giorgi가 바로잡지 않은 것이 기억을 되살렸다는 인과관계를 암시하지만, 지문에는 그런 근거가 없다. B는 앞 내용을 강조하거나 덧붙이는 말인데, 뒤 문장은 앞의 망각을 강화하지 않고 오히려 뒤집는다. D는 비슷한 내용을 이어 줄 때 쓰는 말이라, 알아보지 못하는 것과 기억해 내는 것이라는 상반된 두 상황에 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The earlier sentences show that all winter Nino failed to recognize Giorgi. The sentence after the blank describes the opposite: she remembers the promise he made fifty years ago. So you need a transition that introduces something contrary to what came before, and that's choice C. Choice A suggests that Giorgi's choice not to correct her caused her memory to return, but the text never supports that link. Choice B would emphasize or build on her forgetting, yet the next sentence reverses it. Choice D signals a similar idea, which doesn't fit two opposite states, not recognizing him and then remembering.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.594Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — In the mountain village, old Giorgi holds his wife's hand and realizes she finally remembers the promise he made fifty years ago to love her through forgetting.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"앞 문맥(겨울 내내 알아보지 못함, Giorgi가 바로잡지 않음)과 뒤 문장(결혼 서약을 기억해 냄)은 명확한 대비 관계이므로 'Still'(C)이 정답으로 타당하다. A는 직전 문장 'learned not to correct her'를 원인으로 오독하면 끌리는 그럴듯한 오답이고, B·D는 각각 강조·유사를 나타내 상반 관계에 맞지 않는다. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 같은 결론과 글자 참조를 갖고 모순이 없으며, 영어 해설은 자연스럽고 한글이 없다. 지문은 창작 서사로 저작권 문제 없음. 두 정보(앞의 망각 상황 + 뒤의 기억 회복)를 연결해 판단해야 하고 A가 부분적 근거를 가진 매력적 오답이라 medium에 적합하다."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"대조 관계(겨울 내내 알아보지 못함 → 결혼 서약을 기억함)가 분명하므로 'Still,'이 맞다. 'Consequently'는 Giorgi가 정정하지 않은 행동과 결과를 잇는 그럴듯한 오답이고, 'Indeed'는 약한 오답이다. 'Likewise'는 쉽게 배제되므로 난이도는 medium 중에서도 낮은 편이다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-transitions-m-066","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-transitions-m-067","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"medium","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Behind the counter of the ferry kiosk, Sophia measured loose black tea into a paper cup while Mrs. Halloran, who had taught her algebra decades earlier, counted out coins with slow, deliberate fingers. Sophia expected the usual remark about the weather or the late departure. ______ her old teacher said quietly that this crossing would be her last, that she was moving inland to live with her son, and then she took the cup and turned toward the deck without another word.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Accordingly,","Similarly,","For example,","Instead,"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"앞 문장은 Sophia가 날씨나 출항 지연에 대한 평범한 말을 예상했다고 하고, 뒤 문장은 선생님이 전혀 다른 말, 즉 이번이 마지막 항해라는 사실을 털어놓았다고 한다. 예상과 실제가 대비되므로 예상이 다른 일로 대체되었음을 나타내는 D가 정답이다. A는 예상의 결과로 그 말이 나왔다는 뜻이 되는데, 실제 발언은 예상을 뒤집는다. B는 두 내용이 비슷하다는 뜻이지만 고백은 평범한 말과 다르다. C는 '평범한 말'의 예시로 보게 만들지만 이별 고백은 그런 예가 아니다.","explanationEn":"The first sentence tells you that Sophia expected an ordinary remark about the weather or a late departure. The next sentence shows her teacher saying something completely different: this is her final crossing. Since what actually happened replaces what Sophia expected, D is correct. A would mean the confession followed logically from Sophia's expectation, but it actually overturns that expectation. B would mean the two remarks are alike, and C would treat the confession as an example of small talk, but a farewell announcement is neither similar to small talk nor an example of it.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.594Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Sophia, the island ferry kiosk clerk, listens as her aging former teacher orders tea and reveals this is the last voyage she'll make, her final wisdom unspoken.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 D(Instead) 검증: 'expected the usual remark' 뒤에 예상과 다른 발언이 이어지므로 대체/대조 전환어가 적절. Accordingly(결과), Similarly(유사), For example(예시)은 모두 논리적으로 배제됨. 해설 한·영 모두 글자 참조와 결론이 일치하며 영어는 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 서사형 지문은 SAT 전환어 문항에서 다소 드물지만 형식상 허용 범위. 난이도: 예상→실제 대비를 읽어내야 하고, A는 '예상대로'로 오독하면 끌릴 수 있어 medium에 적합. 원작 지문 표절 의심 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["too_easy","eliminated:3"],"note":"'expected ... usual remark' 직후의 대조 신호가 매우 명확해 Instead가 즉시 드러남. 오답 A/B/C 모두 부분적 근거가 약해 비교 없이 배제 가능하므로 medium보다 쉬움.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-transitions-m-067","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-transitions-m-068","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"medium","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"For the whole crossing, Marcus had planned to let the letter drop into the ferry's churning wake, giving his mother's last words to the sea the way she had once handed him off to his aunt. Her handwriting still leaned eagerly forward, as if she had expected to be there when he read it. When the ferry finally slowed outside the harbor at Bequia, though, he did not open his hand over the railing. ______ he smoothed the envelope flat against his knee and read it a fourth time.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Instead,","Nevertheless,","Consequently,","Likewise,"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"앞 문장은 Marcus가 계획했던 행동(편지를 바다에 놓아 버리기)을 하지 않았다는 내용이고, 빈칸 뒤 문장은 그 대신 실제로 한 행동(편지를 펴서 다시 읽기)을 보여 준다. 따라서 하지 않은 행동을 다른 행동으로 대체하는 A가 정답이다. B는 지문 전체에 대조(though)가 있어 그럴듯하지만, 편지를 버리지 않은 것과 다시 읽는 것은 서로 반대되지 않으므로 '그럼에도'의 양보 관계가 성립하지 않는다. C는 두 행동이 이어진다는 점에서 그럴듯하지만, 손을 펴지 않은 것이 다시 읽는 행동의 원인은 아니다. D는 두 행동을 유사한 것으로 보지만, 뒤 문장은 앞 문장과 비슷한 행동이 아니라 그 행동을 대신한 것이다.","explanationEn":"The sentence before the blank tells you what Marcus did not do (drop the letter over the railing), and the sentence after it tells you what he did in its place (smooth the envelope and reread it). A transition that marks a replacement action fits, so A is correct. B may look right because the passage already contains a contrast (\"though\"), but not throwing the letter away and rereading it do not oppose each other, so \"despite this\" does not make sense. C seems plausible because one action follows the other, but keeping his hand closed did not cause him to reread the letter. D treats the two actions as similar, but the second action takes the place of the first rather than resembling it.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.594Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On the Caribbean ferry, Marcus clutches a letter that arrived from his estranged mother three weeks after her funeral, her words still warm with intention.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"앞 문장(계획한 행동을 하지 않음) 뒤에 대체 행동이 이어지므로 'Instead'가 유일하게 논리적임을 직접 확인. B는 앞 문장의 'though'로 인해 훑어 읽으면 매력적이나 양보 관계가 성립하지 않고, C는 시간적 연속성 때문에 부분적으로 그럴듯하며, D도 문법적으로 말이 됨. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 동일한 결론과 선택지 참조를 가지며 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 창작 서사 지문으로 저작권 의심 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"부정문 다음에 대체 행동이 오는 전형적인 Instead 구조임. Nevertheless가 though와 결합해 그럴듯한 함정 역할을 하여 medium에 적합함.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-transitions-m-068","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-transitions-m-069","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"medium","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"The delivery boat bumped against the island school's pier, and Mr. Fraser handed Ailsa a single envelope addressed to her father, who had drowned the winter before. Ailsa knew her mother would want to open anything of his herself; she had said so quietly, almost fiercely, when the first condolence cards arrived. ______ Ailsa slid her thumb under the flap before she reached the end of the pier, unable to bear the long walk home across the moor without knowing what was inside.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Accordingly,","Even so,","In particular,","For this reason,"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"앞 문장은 어머니가 아버지의 우편물을 직접 열고 싶어 한다는 사실을 아일사가 알고 있었다는 내용이고, 뒷문장은 그럼에도 그녀가 봉투를 열어 버린다는 내용이다. 알고 있던 사실에 반하는 행동이므로 양보 후 반전을 나타내는 B가 정답이다. A와 D는 인과 관계를 나타내는데, 어머니의 바람이 오히려 봉투를 여는 이유가 된다는 뜻이 되어 논리가 거꾸로 된다. C는 앞 내용의 구체적인 예를 드는 표현이지만, 봉투를 여는 행동은 어머니의 바람을 구체화하는 예가 아니라 그 바람을 거스르는 행동이다.","explanationEn":"The first sentence tells you that Ailsa knew her mother wanted to open anything of her father's herself. The next sentence shows Ailsa opening the envelope anyway. Since she acts against what she knows, you need a transition that signals contrast after a concession, so B is correct. A and D signal cause and effect, which would mean her mother's wish was the reason Ailsa opened the letter, and that gets the logic backward. C introduces a specific example of what came before, but opening the envelope goes against the mother's wish rather than illustrating it.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.594Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Young Ailsa watches the island school's delivery boat arrive with a letter addressed to her late father, and she must decide whether to open it.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"앞 문장(어머니가 직접 열고 싶어 함을 앎)과 뒷문장(그럼에도 봉투를 엶)의 관계는 양보·반전이므로 B \"Even so\"가 유일하게 타당. A·D는 인과로 논리가 역전되고 C는 예시 관계가 아님. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 동일 결론과 선택지 참조, 모순 없음. 앞 문장이 두 절로 길어 반전 관계를 파악하려면 정독이 필요하고, 인과 오답 두 개가 표면상 그럴듯하여 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"대비가 분명해서 오답 셋 중 둘(A, D)이 같은 인과 계열이라 묶어서 배제된다. 그래도 정독이 필요해 medium 하한으로는 적합하다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-transitions-m-069","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-transitions-m-070","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"medium","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Rune leaned back against the cedar boards and watched his grandson, Eirik, study the thermometer by the door as if it might tell him something besides the heat. The boy had not mentioned the lake once all evening, not even when Rune joked about the old fishing hut. ______ every question Eirik asked seemed to drift toward it: how long the snow used to stay, whether the cousins still skated at Easter, why the hut now sat on the shore instead of out on the ice.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Indeed,","As a result,","Still,","For instance,"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"앞 문장은 에이리크가 저녁 내내 호수를 한 번도 언급하지 않았다고 말하고, 뒤 문장은 그런데도 그의 질문이 모두 호수 쪽으로 향했다고 말하므로 양보 후 반전 관계이며 C가 정답이다. A는 앞 내용을 강조·강화할 때 쓰는데, 뒤 문장은 '언급하지 않았다'를 강화하지 않고 오히려 그와 대조된다. B는 인과를 나타내지만 호수를 언급하지 않은 것이 질문이 호수로 향한 원인이 되지는 않는다. D는 앞 문장의 예시를 제시하는 말인데, 호수로 향하는 질문들은 침묵의 예가 아니라 침묵과 대조되는 내용이다.","explanationEn":"The first sentence says Eirik never mentioned the lake all evening, and the next sentence says that, even so, every question he asked drifted back toward it. That's a concession followed by a contrast, so C is the answer. A would add emphasis to the previous point, but the second sentence goes against \"never mentioned\" instead of strengthening it. B signals cause and effect, and staying quiet about the lake doesn't cause his questions to turn toward it. D would bring in an example of the previous claim, but questions that keep circling the lake aren't examples of his silence. They contrast with it.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.594Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Rune sits in the Norwegian sauna and observes his grandson staring at the thermometer, sensing the boy knows the ice melts earlier every year.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"앞 문장 '호수를 한 번도 언급하지 않았다'와 뒤 문장 '모든 질문이 호수 쪽으로 향했다'는 명백한 양보-대조 관계로 C(Still)가 정답임을 직접 확인. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 같은 결론과 글자 참조를 가지며 오답 배제 근거도 정확. 영어 해설은 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 'Indeed'는 질문이 호수 관심을 확인한다고 훑어 읽으면 고를 수 있고, 'As a result'도 표면적으로 그럴듯해 비교가 필요하므로 medium에 적합. 창작 지문으로 저작권 문제 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"'호수를 언급하지 않음'과 '질문이 모두 호수로 향함'이 대조되므로 Still이 맞다. Indeed와 For instance는 겉보기 연결 때문에 고르기 쉬운 오답이고, As a result도 회피에서 집착으로 이어진다고 읽으면 그럴듯해 보인다. 중간 난이도에 맞다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-transitions-m-070","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-transitions-m-072","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"medium","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"On the long walk up from the station, Tommy had planned to tell Robert everything: the roof fall that had kept his father home from the pit for a whole winter, the night shifts he himself had taken on at sixteen, the girl from the next valley he meant to marry. ______ when the two of them reached the old stile where they had once carved their initials, he remarked only that the weather had turned. Robert, studying the faded letters, seemed to understand that this would be all.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Yet,","As a result,","Indeed,","Afterward,"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"첫 문장은 Tommy가 모든 것을 말하려고 계획했다는 내용이고, 빈칸 뒤 문장은 실제로는 날씨 이야기만 했다는 내용이므로 기대와 다른 결과를 나타내는 대조가 필요하다. 그래서 A가 정답이다. B는 많은 이야기를 하려던 계획이 침묵의 원인이 될 수 없으므로 인과 관계가 맞지 않는다. C는 앞 내용을 강조하거나 보강하는 말인데 뒤 문장은 오히려 계획을 뒤집는다. D는 시간 순서상 그럴듯해 보이지만 걸어가는 동안 세운 계획과 실제 행동 사이의 대조를 드러내지 못한다.","explanationEn":"The first sentence says Tommy planned to tell Robert everything, but the next sentence shows that he only mentioned the weather, so the transition has to signal that what happened went against what he expected. That makes A correct. B is wrong because his plan to say a lot can't be the cause of him saying almost nothing. C would introduce something that reinforces the plan, but the second sentence actually undercuts it. D can seem to fit because the events happen in time order, but it misses the contrast between what Tommy meant to do and what he really did.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.595Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Coal miner's son Tommy and his childhood friend Robert acknowledge the distance between them without words, their separate paths now measured in years.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"계획(모든 것을 말하려 함) vs 실제(날씨만 언급)의 대조가 명확하여 'Yet'이 유일하게 논리적임. B(인과)·C(강조)는 논리적으로 배제되고, D(Afterward)는 시간 순서상 그럴듯해 비교가 필요함. 다만 B와 C의 매력도가 낮아 medium 중에서는 다소 쉬운 편이며, 'Yet, when...'처럼 쉼표 뒤에 종속절이 오는 구조는 다소 어색하지만 허용 범위임. 해설 한·영 모두 정답 A를 일관되게 뒷받침하며 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 원작 문체를 연상시키나 창작 지문으로 보임."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"계획(모든 것을 말하려 함)과 실제(날씨 이야기만 함) 사이의 대조가 분명하므로 정답은 A(Yet)이다. D(Afterward)는 시간 순서상 그럴듯해 보여 매력적인 오답이다. 다만 대조 신호가 비교적 뚜렷해서 medium 중에서도 쉬운 편이다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-transitions-m-072","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-e-077","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"easy","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"For eleven years, Pedro and Mateo had argued about whose breeding methods produced the smarter sheep. At last they agreed to settle the matter with a herding contest on the village green. Pedro's dog circled the flock with perfect precision, and the sheep trotted neatly toward the gate. Then Mateo's oldest ewe wandered over to the judges' table and calmly began eating the prize ______ both men burst out laughing at the same moment.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["ribbon,","ribbon, and","ribbon","ribbon, then"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"빈칸 앞 \"Then Mateo's oldest ewe ... the prize ribbon\"과 뒤 \"both men burst out laughing ...\"은 각각 독립절이다. 두 독립절은 쉼표와 등위접속사 and로 연결할 수 있으므로 B가 정답이다. A는 쉼표만으로 두 독립절을 이어 쉼표 스플라이스가 된다. C는 문장부호 없이 이어 붙인 무종지문(run-on)이다. D의 then은 등위접속사가 아닌 부사이므로 쉼표와 함께 써도 여전히 쉼표 스플라이스이다.","explanationEn":"The words before the blank (\"Then Mateo's oldest ewe ... the prize ribbon\") form an independent clause, and so do the words after it (\"both men burst out laughing ...\"). You can join two independent clauses with a comma plus a coordinating conjunction such as \"and,\" so B is correct. A uses only a comma, which creates a comma splice. C joins the clauses with no punctuation at all, which makes a run-on sentence. D uses \"then,\" which is an adverb, not a coordinating conjunction, so a comma before it still leaves a comma splice.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.595Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Rival ranchers Pedro and Mateo settle their long argument about breeding methods through an elaborate sheep-herding contest that ends in unexpected laughter.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"검산: 빈칸 앞(\"Then Mateo's oldest ewe wandered ... the prize ribbon\")과 뒤(\"both men burst out laughing ...\") 모두 독립절. B(쉼표+and)만 적법. A 쉼표 스플라이스, C 무종지문, D는 접속부사 then으로 여전히 쉼표 스플라이스. 해설 한·영 모두 정답과 글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 단일 규칙(독립절 연결)으로 풀리고 오답은 전형적 오개념이므로 easy 적합. 원문은 창작 서사로 저작권 의심 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"쉼표+등위접속사 규칙 하나로 풀린다. 오답 A, C, D는 각각 쉼표 스플라이스, 무종지문, 'then' 쉼표 스플라이스로, 전형적인 오개념이다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-boundaries-e-077","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-e-078","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"easy","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Every evening after the last ferry departed, Nikos wiped down the counter of his kiosk and set out a worn deck of cards. His opponent, a retired schoolteacher named Eleni, ______ at the same plastic table she had claimed since June. As the summer crowds thinned, the stakes grew: first a bottle of lemonade, then a week of free coffee, and finally the kiosk's faded umbrella.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["sits","will sit","sat","is sitting"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 장면은 departed, wiped, set, had claimed, thinned, grew처럼 과거 시제로 서술된다. 따라서 빈칸에도 과거형 동사 C(sat)가 와야 시제가 일관된다. A(sits)와 D(is sitting)는 현재 시제라서 과거 서사의 흐름과 어긋난다. B(will sit)는 미래 시제라서 이미 일어난 장면을 묘사하는 문맥에 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"This scene is told in the past tense: departed, wiped, set, had claimed, thinned, and grew. So the blank also needs a past-tense verb, and C (sat) keeps the tense consistent. A (sits) and D (is sitting) are present tense, so they break the past-tense flow of the story. B (will sit) is future tense, which doesn't fit a scene that has already happened.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.595Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Island ferry kiosk owner Nikos challenges a regular customer to a long-standing card game, stakes rising as the summer season draws to its close.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"지문 전체가 과거 시제(departed, wiped, set, had claimed, thinned, grew)로 서술되므로 빈칸에는 과거형 sat(C)가 맞다. 해설(한·영) 모두 정답과 선택지 글자 참조가 일치하고 모순 없음. 시제 일관성이라는 단일 규칙으로 풀리며, 오답은 현재·현재진행·미래 시제라는 전형적 오개념이어서 easy 난이도에 적합. 원문 창작 지문으로 저작권 의심 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"이 문항은 시제 일관성 규칙 하나로 풀린다. 지문에 과거형 단서가 직접 여러 개 나와 easy 난이도에 맞는다. 오답은 현재·미래·현재진행형으로, 전형적인 시제 오답이다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-e-078","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-e-079","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"easy","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Every spring, Hans returned to his small allotment garden on the edge of Berlin. Kneeling in the dark soil, he ______ the tomato seedlings in three crooked rows, exactly as he had promised Anna thirty years earlier, the week before she boarded the train to Prague.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["plants","will plant","has planted","planted"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 지문은 returned, had promised, boarded 등 과거 시제로 서술되므로 빈칸의 동사도 과거 시제여야 한다. 따라서 과거형인 D가 정답이다. A는 현재 시제라 과거 서사와 어긋난다. B는 미래 시제로 매년 봄 이미 일어난 행동을 나타낼 수 없다. C는 현재완료로 과거 서사의 시간 틀과 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The passage tells the story in the past tense with verbs such as \"returned,\" \"had promised,\" and \"boarded,\" so the verb in the blank should also be in the past tense. That makes D, the past-tense form, correct. A uses the present tense, which clashes with the past-tense narration. B uses the future tense, but the sentence describes something Hans already did each spring. C uses the present perfect, which doesn't fit the past-tense time frame of the story.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.595Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — In his Berlin allotment garden, Hans plants tomatoes in the same pattern he promised Anna thirty years ago before she left for Prague.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"과거 시제 일치(returned, had promised, boarded)라는 단일 규칙으로 해결되는 문항. D \"planted\"만 맥락에 맞음. A(현재), B(미래), C(현재완료)는 전형적 시제 오개념 오답으로 적절. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 원작 지문 표절 의심 없음. 난이도 easy 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"과거 서사 시제 일치 단일 규칙 문항. returned가 직접 단서이고, 오답은 전형적인 시제 오개념이다. 다만 분류상 form_structure_sense보다는 시제(verb tense) 문항에 가깝다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-e-079","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-e-080","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"easy","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"As the houseboat drifted past the coconut groves of Alappuzha, Vikram watched the boatman's daughter coil a wet rope on the deck. He recognized her slowly, the way one recalls a half-forgotten song. Twenty years earlier, when he was a boy of seven, she ______ him out of the dark backwater after he slipped from the dock. Neither of them had spoken of that afternoon since, and now she simply nodded at him and returned to her work.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["had pulled","pulls","will pull","is pulling"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 지문은 과거 시제(drifted, watched, recognized)로 서술되고, 빈칸은 그보다 더 앞선 사건(Twenty years earlier)을 가리키므로 과거완료 A가 맞다. B는 현재 시제라 과거 서술과 맞지 않는다. C는 미래 시제라 이미 일어난 일을 표현할 수 없다. D는 현재진행형이라 20년 전의 일에 쓸 수 없다.","explanationEn":"The passage is told in the past tense (drifted, watched, recognized), and the blank describes something that happened even earlier (\"Twenty years earlier\"), so the past perfect in A is correct. B is present tense, which doesn't fit the past-tense narration. C is future tense and can't describe something that already happened. D is present progressive, which doesn't work for an event from twenty years ago.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.595Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On the Kerala houseboat, guest Vikram encounters the boatman's daughter and learns she once saved him from drowning as a child, though neither has spoken since.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"과거 서술 + \"Twenty years earlier\"라는 명시적 단서로 과거완료 had pulled가 유일하게 성립. 오답은 모두 현재/미래 계열이라 시제 일치 규칙 하나로 즉시 배제되며, 이는 easy 난이도에 부합한다. 다만 단순 과거(pulled)가 선택지에 없어 변별력이 낮은 편이나, 평이한 easy 문항으로 적절하다. 한·영 해설 결론 및 글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 독창적 서사 지문으로 저작권 우려 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"과거 서술 속 더 이전 사건 → 과거완료라는 규칙 하나로 풀리고, 'Twenty years earlier'가 단서로 직접 드러남. 오답은 모두 시제 불일치라 규칙을 알면 바로 배제됨. 오답 중에 단순과거 'pulled'가 없어서 정답 시비가 생길 여지도 없음.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-e-080","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-e-081","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"easy","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"On the small Scottish island, news moves faster than the ferry. Every evening, the whispers about the new teacher, Miss Campbell, ______ from the harbor to the church steps: she left the mainland in disgrace, some say, or she is running from a broken engagement. Hamish, the shyest boy in her class, hears none of it. He notices only her gentle hands as she smooths the wrinkled pages of his notebook.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["travels","travel","has traveled","is traveling"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"빈칸 동사의 주어는 복수 명사 \"the whispers\"이고, \"about the new teacher, Miss Campbell\"은 주어를 꾸미는 수식어일 뿐이다. 따라서 복수 동사가 필요하며, 지문 전체가 현재 시제(moves, say, hears)이므로 B가 맞다. A, C, D는 모두 단수 동사여서 수식어 속 단수 명사 \"teacher\"나 \"Miss Campbell\"에 잘못 맞춘 형태이다.","explanationEn":"The subject of the verb in the blank is the plural noun \"the whispers.\" The phrase \"about the new teacher, Miss Campbell\" only describes that subject. So you need a plural verb, and because the passage is told in the present tense (moves, say, hears), B is correct. A, C, and D are all singular verbs, so they wrongly agree with the singular nouns \"teacher\" or \"Miss Campbell\" in the modifying phrase.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.595Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On the Scottish island, whispers travel that new teacher Miss Campbell is hiding a scandal, but shy Hamish notices only her gentle hands.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"주어 \"the whispers\"(복수) + 전치사구 수식어(\"about the new teacher, Miss Campbell\") 사이의 수 일치 단일 규칙 문항. 정답 B(travel)만 복수형이며 A·C·D는 모두 단수형으로 수식어 내 단수 명사에 끌린 전형적 오개념 오답. 현재 시제 맥락(moves, say, hears)과도 일치. 해설 한/영 모두 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 지문은 창작 원문으로 보이며 저작권 의심 없음. 난이도 easy 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"주어-동사 수일치 단일 규칙 문항이며, 수식구가 끼어들어 생기는 전형적 오개념을 오답으로 활용함. 오답 A, C, D가 모두 단수형이라 B만 남음. 다만 유형 분류는 form_structure_sense보다 주어-동사 일치에 더 가까움.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-e-081","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-cross_text_connections-e-082","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Cross-Text Connections","difficulty":"easy","skill":"cross_text_connections","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Text 1\nIn this excerpt from a short story, the narrator describes the widow Cathleen setting out from the mining town. Cathleen told the neighbors she was walking to the next county only to return the borrowed hymnal to her sister's church. She insisted it was a simple errand of honesty, nothing more, and that she had no wish to see Margaret at all.\n\nText 2\nA literary critic writing about the same story argues that the hymnal is merely an excuse. The critic points out that Cathleen could have mailed the book cheaply, yet she walks for two days. In the critic's view, the long journey shows that Cathleen secretly hopes to make peace with her sister.","question":"Based on the texts, how would the critic in Text 2 most likely respond to Cathleen's stated reason for her trip, as described in Text 1?","options":["By agreeing that the trip is only about returning the book, since Cathleen is known for being honest","By agreeing that Cathleen wants to avoid Margaret, since the journey takes her two days","By suggesting that Cathleen's actions reveal a motive different from the one she gives","By suggesting that Cathleen's neighbors pushed her to make the trip against her will"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"Text 1에서 Cathleen은 찬송가를 돌려주려는 것뿐이고 언니를 만날 생각이 없다고 말한다. Text 2의 비평가는 책을 우편으로 보낼 수 있었는데도 이틀을 걸어간 점을 들어, 실제로는 화해를 바란다고 본다. 따라서 비평가는 행동이 말한 이유와 다른 동기를 드러낸다고 반응할 것이므로 C가 정답이다. A와 B는 Text 2가 반박하는 Cathleen의 주장에 동의하는 것이라 틀렸고, D의 이웃의 압력은 두 글 어디에도 나오지 않는다.","explanationEn":"In Text 1, Cathleen says she is only returning the hymnal and doesn't want to see her sister. The critic in Text 2 notes she could have mailed the book but walked for two days instead, which suggests she secretly wants to reconcile. So the critic would say her actions reveal a motive different from the one she states, which makes C correct. A and B agree with Cathleen's own explanation, and that's exactly what Text 2 argues against. D is wrong because neither text says the neighbors pressured her.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.596Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Widow Cathleen makes the long journey from the mining town to the next county to return a borrowed hymnal to her estranged sister's church.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"Text 1의 표면적 이유(찬송가 반납, 언니 회피)와 Text 2 비평가의 반론(우편 가능했으나 이틀 도보 → 화해 희망)이 명확히 대비되어 C가 유일한 정답. A·B는 비평가가 반박하는 Cathleen의 주장에 동의하는 전형적 오답, D는 지문 밖 정보. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 단일 개념(두 텍스트 관점 대비), 한 단계 추론으로 easy 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"Text 2가 '찬송가는 핑계'라고 직접 말하므로 한 단계 추론으로 C가 나온다. A·B는 Cathleen이 밝힌 이유를 그대로 받아들이는 오답이고, D는 지문에 없는 내용이다. Margaret가 언니라는 점은 문맥으로 알 수 있다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-cross_text_connections-e-082","intendedSkill":"cross_text_connections","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-cross_text_connections-e-083","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Cross-Text Connections","difficulty":"easy","skill":"cross_text_connections","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Text 1\nIn the studio, Yuki dipped the test bowl and pulled it out slowly. \"Forty years,\" he told Takeshi, \"and I still could not write this down for you. The glaze must be learned by watching me, again and again. Only my eyes can teach it.\"\n\nText 2\nTakeshi tried once and the glaze ran thin. Yuki said nothing. He placed his hands over the boy's wrists and they dipped the bowl together. On the fourth try, Takeshi felt the slight drag of the liquid and slowed without being told. Yuki stepped back and smiled. The boy's hands had learned what no amount of watching had shown him.","question":"Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to Yuki's claim in Text 1 about how the glaze technique must be learned?","options":["By agreeing that the technique can be learned only by watching Yuki many times","By agreeing that the technique is too difficult for a young apprentice to learn at all","By suggesting that the technique is best learned from written instructions","By suggesting that the technique is learned through the feel of doing it, not only through watching"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"Text 1에서 Yuki는 유약 기법을 자신을 지켜보는 것으로만 배울 수 있다고 말한다. Text 2에서 Takeshi는 직접 손으로 액체의 저항을 느끼며 배우고, 마지막 문장은 아무리 지켜봐도 알 수 없던 것을 손이 배웠다고 밝히므로 D가 정답이다. A는 Text 2의 마지막 문장과 반대된다. B는 Takeshi가 결국 기법을 익혔으므로 틀리고, C의 글로 된 지시는 두 글 어디에도 지지되지 않는다.","explanationEn":"In Text 1, Yuki says the glaze can be learned only by watching him. In Text 2, Takeshi learns by feeling the drag of the glaze with his own hands, and the last sentence says his hands learned what watching had not shown him, so D is correct. A goes against that last sentence. B is wrong because Takeshi does learn the technique, and C is wrong because neither text supports learning from written instructions.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.596Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Master potter Yuki teaches young apprentice Takeshi a glaze technique that took him forty years to perfect, watching for the moment the boy's hands understand.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 D 검산 완료: Text 2 마지막 문장(\"The boy's hands had learned what no amount of watching had shown him\")이 Text 1의 '지켜보는 것만으로 배운다'는 주장에 직접 대응한다. A는 Text 2와 정면 모순, B는 Takeshi가 4번째 시도에 성공하므로 배제, C는 Text 1이 글로 쓸 수 없다고 명시하므로 배제. 한·영 해설 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 단서가 지문에 명시적이고 추론 한 단계, 어휘 평이 — easy 적합. 창작 지문으로 저작권 의심 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"마지막 문장에 단서가 직접 드러나 한 단계 추론으로 풀 수 있음. 오답들은 전형적 오독이고, C는 Text 1의 'could not write this down'과 연결되는 함정임.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-cross_text_connections-e-083","intendedSkill":"cross_text_connections","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-cross_text_connections-e-084","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Cross-Text Connections","difficulty":"easy","skill":"cross_text_connections","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Text 1\nIn this excerpt from a novel, Anjali has recently begun speaking again with her brother, Ravi, after years of silence. During the monsoon, a delayed letter from him arrives.\nThe envelope was soft with rain, and the stamp showed a date from the winter before. Anjali read it on the veranda. Ravi's words were cold and stiff. He wrote that he did not expect her to forgive him and that perhaps they were better off as strangers. She folded the page and felt the old hurt return, as if the past months of phone calls had meant nothing.\n\nText 2\nIn this later excerpt from the same novel, Anjali shows the letter to her aunt, who reads it carefully before speaking.\n\"Look at the date,\" her aunt said. \"He wrote this before he called you. This is the man he was in January, not the man he is now. A letter can only tell you how someone felt on the day the ink dried. The phone calls since then are the newer truth.\"","question":"Based on the texts, how would the aunt in Text 2 most likely respond to Anjali's reaction to the letter in Text 1?","options":["She would say that Anjali is wrong to let the letter outweigh the more recent phone calls.","She would say that Anjali is right to treat the letter as proof that Ravi still wants distance.","She would say that Anjali is wrong to read the letter at all before Ravi explains it.","She would say that Anjali is right to blame the postal service for the letter's cold tone."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"Text 1에서 안잘리는 편지를 읽고 최근 몇 달의 통화가 아무 의미 없었던 것처럼 느낀다. Text 2의 이모는 편지가 쓰인 날의 감정만 보여 줄 뿐이고 그 뒤의 통화가 \"더 새로운 진실\"이라고 말한다. 따라서 이모는 편지를 최근 통화보다 무겁게 여기는 안잘리의 반응이 틀렸다고 할 것이므로 A가 정답이다. B는 이모가 편지를 지금 라비의 마음으로 보지 않으므로 틀리다. C는 이모가 편지를 읽지 말라고 한 적이 없고 오히려 읽고 날짜를 확인하라고 하므로 틀리다. D는 이모가 문제 삼는 것이 우편이 늦은 사실이 아니라 편지가 쓰인 시점이므로 틀리다.","explanationEn":"In Text 1, Anjali reads the letter and feels as if months of phone calls \"had meant nothing.\" In Text 2, the aunt says a letter only shows how someone felt on the day it was written, and that the later phone calls are \"the newer truth.\" So the aunt would tell Anjali she is wrong to let the old letter count for more than the recent calls, which makes A correct. B is wrong because the aunt says the letter does not show who Ravi is now. C is wrong because the aunt never tells Anjali not to read it; in fact, she reads it and points out the date. D is wrong because the aunt cares about when the letter was written, not about the mail being slow.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.596Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — During the monsoon, Anjali receives a letter from her brother in London sent during their estrangement, his words arriving after reconciliation has begun.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"Text 2의 이모 발언(\"The phone calls since then are the newer truth\")이 Text 1의 안잘리 반응(\"통화가 아무 의미 없었던 것처럼\")과 직접 대응되어 A가 명확히 정답. B는 정반대, C는 지문에 근거 없음, D는 '지연 배달'을 '어조'와 혼동하는 전형적 오개념. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 결론과 선택지 참조가 일치하며 오류 없음. 단일 단계 추론으로 easy 난이도에 적합. 선택지 D가 다소 약하지만 허용 범위."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"이모의 \"newer truth\" 발언이 직접적인 단서이고, 한 단계 추론으로 A가 나온다. D는 다소 약한 오답이지만 편지가 늦게 도착했다는 설정에 근거하고 있어 그럴듯하다. 겨울과 1월이라는 날짜도 서로 맞는다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-cross_text_connections-e-084","intendedSkill":"cross_text_connections","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-transitions-e-085","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"easy","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Last spring, the prospector William borrowed a shovel from James, his neighbor on the creek, and promised to return it within a week. ______ the shovel still leaned against William's cabin when the aspen leaves turned gold. Now that their claims overlapped on the same gravel bar, William insisted the tool was fair payment for the ground James had staked.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["For example,","However,","Similarly,","Therefore,"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"첫 문장은 윌리엄이 일주일 안에 삽을 돌려주겠다고 약속했다는 내용이고, 다음 문장은 가을이 되어서도 삽이 여전히 그의 오두막에 있었다는 내용이다. 약속과 실제 행동이 서로 반대되므로 대조를 나타내는 B가 정답이다. A는 앞 문장의 예시를 들 때 쓰지만, 삽을 돌려주지 않은 것은 약속의 예시가 아니다. C는 비슷한 내용을 덧붙일 때 쓰는데, 두 문장은 비슷하지 않고 반대된다. D는 결과를 나타내지만, 돌려주겠다는 약속 때문에 삽을 계속 가지고 있게 된 것은 아니다.","explanationEn":"The first sentence tells you that William promised to return the shovel within a week, and the next sentence tells you the shovel was still at his cabin months later. What he promised and what he actually did are opposites, so you need a contrast word, which makes B correct. A introduces an example, but keeping the shovel isn't an example of the promise. C signals a similar idea, but these two sentences are opposites, not similar. D signals a result, but the promise to return the shovel did not cause William to keep it.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.596Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Prospector William refuses to return the shovel he borrowed from prospector James last spring, the debt now tangled with their competing claims.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"약속(일주일 내 반환) vs. 실제(가을까지 미반환)의 명확한 대조로 However가 유일하게 성립. 오답 A/C/D는 각각 예시·유사·결과라는 전형적 전환어 범주로 그럴듯하되 규칙을 알면 즉시 배제됨. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 동일 결론과 글자 참조를 가지며 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 세 번째 문장의 'Now that'은 이후 상황 전개이므로 빈칸 판단에 영향 없음. 가상의 인물 서사로 저작권 문제 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"약속(일주일 내 반납)과 실제(가을까지 미반납)의 대조가 명확해 However가 유일한 정답. 한 단계 추론으로 풀리는 easy 수준. 'months later'는 봄→가을로 보아 타당함.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-transitions-e-085","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-transitions-e-086","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"easy","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"The matatu lurched down Ngong Road, its speakers thumping. Omondi and Kariuki, neighbors for eleven years, rarely agreed on anything: not football, not politics, not even which stall sold the best chapati. When an elderly woman with a heavy basket climbed aboard, the two men glared at each other as usual. ______ both of them jumped up at the same instant to offer her a seat, and each reached for her basket before the other could.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["For example,","Similarly,","Even so,","As a result,"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"앞 문장은 두 사람이 거의 의견이 맞지 않고 서로를 노려본다고 하는데, 뒷 문장에서는 둘이 똑같이 할머니를 돕는다. 앞의 내용으로 보아 예상과 다른 일이므로 대조를 나타내는 C가 정답이다. A는 예시를 뜻하지만 돕는 행동은 의견 불일치의 예가 아니다. B는 유사함을 뜻하는데 두 문장은 비슷한 내용이 아니라 반대 방향이다. D는 결과를 뜻하지만 서로 노려본 것이 돕는 행동의 원인은 아니다.","explanationEn":"The earlier sentences say the two men rarely agree and glare at each other, but the last sentence shows them both helping the woman in the same way. That goes against what you'd expect, so you need a contrast transition, which makes C correct. A brings in an example, but helping the woman isn't an example of their disagreement. B signals similarity, but the two sentences point in opposite directions. D signals a result, and glaring at each other didn't cause them to help.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.597Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On the Nairobi matatu, neighbors Omondi and Kariuki race to help an elderly passenger simultaneously, their competition revealing their shared decency.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"지문은 '거의 의견이 맞지 않음·서로 노려봄' 뒤에 '동시에 도움'이라는 명확한 반전 구조로, 대조 전환어(Even so)가 유일하게 성립한다. 오답 A(예시)·B(유사)·D(결과)는 전형적 오개념 선택지로 적절하며, 단서가 직접 드러나 easy 난이도에 부합한다. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 정답 C와 각 오답 배제 근거를 일관되게 제시하며 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 원문 창작 지문으로 저작권 우려 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"대조(양보) 관계가 하나뿐이고 단서(rarely agreed, glared)가 지문에 바로 드러남. 오답은 예시·유사·결과로 모두 전형적인 오답 유형임. 'Similarly'는 겉으로 보면 'both… same instant'와 연결되어 그럴듯해 보이지만 결국 배제됨.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-transitions-e-086","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-transitions-e-087","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"easy","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Theresa had practiced a dozen opening lines on her long walk to the Chicago platform, and each one was meant to bring up the summer that she and Samuel had once promised would last forever. When Samuel stepped into the same southbound car and sat down across from her, she had every chance to say one of them. ______ she only nodded at him and turned toward the window, letting the rattle of the train fill the silence.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["For example,","Additionally,","Therefore,","Instead,"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"앞 문장은 Theresa가 할 말을 연습했고 말할 기회도 충분했다고 하고, 뒷문장은 그녀가 고개만 끄덕이고 창밖을 보았다고 한다. 기대했던 행동 대신 다른 행동을 했으므로 대체·대조를 나타내는 D가 정답이다. A는 예시를 나타내지만 고개를 끄덕인 것은 말을 할 기회의 예가 아니다. B는 같은 방향의 정보를 더할 때 쓰므로 반대되는 내용에는 맞지 않는다. C는 결과를 나타내지만, 말할 기회가 있었다는 사실 때문에 침묵했다는 것은 논리적이지 않다.","explanationEn":"The earlier sentences tell you that Theresa practiced what to say and had every chance to say it. The last sentence says she only nodded and looked out the window. She did something other than what you would expect, so D, which shows one action taking the place of another, is correct. A introduces an example, but nodding is not an example of having a chance to speak. B adds information that points the same way, so it doesn't fit an opposite outcome. C signals a result, but having a chance to speak would not logically cause her to stay silent.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.597Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On the 1960s Chicago platform, Theresa and Samuel board the same train heading south and neither speaks of the summer they once promised forever.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"앞 문장(연습했고 말할 기회가 충분했다)과 뒷문장(고개만 끄덕이고 침묵했다)의 대체·대조 관계가 명시적이며 \"Instead,\"가 유일하게 논리적임. A(예시)·B(첨가)·C(결과)는 전형적 오답 범주로 규칙을 알면 즉시 배제 가능. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 정답 D를 정확히 뒷받침하고 글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 지문은 창작 서사로 저작권 의심 없음. easy 난이도에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"기회가 있었는데 말하지 않았으므로 대체를 뜻하는 'Instead'가 정답이다. 단서가 지문에 직접 드러나고 한 단계 추론으로 풀린다. 오답은 전형적인 연결어 오개념이다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-transitions-e-087","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-transitions-e-088","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"easy","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"All afternoon on the porch, Elena's father had argued that she should stay in Texas and run the family hardware store rather than move to Chicago for art school. Elena expected him to keep arguing until dinner. ______ when an unexpected storm rolled in and thunder shook the porch boards, he stopped mid-sentence, pulled his chair beside hers, and quietly watched the rain with her.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Instead,","Similarly,","For example,","In addition,"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"앞 문장은 엘레나가 아버지가 저녁까지 계속 논쟁할 것이라 예상했다는 내용이고, 뒤 문장은 아버지가 말을 멈추고 조용히 비를 바라봤다는, 예상과 반대되는 결과이다. 따라서 예상과 다른 일이 일어났음을 나타내는 대조 전환어 A가 정답이다. B는 유사성을 나타내지만 두 문장은 서로 반대된다. C는 예시를 나타내는데, 아버지가 침묵한 것은 계속 논쟁하는 것의 예가 아니다. D는 같은 방향의 정보 추가를 나타내므로 대조 관계에 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The first sentence says Elena expected her father to keep arguing until dinner, but the next sentence shows the opposite: he stopped talking and quietly watched the rain with her. So you need a contrast transition that shows something different from what was expected happened, which makes A correct. B signals similarity, but these two sentences point in opposite directions. C introduces an example, and his falling silent isn't an example of him continuing to argue. D adds more information in the same direction, so it doesn't fit a contrast either.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.597Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On the Texas porch during an unexpected storm, Elena and her father pause their argument about her future, the thunder demanding their temporary truce.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"\"Elena expected him to keep arguing\" vs. \"he stopped mid-sentence... quietly watched the rain\" is a clear expectation-vs-reality contrast; \"Instead, when ... , he stopped\" reads naturally. B (similarity), C (example), D (addition) are standard distractors that are eliminated once the contrast is recognized. Korean and English explanations match each other and the answer key; no Korean in the English explanation. Original narrative text, no copyright concern. Single-step inference with explicit cue—appropriate for easy."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"예상(계속 논쟁)과 실제(침묵)가 대조되므로 Instead가 맞다. 한 단계 추론으로 풀리고, 오답들은 전형적인 전환어 오개념에 해당한다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-transitions-e-088","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-transitions-e-089","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"easy","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Every summer for thirty years, Christos had sold tickets at the ferry kiosk in Piraeus, speaking to passengers only when he had to. One July morning, he overheard the new summer worker, Eleni, telling a deckhand that she was searching for a man in an old photograph. When she held it up, Christos recognized the face immediately: it was his brother Nikos, who had left the island decades ago and whom Christos had wondered about ever since. ______ when Eleni turned to ask whether he knew the man, Christos simply shook his head and went back to counting coins.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["For example,","Even so,","Therefore,","In addition,"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"앞 문장에서 Christos는 사진 속 얼굴이 수십 년 동안 궁금해하던 형 Nikos임을 즉시 알아본다. 그런데 뒤 문장에서는 그 남자를 아느냐는 질문에 고개를 젓는다. 이는 예상과 반대되는 행동이므로 대조를 나타내는 B가 정답이다. A는 앞 내용의 예시를 들 때 쓰는데, 고개를 젓는 행동은 알아본 것의 예가 아니다. C는 결과를 나타내지만, 알아봤기 때문에 모른 척했다는 인과는 지문에 드러나지 않는다. D는 비슷한 내용을 덧붙일 때 쓰므로 상반된 두 내용을 잇기에 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"In the previous sentence, Christos immediately recognizes the face in the photo as his brother Nikos, whom he has wondered about for decades. In the next sentence, though, he shakes his head when he is asked if he knows the man. That action goes against what we would expect, so you need a contrast transition, and B is correct. A introduces an example, but shaking his head is not an example of recognizing his brother. C signals a result, and the text never says that recognizing Nikos caused Christos to deny knowing him. D adds a similar point, so it can't connect two ideas that oppose each other.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.597Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — At the Greek ferry kiosk, quiet Christos overhears that the new summer worker is searching for someone, and he recognizes the face from decades of wondering.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"앞 문장(형 Nikos를 즉시 알아봄)과 뒤 문장(아느냐는 질문에 고개를 저음)이 명백한 반전 관계이므로 대조 전환어 B가 유일하게 성립. A(예시)·C(결과)·D(첨가)는 규칙을 알면 바로 배제되나 초보자에게는 그럴듯한 전형적 오답. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 B를 정확히 뒷받침하고 글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 빈칸 뒤 소문자 'when'과 선택지 쉼표 형식도 일관. 단일 개념(대조 전환)·한 단계 추론으로 easy에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"알아봤다는 내용과 모른 척한다는 행동이 분명히 대조된다. 빈칸 뒤가 소문자 'when'으로 이어지는 형식도 맞다. 오답은 예시·인과·첨가를 나타내는 전형적인 오개념 선택지다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-transitions-e-089","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-transitions-e-090","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"easy","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"As the ferry pulled away from Karaköy, Yusuf turned his late uncle's pocket watch over in his palm. The silver case was tarnished, the glass was scratched, and the watch lost nearly ten minutes every day, so it was useless for catching the morning boat on time. ______ it was the only thing his uncle, a man he had not spoken to in twelve years, had chosen to leave him, and Yusuf could not bring himself to drop it into the gray water of the Bosphorus.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["For example,","Therefore,","Still,","In addition,"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"앞 문장은 시계가 낡고 시간이 맞지 않아 쓸모없다는, 버려야 할 실용적 이유를 제시한다. 뒤 문장은 그럼에도 삼촌이 남긴 유일한 물건이라 버릴 수 없다는 반대 방향의 이유를 제시하므로 대조의 전환어 C가 정답이다. A는 앞 내용의 예시를 들 때 쓰지만, 뒤 문장은 쓸모없음의 예가 아니다. B는 결과를 나타내는데, 쓸모없다는 사실이 간직할 이유가 되지는 않는다. D는 같은 방향의 내용을 덧붙일 때 쓰지만, 두 문장은 서로 반대 방향이다.","explanationEn":"The first sentence gives practical reasons to get rid of the watch: it's tarnished, scratched, and loses time, so it's useless. The second sentence gives a reason pointing the other way: it was the only thing his uncle left him, so Yusuf can't throw it away. That's a contrast, so C is the answer. A introduces an example, but the second sentence isn't an example of the watch being useless. B signals a result, but the watch being useless doesn't lead to Yusuf keeping it. D adds a point in the same direction, but these two sentences point in opposite directions.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.597Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On the Istanbul ferry, Yusuf inherits his estranged uncle's tarnished pocket watch and spends the commute calculating whether nostalgia or practicality should determine whether he keeps this small, unremarkable thing.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"앞 문장(쓸모없음→버릴 이유)과 뒤 문장(유일한 유품→버릴 수 없음)이 명확히 대조되어 'Still'이 유일하게 논리적. 오답은 예시·결과·첨가라는 전형적 전환어 범주로 그럴듯하면서도 대조 규칙만 알면 배제 가능. 한·영 해설 모두 C를 일관되게 뒷받침하고 자연스러움. 지문은 창작 서사로 저작권 의심 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"앞뒤 문장이 '쓸모없음'과 '버릴 수 없음'으로 분명히 대조되어 단서가 지문에 직접 드러남. 단일 대조 규칙으로 해결되며 오답은 전형적인 전환어 오개념임.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-transitions-e-090","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-transitions-e-091","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"easy","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"The following text is adapted from a short story. Morag lives on a small Scottish island.\n\nFor as long as Morag could remember, her parents had spoken of the mainland school as the place she would go when she turned twelve, and she had always believed she would be glad to leave. ______ as the ferry rounded the headland that grey morning, she found herself gripping the schoolyard railing, as though the boat might carry her off before she was ready.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Similarly,","For example,","As a result,","Yet,"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"첫 문장에서 Morag는 섬을 떠나면 기쁠 거라고 늘 믿었다고 한다. 그런데 둘째 문장에서는 배가 다가오자 떠나지 않으려는 듯 난간을 꽉 붙잡는다. 예상과 실제 반응이 반대이므로 대조를 나타내는 D가 정답이다. A는 비슷한 내용을 덧붙일 때 쓰므로 맞지 않고, B는 앞 내용의 예시가 아니므로 틀리며, C는 기쁠 거라는 믿음 때문에 난간을 붙잡은 것이 아니므로 인과 관계가 성립하지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The first sentence says Morag always believed she would be glad to leave the island. The second sentence shows the opposite: when the ferry comes, she grips the railing as if she doesn't want to go. Since her actual reaction contrasts with what she expected, D, which signals contrast, is correct. A is for adding a similar idea, so it doesn't fit. B is wrong because gripping the railing isn't an example of the first sentence, and C is wrong because believing she'd be glad didn't cause her to grip the railing.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.597Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Young Morag stands at the Scottish island schoolyard knowing her parents expect her to leave for the mainland, watching the ferry arrive and feeling the weight of staying becoming indistinguishable from the weight of going.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"첫 문장(떠나면 기쁠 거라 믿음)과 둘째 문장(배가 오자 난간을 꽉 붙잡음)이 명확한 대조 관계이므로 D 'Yet,'이 정답으로 확실함. 오답 A(유사 추가), B(예시), C(인과)는 전형적 전환어 오개념으로 그럴듯하되 규칙을 알면 바로 배제됨. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 결론과 선택지 참조가 일치하고 모순 없음. 지문은 창작 각색으로 저작권 우려 없음. 사소하게 'schoolyard railing'에서 페리를 본다는 설정이 약간 어색하지만 섬 학교 운동장이 항구를 내려다본다고 보면 무리 없음. easy 난이도에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"기대(떠나면 기쁠 것)와 실제 반응(난간을 붙잡음)이 대조되므로 정답 D(Yet)가 맞다. 오답 A·B·C는 대표적인 오개념이며 단서도 지문에 직접 드러나 easy에 맞다. 다만 'schoolyard railing'은 맥락상 어색하다. 섬을 떠나 본토 학교로 가는 장면이므로 부두나 선착장 난간(pier/harbour railing)이 자연스럽다. 정답 판정에는 영향이 없지만 지문을 다듬을 필요가 있다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-transitions-e-091","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-e-092","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"easy","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- \"The Long Furrow\" is a short story by the fictional author Marit Halvorsen, published in 2019.\n- The story follows two neighboring grain farmers, Soren and Bjorn.\n- For years, the two men have argued about crop rotation: Soren rotates wheat with clover, while Bjorn plants barley in the same fields every season.\n- They agree to a harvest contest to see whose fields produce more grain.\n- Neither man admits that the contest is really about proving who understands the land better.","question":"The student wants to present the hidden reason behind the competition in the story. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["In \"The Long Furrow,\" Soren and Bjorn hold a harvest contest that is secretly about showing which of them knows the land best.","In \"The Long Furrow,\" Soren and Bjorn hold a harvest contest after years of arguing about whether to rotate their crops.","In \"The Long Furrow,\" Soren and Bjorn hold a harvest contest to find out whose fields will produce more grain.","In \"The Long Furrow,\" Soren and Bjorn hold a harvest contest in a story Marit Halvorsen published in 2019."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"목표는 대회의 '숨겨진 이유'를 제시하는 것이다. A는 대회가 사실 누가 땅을 더 잘 아는지 증명하려는 것이라는 마지막 메모를 활용하므로 정답이다. B는 대회의 배경인 오랜 논쟁만 말할 뿐 숨겨진 동기는 밝히지 않는다. C는 더 많은 곡물이라는 표면적 목적이라서 숨겨진 이유가 아니다. D는 출판 정보로 목표와 관계가 없다.","explanationEn":"Your goal is to present the hidden reason behind the contest. A works because it uses the last note: the contest is really about proving who understands the land better. B only gives the background of the long argument and doesn't say what secretly drives the contest. C states the open, surface purpose (more grain), so it isn't a hidden reason. D gives publication details that have nothing to do with the goal.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.598Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Neighboring grain farmers Soren and Bjorn settle their years-long argument about crop rotation through a harvest contest that neither admits is less about winning than proving who understands this land better.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"A는 마지막 메모(숨겨진 동기)를 직접 반영하여 정답이 명확하다. B(배경 논쟁), C(표면적 목적), D(출판 정보)는 모두 메모 기반의 전형적 오답으로 그럴듯하지만 '숨겨진 이유'라는 목표를 알면 바로 배제된다. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 선택지 참조와 결론이 일치하며 자연스럽다. 가상 작가·작품으로 저작권 문제 없음. easy 난이도 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"'hidden reason'과 'secretly'가 직접 대응되어 한 단계로 풀 수 있다. C(표면적 목적)와 B(배경)는 그럴듯한 오답이다. 가상의 작품이라 저작권 문제가 없다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-e-092","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-e-093","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"easy","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- \"The Last Lot\" is a short story by fictional author Dana Whitcomb, published in 2019.\n- The story is set at a cattle ranch auction in eastern Montana.\n- Its main character, Ethan Brandt, attends the auction after his grandfather's death.\n- Ethan raises his bidding paddle for his late grandfather's worn leather saddle.\n- At that moment, the auctioneer's microphone cuts out, and the crowd goes quiet and watches Ethan's face.","question":"The student wants to describe the key moment of the story's plot. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Dana Whitcomb's short story \"The Last Lot,\" published in 2019, takes place at a cattle ranch auction in eastern Montana.","In \"The Last Lot,\" just as Ethan Brandt bids on his late grandfather's saddle, the auctioneer's microphone fails, leaving the silent crowd watching his face.","In \"The Last Lot,\" Ethan Brandt attends a cattle ranch auction in eastern Montana after his grandfather's death.","Dana Whitcomb's 2019 short story \"The Last Lot\" has a main character named Ethan Brandt, whose grandfather has died."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"목표는 이야기 줄거리의 핵심 장면을 묘사하는 것이다. B는 Ethan이 할아버지의 안장에 입찰하는 순간 마이크가 꺼지고 군중이 조용히 그의 얼굴을 지켜보는 사건을 담고 있어 목표에 맞는다. A는 작가, 출판 연도, 배경만 소개할 뿐 사건이 없다. C는 Ethan이 경매에 온 이유를 말하지만 핵심 순간은 빠져 있다. D는 주인공과 그의 상황만 소개하고 장면을 묘사하지 않는다.","explanationEn":"Your goal is to describe the story's key plot moment. B does this: it shows Ethan bidding on his grandfather's saddle just as the microphone fails, while the silent crowd watches him. A only gives the author, the publication year, and the setting, so no event happens in it. C explains why Ethan is at the auction but leaves out the key moment. D just introduces the main character and his situation without describing the scene.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.598Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — At the Montana ranch auction, Ethan bids on his late grandfather's saddle just as the auctioneer's microphone fails, leaving him holding it aloft in accidental silence while the crowd watches his face.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 B 검증: 노트 4·5의 입찰 순간과 마이크 고장, 군중의 침묵·시선을 정확히 결합해 '핵심 장면 묘사'라는 목표를 충족. A·C·D는 모두 배경·인물 소개 정보만으로 사건(핵심 순간)이 없어 규칙(목표에 맞는 정보 선택) 하나로 바로 배제되며, 노트 내용에는 부합해 그럴듯한 오답으로 기능. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 B를 일관되게 지지하고 선택지 글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 가상 작가·작품으로 저작권 문제 없음. 형식 적합. 난이도 easy에 부합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"정답 B만 노트의 핵심 장면(입찰·마이크 고장·군중 침묵)을 담는다. 오답들은 배경·인물 소개라 쉽게 배제되지만 그럴듯하다. 가상 작가라고 밝혀 저작권 문제 없음.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-e-093","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-e-094","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"easy","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- \"The Last Button\" is a short story by a Vietnamese American writer.\n- It was published in a literary magazine in 2019.\n- In the story, a young woman named Phuong spends three hours walking through Hanoi's streets at dawn.\n- She is searching for one button to replace the one her mother lost from an old áo dài, a traditional Vietnamese dress.\n- Phuong's mother is losing her memory, and each vendor Phuong visits feels to her like a small prayer for her mother.","question":"The student wants to describe the plot of the story. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["\"The Last Button\" was written by a Vietnamese American writer and published in a literary magazine.","\"The Last Button\" appeared in 2019 and is set in Hanoi, the capital of Vietnam.","In \"The Last Button,\" Phuong spends three dawn hours in Hanoi searching for a button to replace one lost from her mother's old áo dài.","In \"The Last Button,\" an áo dài is a traditional Vietnamese dress that Phuong's mother once wore."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"목표는 이야기의 줄거리, 즉 인물이 무엇을 하는지 설명하는 것이다. C는 Phuong이 새벽 하노이에서 세 시간 동안 어머니의 아오자이 단추를 찾아다니는 사건을 전달하므로 정답이다. A는 작가와 출판 정보만 담고 있어 줄거리가 아니다. B는 출판 연도와 배경만 제시할 뿐 사건이 없다. D는 아오자이라는 옷을 설명할 뿐 이야기에서 일어나는 일을 말하지 않는다.","explanationEn":"Your goal is to describe the plot, which means telling what happens in the story. C does this: it says Phuong spends three dawn hours in Hanoi looking for a button to replace one lost from her mother's áo dài. A only gives facts about the author and where the story was published, so it's not plot. B gives the year and the setting, but no events. D explains what an áo dài is without saying what happens in the story.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.598Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Phuong travels through Hanoi's dawn streets for three hours to replace a single button her mother lost from an old áo dài, each vendor stop a small prayer for her mother's forgetting to ease.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"C가 노트의 사건 정보(새벽 하노이, 세 시간, 어머니 아오자이 단추 찾기)를 정확히 종합하여 줄거리를 전달함. A·B·D는 출판/배경/용어 정의만 담아 줄거리가 아님. 해설(한·영) 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스러움. 단일 규칙(줄거리=사건)으로 풀리고 오답은 전형적 오개념(배경·출판 정보를 줄거리로 착각)이라 easy 적합. 사소: D의 \"once wore\"는 노트에서 약간 확장된 표현이나 오답 판정에 영향 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"C만 사건(줄거리)을 전달함. 사소한 점: B의 'capital of Vietnam'과 D의 'once wore'는 노트에 없는 정보지만 오답이라 영향 없음. 오답들은 전형적인 '출판·배경 정보' 함정이라 easy 난이도에 맞음.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-e-094","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-e-095","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"easy","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- \"The Festival Bridge\" is a short story by Nalini Perera.\n- The story is set on a tea estate in the hill country of Sri Lanka.\n- Its main character, Roshan, is a supervisor on the estate.\n- During the harvest festival, a decorative bamboo bridge collapses under the weight of dancing children.\n- Roshan's horror turns to laughter when the children tumble unharmed into the soft grass below.","question":"The student wants to tell readers where Perera's story takes place. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["In Perera's \"The Festival Bridge,\" the main character, Roshan, works as a supervisor.","In Perera's \"The Festival Bridge,\" a decorative bamboo bridge collapses during a harvest festival.","In Perera's \"The Festival Bridge,\" Roshan's horror turns to laughter as the children land safely.","In Perera's \"The Festival Bridge,\" the events unfold on a tea estate in Sri Lanka's hill country."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"목표는 이야기의 배경(장소)을 알리는 것이다. D는 스리랑카 고산 지대의 차 농장이라는 장소를 명시하므로 목표를 달성한다. A는 주인공의 직업만, B는 줄거리 속 사건만, C는 인물의 감정 변화만 전달할 뿐 이야기가 어디에서 일어나는지는 밝히지 않는다. 따라서 정답은 D이다.","explanationEn":"Your goal is to tell readers where the story takes place, which means you need its setting. D names that place directly: a tea estate in Sri Lanka's hill country. A tells you only Roshan's job, B describes an event in the plot, and C describes how Roshan's feelings change. None of those three says where the story happens, so D is the best choice.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.598Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On the Sri Lankan tea estate, supervisor Roshan watches the harvest festival's decorative bridge collapse under the weight of dancing children, and his horror transforms into unexpected comedy as everyone tumbles unharmed into the grass below.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"목표(배경/장소 전달)가 명시적이며, D만 장소 정보를 담고 있어 정답이 확정적이다. 오답 A·B·C는 모두 노트의 정보를 정확히 사용하지만 목표(장소)와 무관해 전형적인 '관련 없는 정확한 정보' 오개념 유형이다. 해설 한/영 모두 D를 일관되게 지지하고 선택지 참조가 정확하며 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 가상의 작품·작가로 저작권 문제 없음. 난이도 easy 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"배경(장소)을 묻는 단일 목표형 문항. 정답 D만 장소를 제시한다. A는 '농장' 언급 없이 직업만 말하고, B는 축제라는 사건을 다루며, C는 감정 변화를 다루므로 모두 목표에서 벗어난 전형적 오답이다. 난이도 easy에 적합하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-e-095","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-transitions-h-096","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"hard","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"The following text is adapted from a short story.\n\nAt dawn, Linh found the envelope wedged beneath her door in the narrow Hanoi alley, its paper gone soft as cloth from the long journey north from Hue. Her husband's brother had not written in twenty years, not since the quarrel at the funeral, and his letter never mentioned it: he described the late monsoon, the price of rice, the ache that had settled in his left knee. ______ each page closed with the same small question—whether the persimmon tree their mother had planted beside the alley gate still bore fruit—and Linh understood that he was asking, as carefully as he could, whether anything between them had survived.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Yet,","Likewise,","Consequently,","For instance,"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"정답 A(Yet,): 앞 문장은 편지가 장마, 쌀값, 무릎 통증 같은 평범한 이야기만 하고 다툼은 꺼내지 않는다는 표면적 내용이다. 마지막 문장은 그 평범함 밑에 깔린 숨은 의도, 즉 관계가 아직 남아 있는지 조심스럽게 묻는 마음을 드러낸다. 표면과 의도가 대조되므로 역접 'Yet'이 맞다.\nB(Likewise,): 감나무 질문도 날씨나 쌀값처럼 집안의 사소한 이야기로 보면 그럴듯하다. 하지만 이 문장의 핵심은 그 질문이 앞의 화제들과 '다르게' 숨은 의미를 품고 있다는 점이므로 유사 관계는 강조점에서 벗어난다.\nC(Consequently,): 다툼을 피했기 때문에 돌려서 물었다는 인과로 읽을 수도 있어 방향은 비슷해 보인다. 그러나 마지막 문장은 앞 문장에서 생긴 결과가 아니다. 사소한 내용과 진심 어린 질문 사이의 대비를 보여 주는 문장이다.\nD(For instance,): 마지막 문장은 날씨, 쌀값, 무릎 통증 같은 일상 묘사의 예시가 아니다. 그래서 앞 내용과 연결되지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The answer is A, \"Yet.\" The sentence before the blank tells you what the letter says on the surface. It covers ordinary things like the monsoon, rice prices, and a sore knee, and it never mentions the quarrel. The last sentence shows the hidden purpose under all that ordinary talk: the brother is carefully asking whether their relationship survived. The surface content and the real intent are in contrast, so you need a contrast word like \"Yet.\"\nB, \"Likewise,\" is wrong. You might treat the persimmon question as one more household detail like the weather. But the point of the sentence is that this question is different from those topics because it carries a deeper meaning.\nC, \"Consequently,\" is wrong. You could guess that he asked indirectly because he avoided the quarrel, but the last sentence isn't a result of the one before it. It sets the trivial details against the heartfelt question.\nD, \"For instance,\" is wrong because the last sentence isn't an example of the everyday details about weather, rice, and his knee.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.599Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["abstract_relation_beyond_surface_contrast","goal_vs_content_discrimination"],"note":"앞 문장(다툼을 언급하지 않고 사소한 일상만 서술)과 뒷 문장(감나무 질문이 사실상 관계 회복 여부를 묻는 숨은 의도)은 표면 내용 대 함축 의도의 대조이므로 'Yet'이 유일하게 적합. 'Likewise'는 감나무 질문을 또 하나의 사소한 집안 화제로 보면 부수적 사실과 연결되지만 핵심 강조점(숨은 의미의 차이)과 어긋나는 양질의 오답. 'Consequently'는 인과 방향 오류, 'For instance'는 예시 관계 오류. 해설은 각 선택지 판단을 일관되게 뒷받침. 지문이 문학적으로 다소 길고 삽입구가 많으나 SAT 문학 지문 수준 범위 내이며, 난이도는 길이가 아니라 표면/함축 대조 식별에서 비롯됨."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["abstract_relation_beyond_surface_contrast","goal_vs_content_discrimination"],"note":"표면적으로는 감나무 질문도 일상적 화제(→Likewise 유인)이지만, 숨은 의도와 평범한 겉내용 사이의 함축적 대조를 읽어야 Yet을 고를 수 있다. Consequently는 인과 방향을 잘못 잡은 오답이다. 지문이 다소 길지만 어휘는 평이하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"batch2-D-cross","gid":"sw-transitions-h-096","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":"transitions_purpose_filter_sentence","recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":"recipe","difficultyStatus":"provisional_ai","review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-098","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In his New Science (1725), the Neapolitan philosopher Giambattista Vico proposed that every nation passes through three recurring ages: an age of gods, an age of heroes, and an age of humans. Many readers remember Vico chiefly for this cyclical scheme, but the evidence he relied on to support it was unusual for his time. Rather than drawing primarily on chronicles of kings and battles, Vico examined how language itself had changed. He argued that the earliest peoples spoke in vivid poetic metaphors, describing thunder, for instance, as the voice of an angry deity, and that only much later did speech become abstract and literal. For Vico, then, the shifting texture of words was not a mere byproduct of historical change but a record of it, preserving traces of how earlier minds had understood the world.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Vico argued that nations pass through three recurring ages, a view that later readers have treated as the most important part of his philosophy.","Vico argued that early peoples spoke in poetic metaphors because they lacked the abstract vocabulary that later historians needed to record events.","Vico argued that changes in language could reveal how past peoples thought, and he used this idea to support his account of history's stages.","Vico argued that chronicles of kings and battles were unreliable, so he replaced them with poetry as the main source for historical study."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 비코의 세 시대 순환론을 소개한 뒤, 그가 이 이론의 근거로 언어의 변화를 살폈고 언어를 과거 사람들의 사고방식을 담은 기록으로 보았다는 점을 핵심으로 제시하므로 C가 정답이다. A는 세 시대 이론 자체는 맞지만, 독자들이 그것을 가장 중요하게 여긴다는 내용은 지문이 넘어서려는 통념일 뿐 요지가 아니다. B는 초기의 은유적 언어라는 세부를 다루지만, 그 이유를 후대 역사가의 필요와 연결한 것은 지문에 근거가 없다. D는 비코가 연대기를 '주로' 사용하지 않았다는 점을 연대기가 신뢰할 수 없다고 주장한 것으로 과장하고, 시를 사료로 삼았다는 내용도 지문과 다르다.","explanationEn":"The text introduces Vico's three-age theory, then focuses on the idea that he supported it by studying how language changed, treating words as a record of how earlier minds understood the world. That makes C correct. A gets the three-age theory right, but the claim that readers see it as his most important idea is just the common view the text moves past, not its main point. B picks up the detail about early metaphorical speech, but the text never ties that speech to what later historians needed. D overstates things: the text says Vico didn't rely \"primarily\" on chronicles, not that he called them unreliable, and it never says he used poetry as his main source.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.599Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — Giambattista Vico's cyclical theory of history and linguistic evolution in eighteenth-century philosophy","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"C는 지문의 전환(\"but the evidence he relied on...\")과 결론 문장(\"a record of it\")을 정확히 종합한다. A는 통념 소개 부분만, D는 '주로'라는 한정을 과장, B는 근거 없는 인과를 추가해 각각 부분적 근거를 지녀 비교 배제가 필요하다. 비코 관련 사실(1725, 나폴리, 세 시대, 시적 지혜) 정확. 해설 한·영 일치."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"C가 '통념 소개 후 전환' 구조의 요지를 정확히 담는다. A는 첫 문장만 훑어 읽으면 고르기 쉬운 함정이고, B와 D는 지문 세부를 왜곡한 그럴듯한 오답이라 medium 난이도에 맞다. 비코에 관한 사실관계(1725년 『새로운 학문』, 신·영웅·인간의 세 시대, 시적 은유)도 정확하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-098","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-099","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In the ninth century, monks copying chants for the Christian liturgy began adding small marks called neumes above the words of the text. These signs showed whether the melody rose or fell, but they did not say by how much, so a singer could use them only to recall a tune already learned by ear from a teacher. Around 1030, the Italian monk Guido of Arezzo promoted a system of horizontal lines, each standing for a fixed pitch, on which neumes could be placed. Because a mark's position on the lines now showed its exact pitch, a trained singer could perform a chant never heard before. Guido claimed his method cut a singer's training from ten years to about one, but its larger effect was that a melody written in one monastery could be sung the same way in another far away, which made widely shared versions of a piece possible.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Neumes were developed so that singers no longer had to learn chants by ear from teachers in their own monasteries.","Guido of Arezzo's main achievement was reducing the training time singers needed from about ten years to about one.","Medieval monks placed neumes on horizontal lines mainly to show whether a melody rose or fell between notes.","Placing neumes on lines that fixed exact pitches let music be read without prior hearing, allowing consistent versions of pieces across distant places."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 음의 높낮이 방향만 보여 주던 네우마가 고정 음높이를 나타내는 선 위에 놓이면서 처음 듣는 곡도 부를 수 있게 되었고, 그 결과 멀리 떨어진 곳에서도 같은 형태로 곡이 불리게 되었다는 흐름을 중심으로 하므로 D가 정답이다. A는 틀렸는데, 지문에 따르면 네우마만으로는 귀로 이미 배운 곡을 떠올리는 데밖에 쓸 수 없었다. B는 지문에 나오는 주장이지만, 지문은 '더 큰 효과'가 따로 있었다고 말하므로 핵심이 아닌 세부 내용이다. C는 상승·하강 표시가 원래 네우마의 기능이었고 선의 목적은 정확한 음높이를 나타내는 것이었으므로 둘을 뒤섞었다.","explanationEn":"The text follows one line of development. Neumes showed only which way a melody moved. Once they were placed on lines that fixed exact pitches, singers could perform unfamiliar chants, and the same melody could be sung the same way in distant monasteries. That makes D correct. A is wrong because the text says neumes alone helped singers only recall tunes they had already learned by ear. B is a claim the text does mention, but the text calls something else the \"larger effect,\" so B is a detail, not the main idea. C mixes up the two stages: showing rise and fall was what neumes did on their own, while the lines were added to show exact pitch.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.599Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — The development of musical notation systems from neumes to staff lines enabling composition standardization","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"직접 검산: 지문의 핵심은 네우마(방향만 표시)→고정 음높이 선 위 배치→초견 가창 가능→'더 큰 효과'로 먼 곳에서도 동일한 판본 공유. D가 이를 정확히 요약. A는 네우마가 '귀로 배운 곡 회상용'이었다는 지문과 모순, B는 지문이 명시적으로 '더 큰 효과'에 종속시킨 세부 사항, C는 네우마의 원래 기능과 선의 기능을 뒤섞음. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 같은 결론과 글자 참조를 가지며 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 역사적 사실(9세기 네우마, 귀도 다레초 c.1030, 10년→1년 훈련 단축 주장)도 통상적 서술과 부합. 오답 중 B·C가 지문 내용에 부분적으로 근거를 두어 비교가 필요하고, '더 큰 효과' 문장을 정독해야 B를 배제할 수 있으므로 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"D가 지문 전체 흐름(네우마의 한계, 보표 선, 처음 보는 곡 가창, 먼 곳에서도 같은 형태로 노래)을 종합한다. B는 지문에 명시된 주장이어서 그럴듯한 오답이고, C는 두 단계를 뒤섞었으며, A는 네우마의 실제 역할과 반대다. 옥에 티로, 정답 D만 다른 선택지보다 길고 구체적이어서 단서가 될 수 있다. 그래도 중간 난이도로 적합하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-099","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-101","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In an 1817 letter to his brothers, John Keats coined the phrase \"negative capability\" to describe a quality he believed great writers possess: the ability to remain \"in uncertainties, mysteries, doubts, without any irritable reaching after fact and reason.\" Many readers have taken the phrase as a simple celebration of vagueness or as permission for poets to ignore ideas altogether. Yet Keats's own example of the quality was Shakespeare, a writer whose plays are dense with argument, and Keats criticized the poet and critic Samuel Taylor Coleridge not for thinking too much but for being unable to let an insight stand unless it fit within a complete philosophical system. Read in this context, negative capability does not reject intellectual engagement; it describes a willingness to explore conflicting perspectives fully without forcing them into a premature resolution.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Keats coined the phrase \"negative capability\" mainly to criticize Coleridge, whose poetry he considered less imaginative than Shakespeare's plays.","Keats's notion of negative capability, though often read as a dismissal of thought, is better understood as a capacity to engage with unresolved ideas without settling them too quickly.","Keats's notion of negative capability, though first described in a private letter, became the central principle of Romantic poetry once his correspondence was published.","Keats's notion of negative capability shows that he valued mystery and doubt more highly than the arguments found in Shakespeare's plays."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 '부정적 수용력'을 모호함 예찬이나 사고의 거부로 읽는 흔한 해석을 소개한 뒤, 셰익스피어와 콜리지의 예를 들어 그것이 상충하는 관점을 성급히 결론짓지 않고 탐구하는 능력이라고 재해석하므로 B가 정답이다. A는 콜리지 비판이 언급되긴 하지만 재해석을 뒷받침하는 근거일 뿐 개념을 만든 주된 목적이 아니며, 상상력 비교도 지문에 없다. C의 서간 출판 이후 낭만주의의 중심 원리가 되었다는 내용은 지문에 나오지 않는다. D는 지문이 바로잡으려는 오독을 되풀이하며, 셰익스피어의 논증은 오히려 그 개념의 본보기로 제시된다.","explanationEn":"The text introduces a common reading of negative capability as praise of vagueness or a rejection of ideas, then uses Shakespeare and Coleridge to argue that it really means exploring conflicting perspectives without forcing an early resolution, so B is correct. A takes the Coleridge criticism, which is only evidence for the reinterpretation, and treats it as Keats's main purpose; the text also never compares how imaginative the two writers are. C makes a claim about publication and influence that the text never mentions. D repeats the very misreading the text corrects, since Shakespeare's argument-filled plays are offered as an example of negative capability, not as something it is opposed to.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.599Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — The aesthetic philosophy of negative capability in John Keats' poetry criticism and Romantic imagination","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"지문의 역사적 사실(1817년 형제들에게 보낸 편지, 인용문, 셰익스피어 예시, 콜리지 비판의 취지) 모두 정확. 정답 B는 지문의 '흔한 오독 → 재해석' 구조를 정확히 요약. A와 D는 지문 속 세부(콜리지 비판, 신비·의혹)를 근거로 삼아 비교가 필요한 매력적 오답이고, C는 지문 밖 주장으로 배제 가능. 한국어·영어 해설 결론과 선택지 참조 일치, 영어 자연스러움. medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"1817년 편지(12월, 형제들에게 보냄)와 인용문은 사실과 맞다. 원문은 'without any irritable reaching after fact & reason'이다. 정답 B는 '흔한 오독 → 재해석' 구조를 정확히 요약한다. A와 D는 지문 속 세부 정보(콜리지, 셰익스피어)를 잘못 활용한 오답이라 비교해야 배제된다. C는 지문에 없는 내용이라 비교적 쉽게 배제된다. 중간 난이도에 적합하다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-101","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-103","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"When Buckminster Fuller began promoting the geodesic dome in the late 1940s, critics often treated it as a curiosity: a spherical lattice of triangles that looked more like a toy than a building. Fuller's interest, however, was not mainly in the dome's unusual appearance. He was drawn to a principle he called \"tensegrity,\" in which a structure gets its stability from a continuous network of tension rather than from heavy walls pressing down on one another. Because each triangle in a geodesic frame spreads loads to its neighbors, the dome can enclose a large space using remarkably little material, and it grows relatively stronger as it grows larger.\n\nLater engineers who designed tensile structures—stretched fabric roofs over stadiums and airports, for example—rarely copied the dome's shape. What they took from Fuller was his way of thinking about forces: the idea that a building could be made light by letting tension, distributed across many members, do the work that mass had traditionally done.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Fuller's geodesic domes were initially dismissed by critics, but later engineers proved the critics wrong by adopting the dome's triangular shape for stadiums and airports.","Fuller's geodesic domes are valued chiefly because their triangular frames allow them to become relatively stronger as they increase in size.","Fuller's geodesic domes influenced later tensile structures mainly because those structures, like the domes, were built to enclose very large public spaces.","Fuller's geodesic domes mattered less for their distinctive form than for a principle of distributing tension that later shaped lightweight building design."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 Fuller의 관심이 돔의 외형이 아니라 장력 분산 원리(tensegrity)에 있었고, 후대 인장 구조 설계자들도 형태가 아닌 그 힘에 대한 사고방식을 이어받았다고 말하므로 D가 정답이다. A는 비평가들의 초기 반응은 맞지만, 후대 엔지니어들이 돔의 형태를 \"거의 따라 하지 않았다\"는 내용과 모순된다. B는 크기가 커질수록 강해진다는 세부 사항만 다룰 뿐, 후대 설계에 미친 영향이라는 두 번째 단락의 핵심을 빠뜨렸다. C는 넓은 공간을 덮는다는 공통점을 영향의 원인으로 들었지만, 지문은 그 원인을 장력 원리로 제시한다.","explanationEn":"The text says Fuller cared less about the dome's look than about tensegrity, the idea of getting stability from tension spread across many members. It then says later tensile designers borrowed that way of thinking about forces, not the dome's shape. That makes D correct. A gets the critics' early reaction right, but it contradicts the text, which says later engineers rarely copied the dome's shape. B picks out one true detail, that the dome gets stronger as it gets bigger, but it leaves out the second paragraph's point about the dome's influence. C says the dome influenced later buildings because they also covered large spaces, but the text says the real reason was the principle of distributed tension.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.599Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — The architectural principles of geodesic domes designed by Buckminster Fuller and tensile structure engineering","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 D 검산 완료: 1문단(외형보다 장력 원리 \"however, not mainly in appearance\") + 2문단(후대 설계자가 형태가 아닌 힘에 대한 사고방식을 차용)을 연결해야 하므로 두 단계 판단이 요구됨. A는 비평가 반응은 맞으나 \"rarely copied the dome's shape\"와 모순, B는 사실인 세부사항만 다룬 범위 축소, C는 넓은 공간이라는 공통점을 원인으로 오도—오답 3개 모두 부분적 근거가 있어 medium 적합. 해설(한·영) 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 참고: 지오데식 돔을 tensegrity 원리의 사례로 다소 단순화해 서술했으나(엄밀히는 Fuller의 돔은 압축 부재 중심), Fuller 자신이 두 개념을 함께 홍보했고 지문이 \"a principle he called\"로 Fuller의 관점으로 한정하고 있어 치명적 사실 오류로 보지 않음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"D는 두 단락을 모두 종합한다. A, B, C는 각각 지문의 일부 근거(비평가의 반응, 크기가 커질수록 강해지는 특성, 넓은 공간)를 담고 있어 medium 수준의 매력적인 오답으로 작동한다. 다만 지오데식 돔을 엄밀한 의미의 텐세그리티 구조로 보기는 어렵다. 그래도 Fuller 자신이 두 개념을 연결했으므로 지문의 서술은 허용 범위 안에 있다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-103","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-104","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Medieval chroniclers often filled their histories with reports passed down from earlier authorities, rarely asking whether those reports were plausible. In the Muqaddimah (1377), the North African scholar Ibn Khaldun argued that this habit had let absurd claims survive for centuries, such as accounts of ancient armies numbering in the hundreds of thousands. A historian, he insisted, must test every report against what is known about how human societies actually function: how many people a region's agriculture could feed, how armies were supplied, how cities grew and declined. Only a report consistent with these patterns deserved belief, however respected its source. To supply such patterns, Ibn Khaldun proposed a new discipline devoted to studying social organization itself, which he called \"ilm al-umran.\" Many modern scholars regard this proposal as an early outline of sociology.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Ibn Khaldun maintained that historical reports should be judged by how well they fit the observable workings of societies, and he proposed a field of study to describe those workings.","Ibn Khaldun maintained that historical reports should be judged chiefly by the reputation of the earlier authorities who transmitted them.","Ibn Khaldun maintained that ancient armies were far smaller than chroniclers claimed because agriculture in North Africa could not have supported them.","Ibn Khaldun maintained that history should be replaced by sociology, a discipline that modern scholars later developed from his ideas."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 이븐 할둔이 역사 보고를 사회가 실제로 작동하는 방식과 대조해 검증해야 한다고 주장하고, 그 기준을 제공하려고 새 학문(ilm al-umran)을 제안했다고 설명하므로 A가 두 요소를 모두 담는다. B는 '출처의 권위와 상관없이'라는 지문 내용과 정반대이다. C는 군대 규모 사례를 과장하고 북아프리카 농업으로 한정한 세부일 뿐 중심 생각이 아니다. D는 역사를 사회학으로 '대체'하자는 주장으로 왜곡했으며, 지문에서 새 학문은 역사 서술을 돕는 도구이다.","explanationEn":"The text says Ibn Khaldun wanted historians to test reports against how societies actually function, and that he proposed a new discipline to supply those patterns, so A captures both parts. B reverses the passage, which says a report should be believed only if plausible \"however respected its source.\" C turns one example into the main point and adds a claim about North African agriculture specifically that the text never makes. D misreads the proposal: the new discipline was meant to support history, not replace it.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.599Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — Ibn Khaldun's muqaddimah and the foundational concepts of historiography and social science methodology","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 A 검산: 지문은 (1) 보고를 사회 작동 방식과 대조해 검증, (2) 그 기준을 위한 새 학문 제안의 두 요소를 담고 있으며 A만 둘 다 포함. B는 \"however respected its source\"와 정반대, C는 사례(군대 규모)를 중심으로 격상하고 '북아프리카 농업'이라는 지문에 없는 한정 추가, D는 '대체'로 왜곡. 이븐 할둔·Muqaddimah(1377)·ilm al-umran·사회학 선구자 평가 모두 사실에 부합. 지문은 자체 작성 산문으로 저작권 의심 없음. 해설(한/영) 모두 정답과 일치하고 선택지 참조 정확, 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 난이도: C·D가 지문 요소를 부분 포함해 비교가 필요하고 B도 표면적으로 그럴듯하여 medium 기준 충족(B는 다소 쉽게 배제되나 전체적으로 적합)."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B는 지문과 정반대여서 쉽게 배제되지만, C(세부 사례+근거 없는 한정)와 D(대체로 왜곡+현대 학자 언급)는 부분적인 근거가 있어 비교가 필요하다. 중간 난이도에 적합하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-104","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-105","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"When Samuel Richardson published Pamela in 1740, he told the story entirely through letters, a method he praised for capturing characters' feelings \"to the moment,\" as events unfolded. Critics have often assumed that the epistolary novel faded once later novelists embraced omniscient narrators, surviving only as a historical curiosity. Yet literary scholar Mira Okonjo argues that the form never truly disappeared; instead, writers repeatedly adapted its core technique—assembling a story from documents that characters themselves produce—to whatever media their own era supplied. Bram Stoker's Dracula (1897) mixes diaries, telegrams, and phonograph transcripts, and recent novels have been composed of emails, text messages, and even social media posts. In each case, Okonjo notes, the documents remain fragmentary and partial, so readers must piece together events that no single writer fully understands, just as Richardson's readers once did.","question":"Based on the text, what is Okonjo's position regarding the epistolary novel?","options":["Its practitioners abandoned Richardson's goal of recording feelings as events unfolded, favoring instead the varied documents made available by new media.","Its practitioners have kept Richardson's basic method of building a story from characters' own writings while changing the kinds of writings they use.","Its practitioners stopped using the form once omniscient narrators became dominant, leaving later document-based novels largely unconnected to Richardson.","Its practitioners have preserved Richardson's reliance on letters specifically, since emails and text messages are simply modern forms of the letter."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"오콘조는 이 형식이 사라진 적이 없고, 작가들이 등장인물 스스로 만든 문서로 이야기를 엮는 핵심 기법은 지키면서 각 시대의 매체에 맞게 바꿔 왔다고 주장하므로 B가 정답이다. A는 매체 변화라는 부분은 맞지만, 지문에는 리처드슨의 목표를 버렸다는 내용이 없고 오히려 연속성을 강조한다. C는 지문 속 비평가들의 가정이며, 오콘조는 바로 이 견해를 반박한다. D는 연속성이라는 점은 맞지만, 일기·전보·음성 녹음 기록 등이 쓰였으므로 '편지만' 고수했다는 말은 틀리다.","explanationEn":"B is correct. Okonjo says the form never disappeared: writers kept its core technique of building a story from documents the characters themselves produce, and they adapted it to whatever media their era offered. A gets the media change right, but the text never says writers gave up Richardson's goal. In fact, it stresses continuity. C describes what the critics assumed, and that is exactly the view Okonjo argues against. D gets the continuity right, but it's wrong to say writers stuck to letters specifically, since Dracula uses diaries, telegrams, and phonograph transcripts.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.599Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — The evolution of the epistolary novel form from Samuel Richardson through contemporary narrative experimentation","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"지문의 \"writers repeatedly adapted its core technique—assembling a story from documents that characters themselves produce—to whatever media their own era supplied\"가 B를 직접 뒷받침한다. A는 '리처드슨의 목표를 버렸다'는 점이 지문과 반대(연속성 강조), C는 오콘조가 반박하는 비평가들의 가정, D는 '편지만'이라는 한정이 Dracula의 일기·전보·축음기 기록 사례와 충돌한다. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 동일한 결론과 선택지 참조를 가지며 모순 없음. Pamela(1740), Dracula(1897)와 그 문서 형식 등 사실 관계 정확. 비평가 견해와 학자 견해의 구분 + 핵심 기법 vs 매체 변화라는 두 단계 판단이 필요하고, A·D가 부분적으로 맞는 근거를 가져 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"A와 D는 각각 부분적으로 맞는 근거가 있는 그럴듯한 오답이고, C는 비평가 견해를 이용한 함정이다. 중간 난이도에 적합하다. Pamela(1740)와 Dracula(1897)에 관한 사실은 정확하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-105","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-106","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Wassily Kandinsky, a pioneer of abstract painting in the early twentieth century, often described his work in musical terms, calling some canvases \"compositions\" and \"improvisations.\" In his 1911 treatise Concerning the Spiritual in Art, he argued that colors act on the viewer much as tones act on a listener: a bright yellow, he claimed, rings out like a trumpet, while a deep blue resembles the low, calm voice of a cello. Some scholars have read these statements as evidence that Kandinsky literally heard sounds when he saw colors, a condition known as synaesthesia. Yet his writings suggest a more deliberate aim. Kandinsky presented the correspondences not as private sensations but as principles a painter could learn and apply, arranging colors and forms on a canvas the way a composer arranges notes, so that a picture could stir emotion without depicting any recognizable object.","question":"According to the text, how did Kandinsky's writings present the connections he drew between colors and musical tones?","options":["As private sensations that he experienced involuntarily and that scholars later confirmed were caused by synaesthesia","As descriptions of specific instruments that he intended viewers to imagine hearing whenever they looked at his canvases","As principles that painters could learn and use to organize a picture's elements so that it affected viewers emotionally","As rules borrowed from contemporary composers that he used to give his paintings recognizable subjects drawn from music"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 칸딘스키가 색-음의 대응을 사적 감각이 아니라 화가가 배우고 적용할 수 있는 원리로 제시했으며, 이를 통해 대상 묘사 없이 감정을 일으키려 했다고 말하므로 C가 정답이다. A는 일부 학자의 해석을 언급하지만 지문은 그의 글이 오히려 '사적 감각이 아님'을 시사한다고 하고, 학자들이 확인했다는 내용도 없다. B는 트럼펫·첼로 비유를 활용하지만 관객이 악기 소리를 상상하길 의도했다는 내용은 없다. D는 음악적 용어 사용과 연결되나 작곡가로부터 규칙을 빌렸다거나 인식 가능한 주제를 부여했다는 것은 지문(대상 묘사 없음)과 반대된다.","explanationEn":"The text says Kandinsky presented the correspondences \"not as private sensations but as principles a painter could learn and apply,\" arranging colors and forms so a picture could stir emotion, so C is correct. A borrows the idea that some scholars mention synaesthesia, but the text says his writings point away from private sensations, and it never says scholars confirmed anything. B builds on the trumpet and cello comparisons, but the text never says he wanted viewers to imagine hearing instruments. D picks up on his musical titles, but nothing says he borrowed rules from composers, and the text says his pictures depicted no recognizable object.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.600Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — Wassily Kandinsky's synaesthetic theory linking color and musical sound in abstract painting composition","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 C는 마지막 문장(\"not as private sensations but as principles a painter could learn and apply... stir emotion\")에 직접 근거함. A는 일부 학자의 synaesthesia 해석을 차용한 매력적 오답, B는 트럼펫·첼로 비유 차용, D는 음악 용어·작곡가 비유 차용으로 모두 부분적 근거가 있어 비교가 필요함. '일부 학자의 해석'과 '글의 실제 의도'를 구분해야 하므로 두 단계 판단 요구 — medium 적합. 사실관계(1911 Concerning the Spiritual in Art, compositions/improvisations 명명, 노랑=트럼펫, 파랑=첼로 비유)도 칸딘스키 저술과 부합. 지문은 독창적 서술로 저작권 문제 없음. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 정답 및 오답 배제 근거가 일치하고 선택지 글자 참조 정확."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 C는 지문 마지막 문장을 거의 그대로 바꿔 쓴 것이라 다소 쉬운 편이지만, A·B·D가 각각 지문 요소(공감각, 트럼펫/첼로, 음악 용어)를 활용해 그럴듯함. medium 범위 내.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-106","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-107","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Medieval scholastic philosophers argued at length over the status of universals—general terms such as \"red\" or \"horse.\" Realists held that such terms name features that really exist in many individual things, while nominalists like William of Ockham insisted that only particular things exist and that general terms are merely labels we apply to groups of them. Historians long treated the dispute as a closed chapter of theology, of interest mainly for what it reveals about the medieval church.\n\nLinguist and historian of ideas Mira Castell contends that this view misses how closely the old debate anticipates modern research on categorization. When cognitive scientists ask whether color categories reflect boundaries in the physical world or boundaries drawn differently by each language, Castell notes, they are restating the realist and nominalist positions in experimental form. In her account, the medieval arguments are not museum pieces but early versions of questions that laboratories are still trying to settle.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Castell argues that modern color experiments have finally shown that the nominalist position on general terms was correct.","Castell argues that historians have studied the medieval debate over general terms mainly to understand the beliefs of the medieval church.","Castell argues that Ockham's view of general terms was more influential in medieval theology than the realist position was.","Castell argues that a medieval dispute often seen as purely historical raises issues that researchers continue to investigate."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 보편자 논쟁이 신학의 닫힌 장으로 여겨져 왔지만, Castell은 이 논쟁이 오늘날 범주화 연구가 여전히 풀려는 질문을 미리 제기했다고 본다는 내용이므로 D가 정답이다. A는 색채 실험을 언급하지만 지문은 실험실이 아직 이 문제를 '해결하려 하고 있다'고 했을 뿐 유명론이 옳다고 판명되었다고 하지 않는다. B는 첫 단락에 나오는 역사가들의 견해일 뿐이고, Castell은 오히려 그 견해를 반박한다. C는 Ockham이 언급되긴 하지만 두 입장의 영향력을 비교하는 내용은 지문에 없다.","explanationEn":"The text explains that historians have treated the debate over universals as a closed chapter of theology, but Castell argues that it anticipates questions modern categorization research is still trying to answer, so D is correct. A picks up on the color experiments, but the text says labs are still trying to settle the question, not that they proved nominalism right. B describes the historians' view from the first paragraph, which is the view Castell actually argues against. C mentions Ockham, but the text never compares how influential the two positions were.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.600Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — The philosophical problem of universals in medieval scholasticism and linguistic categorization debates","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 D는 지문의 핵심(역사가들의 '닫힌 장' 견해 vs Castell의 '여전히 연구 중인 질문' 주장)을 정확히 요약함. A는 색채 실험이라는 지문 세부를 차용하되 '해결하려 하고 있다'를 '해결했다'로 왜곡해 정독 여부를 가르는 좋은 오답, B는 지문에 실제 나오는 역사가들의 견해를 Castell의 주장으로 귀속시킨 오답으로 부분적 근거를 가짐. C는 Ockham 언급을 이용하지만 지문에 없는 비교로 비교적 쉽게 배제됨. 두 단락의 대비를 연결해야 하는 구조로 medium에 적합. 보편자 논쟁·Ockham 유명론 서술은 사실에 부합하며 Castell은 가상의 인물로 보임. 한·영 해설 모두 선택지 참조와 결론이 일치하고 영어 해설에 한글 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"D는 지문의 대조 구조(역사가들의 '닫힌 장'이라는 견해 vs. Castell의 '현재도 이어지는 질문'이라는 주장)를 정확히 요약한다. A는 색채 실험 세부를 왜곡해 과장하고, B는 첫 단락의 역사가 견해를 Castell의 주장으로 잘못 돌린다(부분적 근거가 있음). C는 지문에 없는 영향력 비교를 끌어들인다. 오답 대부분이 지문 세부에 기대고 있어 medium 난이도에 맞는다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-107","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-109","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In the early 1900s, many American critics treated ragtime as disposable entertainment—music for saloons and dance halls, unworthy of comparison with the European concert tradition. Scott Joplin's piano rags complicate that judgment. His \"Maple Leaf Rag\" (1899) follows a carefully balanced multi-strain design, with each sixteen-measure section returning and contrasting in a plan as deliberate as that of a classical march or rondo. __Joplin himself printed a warning on several of his scores that ragtime should never be played fast, insisting that the syncopations needed a measured tempo to be heard clearly.__ That instruction suggests that Joplin regarded his rags not as improvised novelties but as fixed compositions whose structure performers were obligated to respect—precisely the attitude critics reserved for \"serious\" music.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It describes a performance practice that critics cited as proof that ragtime was mere dance-hall entertainment.","It presents a detail about Joplin's scores that the text then uses to support a claim about how he viewed his own work.","It introduces a technical feature of ragtime's form that the text then compares with the structure of classical marches.","It offers evidence that Joplin's rags were more difficult to perform than the classical works favored by critics."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 Joplin이 악보에 '빠르게 치지 말라'는 지시를 적었다는 세부 사실을 제시하고, 다음 문장이 'That instruction'으로 그것을 받아 Joplin이 자기 래그를 존중받아야 할 고정된 작품으로 여겼다는 주장의 근거로 삼으므로 B가 정답이다. A는 비평가들이 래그타임을 깎아내렸다는 내용은 지문에 있지만, 그들이 이 연주 관행을 근거로 들었다는 말은 없다. C는 고전 행진곡과의 비교가 지문에 나오기는 하지만 그 비교는 밑줄 앞 문장에서 이루어지며, 밑줄 문장은 형식이 아니라 템포 지시를 다룬다. D는 연주의 난이도를 비교한 적이 없으므로 지문 범위를 넘어선다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence gives a specific detail: Joplin printed a warning on his scores not to play ragtime fast. The next sentence picks it up with \"That instruction\" and uses it as evidence that Joplin saw his rags as fixed compositions that deserved respect, so B is correct. A is wrong because the text does say critics looked down on ragtime, but it never says they pointed to this performance practice as proof. C is wrong because the comparison with classical marches does appear, but it comes in the sentence before the underlined one, and the underlined sentence is about a tempo instruction, not form. D is wrong because the text never compares how hard Joplin's rags are to play with classical works.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.600Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — The development of ragtime musical form and Scott Joplin's compositional sophistication challenging classical hierarchy","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장(악보의 템포 경고)은 바로 다음 문장 'That instruction suggests...'가 받아 Joplin이 자기 작품을 고정된 작곡으로 여겼다는 주장의 근거가 되므로 B가 정확함. A는 비평가의 폄하(지문 내 존재)를 끌어오지만 비평가가 이 관행을 근거로 삼았다는 언급 없음, C는 고전 행진곡 비교(지문 내 존재)를 끌어오지만 그 비교는 앞 문장의 형식 설명에 속함, D는 난이도 비교 부재—오답 구조가 medium 기준 충족. 사실 관계(Maple Leaf Rag 1899, 16마디 다중 스트레인 구조, Joplin의 'Don't play this piece fast' 경고) 모두 정확. 한국어·영어 해설 결론 및 글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 지문은 독창적 서술로 저작권 우려 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"Joplin의 'Do not play this piece fast' 경고는 실제 사실이다. 오답 A와 C는 지문 요소를 부분적으로 활용하고 있어 서로 비교해 봐야 배제할 수 있으므로 medium 난이도에 맞다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-109","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-111","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In Plato's early dialogues, Socrates rarely delivers a lesson. Instead, he asks an interlocutor to define a concept such as courage or piety, then poses questions that expose contradictions in each proposed definition. Many modern instructors cite these exchanges as a model for discussion-based teaching, in which students reach understanding by answering rather than listening. __Yet the dialogues themselves seldom end in understanding: the Euthyphro, for example, closes with its title character hurrying away, no closer to defining piety than when he began.__ Some scholars argue that this unresolved ending is the point, since Socrates' aim was to replace false confidence with an awareness of one's own ignorance, an outcome that teachers who prize tidy conclusions may overlook.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It gives an example showing how Socrates' questions led an interlocutor to a correct definition of a concept.","It offers evidence that modern instructors have misread which dialogues best represent Socrates' method.","It identifies a flaw in Socrates' reasoning that later scholars have tried to correct.","It introduces a feature of the dialogues that complicates the way the method is often applied in classrooms."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 \"Yet\"으로 시작해, 현대 교사들이 학생이 이해에 도달하는 모델로 대화편을 인용한다는 앞 문장과 달리 대화편이 대개 결론 없이 끝난다는 점을 제시하며, 마지막 문장은 이 미해결이 의도된 것이고 깔끔한 결론을 중시하는 교사들이 놓칠 수 있다고 설명한다. 따라서 D가 정답이다. A는 Euthyphro가 정의에 도달하지 못했다는 내용과 반대된다. B는 교사들을 언급하지만, 교사들이 어떤 대화편을 골랐는지가 아니라 결말의 성격이 쟁점이다. C는 결론이 없다는 점을 소크라테스 추론의 결함으로 보지만, 지문은 그것이 의도된 목적일 수 있다고 본다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence begins with \"Yet.\" It contrasts the earlier claim that teachers use the dialogues as a model for reaching understanding with the fact that the dialogues usually end without any resolution. The final sentence then says this lack of resolution may be the point, which teachers who prize tidy conclusions may miss, so D is correct. A is wrong because Euthyphro gets no closer to a definition at all. B mentions teachers, but the issue is how the dialogues end, not which dialogues teachers chose. C treats the missing conclusion as a flaw in Socrates' reasoning, while the text suggests it may have been his aim.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.600Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — The Socratic method as depicted in Platonic dialogues and its influence on philosophical pedagogy","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 \"Yet\"으로 전환해 교사들이 모델로 삼는 방법과 대화편의 미해결 결말 사이의 긴장을 도입하며, 마지막 문장이 이를 교사들이 놓칠 수 있는 지점으로 연결하므로 D가 정확하다. A는 Euthyphro가 정의에 도달하지 못했다는 본문과 모순, B는 '어떤 대화편'을 골랐는지가 쟁점이 아니며, C는 지문이 미해결을 의도된 목적으로 제시하므로 배제된다. B·C는 부분적 근거(교사 언급, 부정적 전환)를 가져 비교가 필요하고 A도 '예시 제시' 형식으로 그럴듯해 medium 기준에 부합. Euthyphro 결말·초기 대화편의 아포리아적 성격 등 사실 관계도 정확하다. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 D를 일관되게 지지하며 선택지 참조가 일치한다."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"To find D, the reader has to link the 'Yet' contrast to the last sentence. B and C both rest on partly true points (teachers, the unresolved ending), so they have to be compared before they can be ruled out. A contradicts the text directly, but it still makes sense as a choice. Euthyphro's ending is described accurately.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-111","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-m-113","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Before the twelfth century, builders who wanted taller churches faced a stubborn problem: the outward thrust of a heavy stone vault could push the supporting walls apart. The flying buttress, an external half-arch that carries this thrust across open air to a massive pier standing well away from the building______ solved the problem with remarkable economy. Relieved of much of the load, walls could be made thinner and opened up for the vast stained-glass windows that define cathedrals such as Chartres.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":[", and it",",","; it","—it"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"\"an external half-arch ... away from the building\"는 주어 \"The flying buttress\"를 설명하는 동격 삽입구이고, 쉼표로 시작했으므로 쉼표로 닫아야 주어와 동사 \"solved\"가 바로 이어진다. 따라서 B가 정답이다. A는 \", and it\"으로 새 절을 만들어 앞의 \"The flying buttress\"가 동사 없는 주어로 남는다. C는 세미콜론 앞부분이 동사 없는 불완전한 절이 되어 세미콜론을 쓸 수 없다. D는 쉼표로 연 삽입구를 대시로 닫아 짝이 맞지 않고, \"it\"이 주어를 중복시켜 앞부분이 역시 동사를 잃는다.","explanationEn":"The phrase \"an external half-arch ... away from the building\" is an appositive that describes the subject \"The flying buttress.\" It opens with a comma, so it has to close with a comma too, which lets the subject connect directly to its verb, \"solved.\" That makes B correct. A uses \", and it\" to start a new clause, which leaves \"The flying buttress\" as a subject with no verb. C puts a semicolon after an incomplete clause that has no verb, and a semicolon needs a complete clause on each side. D closes a comma-opened appositive with a dash, so the pair doesn't match, and \"it\" repeats the subject, which again leaves the first part without a verb.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.600Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — The architectural innovation of the flying buttress in Gothic cathedral construction and engineering principles","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"직접 검산: \"The flying buttress, [동격구], solved ...\" 구조에서 쉼표로 연 동격 삽입구를 쉼표로 닫는 B만 주어-동사 연결을 유지함. A·C·D는 모두 앞부분을 동사 없는 조각으로 남기거나(A, D) 세미콜론 앞 불완전 절(C)을 만듦. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 동일 결론과 글자 참조, 오류 없음. 사실관계(12세기 플라잉 버트레스, 샤르트르 스테인드글라스) 문제 없음. 긴 동격구로 주어-동사 거리를 벌려 훑어 읽으면 A/D에 끌리도록 설계되어 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"긴 동격구 안에 관계절('that carries...')과 분사구('standing...')가 들어 있어서, 주어와 동사 'solved'가 어떻게 연결되는지 끝까지 따라가야 풀린다. 오답 셋은 모두 'it'을 넣어 그럴듯한 독립절을 만든다. 다만 주어 'The flying buttress'에 동사가 없다는 점을 알아채면 모두 배제되므로, 오답 간 변별력은 다소 균일하다. 그래도 medium 수준에는 적합하다. 첫 열두 세기 이전의 건축 문제와 Chartres 관련 서술도 사실과 맞는다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-boundaries-m-113","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-m-116","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In The Role of the Reader (1979), semiotician Umberto Eco distinguished between \"closed\" texts, which steer a reader toward a single predetermined response, and \"open\" texts, which invite many competing interpretations. Yet Eco, whose own scholarship ranged from medieval aesthetics to the conventions of spy novels, insisted that even the most open text has ______ a reader cannot, for example, decide that a novel set in a fourteenth-century monastery is secretly a recipe book.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["limits:","limits,","limits; and","limits, that"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"긴 삽입구(whose own scholarship ... spy novels)를 걷어내면 주절은 'Eco insisted that even the most open text has limits'이고, 빈칸 뒤 'a reader cannot ... decide ...'는 주어와 동사를 갖춘 독립절이다. 뒤 절이 '한계'의 구체적 예시이므로 두 독립절을 연결하며 설명을 도입하는 콜론을 쓴 A가 정답이다. B는 쉼표만으로 두 독립절을 이어 쉼표 오용(comma splice)이 된다. C는 세미콜론 뒤에 등위접속사 and를 덧붙여 불필요하게 이중 연결을 만든다. D는 that 뒤에 이미 완전한 절이 와서 관계절로 볼 수 없고, 비필수 쉼표 뒤의 that도 허용되지 않는다.","explanationEn":"If you set aside the long interrupting phrase (whose own scholarship ... spy novels), the main clause is \"Eco insisted that even the most open text has limits,\" and the words after the blank, \"a reader cannot ... decide ...,\" make up another independent clause with its own subject and verb. That second clause gives a specific example of the limits, so a colon, which joins two independent clauses and introduces an explanation, is correct, and that makes A the answer. B links two independent clauses with only a comma, which is a comma splice. C puts a semicolon and the conjunction \"and\" together, so the two clauses get joined twice. D doesn't work because \"that\" is followed by an already complete clause, so it can't start a relative clause, and \"that\" also isn't used after a comma that sets off nonessential information.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.600Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — Umberto Eco's semiotics theory and the interpretation of cultural signs in postmodern textual analysis","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"검산: 빈칸 앞 'even the most open text has limits'와 뒤 'a reader cannot ... decide ...'는 모두 독립절이며 뒤 절이 앞 절의 예시이므로 콜론(A)이 적절. B는 comma splice, C는 SAT 관례상 세미콜론+and 이중 연결, D는 that 뒤 완전절로 비문. 사실관계(Eco 1979, open/closed text, 중세 미학~스파이 소설 연구)도 정확. 긴 삽입구를 걷어내고 절 구조를 파악해야 하는 두 단계 판단이 필요해 medium에 부합. 참고: C의 '; and'는 일부 문체 규범에서 내부 쉼표가 있는 절에 허용되나 SAT 기준으로는 오답으로 처리되므로 문제 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"긴 삽입구 때문에 주절 구조를 찾아야 하고, 뒤 절이 독립절인지도 확인해야 하는 두 단계 판단 문항이다. 오답 B(comma splice)와 C(세미콜론+and)는 부분적으로 그럴듯해 비교해야 배제된다. 사실관계(Eco, 1979년, 수도원 소설 및 첩보소설 연구 언급)에도 문제가 없다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-boundaries-m-116","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-m-117","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In a fugue, a single melodic idea called the subject is introduced by one voice and then taken up, one after another, by the remaining voices. Bach's fugues in The Well-Tempered Clavier follow a strict plan of entries: the second voice, which enters a fifth higher than the first and is known as the ______ the first voice continues with a countersubject designed to fit against it.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["answer; meanwhile","answer, states the subject while","answer states the subject, while","answer, states the subject; while"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"주어 'the second voice' 뒤에 비필수 삽입절 'which enters ... known as the answer'가 쉼표로 열렸으므로, 'answer' 뒤에도 쉼표로 닫은 다음 동사 'states'가 와야 한다. 그 뒤 'while'은 종속절을 이끌므로 쉼표 없이 이어져도 된다. 따라서 B가 정답이다. A는 삽입절을 닫지 않고 주어에 동사도 주지 않은 채 세미콜론을 써서 앞부분이 독립절이 되지 못한다. C는 삽입절을 닫는 쉼표가 빠져 'which' 절이 끝나는 지점이 불분명하다. D는 삽입절은 바르게 닫았지만, 세미콜론 뒤 'while ...'이 종속절일 뿐이라 독립절이 아니어서 틀렸다.","explanationEn":"The subject \"the second voice\" is followed by a nonessential clause, \"which enters ... known as the answer,\" and that clause opens with a comma. So it needs a closing comma after \"answer,\" and then the main verb \"states\" has to follow. \"While\" begins a dependent clause, so it can come right after without a comma. That makes B correct. A never closes the clause or gives the subject a verb, so the part before its semicolon isn't an independent clause. C leaves out the closing comma, so it isn't clear where the \"which\" clause ends. D closes the clause correctly, but the part after its semicolon (\"while ...\") is only a dependent clause, not an independent one, so the semicolon is wrong.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.600Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — The compositional structure of fugal form in Johann Sebastian Bach's mathematical music architecture","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"검산: 주어 'the second voice' + 비필수 which절(쉼표로 열림) → 'answer,'로 닫고 본동사 'states' 필요. B만 성립. A는 세미콜론 앞이 동사 없는 단편, C는 삽입절 닫는 쉼표 누락, D는 세미콜론 뒤가 종속절. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 정답 B 및 오답 근거와 일치하며 영어 자연스러움. 푸가의 answer가 5도 위로 진입하고 첫 성부가 countersubject를 이어간다는 음악 사실도 통상 설명과 부합. 삽입절 경계 인식 + 세미콜론 규칙의 두 단계 판단이 필요하고 C·D가 부분적으로 그럴듯해 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B를 넣으면 'the second voice, which ... answer, states the subject while the first voice continues ...'가 되어 문법적으로 맞다. 정답을 고르려면 두 단계 판단이 필요하다. 하나는 삽입절을 닫는 쉼표이고, 다른 하나는 while 종속절 앞의 구두점이다. C와 D는 각각 둘 중 한 요소만 맞아서 비교해야 배제된다. 따라서 medium 난이도에 적합하다. 푸가의 answer가 5도 위에서 들어온다는 설명도 사실과 맞는다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-boundaries-m-117","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-cross_text_connections-e-119","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Cross-Text Connections","difficulty":"easy","skill":"cross_text_connections","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Text 1\nMany art historians describe the minaret mainly as a symbol. In their view, the tall tower rising above a mosque was built to mark the building as a place of worship and to show the power of the rulers who paid for it. Its height, they argue, was about meaning, not use.\n\nText 2\nBefore loudspeakers, the muezzin had to climb the minaret five times a day to call people to prayer. Tests in old mosques show that a voice from the top of a tower travels much farther over rooftops than a voice from the ground. For this reason, the minaret's height was first of all a practical answer to the problem of being heard across a city.","question":"Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the art historians' view described in Text 1?","options":["By arguing that the minaret's height mattered mostly because it showed the power of the rulers who paid for it","By arguing that the minaret's height mattered mostly because it made the mosque look different from nearby homes","By arguing that the minaret's height mattered mostly because loudspeakers later made the tower unnecessary","By arguing that the minaret's height mattered mostly because it helped the muezzin's voice reach distant listeners"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"Text 1은 미나렛의 높이가 쓰임이 아니라 상징을 위한 것이라고 보고, Text 2는 높이가 소리를 도시 전체에 전달하는 실용적 해결책이었다고 주장하므로 정답은 D이다. A는 Text 1의 견해를 그대로 되풀이한 것이라 Text 2의 반응이 될 수 없다. B 역시 건물을 구별하는 상징적 기능으로, Text 2가 강조하는 점이 아니다. C는 Text 2가 확성기를 언급하긴 하지만 높이가 중요했던 이유로 제시한 것이 아니다.","explanationEn":"Text 1 says the minaret's height was about meaning, not use, while Text 2 says the height was mainly a practical way to make the call to prayer heard across a city, so D is correct. A just repeats Text 1's own view, so it can't be how Text 2's author would push back. B also describes a symbolic purpose (marking the building), which is not what Text 2 stresses. C mentions loudspeakers, but Text 2 brings them up only to describe the time before them, not as the reason height mattered.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.600Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"D","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — The architectural symbolism of minarets in Islamic mosque design and muezzin acoustic function","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"Text 2의 마지막 문장(\"first of all a practical answer to the problem of being heard across a city\")이 D를 직접 뒷받침한다. A는 Text 1 견해 반복, B는 상징적 기능, C는 확성기 세부사항 오용으로 전형적 오개념 역할을 하며 규칙(두 지문의 핵심 주장 대조)을 알면 즉시 배제된다. 한·영 해설 결론 및 글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 단일 단계 추론, 평이한 어휘로 easy에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"Text 2가 실용적 기능을 직접 밝히고 있어 한 단계 추론으로 풀린다. A·B는 Text 1의 상징적 견해를 옮긴 오답이고, C는 지문에 나오는 단어를 이용한 함정이다. 모두 전형적인 오답 유형이다. 다만 C가 문장 구조상 다소 어색해 쉽게 배제될 수 있다. '흔히 ~로 묘사된다'는 문장과 음향 실험 부분은 지나친 일반화일 수 있지만, 사실 오류로 볼 수준은 아니다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-cross_text_connections-e-119","intendedSkill":"cross_text_connections","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-h-120","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"hard","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- French poet Charles Baudelaire published the essay \"The Painter of Modern Life\" in 1863.\n- In it, he defined modernity as \"the transient, the fleeting, the contingent,\" which he called one half of art.\n- The other half of art, he argued, is \"the eternal and the immovable.\"\n- Baudelaire's model artist was the flâneur, an observer who wanders city crowds while remaining detached from them.\n- Baudelaire believed the flâneur's task was to extract the eternal from the transitory scenes of urban life.","question":"The student wants to explain how Baudelaire's ideal observer related the two halves of art he described. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["For Baudelaire, the flâneur, wandering detached through city crowds, was meant to draw \"the eternal and the immovable\" out of the transient, fleeting scenes he observed.","For Baudelaire, the flâneur was an observer who wandered city crowds while remaining detached from the people around him.","For Baudelaire, whose essay \"The Painter of Modern Life\" appeared in 1863, modernity was \"the transient, the fleeting, the contingent.\"","For Baudelaire, the flâneur rejected the fleeting scenes of the city so that he could devote himself solely to \"the eternal and the immovable.\""],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"정답 A: 목표는 플라뇌르가 예술의 두 반쪽을 어떻게 연결했는지 설명하는 것이다. A는 플라뇌르라는 인물과 두 반쪽(영원한 것과 덧없는 것)을 함께 담고, 덧없는 것에서 영원한 것을 '끌어낸다'는 관계까지 보여 준다.\nB: 플라뇌르에 대한 사실만 있고 예술의 두 반쪽은 빠져 있어 목표를 절반만 달성한다.\nC: 출판 연도와 모더니티의 정의라는 두 사실을 합쳤지만 플라뇌르도 두 반쪽의 관계도 나오지 않아 목표와 무관하다.\nD: 플라뇌르가 덧없는 장면을 '거부했다'는 내용은 노트에 없고, 오히려 그런 장면에서 영원한 것을 추출한다는 노트의 내용과 정반대여서 사실을 왜곡한다.","explanationEn":"Correct answer A: Your goal is to explain how the flâneur connected the two halves of art. A names the flâneur and both halves (the eternal and the transient). It also states the relationship between them: he draws the eternal out of fleeting scenes.\nB: This gives only the facts about the flâneur. It leaves out the two halves of art, so it meets only half of the goal.\nC: This combines two facts, the essay's date and the definition of modernity. But it never mentions the flâneur or how the two halves relate, so this pairing doesn't serve the goal.\nD: The notes never say the flâneur rejected fleeting scenes. In fact, they say he extracted the eternal from those scenes, so D distorts the notes.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.600Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["multi_source_goal_integration","relation_direction_judgment"],"note":"정답 A는 노트 2·3·4·5를 종합해 플라뇌르가 덧없는 것에서 영원한 것을 '추출'한다는 관계를 정확히 서술함. B는 플라뇌르 사실만(한쪽), C는 목표와 무관한 사실 조합, D는 노트에 없는 '거부'를 삽입해 관계 방향을 뒤집은 매력적 오답으로, 단순 사실 선택이 아니라 관계의 방향 판별을 요구함. 1863년 출판, 인용문 등 사실 관계도 정확. 해설은 정답과 오답 근거를 일관되게 설명함."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["multi_source_goal_integration","relation_direction_judgment"],"note":"A는 노트 2·3·4·5를 하나로 묶어 '덧없는 것에서 영원한 것을 끌어낸다'는 관계를 정확히 보여 준다. D는 관계 방향을 거꾸로 뒤집은 매력적 오답이라 관계 방향 판별을 요구한다. 다만 정답 A만 두 반쪽을 모두 담고 있어 키워드만 대조해도 고를 수 있으므로 hard 정도는 중간보다 조금 높은 수준이다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"batch2-D-cross","gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-h-120","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":"rhetorical_synthesis_dual_fact_merge","recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":"recipe","difficultyStatus":"provisional_ai","review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-h-121","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"hard","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- Anamorphosis is a technique in which an image is deliberately distorted so that it appears correctly proportioned only from one specific viewpoint or with a special device.\n- The technique grew out of Renaissance linear perspective, which used geometric projection to map three-dimensional space onto a flat surface.\n- Anamorphic artists extended those same projection rules to an extreme, stretching an image along lines converging toward an unusually oblique viewing position.\n- Hans Holbein the Younger's 1533 painting The Ambassadors contains a smeared shape that resolves into a human skull when viewed from the painting's lower right side.\n- Later artists produced \"mirror anamorphoses,\" which are corrected by reflecting them in a cylindrical mirror placed on the image.","question":"The student wants to emphasize how anamorphosis depended on an existing artistic method. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["In Hans Holbein the Younger's 1533 painting The Ambassadors, a smeared shape resolves into a human skull only when it is viewed from the painting's lower right side.","Anamorphosis was rooted in Renaissance linear perspective: artists took that method's geometric projection rules and pushed them to an extreme, stretching images toward an unusually oblique viewpoint.","Anamorphosis, which emerged during the Renaissance, includes distorted images seen from one viewpoint, Holbein's hidden skull, and later images corrected by cylindrical mirrors.","Anamorphosis later took the form of mirror anamorphoses, distorted images that are corrected by reflecting them in a cylindrical mirror placed on the image."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"정답 B: 목표는 아나모포시스가 기존 기법(선형 원근법)에 의존했다는 점을 강조하는 것이다. B는 원근법의 기하학적 투영 규칙을 극단으로 확장했다는 2·3번 메모를 결합해 그 의존 관계를 직접 보여 준다.\nA: 홀바인 그림이라는 구체적 사례만 제시하는 지나치게 세부적인 문장으로, 어떤 기존 방법에 의존했는지는 말하지 않는다.\nC: 정의·사례·거울 변형을 나열한 지나치게 포괄적인 개관이라 초점을 잃었고, 원근법과의 관계도 빠져 있다.\nD: 목표와 무관한 후대의 거울 아나모포시스를 강조한다. 이는 기존 기법에 의존한 점이 아니라 이후의 발전에 관한 내용이다.","explanationEn":"Correct answer, B: The goal is to emphasize that anamorphosis depended on an existing method. B connects it to Renaissance linear perspective and explains that artists pushed that method's projection rules to an extreme. This combines notes 2 and 3.\nA: This is too narrow. It gives only one example, Holbein's skull, and never names the method that anamorphosis depended on.\nC: This is too broad. It surveys several aspects of the technique, so it loses focus, and it leaves out linear perspective entirely.\nD: This focuses on a different note. Mirror anamorphoses were a later development, so they don't show what anamorphosis grew out of.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.601Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["multi_source_goal_integration","purpose_scope_calibration"],"note":"목표(기존 기법 의존성 강조)가 명확하고, 정답 B는 2·3번 메모를 하나의 문장으로 통합해 선형 원근법→아나모포시스의 의존 관계를 정확히 보여 준다. A는 홀바인 사례만 담은 과잉 구체, C는 정의·사례·후대 변형을 나열한 과잉 포괄(르네상스 언급으로 유인력 있음), D는 목표와 무관한 후대 발전. 홀바인 1533년 The Ambassadors·해골·원통 거울 아나모포시스 등 사실 관계도 정확. 해설은 정답·오답 모두 논리적으로 뒷받침하며 모순 없음. 다만 목표→메모 2·3 매핑이 비교적 직접적이어서 hard 중에서는 난도가 높지 않은 편."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":[],"note":"정답 B는 2·3번 메모를 종합하고 있다. 다만 B만 'linear perspective'와 'method'를 언급해 목표에 쓰인 'existing artistic method'와 어휘가 바로 대응되고, 다른 선택지는 모두 원근법을 전혀 언급하지 않는다. 그래서 키워드 대응만으로 답이 정해진다. 범위를 가늠하거나 확실성 수준을 구분하는 등의 추가 사고가 필요 없어 전형적인 medium 수준이다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"batch2-D-cross","gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-h-121","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":"rhetorical_synthesis_goal_scope_match","recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":"recipe","difficultyStatus":"provisional_ai","review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-122","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Early studies of stereotype threat showed that women who were reminded of a stereotype about gender and math before a test scored lower than women who were not reminded. Many researchers first assumed that the reminder simply lowered the women's motivation or confidence. Psychologist Toni Schmader and her colleagues offered a different account based on cognitive load theory. They noted that solving multistep math problems depends heavily on working memory, the limited mental space used to hold and manipulate information. In their experiments, women under threat did worse on working-memory tasks as well as on math problems, and the more working memory they lost, the lower their math scores fell. The researchers argued that worrying about confirming the stereotype and trying to suppress that worry take up mental resources the problems themselves would otherwise use. If so, a tool that lightens this extra mental work, such as teaching test takers that anxiety is a normal reaction to a hard task, should reduce the performance gap, and later studies have found that it often does.","question":"According to the text, what did Schmader and her colleagues propose to explain why stereotype reminders hurt women's math scores?","options":["The reminders mainly lowered women's motivation, which made them less willing to finish multistep problems.","The reminders made women less confident, which led them to choose easier strategies that produced more errors.","The reminders set off worry and attempts to control it, which used up mental capacity needed to solve the problems.","The reminders made the math problems themselves seem harder, which raised the amount of working memory the problems required."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문에 따르면 Schmader 연구진은 고정관념을 확인하게 될까 걱정하고 그 걱정을 억누르려는 노력이 문제 풀이에 써야 할 작업 기억을 차지한다고 주장했으므로 C가 정답이다. A는 동기 저하를 말하는데, 이는 연구자들이 처음에 가정했던 설명이고 Schmader 연구진이 제시한 설명과는 다르다. B도 자신감 저하라는 초기 가정에 기대고 있으며, 더 쉬운 전략을 고른다는 내용은 지문에 나오지 않는다. D는 작업 기억이라는 개념을 쓰지만 문제의 요구량이 늘었다고 말하는데, 지문은 걱정이 가용 자원을 줄인다고 했을 뿐 문제가 요구하는 양이 늘었다고 하지 않았다.","explanationEn":"C is correct. The text says Schmader's team argued that worrying about confirming the stereotype, and trying to suppress that worry, takes up mental resources the problems would otherwise use. A is wrong because lowered motivation is the explanation researchers first assumed, not the one Schmader's team proposed. B also relies on that early confidence-based view, and the text never mentions anyone choosing easier strategies. D uses the idea of working memory but says the problems demanded more of it. The text instead says worry reduced the working memory available, not that the problems became more demanding.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.601Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"social science research — Stereotype threat effect on mathematical performance in women and cognitive load theory implications","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 C는 지문의 \"worrying about confirming the stereotype and trying to suppress that worry take up mental resources the problems themselves would otherwise use\"를 정확히 재진술. A·B는 지문에 명시된 초기 가정(motivation/confidence)을 Schmader의 설명으로 오귀속시키는 그럴듯한 오답이고, D는 working memory 용어를 차용하되 자원 감소 대 요구량 증가라는 미묘한 차이로 배제되므로 두 단계 판단 요구 충족. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. Schmader 연구 묘사(working memory mediation, 2003/2008)와 anxiety-reappraisal 개입 효과도 실제 문헌과 부합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 C는 지문의 'worrying ... and trying to suppress that worry take up mental resources'를 그대로 바꿔 말한 것이다. A·B는 초기 가정을 활용한 오답이고, D는 작업 기억 개념을 비틀어 만든 오답이라 서로 비교해 봐야 배제된다. medium 난이도에 적합하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-122","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-123","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In 1968, psychologists Robert Rosenthal and Lenore Jacobson reported that elementary students whom teachers had been told were about to \"bloom\" intellectually showed larger IQ gains over a school year than their classmates, even though the \"bloomers\" had actually been chosen at random. The finding, dubbed the Pygmalion effect, was widely taken to show that teacher expectations can powerfully reshape student achievement. Later researchers, however, were more cautious. When education scholar Lee Jussim and colleagues reviewed decades of follow-up studies, they found that teacher expectations do predict student outcomes, but mostly because teachers' judgments are fairly accurate reflections of students' existing abilities. The portion of student achievement actually caused by teachers' beliefs turned out to be real but small, though somewhat larger for students from groups that teachers tended to stereotype negatively.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Research showing that teachers' beliefs strongly shape student achievement has been confirmed by later studies, especially for students who face negative stereotypes.","Follow-up studies revealed that the Pygmalion effect was produced entirely by flaws in how Rosenthal and Jacobson randomly selected their students.","Teachers' expectations are generally inaccurate, which explains why they have only a small influence on how students actually perform.","Later research suggests that teacher expectations influence student achievement less than an early study implied, since those expectations largely mirror students' actual abilities."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 1968년 연구가 교사 기대의 강력한 영향을 보여 준 것으로 받아들여졌지만, 이후 연구에서 그 기대가 대체로 학생의 실제 능력을 정확히 반영하며 기대 자체가 일으키는 효과는 작다는 결과가 나왔다고 설명한다. 이 두 정보를 연결한 D가 정답이다. A는 고정관념 집단에서 효과가 더 크다는 세부는 맞지만, '강한 영향이 확인되었다'는 것은 지문의 결론과 반대다. B는 효과가 '전적으로' 오류라고 하지만 지문은 효과가 실재하되 작다고 한다. C는 효과가 작다는 점은 맞지만, 교사의 판단이 '부정확하다'고 한 것은 지문에서 '상당히 정확하다'고 한 것과 반대다.","explanationEn":"The text says the 1968 study was taken as proof that teacher expectations powerfully shape achievement, but later reviews found that those expectations mostly reflect students' real abilities, and the part actually caused by teachers' beliefs is small. D links these two ideas, so it's the correct answer. A gets one detail right (the effect is larger for stereotyped students), but it says the strong effect was confirmed, which is the opposite of the text's conclusion. B says the effect came entirely from flaws, yet the text calls the effect real, just small. C is right that the influence is small, but it calls teachers' judgments inaccurate, while the text describes them as fairly accurate.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.601Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"social science research — Pygmalion effect in classroom settings and teacher expectation influence on student achievement outcomes","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"지문 요지(초기 연구의 과대 해석 → 후속 연구: 기대는 실제 능력 반영, 인과 효과는 실재하나 작음)를 D가 정확히 종합함. A(고정관념 집단 세부만 맞음), C(효과가 작다는 점만 맞음)는 부분 정답 근거를 가진 오답이고 B도 '무작위 선정' 언급으로 그럴듯함. Rosenthal & Jacobson(1968), Jussim & Harber(2005) 메타 리뷰 내용과 부합하여 사실 오류 없음. 한·영 해설 모두 결론·선택지 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"Rosenthal & Jacobson(1968)과 Jussim의 리뷰 내용이 실제 연구와 맞음. A·C는 지문 일부에 근거가 있어 비교해야 배제되고, B는 '전적으로'라는 표현 때문에 배제됨. medium 난이도에 적합함.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-123","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-125","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Psychologist Lev Vygotsky argued that a child's learning is best understood not by what the child can already do alone but by the gap between that independent performance and what the child can accomplish with guidance from a more knowledgeable partner. He called this gap the zone of proximal development. Later researchers, building on his ideas, introduced the term \"scaffolding\" to describe the temporary support a tutor offers within that zone, such as breaking a task into steps or modeling a strategy.\n\nEducational researchers have since cautioned that scaffolding is often misapplied. Some teachers keep the same level of help in place long after students have mastered a skill, which can make learners dependent on the support rather than independent. Researchers stress that effective scaffolding requires the tutor to watch the learner closely and withdraw assistance gradually as competence grows, so that responsibility for the task shifts to the student.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Vygotsky's zone of proximal development has been replaced in classrooms by scaffolding, a method that measures what students can do without any help.","An approach to teaching grounded in Vygotsky's theory works only when the help it provides is adjusted and reduced as the learner becomes more capable.","Teachers who break tasks into steps and model strategies tend to make their students dependent on outside help rather than independent.","Vygotsky believed that assessing what children can accomplish alone is the most accurate way to understand how they learn."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 비고츠키의 근접발달영역 개념에서 나온 스캐폴딩을 소개한 뒤, 학습자의 역량이 커질수록 도움을 점차 줄여야 효과가 있다고 강조하므로 B가 중심 내용이다. A는 스캐폴딩이 개념을 대체했다고 하고 혼자 할 수 있는 것을 측정한다고 하는데, 지문은 스캐폴딩을 그 영역 안에서 주는 지원으로 설명한다. C는 의존성 문제를 언급하지만 지문은 단계 나누기 자체가 아니라 도움을 거두지 않는 것이 문제라고 본다. D는 비고츠키의 주장과 반대로, 그는 혼자 하는 수행이 아니라 그 차이에 주목했다.","explanationEn":"The text introduces scaffolding as support given within Vygotsky's zone of proximal development, then stresses that it only works when tutors pull back their help as the learner gets more capable. That makes B the main idea. A is wrong on two counts: the text never says scaffolding replaced the zone, and scaffolding is support offered inside that zone, not a way of measuring what students can do alone. C picks up on the dependency concern, but the text blames keeping help in place too long, not breaking tasks into steps itself. D reverses Vygotsky's view, since he focused on the gap between solo and guided performance, not on solo performance by itself.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.601Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"social science research — Zone of proximal development framework in Vygotsky's sociocultural learning theory and scaffolding pedagogy","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 B는 두 단락(비고츠키 이론에 근거한 스캐폴딩 + 역량 성장에 따라 도움을 점차 거둬야 효과적)을 종합한 중심 내용으로 타당하며, \"works only when\"은 지문의 \"effective scaffolding requires\"에 의해 뒷받침된다. A는 대체·측정 왜곡, C는 의존성 원인을 단계 나누기 자체로 잘못 귀속(부분적 근거 있음), D는 비고츠키 주장 반전으로 모두 배제 가능. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 선택지 참조와 결론이 일치하고 정확하며 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 역사적 사실(ZPD, 후대 연구자의 scaffolding 용어 도입)도 정확. 두 단락 연결이 필요한 medium 난이도에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B는 두 단락의 내용을 합쳐 놓은 정답이다. C는 일부 교사가 도움을 계속 유지하는 문제를 단계 나누기 탓으로 잘못 돌린 부분 근거 오답이고, D는 첫 문장의 'not by what the child can already do alone'을 훑어 읽으면 고르기 쉬운 오답이다. A는 비교적 쉽게 배제된다. B의 'works only when'은 지문의 'requires'와 같은 뜻이라 문제없다. 전체적으로 중간 난이도에 맞다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-125","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-126","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In a 1968 study, psychologists John Darley and Bibb Latané had college students talk over an intercom with peers they believed were in other rooms. Partway through, one voice appeared to have a seizure. Participants who thought they were the only other listener almost always left their rooms to get help, and they usually did so quickly. Those who believed four other people were also listening responded less often and more slowly. Notably, the researchers did not find these hesitant participants indifferent: many were sweating and trembling, and they repeatedly asked whether someone was helping. Darley and Latané concluded that the presence of others does not make bystanders stop caring. Instead, it spreads the sense of obligation across the group, so each person feels less personally responsible for acting.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Darley and Latané found that participants who believed they were alone with the victim felt more distress than those who believed others were listening.","Darley and Latané found that participants in larger groups were less concerned about the victim because they assumed the seizure was not serious.","Darley and Latané found that hearing about other listeners made participants slower to act not because it reduced concern but because it weakened each person's sense of duty to respond.","Darley and Latané found that participants who used an intercom were less willing to help than people who see an emergency in person usually are."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"C가 정답이다. 지문은 다른 청취자가 있다고 믿은 참가자가 늦게 반응했지만 땀을 흘리고 떨 만큼 걱정했다고 하며, 그 원인을 관심 부족이 아닌 책임감 분산으로 결론짓는다. A는 혼자인 참가자가 더 빨리 도왔다는 사실과 연결되지만, 지문은 집단 조건 참가자도 심한 고통을 보였다고 하므로 고통의 크기를 비교한 내용이 아니다. B는 집단에서 반응이 줄었다는 점은 맞지만, 관심이 적었다는 설명은 저자들의 결론과 정면으로 어긋나고 발작이 심각하지 않다고 여겼다는 언급도 없다. D는 인터콤 사용에서 나온 그럴듯한 추론이지만, 지문에는 직접 목격한 경우와의 비교가 없다.","explanationEn":"C is correct. The text says participants who believed others were listening responded more slowly, yet they were sweating, trembling, and asking whether anyone was helping. The researchers concluded that the cause was a spread-out sense of responsibility, not a lack of caring. A ties to the fact that participants who thought they were alone helped faster, but the text says the group participants were also clearly distressed, so it never compares how much distress each group felt. B gets right that the groups responded less, but saying those participants cared less contradicts the researchers' conclusion, and the text never says anyone thought the seizure wasn't serious. D is a reasonable guess based on the intercom setup, but the text never compares the study to emergencies people see in person.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.601Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"social science research — Bystander effect diffusion of responsibility in emergencies and Darley Latané experimental paradigm","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 C는 지문의 결론(반응 지연의 원인은 관심 부족이 아닌 책임감 분산)을 정확히 요약함. A는 '혼자 조건이 더 빨리 도움'이라는 사실에 기대지만 고통 비교는 지문에 없음, B는 반응 감소는 맞으나 원인 설명이 결론과 모순, D는 지문에 없는 비교로 배제 가능. 두 정보(지연 반응+신체적 고통 신호)를 연결해야 하므로 medium 적합. 1968년 Darley·Latané 연구(인터콤, 발작, 6인 조건=다른 4명 청취자) 사실관계도 대체로 정확하며 지문은 원문 인용이 아닌 자체 서술임. 한·영 해설 모두 글자 참조와 결론 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"1968년 Darley·Latané 연구의 실제 내용(혼자 조건에서 약 85% 도움, 5인 집단 조건 31%, 반응하지 않은 참가자도 불안 징후를 보임, 책임 분산이라는 결론)과 일치한다. C는 지문의 대조 구조(관심이 줄어든 것이 아니라 책임감이 분산됨)를 그대로 요약한다. A와 B는 지문의 일부 사실에 기대는 오답이고, D는 그럴듯하지만 지문 밖의 추론이다. 정답 C가 다른 선택지보다 길어 눈에 띄는 경향은 있지만 medium 난이도로 적절하다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-126","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-127","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Sociologist Pierre Bourdieu argued that schools, though officially open to all, often reward a kind of familiarity that children acquire at home rather than in the classroom. Students from educated families tend to arrive already comfortable with the vocabulary, reading habits, and tastes that teachers treat as signs of talent. Bourdieu called these assets \"cultural capital.\" Because examiners judge such fluency as natural ability, the advantage looks earned rather than inherited.\n\nAccording to Bourdieu, diplomas then turn this inherited ease into an official credential that employers and institutions recognize. A degree certifies the holder as competent, and in doing so it hides the family advantages that helped produce it. In this way, Bourdieu concluded, an education system that appears to judge merit can quietly pass social rank from one generation to the next.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Bourdieu argued that teachers deliberately favor students from educated families because they share those families' tastes and reading habits.","Bourdieu argued that cultural capital is a more important cause of success in school than natural ability or hard work.","Bourdieu argued that employers value diplomas mainly because degrees reliably show which candidates are competent.","Bourdieu argued that schooling can maintain inequality by treating advantages learned at home as merit and then certifying them with credentials."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 가정에서 얻은 문화적 친숙함이 학교에서 재능으로 오인되고(1단락), 학위가 이를 공식 자격으로 바꿔 가정의 이점을 숨겨 계층이 대물림된다(2단락)는 두 단계를 연결하므로 D가 정답이다. A는 교사가 '의도적으로' 편애한다고 하지만, 지문은 시험관이 그 유창함을 자연스러운 능력으로 오인한다고 할 뿐이다. B는 문화적 자본과 노력·능력을 비교해 순위를 매기는데, 지문은 이런 비교를 하지 않는다. C는 학위가 역량을 인증한다는 세부를 잡았지만, 학위가 가정의 이점을 숨긴다는 핵심을 놓쳐 오히려 반대 방향이다.","explanationEn":"The text links two steps: home-acquired familiarity gets mistaken for talent in school (first paragraph), and diplomas then turn it into official credentials that hide family advantage and pass rank down the generations (second paragraph), so D is correct. A says teachers favor these students deliberately, but the text only says examiners mistake that fluency for natural ability. B ranks cultural capital above ability and effort, a comparison the text never makes. C picks up the detail that degrees certify competence but misses the main point that degrees hide family advantages, so it actually points the opposite way.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.601Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"social science research — Cultural capital concept and Bourdieu's social stratification through educational credential accumulation","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 D는 1단락(가정 이점이 재능으로 오인)과 2단락(학위가 이를 자격으로 인증해 이점을 숨기고 계층 대물림)을 정확히 통합한다. A는 '의도적(deliberately)' 편애라는 지문에 없는 의도를 부가하고, B는 지문에 없는 비교·순위를 만들며, C는 '학위가 역량을 인증한다'는 세부를 잡았으나 핵심(가정 이점 은폐)을 놓친다. A·C는 부분적 근거를 가져 비교가 필요하며 B도 그럴듯해 medium에 적합. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 선택지 참조와 결론이 일치하고 영어 해설에 한글 없음. Bourdieu의 문화자본·학위 논의는 사실에 부합하며 지문은 독창적 요약으로 저작권 우려 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"두 단락을 종합해야 하며, A·C는 부분 근거를 가진 매력적 오답이다. D는 다소 길고 포괄적이라 눈에 띄지만 medium으로 적절하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-127","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-129","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In his 1961 book Asylums, sociologist Erving Goffman drew on a year of fieldwork at a large psychiatric hospital in Washington, D.C., to describe what he called \"total institutions\": settings such as hospitals, prisons, and military barracks where people sleep, work, and spend their leisure in one place, under a single authority, and alongside many others treated alike. Earlier observers had often explained patients' withdrawn or apathetic behavior as a symptom of their illness. Goffman, by contrast, pointed to routine admission procedures—the surrender of personal clothing and possessions, the assignment of numbers, the loss of control over one's daily schedule—and argued that these practices systematically dismantled the identity a person had brought from outside. Much of what staff read as evidence of mental disorder, he suggested, was better understood as an adaptation to the institution itself.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Goffman found that psychiatric hospitals differed from prisons and barracks mainly in how strictly they controlled patients' daily schedules.","Goffman found that behaviors often credited to patients' conditions could instead stem from institutional routines that stripped away their prior sense of self.","Goffman found that patients' apathy was caused chiefly by illness, although admission procedures sometimes made that apathy worse.","Goffman found that a year of fieldwork was needed before staff would allow an outside observer to study admission procedures."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"글에 따르면 Goffman은 환자의 위축된 행동을 질병 탓으로 보던 기존 해석에 반대했습니다. 그는 그런 행동이 입소 절차 때문에 정체성이 무너지면서 기관에 적응한 결과라고 보았으므로 B가 정답입니다. A는 병원, 교도소, 병영을 하나의 범주로 묶은 글의 내용을 대비로 바꾸어 놓았습니다. C는 입소 절차를 언급하지만 원인을 다시 질병에 두어 Goffman의 주장과 반대됩니다. D는 1년간의 현장 연구라는 세부 사항을 근거 없는 주장으로 부풀렸습니다.","explanationEn":"The text says Goffman rejected the earlier view that patients' withdrawn behavior was a symptom of illness. He argued instead that the behavior was an adaptation to admission routines that broke down patients' identities, so B is correct. A turns hospitals, prisons, and barracks into a contrast, but the text groups them together as one category. C mentions admission procedures but still names illness as the main cause, which is the opposite of Goffman's claim. D takes the detail about a year of fieldwork and adds a claim about staff permission that the text never makes.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.601Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"social science research — Total institutions concept in Goffman's ethnographic study of asylums and social identity stripping","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 B는 글의 핵심(질병 증상으로 여겨진 행동 → 정체성 해체 절차에 대한 적응) 을 정확히 요약함. A는 범주화를 대비로 왜곡, C는 인과를 뒤집음(입소 절차 언급으로 부분적 근거 있음), D는 세부 사항을 근거 없는 주장으로 확장. 사실관계(1961년 출간, 워싱턴 D.C. 세인트엘리자베스 병원 약 1년 현장연구, 총체적 기관 정의) 정확. 한·영 해설 모두 동일한 결론과 글자 참조, 자연스러운 영어. 난이도는 '기존 관점 vs Goffman 관점' 대비를 파악해야 C를 배제할 수 있어 medium에 부합하나, 정답이 비교적 명확해 medium 하단에 가까움."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"Asylums(1961)와 St. Elizabeths 현장 연구 관련 사실은 정확함. C는 부분적으로 그럴듯한 오답이고, A·D는 상대적으로 쉽게 배제되지만 medium 수준에 적합함.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-129","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-130","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In their 1991 study of apprenticeship, Jean Lave and Etienne Wenger argued that learning is not chiefly the transfer of knowledge from expert to novice but a process of gradually deepening participation in a \"community of practice.\" Among Yucatec Maya midwives, Liberian tailors, and other groups they examined, newcomers began with peripheral but genuine tasks, such as hemming garments or fetching supplies, and moved toward full membership as they took on more central work. __Notably, many of the apprentice tailors received almost no direct instruction from their masters, yet they reliably became skilled garment makers.__ For Lave and Wenger, this outcome showed that what newcomers absorb through participation, including the shared routines, vocabulary, and standards of a group, can matter more to their development than any formal lesson.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It introduces a claim about expert instruction that Lave and Wenger later question by pointing to the tailors' gradual mastery.","It explains why newcomers in communities of practice begin with peripheral tasks before moving to central ones.","It presents an observation that Lave and Wenger interpret as evidence for their view of how learning occurs.","It describes a limitation of the tailors' apprenticeship that Lave and Wenger say communities of practice should address."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 직접 가르침이 거의 없었는데도 견습 재단사들이 숙련자가 되었다는 관찰을 제시하고, 바로 다음 문장에서 Lave와 Wenger는 이 결과를 참여를 통한 학습이라는 자신들의 견해를 뒷받침하는 근거로 해석하므로 C가 정답이다. A는 '직접 교수'를 언급한다는 점에서 그럴듯하지만, 밑줄 문장은 전문가 교수에 관한 주장을 내세우는 문장이 아니라 그런 교수가 없었다는 사실을 보고하는 관찰이다. B는 주변 과제에서 중심 과제로의 이동을 다루는데, 이 내용은 앞 문장에 있으며 밑줄 문장은 그 이유를 설명하지 않는다. D는 교수 부족을 결함으로 보지만, 저자들은 이를 바로잡을 문제가 아니라 자신들의 이론을 지지하는 증거로 본다.","explanationEn":"C is correct. The underlined sentence reports an observation: the tailors got almost no direct instruction but still became skilled. In the next sentence, Lave and Wenger treat this outcome as evidence that learning happens through participation. A is tempting because the sentence mentions instruction, but the sentence doesn't make a claim in favor of expert teaching. It just reports that such teaching was mostly missing. B is wrong because the movement from peripheral to central tasks is described in the sentence before, and the underlined sentence doesn't explain why it happens. D is wrong because the authors don't treat the lack of instruction as a flaw to fix. They treat it as support for their theory.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.601Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"social science research — Communities of practice framework and Lave Wenger situated learning theory in apprenticeship models","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 \"직접 교수 거의 없음 → 그럼에도 숙련\" 관찰이며, 바로 다음 문장 \"For Lave and Wenger, this outcome showed that...\"이 이를 참여 학습 이론의 근거로 해석함을 명시하므로 C가 정답임을 직접 확인. Lave & Wenger(1991) Situated Learning의 사례(Yucatec 산파, 라이베리아 Vai/Gola 재단사, 직접 교수 거의 없음)는 실제 내용과 일치하여 사실 오류 없음. 지문은 자체 작성된 요약문으로 저작권 우려 없음. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 C를 뒷받침하고 선택지 글자 참조가 일치하며 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 난이도: 밑줄 문장(관찰)과 다음 문장(해석)의 연결이 필요하고, A(교수 언급)·D('yet'의 대비를 결함으로 오독)가 부분 근거를 가진 매력적 오답이며 B도 지문 내용 기반이라 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"Lave & Wenger의 Situated Learning(1991) 내용(유카텍 마야 산파, 라이베리아 재단사, 정당한 주변적 참여)과 사실상 맞음. 오답 A·D가 각각 '교수'와 '교수 부족'이라는 부분 근거를 가져 비교가 필요함. B는 다소 쉽게 배제됨. 중간 난이도에 적합.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-130","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-131","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In their influential 1987 account of politeness, linguists Penelope Brown and Stephen Levinson proposed that speakers everywhere manage \"face,\" the public self-image each person wants to maintain. Requests, criticisms, and refusals threaten face, so speakers soften them with strategies such as indirect phrasing or expressions of solidarity. Brown and Levinson presented this framework as universal. __Researchers studying Japanese conversation, however, have observed that speakers often choose honorific forms not to protect an individual's self-image but to signal their recognition of each participant's fixed position within a social group.__ If such choices are driven mainly by social obligation rather than by efforts to reduce threats to face, then the framework may describe one culturally specific pattern of politeness rather than a pattern found in every language.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It gives an example of the softening strategies that Brown and Levinson argued speakers use to lessen threats to face.","It explains why Brown and Levinson chose to base their framework mainly on data from Japanese conversation.","It describes a method that researchers used to measure how often speakers in different languages use indirect phrasing.","It presents a finding that raises doubts about whether a framework said to apply everywhere actually does."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 'however'로 시작해, 일본어 화자가 경어를 쓰는 이유가 개인의 체면 보호가 아니라 집단 내 위치 인정이라는 관찰을 제시한다. 이는 앞에서 보편적이라고 한 틀에 의문을 제기하고, 마지막 문장에서 그 틀이 문화 특수적일 수 있다는 결론으로 이어지므로 D가 정답이다. A는 경어가 완화 전략처럼 보여 그럴듯하지만, 문장은 그 이론을 뒷받침하는 예가 아니라 반례이다. B는 일본어가 언급되었다는 점을 이용한 오답으로, Brown과 Levinson의 자료 출처는 지문에 나오지 않는다. C는 연구자의 관찰을 측정 방법으로 잘못 해석했고, 빈도 측정 이야기도 지문에 없다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence begins with \"however\" and reports that Japanese speakers use honorifics to acknowledge where people stand in a group, not to protect someone's self-image. That observation challenges the framework the text just called universal, and the last sentence draws the conclusion that the framework may be culturally specific, so D is correct. A looks reasonable because honorifics can seem like softening, but the sentence works as a counterexample to the theory, not as support for it. B picks up on the mention of Japanese, but the text never says where Brown and Levinson got their data. C treats an observation as if it were a measurement method, and the text says nothing about counting how often indirect phrasing is used.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.602Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"social science research — Politeness theory in Brown Levinson face-saving linguistic strategies across cultural contexts","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 'however'로 전환되어 보편성 주장에 대한 반례를 제시하고, 마지막 문장이 이를 받아 틀이 문화 특수적일 수 있다고 결론짓는다. D가 정확. A는 경어=완화 전략이라는 표면적 유사성, B는 '일본어' 언급을 이용한 부분적 근거가 있어 비교가 필요하고 C도 그럴듯함. 해설 양 언어 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. Brown & Levinson(1987) 및 일본어 경어 기반 비판(Ide, Matsumoto)은 실제 학술 논의와 부합. medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["too_easy","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 D는 명확하다. 다만 B와 C는 지문에 근거가 전혀 없어 금방 배제되고, 부분적으로 그럴듯한 오답은 A 하나뿐이다. 'however'와 마지막 문장이 정답을 거의 직접 알려 주므로 medium 기준(부분 근거를 가진 오답 2개 이상)에 미달한다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-131","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-132","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In a widely cited 1999 study, psychologists David Dunning and Justin Kruger asked participants to complete tests of logical reasoning and grammar and then estimate how well they had performed relative to their peers. Those who scored lowest dramatically overestimated their standing, often placing themselves above average. Dunning and Kruger argued that the skills needed to perform a task well are the same skills needed to recognize good performance, so poor performers lack the very knowledge that would reveal their errors. __Some later researchers, however, have noted that a portion of this pattern could arise simply because estimates at the extremes of any scale tend to drift toward the middle, a statistical effect that would occur even if no one's self-knowledge were impaired.__ Still, follow-up experiments found that when low scorers received brief training in the tested skill, their self-assessments became markedly more accurate, a result that a purely statistical account struggles to explain.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It introduces an alternative account of the findings that the text then argues cannot fully replace Dunning and Kruger's explanation.","It introduces an alternative account of the findings that the text then uses to reject Dunning and Kruger's explanation entirely.","It introduces an account of the findings that the training experiments described later were originally designed to confirm.","It introduces an account of why low scorers in the 1999 study chose to place themselves above average on purpose."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 통계적 평균 회귀라는 대안 설명을 제시하고, 이어지는 'Still' 문장은 훈련 실험 결과가 이 통계적 설명만으로는 설명되기 어렵다고 말하므로 A가 정답이다. B는 대안 설명을 제시한다는 점은 맞지만, 글은 원래 설명을 완전히 기각하지 않고 오히려 옹호한다. C는 훈련 실험을 언급하지만, 그 실험은 통계적 설명을 확인한 것이 아니라 그 한계를 드러낸다. D는 통계적 효과는 누구의 의도와도 무관하게 생긴다고 했으므로 '의도적으로'라는 해석이 틀렸다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence offers a different explanation, a statistical drift toward the middle, and the next sentence (\"Still...\") says the training results are hard for a purely statistical account to explain, so A is correct. B gets the alternative account right, but the text doesn't throw out Dunning and Kruger's view. It actually defends that view. C mentions the training experiments, but those experiments show where the statistical account falls short. They weren't designed to confirm it. D is wrong because the statistical effect described happens no matter what anyone intends, so it isn't about low scorers deliberately ranking themselves high.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.602Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"social science research — Dunning Kruger effect and metacognitive bias in self-assessment accuracy among unskilled performers","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 'however'로 대안(평균 회귀) 설명을 도입하고, 이어지는 'Still' 문장이 훈련 실험 결과를 근거로 순수 통계 설명의 한계를 지적하므로 A가 정확히 성립. B는 '완전 기각'이, C는 '확인하도록 설계'가, D는 '의도적'이 본문과 모순되어 배제됨. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 결론과 글자 참조가 일치하고 영어는 자연스러우며 한글 혼입 없음. 사실관계(1999년 Dunning·Kruger 연구, 논리·문법 과제, 평균 회귀 비판, 훈련 후 자기평가 개선)는 대체로 정확함. 다만 훈련 실험은 엄밀히는 1999년 원 논문 내 연구(Study 4)이므로 'follow-up experiments'는 약간 느슨한 표현이나 문항 판단에 영향 없는 수준. 밑줄 문장과 마지막 문장을 연결해야 B를 배제할 수 있어 2단계 판단이 요구되며 B·C가 부분적 근거를 가져 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"'however' 다음에 오는 'Still'의 흐름을 파악해야 하는 두 단계 판단 문항이다. B와 C는 각각 부분적으로 맞는 근거를 갖고 있다. D는 상대적으로 약한 오답이지만 그럴듯하다. 1999년 연구의 실제 검사 과제에는 유머도 있었지만, 지문이 이를 생략한 것은 오류가 아니다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-132","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-133","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Since its introduction in 1998, the Implicit Association Test (IAT) has been used to estimate how strongly people automatically link social groups with particular traits. Participants sort words and images as quickly as possible, and faster responses when, say, a group is paired with \"pleasant\" are taken to reveal an association the participant may not consciously endorse. The test's popularity grew rapidly, and many organizations adopted it in diversity training as a way to diagnose individual bias. __Yet when the same people take the IAT a few weeks apart, their scores often shift considerably, and a person's score is only weakly related to how that person actually treats members of the group in question.__ For this reason, many researchers now argue that the IAT is better suited to tracking average associations across large populations than to labeling any one individual as biased.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It explains the procedure that allows the IAT to detect associations that participants do not consciously endorse.","It presents findings that call into question one use of the IAT described earlier in the text.","It offers evidence that the IAT's popularity among organizations has declined in recent years.","It describes results that support the claim that people's automatic associations change quickly over time."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 시작하며, 점수가 재검사 때 달라지고 실제 행동과 관련이 약하다는 결과를 제시한다. 이는 앞에서 말한 '개인의 편향을 진단하는' 용도에 의문을 제기하고, 마지막 문장의 결론(집단 수준에 더 적합하다)으로 이어진다. 그래서 B가 정답이다. A는 테스트 절차를 설명하는 문장으로, 밑줄 문장이 아니라 둘째 문장의 기능이다. C는 지문에 없는 '인기 하락'을 주장하고 있으며, 지문이 문제 삼는 것은 측정의 신뢰성이다. D는 점수 변동을 실제 연상 자체가 빠르게 변한다는 증거로 잘못 해석한 것으로, 지문은 이를 측정의 한계로 다룬다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence starts with \"Yet\" and reports that IAT scores shift when people retake the test and are only weakly tied to how they actually behave. Those findings undercut the use mentioned just before it, which is diagnosing bias in individuals, and they set up the final sentence's conclusion that the test works better for populations. That makes B the answer. A describes what the second sentence does (it explains the procedure), not what the underlined sentence does. C claims the test has become less popular, but the text never says that; its concern is how reliable the measurement is. D treats the shifting scores as proof that the associations themselves change quickly, but the text presents the shifts as a weakness of the measurement.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.602Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"social science research — Implicit Association Test measuring unconscious bias and automatic stereotype activation measurement","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 직전 문장의 '개인 편향 진단' 용도에 반하는 결과를 제시하고 마지막 결론으로 이어짐 → B 타당. A는 둘째 문장 기능, D는 점수 변동을 실제 연상 변화로 오독한 그럴듯한 오답, C는 지문에 없는 인기 하락. 한·영 해설 결론·글자 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. IAT 관련 사실(1998년 도입, 재검사 신뢰도·행동 예측력 비판) 정확. 두 단계 연결 필요, medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"IAT 도입 연도(1998), 낮은 재검사 신뢰도, 행동 예측력이 약하다는 점은 모두 사실에 부합한다. 오답 D는 점수 변동이라는 부분적 근거가 있어 그럴듯하고, C도 조직 관련 문맥과 이어져 있어 정답과 비교해 봐야 배제된다. A는 비교적 쉽게 배제된다. 정답 B는 'Yet'으로 시작하는 문장이 앞의 개인 진단 용도를 반박한다는 점을 연결해야 고를 수 있어 medium 난이도에 적합하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-133","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-135","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In the 1970s, sociologist Basil Bernstein proposed that children acquire different \"codes\" of speech depending on their family's social position. A restricted code, he argued, relies on meanings shared by speakers and leaves much unstated, whereas an elaborated code spells out meanings explicitly so that listeners without shared context can follow. Critics have often read this as a claim that working-class speech is deficient. __Yet Bernstein insisted that both codes are fully capable of expressing complex thought and that restricted codes are common in close-knit groups of every class.__ His real concern lay elsewhere: schools, he contended, reward the elaborated code almost exclusively, so children who arrive already fluent in it are judged more able, and existing class advantages are quietly passed on.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It provides evidence that elaborated codes are more effective than restricted codes at conveying complex ideas to unfamiliar listeners.","It introduces the distinction between restricted and elaborated codes that the rest of the text goes on to define.","It presents a criticism of Bernstein's theory that the text's final sentence ultimately accepts as valid.","It rejects a common interpretation of Bernstein's view, clearing the way for the text to identify where he located the source of inequality."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 시작해, 비평가들이 노동계급 언어를 결함으로 읽은 해석을 반박한다. 이어 마지막 문장은 그의 진짜 관심사인 학교의 보상 구조를 제시하므로 D가 정답이다. A는 정교한 코드의 우월성을 주장하는데, 밑줄 문장은 두 코드 모두 복잡한 사고가 가능하다고 하므로 반대된다. B는 코드 구분이 이미 두 번째 문장에서 소개되었으므로 틀리다. C는 밑줄 문장이 비판을 제시하는 것이 아니라 반박하는 것이며, 마지막 문장도 그 비판을 받아들이지 않으므로 틀리다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence begins with \"Yet\" and pushes back on the critics' reading that working-class speech is deficient. The final sentence then shows where Bernstein actually saw the problem: schools rewarding the elaborated code. So D is correct. A claims the elaborated code is superior, but the sentence says both codes can express complex thought. B is wrong because the two codes were already introduced and defined in the second sentence. C is wrong because the sentence rebuts the criticism instead of presenting it, and the final sentence doesn't accept that criticism.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.602Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"social science research — Bernstein language codes restricted versus elaborated speech patterns and social class reproduction","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 비평가들의 '결함' 해석을 반박하고, 마지막 문장이 'His real concern lay elsewhere'로 불평등의 원천(학교의 보상 구조)을 제시하므로 D가 정확히 기능을 기술함. A는 두 코드 모두 복잡한 사고 표현 가능이라는 문장 내용과 모순, B는 구분이 이미 2문장에서 도입·정의됨, C는 비판 제시가 아닌 반박이며 결말도 비판을 수용하지 않음. 한·영 해설 모두 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 'In the 1970s' 표현은 Bernstein 이론이 1960년대부터 발전되었다는 점에서 다소 단순화되었으나(대표 저작 Class, Codes and Control 1971) 중대한 사실 오류로 보기 어려움. 난이도는 'Yet'의 반박 기능 파악 + 마지막 문장과의 연결이라는 두 단계 판단이 필요하고, A가 2문장의 내용을 부분적으로 차용해 매력적인 오답으로 기능하므로 medium에 부합(다소 쉬운 편)."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"D는 'Yet'으로 시작하는 반박과 마지막 문장의 학교 이야기를 연결해야 고를 수 있다. A와 C는 지문 내용을 부분적으로 차용한 그럴듯한 오답이다. B는 비교적 쉽게 배제된다. 중간 난이도로 적합하다. 번스타인의 이론 묘사도 대체로 정확하다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-135","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-136","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"According to reactance theory, first proposed by psychologist Jack Brehm in 1966, people who sense that a freedom is being threatened become motivated to restore it, often by embracing the very option they are being pushed away from. Researchers have commonly tested the theory with persuasive messages, finding that forceful wording such as \"you must\" can make audiences less willing to adopt a recommended behavior. __However, a 2019 study by social psychologist Hana Okafor suggests that the strength of this resistance depends less on how a message is worded than on how many alternatives remain open to the listener.__ In her experiments, participants told firmly to choose one of five snack options showed little resistance, whereas participants told just as firmly to choose one of two options resisted strongly, often rejecting both.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It introduces a finding that shifts emphasis away from a factor that earlier research had focused on.","It introduces a finding that confirms the conclusion reached in earlier tests of forceful wording.","It introduces a finding that undermines the claim that people seek to restore threatened freedoms.","It introduces a finding that explains why researchers first began testing the theory with persuasive messages."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 기존 연구가 주목한 요인(메시지의 강압적 표현)보다 남아 있는 선택지 수가 저항의 강도를 좌우한다는 새로운 발견을 제시하므로 A가 정답이다. B는 'However'로 시작해 기존 결론과 강조점을 달리한다는 점을 놓쳤다. C는 오카포르의 연구가 자유 회복 동기 자체를 부정하지 않고 오히려 선택지가 적을 때 강한 저항을 보여 이론을 유지한다는 점에서 틀렸다. D는 연구자들이 설득 메시지로 실험을 시작한 이유는 지문에서 다루지 않으므로 틀렸다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence presents a new finding: the strength of resistance depends more on how many options remain than on the forceful wording that earlier studies focused on, so A is correct. B misses that the sentence begins with \"However\" and moves the emphasis away from the earlier conclusion instead of confirming it. C is wrong because Okafor's study doesn't reject the idea that people try to restore freedoms. In fact, the strong resistance when only two options remained supports the theory. D is wrong because the text never explains why researchers first used persuasive messages to test the theory.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.602Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"social science research — Reactance theory psychological resistance to persuasion and constrained choice motivation theory","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 'However'로 기존 연구(강압적 표현)와 대비하며 저항 강도를 좌우하는 요인을 '남은 선택지 수'로 옮기므로 A가 정확. B는 전환어와 모순, C는 이론 자체를 부정하지 않음(두 선택지 조건에서 강한 저항은 이론을 지지), D는 지문에 근거 없음. Brehm 1966 반응 이론은 사실과 부합하며 Okafor 연구는 가상의 예시로 문제 없음. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 정답 및 선택지 참조가 일치하고 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 전환어 인식 + '수정 vs 반박' 구분이라는 두 단계 판단이 필요하고 B·C가 부분적 근거를 가진 오답이라 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"Hana Okafor 2019 연구는 가상의 인물로 보이며 SAT 형식상 허용된다. 'less on wording than on alternatives' 구문 때문에 강조점 이동(A)을 고르려면 정독이 필요하다. B와 C는 그럴듯한 오답이고 D는 비교적 약하다. medium 난이도에 적합하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-136","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-137","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Psychologists studying moral licensing have found that people who have just done something virtuous sometimes feel freer to act less virtuously afterward, as if their good deed had earned them credit to spend. In one widely cited design, participants who first wrote about their own generous qualities later donated less to charity than participants who wrote about neutral topics. __Yet when researchers asked participants to write about a specific past act of generosity rather than about their generous character, the drop in later donations largely disappeared.__ This contrast has led some scholars to propose that licensing depends less on doing good than on how a person interprets that good: seeing oneself as already \"a generous person\" may relax effort, while recalling concrete actions may instead reinforce a commitment to continue them.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It presents a finding that confirms the donation result from the earlier study and extends it to a new group of participants.","It introduces a variation in study conditions that limits the earlier finding and sets up the interpretation offered afterward.","It describes a methodological flaw in the earlier study that leads scholars to reject the idea of moral licensing.","It offers an example of moral licensing in everyday life that shows the effect is stronger outside the laboratory."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 글쓰기 과제를 '성격'에서 '구체적 행동'으로 바꾸자 기부 감소 효과가 사라졌다고 하여, 앞선 결과가 특정 조건에서만 나타남을 보여 주고, 이어지는 '해석에 따라 달라진다'는 제안의 근거가 된다. 따라서 B가 정답이다. A는 'Yet'으로 시작하는 대조를 무시하고 앞 결과를 확증한다고 보았으므로 틀리다. C는 효과의 한계를 보여 준다는 점은 일부 맞지만, 연구 방법의 결함을 지적하거나 도덕적 면허 개념을 부정하는 것이 아니라 이론을 정교화하는 것이므로 틀리다. D는 밑줄 문장이 일상생활 사례가 아니라 실험 조건을 다루므로 틀리다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence describes a change in the writing task, from generous character to a specific generous act, that made the drop in donations go away. This shows the earlier finding holds only under certain conditions, and it sets up the scholars' interpretation in the final sentence, so B is correct. A misses the contrast signaled by \"Yet\" and treats the sentence as confirming the earlier result. C is partly right that the sentence limits the effect, but it doesn't point out a flaw, and scholars refine the idea of licensing instead of rejecting it. D is wrong because the sentence reports a lab condition, not an everyday example.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.602Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"social science research — Moral licensing phenomenon and ethical credential spending in prosocial behavior studies","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 앞선 결과와 대조되는 조건 변화를 제시하고, 마지막 문장의 해석(\"how a person interprets that good\")을 뒷받침하므로 B가 정확하다. A는 '확증'이라는 점에서 'Yet'의 대조와 모순되고 새로운 참여자 집단 언급도 없음. C는 '한계를 보여 준다'는 점은 부분적으로 맞지만 결함 지적·개념 거부는 지문과 불일치(지문은 이론을 정교화). D는 실험 조건이지 일상 사례가 아님. 해설 한·영 모두 글자 참조 일치, 모순 없음, 영어 자연스러움. 도덕적 면허 연구(Sachdeva et al. 2009 등 성격 vs 행동 회상 조작)와 사실적으로 부합. 독창적 서술로 저작권 우려 없음. 대조 신호 인식 + 뒤 문장과의 연결이라는 두 단계 판단이 필요하고 C가 그럴듯한 오답으로 기능하므로 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"B가 명확한 정답이다. C는 '한계'라는 부분적 근거가 있어 매력적인 오답이다. A는 Yet의 대조 신호를 놓친 사람이 고를 만한 함정이다. D는 비교적 쉽게 배제된다. 문장 기능을 파악하고 마지막 문장과 연결해야 하는 2단계 판단이 필요해 medium 난이도에 맞다. 연구 내용은 Sachdeva et al.(2009)의 실제 연구와 대체로 일치한다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-137","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-138","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In 1950, Theodor Adorno and his colleagues published The Authoritarian Personality, which introduced the F-scale, a questionnaire intended to measure a person's susceptibility to fascist ideas. Respondents rated their agreement with statements such as \"Obedience and respect for authority are the most important virtues children should learn,\" and high scores were taken as evidence of an underlying authoritarian disposition. The scale quickly became one of the most widely used instruments in social psychology. __Yet every item on the original F-scale was worded so that agreement, rather than disagreement, raised a respondent's score.__ Later researchers noted that some people tend to agree with almost any statement put to them, regardless of its content, meaning that a high F-scale score might reflect this general habit of assent as much as any authoritarian outlook. Revised versions of the scale therefore mixed in reversed items, for which disagreement indicated authoritarianism.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It explains a feature of the F-scale's design that accounts for the instrument's rapid adoption by social psychologists.","It presents a detail about the F-scale's wording that illustrates the kind of attitudes Adorno and his colleagues associated with fascism.","It identifies a feature of the F-scale's design that sets up a concern about what the scale's scores actually measured.","It describes a feature of the F-scale's design that later researchers introduced to correct a flaw in the original scale."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 F-척도의 모든 문항이 '동의'할 때만 점수가 오르도록 쓰였다는 설계상 특징을 지적하고, 이어지는 문장은 이것 때문에 높은 점수가 권위주의가 아니라 단순한 동의 경향을 반영할 수 있다는 우려를 제기하므로 C가 정답이다. A는 'Yet'이 앞 문장(널리 사용됨)과 대조를 나타낸다는 점을 놓쳤고, 이 특징이 채택 이유라는 근거도 없다. B는 문항 예시가 앞 문장에 나오긴 하지만, 밑줄 문장은 문항 내용이 아니라 문구 방향을 다룬다. D는 수정판의 역문항을 원본의 특징으로 혼동했다. 역문항은 문제를 바로잡으려고 나중에 추가된 것이고, 밑줄 문장은 원본의 결함 자체를 설명한다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence points out that every item on the original F-scale was worded so that only agreement raised the score. The next sentence then explains why that matters: a high score might reflect a habit of agreeing with anything rather than authoritarianism. So C is correct. A misses the contrast signaled by \"Yet,\" and nothing in the text says this feature explains why the scale was adopted so quickly. B fails because the sentence is about which direction the items were worded, not about the attitudes they described. D confuses the original scale with the revised versions: the reversed items were added later to fix the problem, while the underlined sentence describes the flaw itself.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.602Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"social science research — Authoritarian personality construct and Adorno's study of fascist tendency measurement scales","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장(모든 문항이 동의 방향으로만 작성됨)은 바로 다음 문장의 '동의 경향(acquiescence)' 우려를 예비하는 설계상 특징이므로 C가 유일하게 옳음. 'Yet' 대조 + 다음 문장 연결이라는 두 단계 판단 필요. A(설계 특징+빠른 채택), B(문구+태도), D(설계 특징+후속 연구자)는 각각 지문 요소를 부분적으로 차용해 비교가 필요하므로 medium 적합. F-척도의 전 문항 긍정 방향 서술과 묵종 편향 비판은 역사적 사실과 일치. 한·영 해설 모두 C를 일관되게 뒷받침하며 영어 해설에 한글 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"acquiescence bias에 관한 역사적 사실이 정확함. D는 수정판 문항과 원본을 혼동하게 만드는 오답이고, A는 'Yet' 앞 문장과 연결되는 오답이어서 medium 난이도에 적합함.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-138","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-139","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"During the twentieth century, average scores on intelligence tests rose steadily across many industrialized nations, a trend later named the Flynn effect after political scientist James Flynn, who documented it extensively. Because the gains appeared within just a few generations, too quickly for genetic change to explain them, researchers have looked to environmental causes such as better nutrition, longer schooling, and more familiarity with abstract reasoning. __Yet recent data from Norway and Denmark complicate any simple account: among men born after the mid-1970s, scores have begun to decline, and the drop shows up even when brothers raised in the same household are compared.__ Since brothers share most of their genes and family background, this pattern suggests that whatever drives score changes operates through broad shifts in society rather than through differences between families.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It presents evidence that challenges the claim that test-score gains were too rapid to have a genetic explanation.","It offers a specific example of how improvements in nutrition and schooling raised test scores in certain countries.","It introduces a finding that leads researchers to doubt that intelligence tests measure anything meaningful.","It introduces a finding that reverses the earlier trend and provides the basis for a conclusion about what causes score changes."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 시작해 20세기의 점수 상승 추세가 뒤집힌 노르웨이·덴마크 자료를 제시하고, 이어지는 마지막 문장은 형제 비교라는 이 자료를 근거로 점수 변화가 가족 간 차이가 아니라 사회 전반의 변화에서 온다는 결론을 내린다. 따라서 D가 정답이다. A는 반박의 느낌은 맞지만, 이 자료는 오히려 형제 비교를 통해 유전적 설명을 배제하는 쪽이라 '유전으로 설명하기엔 너무 빠르다'는 주장을 반박하지 않는다. B는 영양·교육을 언급한 앞 문장과 연결되지만, 밑줄 문장은 점수 하락을 다루며 그런 요인이 점수를 올린 사례가 아니다. C는 검사 자체의 타당성을 의심한다는 내용으로, 지문 어디에도 나오지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence opens with \"Yet\" and reports Norwegian and Danish data showing that the twentieth-century rise has turned into a decline. The final sentence then uses the brother comparisons from that data to conclude that score changes come from broad shifts in society, not from differences between families. That makes D the answer. A sounds right because the sentence does complicate things, but the brother data actually helps rule out genetic explanations, so it doesn't challenge the claim that the gains were too fast to be genetic. B ties into the earlier mention of nutrition and schooling, but the underlined sentence is about falling scores, not an example of those factors raising them. C claims researchers doubt the tests mean anything, and nothing in the text says that.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.602Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"social science research — Flynn effect generational intelligence quotient increases and environmental factor debates","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 기존 상승 추세의 반전(노르웨이·덴마크 하락)을 제시하고, 형제 비교 자료가 마지막 문장의 결론(사회 전반의 변화가 원인)의 근거가 되므로 D가 정확하다. A는 '복잡하게 만든다'는 어조에 기대 유전 설명 반박으로 오독하기 쉬우나 실제로는 형제 비교가 유전 요인을 배제하므로 틀림. B는 앞 문장의 영양·교육과 연결되지만 하락을 다루므로 배제. C는 지문에 근거 없음. 사실관계(Flynn 효과, 노르웨이 형제 비교 연구, 덴마크 징집병 자료의 하락)도 실제 연구와 부합. 한·영 해설 결론·선택지 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 반전 식별 + 다음 문장과의 연결이라는 두 단계 판단이 필요해 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"노르웨이 형제 비교 연구(Bratsberg & Rogeberg 2018)와 일치함. 덴마크는 형제 내 분석 근거가 약간 덜 명확하지만 수용 가능한 수준. A·B는 부분 근거가 있는 매력 오답이고 C는 약한 편.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-139","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-cross_text_connections-m-140","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Cross-Text Connections","difficulty":"medium","skill":"cross_text_connections","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Text 1\nLinguistic anthropologist Elinor Ochs argued that most linguistic features do not point to social categories such as gender directly. Instead, a particle or intonation pattern first signals a stance, such as hesitancy or forcefulness, and listeners then link that stance to a social identity. On this view, a sentence-final particle used often by women in Japanese marks gentleness, and only through that stance comes to be associated with femininity.\n\nText 2\nSome sociolinguists studying workplace talk report that certain hedges, like \"sort of,\" are so routinely tied to junior employees that listeners infer rank the instant they hear them, with no apparent attention to stance. Yet these researchers also find that the same hedges, when used by senior managers, are heard as diplomatic rather than subordinate. That reversal suggests listeners still read the hedge first as a stance, tentativeness, whose social meaning depends on who is speaking.","question":"Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to Ochs' claim in Text 1 about how linguistic features come to be associated with social identities?","options":["By suggesting that evidence seeming to challenge the claim, once examined more closely, actually supports it","By suggesting that evidence from workplace talk shows the claim applies to Japanese but not to English","By suggesting that evidence of listeners inferring rank instantly shows the claim to be mistaken","By suggesting that evidence about senior managers shows the claim exaggerates the importance of who is speaking"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"Text 1의 Ochs는 언어 형태가 먼저 태도(stance)를 나타내고, 그 태도를 거쳐 사회적 정체성과 연결된다고 주장한다. Text 2는 처음에 'sort of'가 태도 없이 곧바로 직급을 나타내는 것처럼 보인다는 반례를 소개하지만, 고위 관리자가 쓰면 의미가 뒤바뀐다는 점을 들어 결국 청자가 먼저 태도를 읽는다고 결론 내리므로 A가 정답이다. B는 Text 2가 언어 간 차이를 주장하지 않으므로 틀리다. C는 Text 2 앞부분만 훑어 읽으면 고를 수 있지만, Text 2는 그 증거를 뒤집는다. D는 Text 2가 오히려 화자가 누구인지가 사회적 의미를 결정한다고 말하므로 틀리다.","explanationEn":"In Text 1, Ochs claims that a linguistic feature first signals a stance, and only through that stance does it become linked to a social identity. Text 2 starts with what looks like a counterexample: \"sort of\" seems to signal rank right away. Then it shows that the same hedge means something different when senior managers use it, and it concludes that listeners still read stance first, so A is correct. B is wrong because Text 2 never says the claim works for one language and not another. C is tempting if you only skim the first part of Text 2, but the author goes on to reject that interpretation. D is wrong because Text 2 says the speaker's identity is what shapes the social meaning, which is the opposite of saying Ochs overstates it.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.602Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"social science research — Linguistic indexicality and Ochs' stance markers reflecting social positioning in speech","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"Text 2 presents an apparent counterexample (hedges indexing rank \"with no apparent attention to stance\") and then reverses it via the senior-manager case, concluding listeners read stance first — directly supporting Ochs' indirect-indexicality account, so A is correct. C is the skim trap (first half of Text 2 only); D borrows the phrase \"who is speaking\" but inverts Text 2's point; B introduces a language contrast neither text makes. Korean and English explanations agree in conclusion and letter references, English is natural with no Hangul. Ochs' indirect indexicality is accurately characterized. Two-step reasoning (track Text 2's reversal, then map to Text 1's claim) matches medium difficulty."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"Text 2는 겉보기 반례를 제시한 뒤 이를 Ochs의 간접 지표성(indirect indexicality) 주장을 지지하는 근거로 재해석하므로 A가 명확한 정답이다. C는 앞부분만 훑어 읽은 독자를 노린 강한 오답이고, D는 '화자'라는 요소를 비틀어 비교가 필요하다. B는 상대적으로 약하지만(영어/일본어 대비) 말은 된다. 지문의 Ochs 관련 내용은 사실과 부합한다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-cross_text_connections-m-140","intendedSkill":"cross_text_connections","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-m-141","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In her influential analysis of what she called \"Mock Spanish,\" linguistic anthropologist Jane H. Hill examined how English speakers in the United States borrow Spanish expressions such as \"hasta la vista, baby\" and \"no problemo.\" Such phrases, often dismissed as harmless humor, can quietly reinforce negative stereotypes of Spanish ______ Hill argued that their playful tone depends on listeners recognizing the speakers being imitated as lazy, disorderly, or unserious.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["speakers, in fact,","speakers; in fact,","speakers, in fact;","speakers in fact,"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"빈칸 앞 \"Such phrases ... speakers\"와 뒤 \"Hill argued ... unserious\"는 각각 독립절이다. 'in fact'는 뒤 절을 강조하는 부사구이므로 세미콜론으로 두 절을 나누고 'in fact' 뒤에 쉼표를 찍은 B가 정답이다. A는 두 독립절을 쉼표로만 이어 쉼표 오류(comma splice)가 생긴다. C는 세미콜론 위치가 잘못되어 'in fact'가 앞 절에 붙는데, 그러면 강조 대상이 바뀌고 앞 절 끝에 어색하게 매달린다. D는 절 사이에 아무 경계 표시가 없어 무종지문(run-on)이 된다.","explanationEn":"The words before the blank (\"Such phrases ... Spanish speakers\") and the words after it (\"Hill argued ... unserious\") are both independent clauses. \"In fact\" is a transitional phrase that emphasizes the second clause, so the clauses should be separated by a semicolon placed before \"in fact,\" with a comma after it. That's choice B. Choice A joins the two independent clauses with only commas, which creates a comma splice. Choice C puts the semicolon after \"in fact,\" so the phrase gets awkwardly attached to the end of the first clause and no longer introduces Hill's argument. Choice D has no boundary at all between the clauses, which makes it a run-on sentence.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.602Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"social science research — Mock Spanish and Hill's analysis of language borrowing and ethnic stereotype reinforcement","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"빈칸 앞뒤 모두 독립절이며, 전환어 'in fact'가 뒤 절을 이끄므로 \"speakers; in fact,\" (B)가 표준 용법에 맞음. A는 쉼표 오류, D는 무종지문, C는 세미콜론 자체는 경계를 만들지만 전환어가 앞 절 끝에 붙어 SAT에서 통상 오답으로 처리하는 전형적 배치 오류(해설도 이를 '어색하게 매달린다'로 설명하여 모순 없음). Jane H. Hill의 'Mock Spanish' 분석 언급은 사실과 부합. 두 독립절 판별 + 전환어 위치 판단의 두 단계가 필요해 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"전형적인 SAT 접속부사 경계 문항이다. C도 문법상으로는 성립할 수 있지만, 'in fact'가 뒤 절의 근거를 이끄는 의미로 쓰였으므로 문맥상 배제된다. 해설에서도 그 점을 언급하고 있다. Jane Hill의 Mock Spanish 연구 내용은 사실과 맞다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-boundaries-m-141","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-transitions-m-143","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"medium","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In her 1990 book You Just Don't Understand, linguist Deborah Tannen argued that many men and women in the United States are socialized into different conversational styles: men more often use talk to negotiate status and share information (\"report talk\"), while women more often use it to build connection (\"rapport talk\"). Critics have charged that this framework reinforces stereotypes by treating gender as the sole driver of how people speak. Tannen, though, repeatedly cautioned that these patterns are tendencies observed across groups, not traits of every individual, and that factors such as region, ethnicity, and setting also shape speech. ______ her work is better read as a description of overlapping styles than as a claim that men and women speak entirely separate languages.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Nevertheless,","For example,","Similarly,","Thus,"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"빈칸 앞 문장은 Tannen이 해당 패턴을 개인의 특성이 아닌 집단적 경향으로 보았고 다른 요인도 인정했다는 근거를 제시하고, 빈칸 뒤 문장은 그 근거에서 나온 결론(그녀의 연구는 겹치는 스타일에 대한 기술로 읽어야 한다)을 말한다. 따라서 결과·결론을 나타내는 D가 정답이다. A는 비평가의 주장과 대비된다는 느낌 때문에 끌리지만, 바로 앞 문장과 빈칸 뒤 문장은 대립이 아니라 같은 방향이다. B는 뒤 문장이 앞 내용의 구체적 사례가 아니라 일반적 결론이므로 맞지 않는다. C는 뒤 문장이 앞과 비슷한 별개의 사실을 덧붙이는 것이 아니라 앞 내용에서 추론된 것이므로 부적절하다.","explanationEn":"The sentence before the blank gives evidence: Tannen described these patterns as group tendencies, not traits of every individual, and she acknowledged other influences on speech. The sentence after the blank states the conclusion that follows from that evidence, namely that her work should be read as describing overlapping styles. So D, which signals a result or conclusion, is correct. A may tempt you because the passage does contrast Tannen with her critics, but the sentence right before the blank and the one after it point in the same direction; they don't oppose each other. B doesn't fit because the final sentence is a general conclusion, not a specific example. C doesn't fit because the final sentence is drawn from the previous point rather than added as a separate, parallel point.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.602Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"social science research — Tannen gender discourse patterns and conversational styles between men and women communication","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"빈칸 앞(집단적 경향·다른 요인 인정이라는 근거) → 뒤(겹치는 스타일로 읽어야 한다는 결론) 구조이므로 'Thus'가 유일하게 논리적. A는 지문 전체의 비평가-Tannen 대립 구도 때문에 훑어 읽으면 고르기 쉬운 강한 오답으로, 두 단계 판단(직전 문장과의 관계 확인)이 요구됨. B·C는 상대적으로 약하지만 말은 됨. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 D를 일관되게 뒷받침하고 글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. Tannen 1990년 저서명·report/rapport talk 개념·비판 내용 모두 사실에 부합. 지문은 자체 작성된 설명문으로 저작권 의심 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"Thus가 앞 문장 근거→결론 관계에 정확히 맞음. Nevertheless는 비평가와의 대비 때문에 매력적 오답으로 작동하고, 문단 흐름을 따라가야 배제 가능해 medium에 적합. Tannen 저서 연도·개념(report/rapport talk)도 사실과 일치.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-transitions-m-143","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-e-144","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"easy","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Many popular books claim that men and women speak in fundamentally different ways, as if each sex used its own version of a language. Linguist Deborah Cameron has challenged this idea. She points out that when researchers actually compare large groups of speakers, the differences between men and women are usually small, and the variation within each group is much larger. __For example, studies of who interrupts more in conversation have found that a speaker's role, such as being a boss or a chairperson, predicts interrupting better than whether the speaker is a man or a woman.__ For Cameron, the belief in deep sex differences in speech says more about cultural expectations than about how people really talk.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It offers a specific case that supports Cameron's point that sex is a weak predictor of how people speak.","It offers a specific case that supports the popular claim that men and women speak in fundamentally different ways.","It offers a specific case that shows Cameron later abandoned her view about differences in speech.","It offers a specific case that explains why popular books about language have become so widely read."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 \"For example\"로 시작하며, 바로 앞에서 Cameron이 말한 '남녀 차이는 작고 집단 내부 차이가 더 크다'는 주장을 뒷받침하는 사례이다. 끼어들기를 예측하는 것은 성별보다 역할이라는 내용이므로 A가 정답이다. B는 이 사례가 대중적 주장을 오히려 반박한다는 점을 놓쳤다. C는 Cameron이 견해를 바꿨다는 내용이 지문에 없다. D는 대중서의 인기 이유를 다루지 않으므로 틀리다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence begins with \"For example,\" which tells you it backs up the claim right before it: Cameron's point that differences between men and women are small. It shows that a speaker's role predicts interrupting better than sex does, so A is correct. B is wrong because the example goes against the popular claim instead of supporting it. C is wrong because the text never says Cameron changed her view. D is wrong because the sentence doesn't explain why popular books are widely read.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.602Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"A","seed":"social science research — Cameron language and gender revisionist approach critiquing essentialist sex difference claims","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 \"For example\"로 앞 문장의 Cameron 주장(남녀 차이는 작다)을 뒷받침하는 사례이며, 역할이 성별보다 끼어들기를 더 잘 예측한다는 내용은 A와 정확히 일치한다. B는 방향이 반대, C·D는 지문에 근거 없음. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 A를 일관되게 뒷받침하고 글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음. Deborah Cameron의 실제 입장(The Myth of Mars and Venus)과도 부합하여 사실 오류 없음. 담화 표지 하나로 풀리는 단일 추론 구조로 easy 적합. 오답은 전형적 오개념(지지 대상 혼동, 지문 외 내용) 유형으로 그럴듯함."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"'For example' 단서가 직접 드러나 있고 한 단계 추론으로 풀린다. B는 그럴듯한 오개념이고, C·D는 다소 약하지만 허용 범위이다. Cameron의 견해 서술은 실제 저작(The Myth of Mars and Venus)과 일치한다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-e-144","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-words_in_context-e-145","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Words in Context","difficulty":"easy","skill":"words_in_context","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In the late 1700s, philosopher Jeremy Bentham designed the Panopticon, a circular prison with a central watchtower. Because prisoners could never tell whether a guard was actually looking at them, they behaved as if they were always being watched. Centuries later, Michel Foucault argued that this design reveals how modern institutions control people: the mere possibility of being observed leads individuals to ______ their own behavior, so guards rarely need to use force.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["exaggerate","regulate","abandon","celebrate"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 감시될 수 있다는 가능성만으로 수감자들이 늘 감시받는 것처럼 행동하고, 그래서 간수가 거의 힘을 쓸 필요가 없다고 말한다. 즉 사람들이 스스로 자기 행동을 통제한다는 뜻이므로 '조절하다, 통제하다'를 뜻하는 B가 정답이다. A(과장하다)는 행동을 부풀리는 것이라 스스로 통제한다는 의미와 맞지 않는다. C(포기하다)는 행동을 아예 그만둔다는 뜻이라 감시 때문에 행동을 조심한다는 내용과 어긋난다. D(찬양하다)는 감시를 통한 통제라는 맥락과 관련이 없다.","explanationEn":"The text says prisoners acted as if they were always watched, so guards rarely needed force. That means people control their own behavior, so B, \"regulate,\" is the best fit. A, \"exaggerate,\" would mean making their behavior bigger or more extreme, which is the opposite of keeping it in check. C, \"abandon,\" would mean giving up their behavior completely, not adjusting it carefully. D, \"celebrate,\" has nothing to do with the idea of control through surveillance.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.602Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"B","seed":"social science research — Panopticon surveillance architecture and Foucault's disciplinary power social control mechanisms","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"정답 B 'regulate'는 \"behaved as if they were always being watched\"와 \"guards rarely need to use force\"라는 직접 단서로 뒷받침되며, 오답 A/C/D는 문맥상 명확히 배제된다. 사실 관계(Bentham 1780년대 Panopticon 설계, Foucault의 『감시와 처벌』 논의)도 정확하다. 한·영 해설 모두 선택지 글자 참조가 일치하고 모순 없음. 단서가 명시적이고 어휘 평이하여 easy에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"'regulate their own behavior'는 '스스로 통제하므로 무력이 필요 없다'는 단서 하나로 바로 고를 수 있다. 오답 중 D(celebrate)는 다소 약하지만 easy 난이도로는 받아들일 만하다. 벤담과 푸코에 관한 사실 서술도 정확하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-words_in_context-e-145","intendedSkill":"words_in_context","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-words_in_context-e-146","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Words in Context","difficulty":"easy","skill":"words_in_context","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Sociologist Pierre Bourdieu argued that social class is not only a matter of income but is also carried in the body. Through years of daily life, children absorb ways of speaking, standing, and eating from those around them. Bourdieu called this set of habits the \"habitus.\" Because these habits feel natural rather than learned, people tend to ______ them without noticing, passing the same patterns on to the next generation and helping class differences persist.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["question","abandon","repeat","invent"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 습관이 학습된 것이 아니라 자연스럽게 느껴지기 때문에 사람들이 '알아차리지 못한 채' 그것을 다음 세대로 그대로 전달한다고 말하므로, 빈칸에는 '반복하다'를 뜻하는 C가 와야 한다. A는 의문을 제기한다는 뜻인데, 알아차리지 못한다는 내용과 모순된다. B는 버린다는 뜻이라 같은 패턴을 물려주고 계급 차이가 지속된다는 내용과 맞지 않는다. D는 새로 만들어낸다는 뜻이지만, 지문은 습관이 주변 사람들에게서 흡수된다고 설명한다.","explanationEn":"The text says these habits feel natural, so people act on them \"without noticing\" and pass the same patterns to the next generation. That means people keep doing the habits over and over, so C fits. A doesn't work because questioning a habit means noticing it, which goes against \"without noticing.\" B doesn't work because dropping the habits wouldn't pass the same patterns on or keep class differences going. D doesn't work because the text says the habits are absorbed from others, not newly created.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.603Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"C","seed":"social science research — Practice theory Bourdieu habitus and embodied social structures reproducing class inequality","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"정답 C '반복하다'는 'without noticing', 'passing the same patterns on', 'persist'와 정확히 호응함. 오답 A(알아차림 전제), B(지속과 모순), D(흡수된 것과 모순)는 규칙을 알면 즉시 배제되지만 그럴듯함. 부르디외 하비투스 개념 서술도 사실에 부합. 한·영 해설 모두 결론과 글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 어휘 평이하고 단서 명시적이어서 easy에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"'without noticing'와 'passing the same patterns on'이 직접적인 단서로, 한 단계 추론만 필요함. 오답은 각각 단서 하나씩으로 배제됨. 부르디외 아비투스 설명도 정확함.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-words_in_context-e-146","intendedSkill":"words_in_context","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-e-147","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"easy","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- Anthropologist Josephine Powell studied carpet weaving in rural Anatolia (present-day Türkiye) from the 1970s to the 1990s.\n- In many Anatolian villages, carpets were woven at home as a cottage industry.\n- Women and girls did most of the knotting and weaving on household looms.\n- Men usually sheared the sheep and took finished carpets to sell at town markets.\n- Powell collected more than 1,000 textiles and weaving tools during her research.","question":"The student wants to describe how tasks were split between men and women in Anatolian carpet production. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["In rural Anatolia, anthropologist Josephine Powell studied carpet weaving from the 1970s to the 1990s.","In rural Anatolia, carpets were often woven at home, making weaving a cottage industry in many villages.","In rural Anatolia, Josephine Powell collected more than 1,000 textiles and weaving tools during her research.","In rural Anatolia, women and girls did most of the knotting and weaving, while men sheared the sheep and sold the finished carpets."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"목표는 카펫 생산에서 남녀가 일을 어떻게 나누었는지 설명하는 것이다. D는 여성은 매듭짓기와 직조를 맡고, 남성은 양털 깎기와 판매를 맡았다고 밝혀 남녀 양쪽의 역할을 모두 보여 준다. A는 연구 기간만 말할 뿐 분업은 언급하지 않는다. B는 직조가 가내공업이었다는 사실만 제시하고 누가 어떤 일을 했는지는 말하지 않는다. C는 Powell의 수집품에 관한 내용이라 목표와 관계가 없다.","explanationEn":"Your goal is to describe how men and women split the work of making carpets. D does this because it says women and girls did the knotting and weaving, while men sheared the sheep and sold the carpets, so it covers both sides of the division. A only gives the years of Powell's research and says nothing about who did which tasks. B only says weaving was a cottage industry, without saying who did what. C is about Powell's collection, which has nothing to do with the goal.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.603Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"D","seed":"social science research — Anatolian carpet weaving and gendered division of labor in cottage industry artisanal production","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"D는 노트 3·4번을 정확히 종합해 남녀 분업을 모두 서술하므로 유일한 정답. A·B·C는 노트에 근거한 사실이지만 목표(분업 설명)와 무관하여 규칙(목표 일치)을 알면 바로 배제되며, 그럴듯한 오답으로 기능한다. 한·영 해설 모두 D 지지, 글자 참조 일치, 한글 혼입 없음. 노트 내용(Powell의 Anatolia 연구, 1,000점 이상 수집)은 실제 사실과 부합. 실제 College Board 문항 복제로 의심되는 점 없음. 한 단계 추론, 평이한 어휘로 easy에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"남녀 분업이라는 목표에 맞는 선택지는 D 하나뿐이다. 오답 선택지는 모두 노트에 있는 정확한 사실이지만 목표와 관련이 없어 바로 배제된다. 한 단계 추론으로 풀 수 있으므로 easy에 적합하다. 오답이 너무 쉽게 배제되는 경향이 조금 있으나 허용 범위다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-e-147","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-h-148","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"hard","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- In 1991, anthropologist Jean Lave and computer scientist Etienne Wenger published Situated Learning, which introduced the concept of \"legitimate peripheral participation.\"\n- The concept describes newcomers learning a practice by first taking on small, low-risk tasks within a community and gradually moving toward full participation.\n- Lave's earlier fieldwork among tailors' apprentices in Liberia documented that apprentices began by sewing buttons and hems before cutting cloth.\n- A 2014 survey of 412 hospital nursing trainees found that those assigned graduated ward duties reported somewhat higher confidence than those given full duties immediately.\n- The survey's authors cautioned that the confidence difference was modest and might reflect differences between hospitals rather than the training model itself.","question":"The student wants to present the nursing study's finding with the degree of caution its authors expressed. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["A 2014 survey of nursing trainees suggested that graduated ward duties may be linked to slightly greater confidence, though the effect could stem from differences among hospitals.","A 2014 survey of nursing trainees proved that graduated ward duties produce greater confidence, confirming Lave and Wenger's model of peripheral participation.","A 2014 survey of nursing trainees may have found that graduated ward duties possibly relate to confidence, though Lave and Wenger perhaps introduced peripheral participation in 1991.","A 2014 survey of nursing trainees suggested that apprentices may gain skill by sewing buttons and hems before cutting cloth, though the effect could stem from local customs."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"정답 A: 효과가 '약간' 크다는 점과 병원 간 차이 때문일 수 있다는 저자들의 단서를 그대로 살려 잠정적으로 표현했다. B: 잠정적인 상관 결과를 '증명했다'·'산출한다'고 과장했다. C: 1991년 출간처럼 확정된 사실까지 'perhaps'로 불필요하게 약화시켰다. D: 신중한 어조는 맞지만 내용이 라이베리아 재단사 견습생 현장연구와 섞여 있어 간호 연구 결과를 제대로 전하지 못한다.","explanationEn":"A is correct. It keeps the authors' caution: the confidence gain was small (\"slightly\") and might come from differences between hospitals. B overstates a tentative, correlational result by saying the survey \"proved\" that graduated duties \"produce\" confidence. C weakens facts that are certain, such as the 1991 publication, by adding \"perhaps\" and stacking extra hedges where they aren't needed. D uses the right cautious tone but mixes in details from the Liberian tailors' fieldwork, so it doesn't actually report the nursing study's finding.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.603Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["claim_certainty_discrimination","purpose_scope_calibration"],"note":"노트에 확정적 사실(1991년 출간, 라이베리아 현장연구)과 잠정적 결과(2014 설문, 저자 단서)가 공존하고, A는 'suggested/may be linked/slightly/could stem from' 등으로 저자들의 신중함을 정확히 재현한다. B는 'proved/produce/confirming'으로 과잉 일반화, C는 1991년 출간이라는 확정 사실까지 'perhaps'로 약화시켜 확실성을 과도하게 축소, D는 신중한 어조이나 재단사 견습 내용과 혼동되어 목표 불충족. 단순 접속어 선택이 아니라 어떤 진술에 어느 수준의 헤지가 적절한지 판별해야 하므로 medium 이상. 다만 B·D는 비교적 쉽게 제거되어 A/C 변별이 난이도의 핵심이며, D의 'local customs' 표현은 노트에 근거가 없어 다소 작위적이지만 오답 기능에는 지장 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["claim_certainty_discrimination"],"note":"정답은 하나로 확정된다. 다만 B는 '증명했다'로 과장했고, C는 모든 진술에 헤지를 붙여 어색하며, D는 주제가 아예 다르다. 세 오답 모두 쉽게 걸러져서 실제 난이도는 medium 수준이다. 'modest', 'hospitals' 같은 표현만 대조해 봐도 A를 고를 수 있다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"batch2-D-cross","gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-h-148","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":"rhetorical_synthesis_certainty_level_choice","recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":"recipe","difficultyStatus":"provisional_ai","review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-h-149","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"hard","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- Linguistic relativity is the idea that the language a person speaks can influence how that person thinks.\n- Cognitive scientist Lera Boroditsky has tested whether language affects how people mentally represent time.\n- In a 2001 study, Mandarin speakers, whose language often describes earlier events as \"up\" and later events as \"down,\" answered questions about time faster after viewing vertically arranged visual primes.\n- In the same study, English speakers, whose language mostly describes time with front/back metaphors, answered such questions faster after viewing horizontally arranged primes.\n- In a 2010 study with Alice Gaby, speakers of Kuuk Thaayorre, an Aboriginal Australian language that uses cardinal directions instead of \"left\" and \"right,\" arranged picture sequences from east to west regardless of which way they faced.","question":"The student wants to contrast how the two groups of participants in Boroditsky's 2001 study were affected by the visual primes. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Whereas many earlier researchers doubted linguistic relativity, Mandarin speakers in Boroditsky's 2001 study answered questions about time faster after viewing vertically arranged primes.","Whereas Mandarin speakers in Boroditsky's 2001 study answered questions about time faster after viewing vertically arranged primes, English speakers did so after viewing horizontally arranged ones.","Whereas Mandarin speakers in Boroditsky's 2001 study answered questions about time faster after viewing vertically arranged primes, Kuuk Thaayorre speakers in a 2010 study arranged pictures from east to west.","Whereas Mandarin speakers in Boroditsky's 2001 study could understand time only through vertically arranged primes, English speakers were unable to process vertical primes at all."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"정답 B: 2001년 연구의 두 집단(중국어 화자·영어 화자)을 모두 다루고, 각각 세로 배열 자극 뒤와 가로 배열 자극 뒤에 더 빨리 답했다는 서로 다른 반응을 대조한다. 목표를 그대로 달성한다.\nA: 중국어 화자에 대한 결과만 담았다. 'Whereas' 뒤에 붙은 '초기 연구자들의 의심'은 노트에 없는 내용이고, 영어 화자 쪽 결과가 빠져서 목표의 절반만 이룬다.\nC: 두 사실을 합치긴 했지만 대조 대상이 2010년 연구의 Kuuk Thaayorre 화자다. 2001년 연구의 두 참가 집단을 대조하라는 목표와 맞지 않는 조합이다.\nD: '오직 세로로만 이해했다', '세로 자극을 전혀 처리하지 못했다'는 주장은 노트에 없다. 노트가 말하는 것은 반응 속도가 더 빨랐다는 점뿐이므로 사실을 왜곡한 선택지다.","explanationEn":"Correct answer, B: This choice covers both groups from the 2001 study, Mandarin speakers and English speakers. It contrasts their results: Mandarin speakers answered faster after vertical primes, and English speakers answered faster after horizontal ones. That is exactly what the goal asks for.\nA: This choice gives only the Mandarin speakers' result. Its contrast is with earlier researchers' doubts, which the notes never mention, and the English speakers' result is missing. So it does only half the job.\nC: This choice does combine two facts, but it compares Mandarin speakers with Kuuk Thaayorre speakers from the 2010 study. The goal is to contrast the two groups in the 2001 study, so this is the wrong pairing.\nD: This choice claims Mandarin speakers could understand time \"only\" through vertical primes and that English speakers \"were unable to process\" vertical primes. Neither claim is in the notes. The notes only say which primes led to faster answers, so this choice distorts the findings.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.603Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["multi_source_goal_integration","purpose_scope_calibration","claim_certainty_discrimination"],"note":"정답 B는 2001년 연구의 두 집단(중국어/영어 화자)과 각기 다른 프라임 반응을 정확히 대조하며 노트 3·4를 통합한다. A는 한쪽 결과만 + 노트에 없는 '초기 연구자들의 의심'(체크리스트 4·5 충족), C는 두 노트를 결합했으나 2010년 연구로 범위 이탈(purpose_scope_calibration 요구), D는 '오직/전혀'로 속도 차이를 능력 유무로 과장(claim_certainty_discrimination). Boroditsky 2001(Mandarin 수직/English 수평 프라임), Boroditsky & Gaby 2010(Kuuk Thaayorre 동→서 배열) 모두 실제 연구와 부합. 해설은 정답 및 오답 근거를 정확히 기술하며 모순 없음. 다만 오답 A·D는 비교적 쉽게 배제되어 hard 중 하위 수준(borderline)으로 판단되며, 실질적 난이도는 C의 범위 판별에서 나온다."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["multi_source_goal_integration","purpose_scope_calibration","claim_certainty_discrimination"],"note":"C는 다른 연구를 끌어온 범위 오류형 오답이고, D는 결과를 과잉 일반화한 확실성 오류형 오답이다. 둘 다 hard 수준의 변별을 요구한다. 다만 정답이 'Whereas' 구조로 두 집단을 대조하고 있어 비교적 쉽게 찾을 수 있다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"batch2-D-cross","gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-h-149","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":"rhetorical_synthesis_dual_fact_merge","recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":"recipe","difficultyStatus":"provisional_ai","review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-h-150","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"hard","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Code-switching, the alternation between two languages within a single conversation, was once dismissed as a sign that bilingual speakers lacked full command of either language. Sociolinguist Mariam Osei has challenged that view. Having recorded more than 300 hours of casual conversation among Twi-English bilingual teenagers in South London, ______ that the speakers' switches into Twi clustered at moments when they were asserting loyalty to friends or distancing themselves from teachers, suggesting that the practice functions as a deliberate tool for negotiating social identity.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["the neighborhood's secondary schools reported","Osei's published study revealed","Osei found","the teenagers themselves noticed"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"분사구문 'Having recorded more than 300 hours of ... conversation'은 녹음을 한 행위자를 주어로 가져야 한다. 녹음을 한 사람은 연구자 Osei이므로 'Osei found'(C)가 정답이다. A: 지역 학교들은 녹음 행위와 아무 관계없는 엉뚱한 주어로, 현수 수식어가 된다. B: 'Osei's published study'는 Osei와 관련은 있지만 사람이 아닌 저작물이다. 연구 결과물이 직접 300시간을 녹음할 수는 없으므로 수식 대상이 맞지 않는다. D: 'the teenagers'는 복수 주어와 'noticed'가 문법적으로 잘 맞고 지문에도 나오는 명사이지만, 이들은 녹음된 대상이지 녹음한 사람이 아니다. 따라서 의미상 수식어가 가리킬 수 없다.","explanationEn":"The sentence begins with the participial phrase \"Having recorded more than 300 hours of casual conversation...\". Whatever comes right after the comma has to be the one who did the recording. That was the researcher, Osei, so \"Osei found\" (C) is correct. A is wrong because the neighborhood's schools have nothing to do with the recording, which leaves the modifier dangling. B names something closely tied to Osei, her published study, but a study is a written work, not a person. A study can't record conversations. D uses a plural subject that agrees with its verb and appears in the passage. However, the teenagers were the people being recorded, not the ones doing the recording, so the modifier can't logically describe them.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.603Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["dangling_modifier_subject_matching"],"note":"문두 분사구문 'Having recorded...'의 행위자는 연구자 Osei이며 C만 이에 부합한다. A·B·D 모두 문법적으로 완전한 문장이고 시제가 동일(과거)하여 수일치·시제로는 변별 불가. B(Osei's published study)는 사람 vs 저작물 범주 함정, D(the teenagers)는 지문에 등장하는 명사이자 녹음 '대상'이라는 의미적 함정으로 설계되어 수식어-피수식어의 의미 연결 추론을 실제로 요구한다. 해설은 각 오답의 탈락 사유를 정확히 서술하며 모순 없음. 가상의 연구자·연구로 사실 오류나 저작권 문제 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["dangling_modifier_subject_matching"],"note":"B(Osei's study, 소유격 함정)와 D(지문에 나오는 teenagers)는 그럴듯한 오답이다. 수일치로는 정답을 가를 수 없다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"batch2-D-cross","gid":"sw-boundaries-h-150","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":"boundaries_dangling_modifier_subject_matching","recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":"recipe","difficultyStatus":"provisional_ai","review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-h-151","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"hard","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In many classrooms of the early 1980s, computers served mainly to drill students on arithmetic facts and to score their answers ______ Logo, the programming language that mathematician Seymour Papert helped design, children gave commands to a screen \"turtle\" so that it would draw shapes, teaching the machine instead of being taught by it.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":[", so in",", in","but in;",", but in"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장은 독립절 두 개로 되어 있다. 앞 절은 컴퓨터가 아이들을 반복 훈련하고 채점하는 데 쓰였다는 내용이고, 뒤 절(in Logo ... children gave commands ...)은 아이들이 오히려 기계를 가르쳤다는 내용이다. 두 절은 서로 대조 관계이므로 쉼표에 대조의 등위접속사 but을 더한 D가 정답이다. A: 쉼표+등위접속사라는 구조는 맞지만, so는 인과를 나타낸다. 반복 훈련 때문에 Logo에서 아이들이 기계를 가르치게 된 것이 아니므로 논리 관계가 맞지 않는다. B: 독립절 두 개를 쉼표 하나로만 이어서 콤마 스플라이스가 된다. C: 세미콜론이 절 경계가 아니라 전치사구 'in Logo' 한가운데에 들어가 있다. 그 결과 뒤쪽은 독립절이 되지 못하고, 앞쪽도 'but in'에서 어색하게 끊긴다.","explanationEn":"This sentence is made of two independent clauses. The first says computers were used to drill and score students. The second (in Logo ... children gave commands ...) says children taught the machine instead. These ideas contrast, so the right fix is a comma plus the contrasting conjunction \"but,\" which is choice D. Choice A has the right structure (comma plus a coordinating conjunction), but \"so\" signals cause and effect. The drilling did not cause children to program the turtle, so the logic doesn't fit. Choice B joins two independent clauses with only a comma, which is a comma splice. Choice C puts the semicolon in the middle of the phrase \"in Logo\" instead of at the boundary between the clauses. That leaves \"but in\" hanging awkwardly, and what follows the semicolon is not an independent clause.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.603Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["independent_clause_boundary_judgment","inserted_modifier_vs_clause_discrimination"],"note":"정답 D 검증: 앞 절(computers served ... answers)과 뒤 절(in Logo, [동격 삽입], children gave commands ...)이 모두 독립절이며 대조 관계 → ', but' 적합. B는 콤마 스플라이스, C는 'in; Logo'로 전치사구 내부에 세미콜론. A(', so')는 구두점 구조는 맞으나 인과 관계가 문맥과 불일치. 수험생은 'in Logo, the programming language ..., children' 에서 동격 삽입구를 절 경계로 오인하지 않고 뒤 절의 주어(children)를 찾아내야 하므로 medium 이상의 사고가 요구됨. 유의점: A는 문법이 아닌 논리(접속사 의미)로만 배제되는 선택지로, 실제 SAT boundaries 문항에서는 다소 드문 변별 방식이나 레시피 체크리스트(항목 2·3)에 부합하므로 형식상 허용 범위로 판정. 사실관계(Logo, Papert, 거북이 그래픽, 1980년대 초 드릴 위주 활용)는 정확함."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["independent_clause_boundary_judgment","inserted_modifier_vs_clause_discrimination"],"note":"정답 D는 대조 관계(반복 훈련 대 아이들이 기계를 가르침)에 맞습니다. A는 so 때문에 인과 관계로 잘못 연결됩니다. B는 콤마 스플라이스, C는 절 경계가 아닌 곳에 세미콜론이 있습니다. 문두 전치사구와 동격 삽입구가 있어 뒤 절의 주어(children)를 찾아야 하므로, 단순한 구두점 판단보다 사고가 더 필요합니다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"batch2-D-cross","gid":"sw-boundaries-h-151","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":"boundaries_clause_relation_punctuation_choice","recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":"recipe","difficultyStatus":"provisional_ai","review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-152","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"The Peace of Westphalia, signed in 1648, ended the Thirty Years' War, a conflict that had begun largely as a struggle between Catholic and Protestant rulers within the Holy Roman Empire. Textbooks often credit the treaties with inventing the modern system of sovereign states, each free from outside interference in its internal affairs. Historian Andreas Osiander and others, however, point out that the documents themselves say little about sovereignty as an abstract principle. Instead, they spend most of their pages settling specific disputes: restoring confiscated lands, confirming the rights of particular princes, and guaranteeing that Calvinism would be tolerated alongside Catholicism and Lutheranism. In this view, the treaties' lasting importance came less from any new theory of statehood than from the practical precedent they set: rulers who disagreed about religion could still negotiate a durable settlement rather than fight until one faith prevailed.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Although often praised for establishing state sovereignty, the Westphalian treaties mattered chiefly because they showed that religious rivals could reach a lasting negotiated peace.","Although the Thirty Years' War began as a religious conflict, the Westphalian treaties were concerned mainly with dividing territory among the Empire's princes.","Although historians long overlooked the Westphalian treaties, recent scholars have shown that they created the principle of noninterference in internal affairs.","Although Calvinism gained toleration at Westphalia, Catholic and Lutheran rulers continued to resist that settlement for decades afterward."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 조약이 주권 국가 체제를 발명했다는 통설에 의문을 던지고, 조약의 진짜 중요성은 종교가 다른 통치자들도 협상으로 지속적 평화를 이룰 수 있다는 실질적 선례에 있다고 결론짓는다. 따라서 A가 정답이다. B는 지문에 언급된 영토 반환 같은 세부를 다루지만, 조약의 의의라는 결론은 빠져 있고 종교적 관용도 무시한다. C는 지문의 주장을 뒤집은 것이다. 지문은 학자들이 조약과 주권 원칙의 연결을 의심한다고 말한다. D는 이후의 저항을 말하는데, 이는 지문에 나오지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The text questions the common claim that the treaties invented sovereign statehood. It concludes that their real significance was a practical precedent: rulers of different faiths could negotiate a durable peace. That makes A correct. B picks up details the passage does mention, like the land settlements, but it leaves out the passage's conclusion about why the treaties mattered and ignores religious toleration. C reverses the argument, because the passage says scholars doubt that the treaties established sovereignty as a principle. D describes later resistance to the settlement, which the text never mentions.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.603Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"history and civics — The Treaty of Westphalia 1648 and its establishment of sovereign nation-state system ending religious warfare","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 A는 지문의 양보(통설: 주권 발명)와 결론(종교적 경쟁자 간 지속적 협상 평화의 선례)을 정확히 포착한다. B는 지문에 실제 언급된 세부(영토 반환·제후 권리)를 근거로 삼아 그럴듯하지만 결론을 놓치고, C는 주장을 뒤집었으며, D는 지문 밖 내용으로 말은 된다. 역사적 사실(1648년, 30년 전쟁, Osiander의 '베스트팔렌 신화' 비판, 칼뱅주의 공인)도 정확. 한·영 해설 모두 일치하고 영어 자연스러움. 양보·전환 구조를 읽어야 하므로 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B는 지문의 세부(영토 문제 해결)를 근거로 삼아 그럴듯한 오답이다. C는 주권 통설을 끌어와 훑어 읽는 수험생을 노린다. D는 약한 오답이지만 Calvinism 관용이라는 근거가 있어 말이 된다. medium 난이도에 적합하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-152","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-153","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Accounts of the Haitian Revolution often begin with the uprising of August 1791, when enslaved workers in Saint-Domingue's Northern Plain set fire to sugar plantations that had made the colony France's most profitable possession. Some historians, however, emphasize that the revolt's success depended less on that single night than on years of organizing that came before it. Enslaved people had built networks across plantations through markets, religious gatherings such as the Bois Caïman ceremony, and the movement of coachmen and drivers who carried messages between estates.\n\nOver the following decade, leaders including Toussaint Louverture turned these networks into disciplined armies capable of defeating French, Spanish, and British forces. When Napoleon sent an expedition in 1802 to restore slavery, it was the depth of this earlier coordination, historians argue, that allowed resistance to survive the capture of Louverture himself, leading to Haiti's independence in 1804.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["The burning of sugar plantations in 1791 was the decisive event that ended France's control over Saint-Domingue.","Connections that enslaved people had established well before 1791 help explain why the revolution ultimately succeeded.","Toussaint Louverture's military leadership was the main reason Haitian forces defeated three European powers.","Religious gatherings such as the Bois Caïman ceremony were the primary means by which enslaved people shared information."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 1791년 봉기 하나보다 그 이전 수년간 노예들이 시장, 종교 모임, 마부 등을 통해 만든 연결망이 혁명 성공의 바탕이었다는 역사가들의 견해를 제시하며, 루베르튀르가 체포된 뒤에도 저항이 지속된 이유로 그 연결망을 든다. 따라서 B가 중심 내용이다. A는 지문이 오히려 반박하는 '단 하룻밤' 관점이다. C는 루베르튀르가 언급되지만 지문은 그가 체포된 뒤에도 저항이 살아남았다고 해 그의 지도력만을 핵심 원인으로 보지 않는다. D는 종교 모임이 여러 수단 중 하나로만 나오므로 '주된' 수단이라는 것은 과장이다.","explanationEn":"The text presents historians' view that the revolution succeeded because of years of organizing before 1791, through markets, religious gatherings, and messengers, more than because of the August uprising alone. It also says this coordination let resistance survive even after Louverture was captured. So B is the main idea. A states the \"single night\" view that the text pushes back against. C picks up on Louverture, but the text points out that resistance went on without him, so his leadership isn't presented as the main cause. D takes one detail too far: religious gatherings are only one of several ways networks formed, and the text never calls them the primary one.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.603Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"history and civics — The Haitian Revolution 1791-1804 and enslaved people's successful overthrow of French colonial plantation economy","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 B 검산: 지문 1단락 \"success depended less on that single night than on years of organizing\" + 2단락 \"depth of this earlier coordination... allowed resistance to survive\"가 B를 직접 뒷받침. A는 지문이 반박하는 관점, C는 루베르튀르 체포 후에도 저항 지속이라는 서술과 상충, D는 여러 수단 중 하나를 '주된' 것으로 과장. 역사적 사실(1791 Northern Plain 봉기, Bois Caïman, 1802 르클레르 원정, 1804 독립) 오류 없음. 해설 한·영 결론 및 선택지 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 난이도: 두 단락 연결(조직화 → 체포 후 생존)이 필요하고 C·D가 부분적으로 지문 근거를 가져 비교가 필요하므로 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"정답 B는 지문 전체(1791년 이전 조직화→성공, 루베르튀르 체포 후에도 저항이 이어짐)로 뒷받침됨. A·C·D는 모두 지문의 세부 내용에 근거한 그럴듯한 오답이라 비교가 필요해 medium에 맞음. 사실 관계(1791년 8월 봉기, 부아 카이망 의식, 1802년 원정, 1804년 독립)도 정확함. 1802년 원정이 노예제 '복원' 목적이었다는 점은 역사학계에서 해석이 갈리지만 지문이 역사가들의 견해로 제시하므로 허용 범위로 봄.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-153","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-154","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"When Parliament repealed the Corn Laws in 1846, ending tariffs that had kept the price of imported grain high, many observers treated the decision as a simple victory of manufacturers over landowners. Historian Cheryl Schonhardt-Bailey has argued that this picture is incomplete. By the 1840s, she notes, many large landowners had invested heavily in railways, canals, and urban property, so their wealth increasingly depended on the same industrial expansion that manufacturers championed. For these landowners, cheaper bread for factory workers promised busier towns and more profitable investments, which made the loss of agricultural protection easier to accept. In Schonhardt-Bailey's view, repeal passed not only because industrial interests overpowered the landed class but also because the economic interests of a significant part of that class had already shifted toward free trade.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Repeal of the Corn Laws occurred mainly because manufacturers gained enough political power to defeat landowners who opposed free trade.","Repeal of the Corn Laws occurred mainly because landowners came to believe that cheaper bread would improve the lives of factory workers.","Repeal of the Corn Laws was made possible in part because many landowners' investments had tied their fortunes to industrial growth.","Repeal of the Corn Laws was made possible in part because railways and canals lowered the cost of importing foreign grain."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 Corn Laws 폐지를 제조업자의 단순한 승리로 보는 시각이 불완전하다는 Schonhardt-Bailey의 주장을 소개한다. 그녀는 많은 지주가 철도·운하·도시 부동산에 투자하면서 이해관계가 이미 산업 성장 쪽으로 옮겨 갔다고 본다. 따라서 C가 중심 생각이다. A는 지문이 '불완전하다'고 비판하는 기존 견해이다. B는 값싼 빵을 언급하지만, 지주의 동기는 노동자 복지가 아니라 자기 투자 수익이었다. D는 철도와 운하를 지주의 투자 대상이 아니라 곡물 수입 비용을 낮춘 요인으로 잘못 연결한다.","explanationEn":"The text presents Schonhardt-Bailey's argument that seeing repeal as a simple win for manufacturers misses part of the story. In her view, many landowners had invested in railways, canals, and urban property, so their interests had already moved toward industrial growth and free trade. That makes C the main idea. A is the older view that the text calls incomplete. B mentions cheaper bread, but the landowners cared about profits on their investments, not about improving workers' lives. D treats railways and canals as things that lowered the cost of grain imports, when the text describes them only as investments landowners made.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.603Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"history and civics — The British Corn Laws repeal 1846 and free trade policy shift reshaping industrial economy","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"지문의 중심 생각(지주의 투자 다변화로 이해관계가 자유무역 쪽으로 이동했다는 Schonhardt-Bailey의 주장)을 C가 정확히 요약함. A는 지문이 '불완전'하다고 비판하는 기존 견해, B는 '값싼 빵'을 지주의 이타적 동기로 왜곡, D는 철도·운하를 투자 대상이 아닌 수입 비용 요인으로 오독 — 세 오답 모두 지문 요소를 포함해 비교가 필요하고 D도 그럴듯함. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 정답 및 오답 배제 근거가 일치하며 한글 혼입 없음. Schonhardt-Bailey의 실제 주장(지주의 포트폴리오 다변화)과도 부합하여 사실 오류 없음. 지문은 자체 작성된 설명문으로 저작권 우려 없음. 중간 난이도 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"C의 'in part'가 지문의 'not only...but also'와 맞는다. A는 기존 견해를 그대로 옮긴 함정이다. B는 값싼 빵이라는 세부를 쓰지만 동기를 잘못 짚었다. D는 철도·운하라는 세부를 다른 인과에 잘못 연결했다. 오답 모두 부분적 근거가 있어 medium 난이도에 적합하다. Schonhardt-Bailey의 실제 주장(지주의 포트폴리오 다각화)과도 부합한다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-154","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-155","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"The Satsuma Rebellion of 1877 is often remembered as the last stand of Japan's samurai against modernization, a romantic clash between swords and rifles. Historians who have examined the rebels' own petitions and letters, however, describe a more complicated picture. Many of the men who followed Saigō Takamori did not reject Western weapons or industry; in fact, the rebel army carried modern rifles and artillery wherever it could get them. What united the rebels was anger at the Meiji government's centralization of power in Tokyo, which had abolished the domains, ended samurai stipends, and banned the wearing of swords in public. These measures took away the status and income that had long defined the samurai class while concentrating authority in a small group of officials. Seen this way, the rebellion was less a refusal of new technology than a protest against who would hold power in the new state and on what terms.","question":"Based on the text, how do historians who studied the rebels' writings interpret the Satsuma Rebellion?","options":["They argue that the rebels were mostly driven by a refusal to give up traditional weapons such as swords in favor of the firearms the Meiji army used.","They argue that the rebels' main goal was to get Western industry adopted faster than the officials in Tokyo were willing to allow.","They argue that the rebels objected mainly to losing their stipends and did not care how political authority was organized in the new state.","They argue that the rebels were reacting mainly to how the reforms redistributed status and political control, not to modern technology itself."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 반란군이 근대 무기를 거부하지 않았고, 권력의 도쿄 집중과 사무라이 지위·수입 박탈에 분노했다고 설명하므로 D가 정답이다. A는 '검 대 소총'이라는 대중적 통념을 따르는데, 역사가들은 바로 이 통념을 반박한다. B는 반란군이 서구 무기를 사용했다는 세부 내용을 확대 해석했을 뿐, 산업화를 더 빨리 하라고 요구했다는 근거는 없다. C는 녹봉 폐지는 맞게 짚었지만, 지문이 권력 집중을 핵심 분노로 강조하므로 '정치 권한에는 관심 없었다'는 부분이 틀렸다.","explanationEn":"The correct answer is D. The text says the rebels didn't reject modern weapons and were angry about power being centralized in Tokyo and about losing their status and income, which is exactly what D states. A repeats the popular \"swords versus rifles\" image, and that's the view the historians argue against. B stretches the detail that the rebels used Western arms, but nothing in the text says they wanted industry adopted faster. C gets the lost stipends right, but it's wrong to say the rebels didn't care how authority was organized, because the text names centralization of power as a main source of their anger.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.603Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"history and civics — The Satsuma Rebellion 1877 and samurai resistance to Meiji modernization centralization reforms","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"지문 마지막 문장(\"less a refusal of new technology than a protest against who would hold power\")이 D를 직접 뒷받침하며, 역사가들의 견해를 묻는 질문이므로 대중적 통념(A)과 구분하는 2단계 판단이 필요함. C는 녹봉 폐지라는 부분적 근거를 가지며 B는 '서구 무기 사용' 세부를 확대한 그럴듯한 오답으로, medium 기준 충족. 역사적 사실(1877년, 사이고 다카모리, 폐번치현·질록처분·폐도령, 반란군의 근대 소총 사용) 모두 무리 없음. 한·영 해설 결론 및 선택지 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"D는 마지막 문장을 바꿔 말한 것이다. A는 통념, C는 일부만 맞는 오답이다. B는 비교적 쉽게 배제되지만 그럴듯하다. 역사적 사실(번 폐지, 녹봉 폐지, 폐도령)도 정확하다. 목표 난이도(medium)에 적합하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-155","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-160","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In March 1918, Bolshevik Russia signed the Treaty of Brest-Litovsk with the Central Powers, ending its part in World War One. The terms were severe: Russia gave up Poland, the Baltic territories, Finland, and Ukraine, which together held about a third of its population and much of its coal and grain. Many historians have described the treaty simply as a humiliating defeat forced on a collapsing state. __Yet Lenin had pushed for accepting the terms over the objections of many fellow Bolsheviks, arguing that the new regime could not survive both a foreign war and the struggle to hold power at home.__ Seen this way, the treaty was a calculated trade of territory for time, and when Germany lost the war later that year, the Bolsheviks quickly declared the agreement void.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It introduces a detail that complicates a common view of the treaty and prepares for a different reading of it.","It introduces a detail that explains why the treaty's territorial losses were as large as the text earlier indicates.","It introduces a detail that supports the historians' claim that Russia was a collapsing state in 1918.","It introduces a detail that shows how Germany eventually came to reject the terms of the treaty."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 시작해 조약을 단순한 굴욕적 패배로 보는 통념에 반하는 사실, 즉 레닌이 국내 권력 유지를 위해 의도적으로 조약 수락을 밀어붙였다는 점을 제시하고, 이어지는 '영토와 시간을 맞바꾼 계산된 거래'라는 해석의 토대를 마련하므로 A가 정답이다. B는 앞 문장의 영토 상실 내용과 연결되어 보이지만, 밑줄 문장은 손실 규모가 왜 컸는지를 설명하지 않는다. C는 국내 투쟁이라는 언급이 '붕괴하는 국가'와 겹쳐 보이지만, 문장의 역할은 역사가들의 견해를 지지하는 것이 아니라 그 견해를 복잡하게 만드는 것이다. D는 마지막 문장 내용과 혼동한 것으로, 조약을 무효로 선언한 쪽은 독일이 아니라 볼셰비키이고 밑줄 문장에서도 다루지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence begins with \"Yet\" and gives a fact that cuts against the common view of the treaty as nothing more than a humiliating defeat: Lenin deliberately pushed for accepting it so the regime could hold power at home. That fact sets up the next sentence's reading of the treaty as a calculated trade of territory for time, so A is correct. B links the sentence to the territorial losses mentioned earlier, but the sentence never explains why those losses were so large. C picks up on the mention of a struggle at home, which might seem to fit the \"collapsing state\" view, but the sentence complicates the historians' view instead of supporting it. D mixes up the final sentence: it was the Bolsheviks, not Germany, who declared the treaty void, and the underlined sentence doesn't discuss that at all.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.603Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"history and civics — The Treaty of Brest-Litovsk 1918 and Bolshevik Russia's exit from World War One conflict","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 통념(굴욕적 패배)에 반하는 레닌의 의도적 수락 근거를 제시하고 다음 문장의 '영토-시간 교환' 해석을 준비하므로 A가 정확. B(영토 손실 규모 설명)·C(붕괴 국가 견해 지지)는 지문 일부와 부분적으로 겹쳐 비교가 필요하고, D는 마지막 문장과의 혼동으로 성립 가능한 오답. 역사적 사실(1918년 3월 체결, 상실 영토, 레닌의 당내 반대 극복, 독일 패전 후 볼셰비키의 무효 선언) 모두 정확. 한·영 해설 결론 및 선택지 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 두 단계 판단(통념 대비 + 이어지는 재해석 연결)이 요구되어 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"사실관계(1918년 3월, 영토·인구 약 1/3, 11월 무효화) 정확. C가 가장 강한 오답이고 B는 그럴듯하며, D는 비교적 쉽게 배제됨. 중간 난이도로 적절.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-160","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-161","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In the decades after 1937, accounts of the Nanjing Massacre, in which Japanese troops killed large numbers of Chinese civilians and prisoners after capturing the city, were often dismissed in Japan as wartime propaganda. Historians seeking to establish the scale of the atrocities therefore faced a problem of credibility: testimony from Chinese survivors, however detailed, could be waved away as biased. Some researchers responded by turning to sources that skeptics could not easily reject. __Among the most revealing of these were the diaries of Japanese soldiers themselves, several of which record executions of captives in matter-of-fact entries written with no expectation of public scrutiny.__ Because such documents came from the perpetrators' side and were not produced to persuade anyone, they made it far harder to claim that the massacre had been invented by its victims.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It introduces survivor testimony that historians relied on to counter claims that the massacre was wartime propaganda.","It presents a specific kind of evidence that addresses the difficulty of credibility described earlier in the text.","It identifies a kind of evidence whose reliability the text goes on to question because of who produced it.","It offers a detail that explains why skeptics in Japan first came to doubt accounts of the massacre."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 생존자 증언이 편향되었다며 무시당하는 신뢰성 문제를 제기한 뒤, 밑줄 문장에서 일본 병사들의 일기라는 구체적 증거를 제시하고, 마지막 문장에서 그것이 왜 문제를 해결하는지 설명한다. 따라서 B가 정답이다. A는 반박 기능은 맞지만 밑줄 문장의 증거는 생존자 증언이 아니라 가해자 측 일기이다. C는 증거의 출처를 언급하지만, 지문은 그 출처 때문에 오히려 신뢰성이 높다고 말한다. D는 회의론을 언급하지만, 밑줄 문장은 의심의 원인을 설명하지 않고 의심을 반박한다.","explanationEn":"The text first raises a credibility problem: survivor testimony could be dismissed as biased. The underlined sentence then presents a specific kind of evidence, Japanese soldiers' diaries, and the final sentence explains why that evidence solves the problem. So B is correct. A gets the rebuttal role right, but the evidence in the sentence is perpetrators' diaries, not survivor testimony. C mentions who produced the evidence, but the text says that origin makes the diaries more credible, not less. D brings up the skeptics, but the sentence answers their doubts instead of explaining where those doubts came from.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.603Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"history and civics — The Nanjing Massacre 1937 and Japanese military atrocities during Second Sino-Japanese War","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 앞서 제기된 신뢰성 문제에 대한 구체적 증거(가해자 측 일기)를 제시하며, 마지막 문장이 그 효과를 설명하는 구조. B 정답 확인. A(증언 종류 오류), C(신뢰성 방향 반대), D(의심의 원인 아님) 모두 적절히 배제됨. 한국어·영어 해설 결론과 글자 참조 일치, 사실 오류 없음, medium 난이도 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"정답 B가 명확하다. A(생존자 증언), C(신뢰성 의심)는 지문의 단어를 끌어온 그럴듯한 오답이라 비교가 필요하다. D는 비교적 쉽게 배제된다. 지문의 사실 서술(일본 병사 일기 등)은 역사적으로 타당하다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-161","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-162","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In April 1955, delegates from twenty-nine Asian and African states gathered in Bandung, Indonesia, to discuss cooperation among nations that had recently won, or were still seeking, independence from colonial rule. Many Western observers predicted that the meeting would simply split into pro-American and pro-Soviet blocs, since several attending governments already had close ties to one of the superpowers. __Yet the conference's final communiqué endorsed ten principles, including respect for sovereignty and abstention from collective defense arrangements serving the interests of any great power, that nearly every delegation accepted.__ Historians now view those principles as an early basis for the Non-Aligned Movement, which was formally launched in Belgrade in 1961.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It explains why several attending governments chose to keep their existing ties to one of the superpowers.","It identifies the specific disagreements that kept the delegations from issuing a joint statement.","It presents an outcome that runs counter to a forecast described earlier and sets up a later claim about the meeting's legacy.","It describes the circumstances in Belgrade that led to the formal launch of the Non-Aligned Movement."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 시작해 회의가 강대국 진영별로 쪼개질 거라던 서방의 예측과 달리 거의 모든 대표단이 10개 원칙을 받아들였다는 결과를 보여 주고, 이 원칙은 다음 문장에서 비동맹운동의 토대로 이어진다. 따라서 C가 정답이다. A는 강대국과의 유대가 언급되긴 하지만 밑줄 문장은 그 이유를 설명하지 않는다. B는 공동 성명이 실제로 채택되었으므로 내용과 반대된다. D는 베오그라드가 마지막 문장에 나오긴 하지만 밑줄 문장은 반둥 회의의 결과를 다룰 뿐 베오그라드 상황을 설명하지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence starts with \"Yet,\" which tells you it contrasts with the Western prediction that the conference would split into superpower blocs. It shows that nearly every delegation accepted ten shared principles, and the next sentence links those principles to the Non-Aligned Movement. That makes C correct. A is wrong because the text does mention superpower ties, but the underlined sentence doesn't explain why governments kept them. B is wrong because a joint communiqué actually was issued, so it says the opposite of the text. D is wrong because Belgrade appears only in the final sentence, while the underlined sentence describes what happened at Bandung, not the conditions in Belgrade.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.603Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"history and civics — The Bandung Conference 1955 and Non-Aligned Movement establishment opposing Cold War superpowers","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 서방 예측(진영 분열)과 대비되는 결과(거의 모든 대표단이 10개 원칙 수용)를 제시하고, 다음 문장의 비동맹운동 유산 주장으로 이어지므로 C가 정확. 역사적 사실(1955년 반둥, 29개국, 10개 원칙, 1961년 베오그라드 NAM 출범) 모두 정확. A·D는 지문 내 실제 언급(강대국 유대, 베오그라드)을 활용한 부분적 근거 있는 오답, B는 직접 모순이지만 말이 되는 오답. 한국어·영어 해설 결론과 선택지 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 난이도는 대비 신호 파악+뒤 문장 연결이라는 두 단계 판단이 필요해 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["too_easy","eliminated:3"],"note":"정답 C는 예측과 반대되는 결과 제시 + 이후 유산 주장 연결이라는 두 기능을 정확히 담고 있다. 사실관계(1955년 반둥, 29개국, 10개 원칙, 1961년 베오그라드)도 정확하다. 다만 오답이 약하다. B는 공동 성명이 채택되었다는 본문 내용과 정면으로 어긋나 바로 배제된다. A와 D는 본문 단어(초강대국과의 유대, 베오그라드)를 빌려 왔을 뿐 밑줄 문장의 내용과 연결되지 않아 비교해 볼 필요 없이 탈락한다. 'Yet' 하나만 봐도 대조 기능이 드러나고 C만 이를 담고 있어 훑어 읽어도 맞힐 수 있다. 따라서 medium 기준(부분적으로 맞는 근거를 가진 오답 2개 이상)에 미달한다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-162","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-words_in_context-m-163","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Words in Context","difficulty":"medium","skill":"words_in_context","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"When East German authorities strung barbed wire across Berlin on the night of August 13, 1961, many Western observers assumed the barrier would be temporary, a crude measure that would be dismantled once the flood of emigrants slowed. Instead, over the following years the wire was replaced by concrete slabs, watchtowers, and a cleared \"death strip,\" and the structure came to seem less like an emergency improvisation than a permanent feature of the city. For historians, this hardening is significant: it shows that the division of Berlin was not a passing crisis but had become ______ in the physical landscape itself, making the ideological split between East and West visible on every street it crossed.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["concealed","contested","anticipated","entrenched"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 임시 철조망이 콘크리트·감시탑 등으로 바뀌며 '영구적 특징'이 되었고, 분단이 '일시적 위기가 아니었다'고 대비하므로 빈칸에는 깊이 굳어 고착되었다는 뜻이 필요하다. 따라서 D(entrenched)가 정답이다. A(concealed)는 분단이 '모든 거리에서 보이게' 되었다는 내용과 정반대이다. B(contested)는 베를린 분단이 실제로 논쟁 대상이었다는 점에서 그럴듯하지만, 지문의 초점은 영구화이지 이견이 아니다. C(anticipated)는 서방 관찰자들이 장벽이 일시적일 것이라고 예상했다는 부분과 연결되어 보이지만, 오히려 그들은 영구화를 예상하지 못했으므로 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The passage contrasts the early view of the barrier as temporary with its transformation into concrete walls and watchtowers that made it \"a permanent feature,\" so the blank needs a word meaning firmly and lastingly established. That makes D (entrenched) the correct choice. A (concealed) contradicts the claim that the split became visible on every street. B (contested) sounds plausible because the division was politically disputed, but the passage is about permanence, not disagreement. C (anticipated) may seem to fit the mention of observers' expectations, but those observers expected the barrier to be temporary, so its permanence was not anticipated.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.604Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"history and civics — The Berlin Wall construction 1961 and divided German city symbolizing ideological partition","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"빈칸 앞 '일시적 위기가 아니라'와 '영구적 특징' 대비로 '깊이 굳어진'(entrenched)이 유일하게 정확히 맞음. 역사적 사실(1961.8.13 철조망→콘크리트·감시탑·죽음의 띠) 정확. 오답 중 B(contested)·C(anticipated)는 지문 일부와 연결되는 부분적 근거가 있어 비교가 필요하고 A는 '보이게 되었다'와 정반대로 말은 됨. 해설 한·영 결론 및 글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 단서가 비교적 뚜렷해 medium 중 다소 쉬운 편이나 두 정보(임시→영구 전환 + '보이게' 됨) 연결이 필요하므로 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"'entrenched in the physical landscape'는 영구화를 정확히 나타낸다. contested와 anticipated는 부분적 근거가 있어 그럴듯한 오답이고, concealed는 visible과 모순되어 배제된다. 사실 관계(1961년 8월 13일, 철조망에서 콘크리트 장벽으로의 전환)도 정확하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-words_in_context-m-163","intendedSkill":"words_in_context","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-h-165","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"hard","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In November 1995, delegations from Bosnia and Herzegovina, Croatia, and the Federal Republic of Yugoslavia met at Wright-Patterson Air Force Base near Dayton, Ohio, to negotiate an end to more than three years of war. Isolated on the base for three weeks and pressed daily by American mediator Richard Holbrooke, ______ a settlement that divided Bosnia into two largely autonomous entities under a single, weak central government.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["the air force base's remote location eventually produced","the delegations' leaders eventually accepted","the leaders' signed treaty eventually established","the three weeks of talks eventually yielded"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"정답 B. 문두 분사구문 'Isolated on the base for three weeks and pressed daily by American mediator Richard Holbrooke'의 의미상 주어는 기지에 고립되어 중재자에게 매일 압박을 받은 존재여야 한다. 그런 존재는 사람, 즉 대표단의 지도자들뿐이므로 주절 주어는 'the delegations' leaders'가 되어야 한다.\nA: 'the air force base's remote location'은 수식어와 관계없는 엉뚱한 명사다. 기지의 위치가 기지에 고립되거나 홀브룩에게 압박받을 수는 없으므로 현수 수식어(dangling modifier)가 된다.\nC: 'the leaders' signed treaty'는 지도자들 자체가 아니라 그들이 만든 결과물(조약)이다. 범주가 다른 명사이므로 조약이 3주간 고립되고 압박받았다는 엉뚱한 뜻이 된다.\nD: 'the three weeks of talks'는 문맥과 관련이 있고 복수 동사와도 잘 어울리지만, '3주간의 회담'이 '기지에서 3주간 고립되었다'는 것은 말이 안 되며 중재자에게 압박받을 수도 없다. 의미상 수식 대상이 될 수 없다.","explanationEn":"The answer is B. The sentence opens with a participial phrase: \"Isolated on the base for three weeks and pressed daily by American mediator Richard Holbrooke.\" Whatever comes right after the comma must be the thing that was isolated and pressed. Only people can be pressed by a mediator, so the subject has to be \"the delegations' leaders.\"\nA is wrong because \"the air force base's remote location\" has nothing to do with the modifier. A location can't be isolated on the base or pressured by Holbrooke, so the modifier dangles.\nC is wrong because \"the leaders' signed treaty\" is something the leaders produced, not the leaders themselves. With this subject, the sentence says the treaty was isolated and pressured.\nD is tempting because it fits the context and the plural verb works. But \"three weeks of talks\" can't be \"isolated on the base for three weeks,\" and talks can't be pressed by a mediator. The modifier can't logically describe it.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.604Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["dangling_modifier_subject_matching"],"note":"문두 분사구문 'Isolated... and pressed daily by Holbrooke'의 의미상 주어는 사람(대표단 지도자들)뿐이므로 B가 유일한 정답. A/C/D 모두 문법적으로 완전한 문장이며, 특히 D는 문맥상 관련 있는 명사(3주간의 회담)로 구성되어 의미적 연결 추론을 실제로 요구함. 모든 동사가 과거형이라 수일치로는 변별 불가. 데이턴 협상 관련 사실(1995년 11월, 라이트-패터슨 기지, 홀브룩, 두 개의 자치 실체·약한 중앙정부) 정확."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["dangling_modifier_subject_matching"],"note":"이중 분사구문(isolated/pressed)의 의미상 주어는 사람이어야 한다. D(talks)와 C(treaty)는 문맥과 관련이 있어 그럴듯한 오답이다. 모든 선택지가 과거형이라 수일치로는 정답을 가를 수 없다. 데이턴 협정 관련 사실(1995년 11월, 라이트-패터슨 공군기지, 약 3주, 두 개의 자치체)도 정확하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"batch2-D-cross","gid":"sw-boundaries-h-165","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":"boundaries_dangling_modifier_subject_matching","recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":"recipe","difficultyStatus":"provisional_ai","review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-168","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In the brewing towns of the southern Low Countries during the seventeenth and eighteenth centuries, a brewery's most valuable asset was often invisible: the particular yeast culture that gave its beer a distinctive flavor. Unlike a recipe, which could be copied once written down, a yeast culture had to be kept alive, carried from batch to batch, and handled with skill that only experience could teach. Brewing guilds turned this fact to their members' advantage. Guild rules limited how many apprentices a master could take on, required apprentices to serve for years before they could brew on their own, and barred journeymen from setting up rival breweries within a set distance of their former masters.\n\nHistorians have sometimes read such rules simply as tools for keeping out competitors. Economic historian Lieve Claes argues that this reading misses their main function. Because no law at the time protected a living culture as property, she contends, the guilds' control over who could learn brewing, and when, served as a substitute for patent protection: the knowledge needed to maintain a valuable strain passed only to those bound by long obligations to the brewery that owned it.","question":"According to Claes, what was the chief purpose of the guild rules governing apprentices and journeymen?","options":["They kept the skills needed to maintain a brewery's yeast culture within a circle of workers committed to that brewery, protecting the culture when no law did.","They kept rival breweries far from established masters, protecting the masters' local customers when the guilds feared growing competition.","They kept written recipes within a circle of trusted guild members, protecting those recipes when copying became easy.","They kept apprentices in long periods of training, protecting the quality of guild beer when inexperienced brewers threatened its reputation."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"Claes는 법이 살아 있는 효모 배양균을 재산으로 보호하지 못했기 때문에, 길드가 누가 언제 양조를 배우는지 통제한 것이 특허를 대신하는 역할을 했다고 주장한다. 그래서 효모를 유지하는 지식이 양조장에 오래 묶인 사람들에게만 전해졌다는 A가 정답이다. B는 Claes가 핵심을 놓쳤다고 비판한 역사가들의 '경쟁 배제' 해석이다. C는 지문에서 쉽게 베낄 수 있다고 대비시킨 레시피를 보호 대상으로 착각한 것이다. D의 긴 수습 기간은 실제 규칙이 맞지만, 지문은 그 목적을 맥주의 품질이나 평판과 연결하지 않는다.","explanationEn":"Claes argues that because no law protected a living yeast culture as property, the guilds' control over who could learn brewing, and when, worked as a substitute for patent protection. That makes A correct: the know-how for keeping a strain alive passed only to workers bound to the brewery that owned it. B describes the \"keeping out competitors\" reading, which is the view Claes says misses the rules' main function. C gets the thing being protected wrong, since the text contrasts written recipes, which could be copied, with yeast cultures. D mentions a real rule, the long apprenticeship, but the text never connects it to beer quality or reputation.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.604Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"economics and business — Belgian brewing guilds and proprietary yeast strains as trade secrets enforced through apprenticeship restriction","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"지문 2문단 \"served as a substitute for patent protection… passed only to those bound by long obligations to the brewery\" 가 A와 정확히 대응. B는 Claes가 반박한 역사가들의 해석(훑어 읽으면 고르기 쉬운 매력적 오답), C는 레시피/효모 대비를 뒤집은 것, D는 실제 규칙이나 목적 귀속이 지문에 없음. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 동일 결론·글자 참조, 모순 없음. 가상의 역사가 설정으로 사실 오류 없음. 두 관점 구분 + 보호 대상 식별이라는 2단계 판단이 필요해 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B는 실제 규칙(거리 제한)과 역사가들의 해석을 근거로 하고, D는 실제 규칙(긴 수습 기간)을 근거로 해 둘 다 부분적으로 맞는 근거가 있다. C는 레시피 대비를 잘못 읽은 경우다. 정답 A는 Claes의 주장을 정확히 바꿔 말한 것이다. medium 난이도에 적합하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-168","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-169","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Norway produces more farmed Atlantic salmon than any other country, most of it raised in open-net pens anchored in coastal fjords. Because the mesh of these pens lets water flow freely between farm and sea, parasites such as salmon lice can multiply among the densely packed farmed fish and then drift outward, where they attach to young wild salmon migrating past on their way to the ocean. Studies along the Norwegian coast have linked high lice levels near farms to lower survival among these wild migrants. Yet the farms' operating costs barely reflect this harm: a company pays for feed, labor, and treatments for its own fish, but the losses suffered by wild populations, and by the river anglers and tourism businesses that depend on them, appear on no farm's balance sheet. Economists describe such a situation as a negative externality, and some argue that Norway's recent move to tie permitted production growth to measured lice levels in each coastal zone is an attempt to make producers bear part of a cost that the open-net design had pushed onto others.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Salmon lice that develop in open-net pens are the main reason wild Atlantic salmon populations in Norway have declined, so Norway has banned further expansion of coastal farming.","Open-net salmon farming in Norway passes parasite-related harm onto wild fish and those who rely on them without that harm appearing in farm costs, a problem some regulation tries to correct.","Norwegian salmon farms spend heavily on feed, labor, and lice treatments, which economists argue makes open-net farming more costly than alternative methods.","River anglers and tourism businesses in Norway have demanded compensation from salmon farms because lice from the pens have reduced the number of wild salmon."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 글은 개방형 가두리에서 퍼진 연어 이가 야생 연어에 피해를 주지만 그 비용이 양식장 비용에 반영되지 않는다는 점(부정적 외부효과)과, 일부에서 이를 바로잡으려는 시도로 보는 규제를 함께 다루므로 B가 정답이다. A는 이와 야생 연어 감소의 연관은 맞게 짚었지만 '주된 원인'이라고 과장했고, 글은 확장 금지가 아니라 이 수치에 따라 성장을 허용하는 규제를 설명한다. C는 양식장이 사료·인건비·처치 비용을 낸다는 세부는 맞지만, 글의 요점은 양식장이 부담하지 '않는' 비용이고 다른 양식 방식과의 비교는 나오지 않는다. D는 낚시꾼과 관광업체가 피해를 본다는 내용은 맞지만, 이들이 보상을 요구했다는 내용은 글에 없다.","explanationEn":"B is correct because the passage explains that lice spreading from open-net pens harm wild salmon, yet that cost never shows up in farm expenses (a negative externality), and it presents a regulation that some see as an attempt to fix this. A rightly links lice to wild salmon losses, but it overstates them as the \"main reason,\" and the passage describes rules that tie growth to lice levels, not a ban on expansion. C repeats real details about feed, labor, and treatment costs, but the passage's point is about the costs farms do not pay, and it never compares open-net farming with other methods. D correctly notes that anglers and tourism businesses are harmed, but the passage never says they asked for compensation.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.604Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"economics and business — Norwegian salmon farming open-net cage externalities imposing disease spillover costs onto wild Atlantic stocks","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"지문의 핵심(개방형 가두리 → 야생 연어 피해 → 비용 미반영=부정적 외부효과 → 이를 교정하려는 규제)을 B가 정확히 포괄. A는 '주된 원인'과 '확장 금지'로 과장·왜곡, C는 세부(사료·인건비·처치비)는 맞으나 요지와 반대 방향이며 대안 방식 비교는 지문에 없음, D는 피해 당사자는 맞으나 보상 요구는 미언급. 오답 셋 모두 부분적 근거를 가져 비교 배제가 필요하므로 medium 적합. 노르웨이 최대 생산국·이 수치 기반 생산 증가 규제(신호등 시스템)는 사실과 부합. 한·영 해설 결론 및 선택지 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"Norway's traffic-light system (tying production growth to lice levels by zone) matches reality. The wrong options are partly right and are each ruled out for a different reason. B is a bit longer than the others, but that is within the acceptable range.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-169","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-171","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In the early nineteenth century, much of the indigo grown in Bengal was sold through a few London merchant houses. These houses often agreed among themselves on what they would pay at the city's quarterly auctions. Some historians have argued that this coordination kept prices artificially low, squeezing the planters who shipped dye from India. Economic historian Priya Natarajan finds that account incomplete. __Comparing auction records with planters' private ledgers, she found that in years when the syndicates' agreed bids fell, planters' costs often fell even faster, because the same merchant houses were extending them cheaper credit against future harvests.__ In Natarajan's view, the syndicates controlled the trade less through the auction price itself than through the loans that tied planters to them season after season.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It shows that the merchant syndicates' coordinated bidding had no measurable effect on the prices paid for Bengal indigo.","It gives evidence supporting the historians' claim that the syndicates kept prices low mainly to squeeze Bengal planters.","It explains how the London merchant houses first came to agree among themselves on bids at the quarterly auctions.","It gives evidence that complicates an earlier interpretation and leads to the alternative explanation stated afterward."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 Natarajan이 기존 해석(담합이 가격을 낮춰 재배자를 압박했다)을 '불완전하다'고 본 근거로, 입찰가 하락과 함께 신용 비용도 내려갔다는 기록 비교 결과를 제시한다. 이것이 마지막 문장의 대안적 설명(통제는 대출을 통해 이루어졌다)으로 이어지므로 D가 정답이다. A는 입찰가가 실제로 떨어졌다는 내용과 모순되며, 과장된 주장이다. B는 문장이 가격 하락을 언급하긴 하지만 기존 주장을 지지하는 것이 아니라 복잡하게 만든다는 점을 놓쳤다. C는 담합의 기원을 다루는데, 지문은 그 내용을 전혀 설명하지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence gives the evidence behind Natarajan's view that the earlier account is \"incomplete.\" Her records show that planters' costs fell along with the bids, because of cheap credit. That finding leads into the final sentence's alternative explanation, that control worked through loans, so D is correct. A goes too far and contradicts the text: the bids did fall, so the bidding wasn't shown to have no effect. B notices that prices fell, but it misses that the sentence complicates the historians' claim instead of supporting it. C is about how the agreements began, and the text never explains that.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.604Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"economics and business — Indian indigo dye price fixing by London merchant syndicates during colonial monopoly trade control","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 \"finds that account incomplete\" 뒤에 오는 근거이며, 마지막 문장의 대안 설명(대출을 통한 통제)으로 이어지므로 D가 유일한 정답. A는 입찰가가 실제로 떨어졌다는 본문과 모순(과잉 진술), B는 방향이 반대(지지가 아닌 복잡화), C는 지문에 없는 기원 설명. A·B는 부분적 근거(가격 하락 언급, 기존 해석 약화)를 가져 비교가 필요하고 C도 지문 소재와 연결되어 medium에 적합. 한·영 해설 모두 D를 일관되게 뒷받침하며 선택지 참조 정확, 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 가상의 학자명 사용으로 사실 오류·저작권 우려 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["too_easy","eliminated:2"],"note":"비교가 필요한 오답은 B 하나뿐이다. A('효과 없음')는 극단적 진술이고 지문과도 바로 모순되며, C(담합의 기원)는 지문에 근거가 전혀 없어 쉽게 배제된다. 정답 D는 '반증 증거 → 대안 설명'이라는 전형적 구조라서 훑어 읽어도 고를 수 있다. 오답 3개 중 최소 2개가 부분적으로 맞는 근거를 가져야 한다는 medium 기준에 미달한다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-171","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-172","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Accounts of colonial Potosí's enormous silver output often credit two factors: unusually rich ore and the mercury amalgamation process, which let refiners extract silver from lower-grade rock. Economic historian Rossana Quiroga argues that these accounts miss a third factor, labor costs. In the 1570s Viceroy Francisco de Toledo expanded the earlier labor demands of the encomienda system into the mita, a rotating draft that required Andean communities to send about one-seventh of their adult men to the mines each year. __Drafted workers, or mitayos, were paid wages, but officials fixed those wages at roughly a third of what freely hired miners earned for similar work.__ Since mitayos also had to pay for their own travel and food, their home villages often sent money and supplies to keep them alive. In effect, Quiroga contends, Andean communities were covering part of the mines' labor bill, and mine owners' profits depended as much on this hidden subsidy as on the quality of the ore.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It identifies the specific arrangement that the text later shows shifted mining costs onto Andean villages.","It presents the conventional explanation for Potosí's silver output that Quiroga's argument challenges.","It offers evidence that the mita was less coercive than its description as a forced draft would suggest.","It describes a cost of the mercury amalgamation process that the text later says refiners passed on to workers."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 미타요의 임금이 자유 노동자의 약 3분의 1로 고정되었다는 사실을 제시하고, 이어지는 문장들은 이 낮은 임금 때문에 마을들이 노동자를 부양해야 했고 결국 광산 노동비 일부를 떠안았다고 설명하므로 A가 정답이다. B는 틀렸다. 통념적 설명(풍부한 광석, 아말감 공정)은 첫 문장에 나오며, 밑줄 문장은 오히려 Quiroga의 주장을 뒷받침한다. C는 임금이 지급되었다는 점만 보고 고른 오답으로, 이 문장의 요점은 임금이 억제되었다는 것이지 강제성이 약했다는 것이 아니다. D는 아말감 공정이 지문에 언급되어 그럴듯해 보이지만, 임금은 정련 공정의 비용이 아니라 노동 징발 제도의 일부이다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence states that mitayos' wages were fixed at about a third of free miners' pay. The sentences after it explain that because pay was so low, home villages had to support the workers, which meant they were covering part of the mines' labor costs. So A is correct. B is wrong because the conventional explanation (rich ore and amalgamation) comes in the first sentence, and the underlined sentence actually supports Quiroga's challenge to it. C picks up on the fact that wages were paid, but the point of the sentence is that wages were kept low, not that the system was less coercive. D may seem plausible because amalgamation appears in the text, but the wages belong to the labor draft, not to the refining process.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.604Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"economics and business — Peruvian silver mining encomienda labor system extracting colonial wealth through forced wage suppression mechanisms","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장(미타요 임금을 자유 노동자의 약 1/3로 고정)은 이후 문장에서 마을이 노동자를 부양하게 된 원인으로 연결되므로 A가 정확하다. B는 첫 문장의 통념 설명과 혼동을 유도하고, C는 '임금 지급'이라는 표면 정보를, D는 지문에 등장한 아말감 공정을 활용한 그럴듯한 오답으로 기능한다. 역사적 사실(톨레도의 1570년대 미타 제도화, 약 1/7 징발, 미타요 임금이 자유 노동자보다 낮음)은 통설과 부합한다. Quiroga는 허구적 학자로 보이나 SAT 관행상 문제 없음. 한·영 해설 모두 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 두 단계 판단(문장 내용 파악 + 이후 문맥 연결)이 요구되어 medium에 적합하다."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"A가 정답이려면 밑줄 문장(낮게 고정된 임금)을 이후 문장(마을의 보조, 숨은 보조금)과 연결해야 하므로 두 단계 판단이 필요하다. B는 지문에 나오는 통념적 설명을, D는 아말감 공정 언급을, C는 임금 지급 사실을 각각 이용해 그럴듯해 보인다. 다만 B와 D는 비교적 쉽게 배제된다. 역사적 배경(톨레도, 1570년대, 성인 남성 약 7분의 1)은 대체로 정확하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-172","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-173","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In the seventeenth century, the Dutch East India Company (VOC) sought to control the global supply of cloves and nutmeg by confining their cultivation to a few islands it governed directly, such as Ambon and the Banda Islands. Company officials regularly sent expeditions to uproot spice trees growing elsewhere in the archipelago, and VOC trading posts on Java were forbidden to buy spices from local growers. Some historians have described these measures as evidence that the company feared Javanese farmers would outproduce its own plantations. __Yet the records of the trading posts themselves suggest a different worry: officials complained far more often about Javanese merchants reselling spices to English and Portuguese buyers than about the size of Javanese harvests.__ On this reading, the restrictions had less to do with how much farmers grew than with who could carry the spices to market, since any leak beyond the company's ships would weaken its ability to set prices in Europe.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It presents evidence that Javanese harvests were too small to threaten the company's plantations, which supports the historians' view mentioned earlier.","It introduces documentary evidence that points to a concern other than the one some historians have emphasized, setting up the interpretation that follows.","It introduces a claim about English and Portuguese buyers that the rest of the text goes on to show was exaggerated by company officials.","It introduces an example of the company's policies on Java that illustrates the expeditions to uproot spice trees described earlier."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 \"Yet\"으로 시작해 일부 역사가들의 해석(자와 농민의 생산 경쟁에 대한 두려움)과 달리, 교역소 기록이 재판매 문제라는 다른 우려를 보여 준다고 제시하며, 이어지는 문장이 이를 바탕으로 해석을 전개하므로 B가 정답이다. A는 기록을 언급한다는 점은 맞지만, 수확 규모가 작았다고 주장하지 않았고 역사가들의 견해를 지지하는 것도 아니라 반박한다. C는 영국·포르투갈 구매자를 언급한다는 점은 맞지만, 뒤 문장은 그 우려가 과장되었다고 하지 않고 오히려 이를 해석의 근거로 삼는다. D는 회사 정책과 연결된 것처럼 보이지만, 밑줄 문장은 정책의 예시가 아니라 기록을 근거로 한 반론이다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence opens with \"Yet.\" It says the trading-post records point to a different worry, Javanese merchants reselling spices to rivals, not the fear of being outproduced that some historians have emphasized. The final sentence then builds its interpretation on that evidence, so B is correct. A is right that the sentence cites records, but the sentence never says Javanese harvests were small, and it challenges the historians' view instead of supporting it. C is right that the sentence mentions English and Portuguese buyers, but the text never calls that worry exaggerated; it uses the worry as the basis of its interpretation. D fails because the sentence isn't an example of a company policy; it offers evidence that pushes back on an earlier interpretation.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.604Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"economics and business — Indonesian spice monopoly enforcement and Dutch trading post restrictions preventing Javanese cultivation competition","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 \"Yet\"으로 역사가들의 해석과 대비되는 기록 증거를 제시하고, 마지막 문장(\"On this reading\")이 이를 바탕으로 해석을 전개하므로 B가 정확하다. A는 기록을 인용한다는 점만 맞고 수확 규모·역사가 지지 부분이 틀림, C는 영국·포르투갈 언급은 맞으나 '과장'은 본문에 없음, D는 정책 예시가 아님. 두 오답(A, C)이 부분적 근거를 지녀 비교가 필요하고 D도 표면적으로 그럴듯해 medium에 적합. VOC의 Ambon·Banda 집중 재배와 향신료 나무 제거 원정은 역사적 사실에 부합하며, 역사가들의 해석은 가설적 틀로 제시되어 사실 오류 없음. 한·영 해설 모두 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"B만 성립한다. A는 기록에 대한 부분적 근거가 있고 C는 구매자 언급이라는 부분적 근거가 있으며, D도 말은 된다. 지문은 VOC 독점 정책을 단순화해 서술했지만 문항 판단에는 영향이 없다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-173","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-174","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"For decades, Merino sheep graziers in Australia sold their greasy fleece at auction and simply accepted whatever price the market offered that week. When wool futures contracts became widely available, economists expected growers to use them eagerly to lock in prices months ahead of shearing. Yet adoption among individual graziers remained low, largely because a single family farm rarely produced enough wool to match the standardized contract sizes. __Grazier cooperatives, however, could pool the clips of dozens of members into volumes large enough to trade.__ Once several cooperatives in New South Wales began hedging on their members' behalf, participating growers reported far steadier incomes than neighbors who continued selling only at auction.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It explains why economists first expected graziers to adopt futures contracts eagerly.","It identifies a weakness of futures contracts that led most cooperatives to keep selling at auction.","It presents a way around the obstacle that had kept individual graziers from using futures contracts.","It gives evidence that cooperative members earned steadier incomes than growers who sold only at auction."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"앞 문장은 개별 농가의 생산량이 표준 계약 규모에 못 미쳐 선물 이용이 저조했다는 장애를 제시하고, 밑줄 문장은 협동조합이 물량을 합쳐 그 장애를 극복할 수 있었음을 보여 주므로 C가 정답이다. A는 경제학자들의 기대를 언급하지만 그 기대의 이유는 밑줄 문장이 아니라 그 앞에서 다뤄진다. B는 계약 규모 문제를 떠올리게 하지만, 협동조합은 오히려 헤지를 시작했으므로 지문과 반대된다. D의 소득 안정은 지문에 나오지만 밑줄 문장이 아니라 마지막 문장이 제시하는 결과이다.","explanationEn":"The sentence before the underlined one names an obstacle: one family farm usually couldn't produce enough wool to fill a standardized contract. The underlined sentence shows how cooperatives got past that by pooling their members' wool, so C is correct. A brings up the economists' expectation, but the underlined sentence doesn't explain why they expected it. B points to the contract-size issue, but it's wrong because the cooperatives actually started hedging instead of sticking with auctions. D describes the steadier incomes, which is a result reported in the final sentence, not in the underlined one.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.604Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"economics and business — Australian wool greasy fleece price hedging futures adoption by Merino sheep grazier cooperatives","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 직전 문장이 제시한 장애(계약 규모 대비 개별 농가 생산량 부족)에 대한 해결책(협동조합의 물량 합산)을 제시하므로 C가 명확히 옳다. A는 밑줄 이전 내용, D는 마지막 문장 내용을 가리키며, B는 지문과 반대되는 서술로 지문 요소를 재활용한 적절한 오답 구성이다. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 동일 결론과 글자 참조를 가지며 모순 없음. 지문은 창작 서술로 보이며 저작권 문제 없음. 장애→해결 연결이라는 두 단계 판단이 필요해 medium에 적합하다."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답을 고르려면 앞 문장의 장애와 'however'로 이어지는 해결책을 연결해야 함. B·D는 지문 요소를 부분적으로 활용한 매력적인 오답임.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-174","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-boundaries-m-175","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In many batik workshops in Pekalongan, Indonesia, design knowledge has long passed from master artisans to apprentices through years of shared work rather than written records. This informal system created a problem when Indonesia began offering copyright protection for traditional motifs: officials needed documentation of who had developed a pattern, yet the cooperative that registered one of the region's best-known floral designs, a motif refined over three generations of a single family's ______ no sketches older than a decade to submit as evidence.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["workshop had","workshop; had","workshop, and had","workshop, had"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"'a motif refined over three generations of a single family's workshop'은 'one of the region's best-known floral designs'를 설명하는 동격 삽입구이다. 이 삽입구는 design 뒤 쉼표로 시작했으므로 끝에도 쉼표를 찍어 닫아야 하고, 그 뒤에 주어 the cooperative의 동사 had가 이어진다. 그래서 정답은 D이다. A는 닫는 쉼표가 빠져 삽입구가 끝나지 않는다. B의 세미콜론은 주어와 동사를 갈라놓고, 세미콜론 앞부분은 독립절도 아니다. C의 and는 앞에 동사가 없는데 동사를 나열하는 꼴이 되어 주어 the cooperative에 짝지을 동사가 사라진다.","explanationEn":"The phrase \"a motif refined over three generations of a single family's workshop\" is an appositive. It describes \"one of the region's best-known floral designs.\" It opens with a comma after \"designs,\" so it needs a matching comma to close it. After that comes \"had,\" the verb for the subject \"the cooperative.\" That makes D the answer. A leaves out the closing comma, so the appositive never ends. B puts a semicolon between the subject and its verb, and what comes before the semicolon isn't an independent clause. C adds \"and,\" which suggests a second verb in a list, but no first verb exists, so the subject is left without a proper verb.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.604Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"economics and business — Indonesian batik textile production guild knowledge transmission and design copyright protection mechanisms","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"주어 the cooperative + 관계절 + 동격 삽입구(a motif ... workshop) 뒤에 본동사 had가 와야 하므로 닫는 쉼표가 있는 D가 유일하게 올바름. A(닫는 쉼표 누락), B(세미콜론 앞이 독립절 아님), C(짝 없는 and) 모두 정당하게 배제됨. 한국어 해설의 'design 뒤'는 'designs'의 사소한 표기 차이로 판정에 영향 없음. 긴 문장에서 주어·삽입구·동사 경계를 추적해야 하므로 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"긴 주어 속 동격구를 닫는 쉼표 문제. 수식어가 길어서 주어-동사 연결을 추적해야 하므로 medium에 적합함. 오답들도 그럴듯함.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-boundaries-m-175","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-e-176","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"easy","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In the Mekong Delta, many rice mills sit close together along the same canals. Economists studying the region noticed that mills in these clusters were more likely to buy modern polishing and color-sorting machines than mills located far from others. __One explanation is that when a mill owner sees a neighbor's new machine produce cleaner, export-quality rice, the owner can judge its value without taking a costly risk.__ Because buyers overseas pay more for such rice, this kind of easy, local learning may help explain why export-oriented technology spread fastest where mills were crowded together.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It offers a possible reason for the pattern that the economists observed.","It offers a criticism of the method that the economists used.","It offers an example of a mill that refused to adopt new machines.","It offers a prediction about how overseas rice prices will change."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"앞 문장은 밀집 지역 정미소가 현대식 기계를 더 많이 도입했다는 관찰을 제시하고, 밑줄 문장은 \"One explanation is\"로 시작해 그 이유(이웃의 기계를 보고 위험 없이 가치를 판단)를 제시하므로 정답은 A이다. B는 지문이 경제학자의 연구 방법을 비판하지 않으므로 틀렸다. C는 밑줄 문장이 기계 도입을 거부한 정미소가 아니라 이웃의 도입을 관찰하는 상황을 다루므로 틀렸다. D는 해외 가격이 언급되긴 하지만 그 변화를 예측하지 않으므로 틀렸다.","explanationEn":"The sentence before the underlined one describes what the economists observed: mills in clusters were more likely to adopt modern machines. The underlined sentence starts with \"One explanation is\" and gives a reason for that pattern, so A is correct. B is wrong because the text never criticizes how the economists did their research. C is wrong because the sentence is about a mill owner watching a neighbor adopt a machine, not about a mill refusing one. D is wrong because overseas prices are mentioned, but the text never predicts how they will change.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.604Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"A","seed":"economics and business — Thai rice mill clustering in Mekong Delta and export-oriented milling technology adoption patterns","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"밑줄 문장이 \"One explanation is\"라는 명시적 신호어로 앞 문장의 관찰 패턴에 대한 이유를 제시하므로 A가 정확. 오답 B(방법 비판), C(거부 사례), D(가격 예측)는 지문에 근거가 없으나 전형적 오개념으로 그럴듯함. 한·영 해설 모두 결론·선택지 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 단일 규칙·한 단계 추론으로 easy 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"\"One explanation is\"라는 명시적 단서로 한 단계 추론이면 풀린다. 오답 B와 D는 지문에 나오는 요소(경제학자, 해외 가격)를 활용한 전형적 오답이다. C는 다소 약하지만 허용 범위다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-e-176","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-h-177","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"hard","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- In the late 1800s, Jamaican smallholders grew bananas on small plots and sold them to many competing foreign shippers.\n- By the early 1900s, the Boston-based United Fruit Company had absorbed most rival shippers on the island.\n- With few other buyers left, growers had little choice but to accept the prices the company offered—a market condition economists call monopsony.\n- In some seasons, the company rejected bunches it judged too small, leaving growers with unsold fruit.\n- Low earnings pushed thousands of Jamaican workers to migrate to Panama, Costa Rica, and Cuba for wage labor.","question":"The student wants to emphasize how a change in the number of buyers shifted bargaining power in Jamaica's banana trade. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["In some seasons, United Fruit rejected banana bunches it judged too small, so Jamaican growers were left holding fruit they could not sell.","Once United Fruit had absorbed most rival shippers, Jamaican growers who had once sold to many competing buyers were left to accept whatever prices the company set.","From small-plot farming in the 1800s to company consolidation and widespread migration abroad, Jamaica's banana economy underwent many changes over several decades.","Because banana earnings were low, thousands of Jamaican workers left the island to take wage jobs in Panama, Costa Rica, and Cuba."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"정답 B: 많은 경쟁 구매자→United Fruit의 경쟁사 흡수→재배자가 가격을 그대로 받아들여야 함이라는 흐름으로, 구매자 수의 변화가 협상력을 어떻게 옮겼는지 강조한다. A: 너무 세부적이다. 작은 송이를 거부한 사례 하나만 들고, 구매자 수가 줄었다는 점은 빠져 있다. C: 너무 포괄적이다. 수십 년간의 변화를 나열하기만 해서 협상력이라는 초점이 흐려진다. D: 목표와 다른 항목(노동 이주)을 강조한다. 이주는 결과일 뿐, 구매자 수와 협상력의 관계는 다루지 않는다.","explanationEn":"B is correct. It links the change from many competing buyers to the company absorbing its rivals, and then to growers having to accept whatever prices the company set. That shows how fewer buyers moved bargaining power to United Fruit. A is too narrow: it gives one example (rejected bunches) and never mentions the drop in the number of buyers. C is too broad: it lists decades of changes and loses the focus on bargaining power. D highlights a different note, labor migration, which was an effect and doesn't explain how buyer numbers changed bargaining power.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.605Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["multi_source_goal_integration","purpose_scope_calibration","relation_direction_judgment"],"note":"목표(구매자 수 변화→협상력 이동)에 정확히 부합하는 B가 노트 1·2·3을 인과 순서로 통합한 유일한 선택지. A는 개별 사례(과잉 구체), C는 수십 년 개관(과잉 포괄), D는 결과(이주)만 다뤄 초점 이탈. 해설은 각 오답 결함을 정확히 설명하며 모순 없음. United Fruit의 보스턴 기반·자메이카 바나나 무역 지배, 파나마·코스타리카·쿠바 이주 등 역사적 사실도 정확. 세 노트의 인과 방향을 목적에 맞게 종합해야 하므로 medium 수준의 단일 사실 선택을 넘어선다."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["multi_source_goal_integration","purpose_scope_calibration"],"note":"B만 노트 1·2·3을 묶어 '많은 구매자→소수 구매자→가격 수용'이라는 변화와 협상력 이동을 함께 보여 준다. A는 지나치게 구체적이고 C는 지나치게 포괄적이며 D는 초점이 다르다. 오답이 비교적 쉽게 걸러진다는 점에서 hard로서는 경계선 수준이다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"batch2-D-cross","gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-h-177","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":"rhetorical_synthesis_goal_scope_match","recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":"recipe","difficultyStatus":"provisional_ai","review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-h-178","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"hard","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- In the 1970s, South Korea's government designated shipbuilding a strategic export industry.\n- Hyundai Heavy Industries, part of the Hyundai chaebol, opened its Ulsan shipyard in 1974; the group also owned steel-processing, engine-making, and shipping affiliates.\n- Government records show that state-backed export credits covered a large share of the financing that foreign buyers used to order Korean-built ships during this period.\n- In a 2019 study, economist Ji-won Park compared shipyards across several countries and found that vertically integrated yards tended to have lower costs per ton, but she noted that her data could not rule out other explanations, such as differences in labor costs.\n- A separate 2021 survey by Daniel Ortiz found that shipowners ranked delivery speed above price when choosing a builder.","question":"The student wants to present Park's research while accurately reflecting how strongly its findings are supported. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Park's 2019 study demonstrated that vertical integration, like that of Hyundai's affiliates, caused Korean shipyards to build ships at lower costs per ton than their rivals.","Park's 2019 study suggested that state-backed export credits may possibly have covered some of the financing foreign buyers used to order Korean-built ships.","Park's 2019 study found that vertically integrated shipyards tended to have lower costs per ton, though other factors, such as labor costs, may also explain the pattern.","Park's 2019 study found that shipowners likely ranked delivery speed above price, though other factors may also have influenced their choice of builder."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"정답 C: Park의 결과(통합 조선소가 단위 비용이 낮은 경향)와 그 한계(인건비 등 대안 설명 배제 불가)를 그대로 반영한다. A: '경향'과 상관관계를 '입증했다', '원인이 되었다'로 부풀렸다. B: 수출 신용 이야기는 정부 기록으로 확인된 사실인데 'may possibly'로 약하게 만들었고, Park의 연구 내용도 아니다. D: 조심스러운 말투는 맞지만 Ortiz 설문 내용을 Park 연구로 잘못 붙였다.","explanationEn":"C is correct. It reports what Park actually found, that vertically integrated yards tended to have lower costs per ton, and it keeps her caveat that other explanations, like labor costs, can't be ruled out. A goes too far: it turns a tendency into proof (\"demonstrated\") and a cause (\"caused\"), even though Park's data couldn't rule out other explanations. B goes the other way: the export-credit point comes from government records, so the notes present it as established, and B weakens it for no reason with \"may possibly.\" It also wasn't part of Park's study. D sounds appropriately careful, but the delivery-speed finding comes from Ortiz's 2021 survey, not Park's study.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.605Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["claim_certainty_discrimination","multi_source_goal_integration","purpose_scope_calibration"],"note":"노트에 확정적 진술(정부 지정, 울산 조선소 개장, 정부 기록상 수출신용)과 잠정적 진술(Park의 '경향', 대안 설명 배제 불가)이 공존하며, 정답 C는 Park의 결과와 한계를 정확한 확실성 수준으로 반영한다. A는 'demonstrated/caused'로 과잉 일반화, B는 정부 기록으로 확인된 사실을 'may possibly...some'으로 과도하게 축소(동시에 Park 연구로 오귀속), D는 Ortiz 설문을 Park에게 오귀속. 해설은 각 선택지의 결함을 정확히 짚으며 모순 없음. 사실관계(현대중공업 울산 1974, 1970년대 전략수출산업 지정)도 무리 없음. 소소한 점: B가 확실성 축소와 오귀속 두 결함을 겸해 귀속만으로도 제거 가능하지만 체크리스트 4 항목 충족에는 지장 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["claim_certainty_discrimination","multi_source_goal_integration"],"note":"정답 C는 '경향'이라는 결과와 대안 설명을 배제할 수 없다는 한계를 모두 정확히 반영함. A는 상관관계를 인과·입증으로 과잉 일반화했고, B는 확정된 사실을 과도하게 약화한 데다 출처도 잘못 붙였으며, D는 출처를 잘못 붙였음. B와 D는 출처 오귀속만으로도 쉽게 제거되므로 변별력은 다소 약함.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"batch2-D-cross","gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-h-178","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":"rhetorical_synthesis_certainty_level_choice","recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":"recipe","difficultyStatus":"provisional_ai","review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-179","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Tardigrades, microscopic animals found in mosses and soils worldwide, can survive near-total dehydration by entering a state called anhydrobiosis, in which metabolism becomes nearly undetectable. For years, researchers assumed the animals relied mainly on the sugar trehalose, which protects dried cells in organisms such as brine shrimp. Yet many tardigrade species produce little or no trehalose. In 2017, biologist Thomas Boothby and colleagues reported that tardigrades instead make a family of intrinsically disordered proteins, which lack a fixed shape while the animal is hydrated. As water is lost, these proteins form a glassy solid that appears to trap other cellular molecules in place, keeping them from unfolding or clumping together. When the team inserted genes for the proteins into yeast and bacteria, the microbes became noticeably better at surviving drying, suggesting that the proteins themselves, rather than some other feature of tardigrade biology, provide much of the protection.","question":"According to the text, what did Boothby and colleagues' research indicate about how tardigrades withstand dehydration?","options":["Tardigrades withstand dehydration chiefly because they make more trehalose than brine shrimp do, which keeps their cells glassy.","Tardigrades withstand dehydration chiefly because their proteins keep a fixed shape even after water is lost from their cells.","Tardigrades withstand dehydration chiefly because yeast and bacteria living inside them supply genes that resist drying.","Tardigrades withstand dehydration chiefly because certain shapeless proteins solidify as water leaves, holding other molecules steady."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 많은 완보동물이 트레할로스를 거의 만들지 않으며, 대신 수화 상태에서 고정된 형태가 없는 단백질이 탈수 시 유리질 고체가 되어 다른 분자의 변성·응집을 막는다고 설명하므로 D가 정답이다. A는 '유리질'이라는 단어를 맞게 썼지만 트레할로스 의존은 지문이 반박한 기존 가정이다. B는 단백질이 보호한다는 점은 맞으나, 실제로는 수화 상태에서 형태가 없다가 건조 시 고체화하는 것이므로 '고정된 형태 유지'는 틀렸다. C는 효모·세균이 등장하지만 이는 유전자를 주입받은 실험 대상이지 유전자 공급원이 아니다.","explanationEn":"D is correct: the text says many tardigrades make little trehalose and instead produce proteins with no fixed shape while hydrated, which form a glassy solid during drying that keeps other molecules from unfolding or clumping. A borrows the word \"glassy,\" but relying on trehalose is the earlier assumption the text challenges. B is right that proteins protect the cells, but it gets their behavior backward, since the proteins lack a fixed shape and then solidify. C mentions yeast and bacteria, but those microbes received the tardigrade genes in the experiment. They weren't the source of the genes.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.605Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"life science — Tardigrade cryptobiosis mechanism and anhydrobiotic survival enabling extreme environmental stress resistance","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"지문 검산: 많은 완보동물은 트레할로스를 거의 만들지 않고(A 배제), 수화 시 고정 형태가 없는 단백질이 건조 시 유리질 고체가 되어 다른 분자를 고정(D 일치, B 배제), 효모·세균은 유전자를 주입받은 실험 대상(C 배제). 정답 D 확정. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 D 지지, 글자 참조 일치, 한글 없음. Boothby 2017 연구(TDPs, 효모·세균 발현 시 건조 내성 향상) 사실과 부합. A·B는 지문 단어(유리질, 단백질)를 차용한 부분적 근거 보유로 비교 필요, C도 지문 소재 사용으로 그럴듯함 — medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"D는 지문(형태 없는 단백질 → 탈수 시 유리질 고체 → 분자 고정)을 정확히 바꿔 말함. A·B는 지문의 표현(glassy, 단백질 보호)을 부분적으로 빌린 그럴듯한 오답. C는 비교적 쉽게 배제되지만 실험 내용을 잘못 읽으면 고를 수 있어 medium 범위 안.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-179","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-183","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"The spots on a spotted hyena's coat vary widely among individuals, and biologists have long assumed that such patterns arise from a Turing-type reaction-diffusion process, in which interacting chemical signals spread through embryonic skin and settle into regularly spaced patches. Developmental biologist Mariam Okonjo recently tested this assumption by comparing spot size and spacing across hyena cubs from different body regions. She found that spots on the flanks and back were spaced at roughly even intervals, as a reaction-diffusion model would predict. On the legs, however, spots grew steadily smaller and more crowded toward the paws, a pattern that tracked a gradient in the concentration of a pigment-regulating protein running from the shoulder to the foot.\n\nOkonjo argues that the reaction-diffusion process is not wrong but incomplete: it seems to generate the basic spotted arrangement, while the protein gradient modifies how that arrangement is expressed in different parts of the body. She cautions that the gradient alone could not produce spots at all, since tissue exposed to the protein in the absence of the signaling interactions develops only uniform shading.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Okonjo's findings show that the spacing of hyena spots is determined by a protein gradient rather than by a reaction-diffusion process, as researchers had previously believed.","Okonjo's findings show that hyena spots on the flanks and back are spaced more evenly than spots on the legs because the legs develop later in the embryo.","Okonjo's findings show that a pigment-regulating protein can produce uniform shading in hyena skin even when chemical signals do not interact.","Okonjo's findings show that hyena coat patterns likely result from a reaction-diffusion process working together with a protein gradient that alters spots by body region."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 반응-확산 과정이 기본 점무늬를 만들고 단백질 농도 기울기가 신체 부위별로 그 무늬를 변형한다는, 두 메커니즘의 결합을 핵심으로 제시하므로 D가 정답이다. A는 기울기가 반응-확산을 '대체'한다고 하여, 기존 모형이 틀린 게 아니라 불완전하다는 주장과 기울기만으로는 점이 생기지 않는다는 경고에 어긋난다. B는 몸통과 다리의 간격 차이를 맞게 언급하지만, 그 원인을 지문에 없는 발생 시기 탓으로 돌린다. C는 마지막 문장의 세부 사항으로 사실이지만 글 전체의 중심 생각이 아니라 보조 근거에 그친다.","explanationEn":"D is correct because the text's central claim is that reaction-diffusion produces the basic spotted layout, while a protein gradient changes how the spots look in different body regions, so the two mechanisms work together. A says the gradient replaces reaction-diffusion, but Okonjo calls the older model incomplete, not wrong, and warns that the gradient alone can't make spots. B correctly notes that the spacing differs between the trunk and the legs, but it blames the difference on developmental timing, which the text never mentions. C is a true detail from the last sentence, but it only supports the argument and isn't the main idea.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.605Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"life science — Hyena spotted coat pattern formation and developmental biology pigmentation gradient mechanisms","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 D 검산 완료: 지문 2문단의 \"not wrong but incomplete… generate the basic arrangement… gradient modifies\" 가 두 메커니즘의 협력을 명시하며, D가 이를 정확히 종합함. A는 '대체' 주장으로 지문의 '불완전' 및 '기울기만으로는 점 불가' 경고와 모순, B는 지문에 없는 발생 시기 원인을 도입, C는 마지막 문장의 보조 세부에 그침. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 결론·글자 참조 일치하고 영어 자연스러우며 한글 혼입 없음. 가상 연구자(Okonjo) 설정으로 저작권 의심 없음. 1문단(부위별 차이)과 2문단(해석)을 연결해야 하고, A·B가 부분적으로 맞는 근거를 지녀 비교 배제가 필요하므로 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"D가 두 메커니즘의 결합이라는 중심 생각을 정확히 요약함. A는 '대체'라는 오독을 노린 유력한 오답이고, B와 C는 부분적으로 맞는 근거를 가짐. 가상 연구자와 가상 연구 설정이므로 저작권 문제는 없음. 지문 속 'from different body regions' 수식 구조가 약간 어색하지만 문항 판정에는 지장이 없음.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-183","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-184","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"African lungfish survive seasonal droughts by burrowing into drying mud and sealing themselves inside a mucus cocoon, where they can remain for months or even years. For decades, researchers assumed that this dormancy, called estivation, was mainly a matter of slowing down: with no food or water available, the fish's metabolism simply drops, much as a car engine idles. However, recent studies by physiologists examining estivating lungfish tissues suggest a more active picture. Although overall oxygen consumption falls sharply, the fish increase production of certain antioxidant enzymes and convert toxic ammonia into less harmful urea, and their muscle cells switch on genes that limit the breakdown of protein. These findings indicate that estivation is not just reduced activity but a regulated state in which the lungfish's body works to protect its organs until water comes back.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Evidence suggests that lungfish dormancy involves targeted biological processes that preserve the body, not merely a general decline in metabolic activity.","Evidence suggests that lungfish dormancy depends mainly on the mucus cocoon, which shields the body from drying out in hardened mud.","Evidence suggests that lungfish dormancy causes oxygen consumption to fall more sharply than researchers had previously believed.","Evidence suggests that lungfish dormancy is triggered by a buildup of ammonia that forces the fish to stop feeding during droughts."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 글은 휴면을 단순히 대사가 느려지는 것으로 보던 기존 견해와, 항산화 효소·요소 전환·단백질 보호 같은 능동적·조절적 과정을 보여 주는 최근 연구 결과를 대비시키므로 A가 정답이다. B는 지문에 나오는 점액 고치를 언급하지만, 고치는 배경 설명일 뿐 핵심 주장이 아니다. C는 산소 소비 감소라는 실제 세부 내용을 쓰지만, 그 감소 폭이 예상보다 크다는 말은 지문에 없고 요지도 아니다. D는 암모니아를 원인으로 잘못 연결했는데, 지문에서 암모니아는 휴면 중에 요소로 전환되는 물질일 뿐이다.","explanationEn":"A is correct because the text contrasts the old view that estivation is just slowing down with new evidence of active, regulated processes: making antioxidant enzymes, converting ammonia to urea, and switching on genes that protect muscle protein. B mentions the mucus cocoon, which does appear in the text, but the cocoon is only background, not the main point. C uses a real detail, falling oxygen consumption, but the text never says the drop is bigger than researchers expected, and that isn't the focus. D wrongly treats ammonia as the cause of dormancy, while the text only says ammonia gets converted into urea during dormancy.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.605Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"life science — Lungfish estivation physiology and metabolic suppression during prolonged drought dormancy periods","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"지문 구조(기존 견해 → However → 최근 연구 → These findings indicate)가 명확하고, A가 마지막 문장의 요지를 정확히 재진술함. B·C는 지문 속 실제 세부(점액 고치, 산소 소비 감소)를 활용해 부분적으로 그럴듯하며, D는 암모니아를 원인으로 뒤집은 인과 왜곡 오답으로 말이 됨. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 A 정답, 각 오답 배제 근거 일치. 과학적 내용(항산화 효소 증가, 암모니아→요소 전환, 단백질 분해 억제)도 실제 폐어 연구와 부합. 저작권 의심 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"A는 '기존 견해와 새 증거'의 대비 구조를 그대로 요약한다. B와 C는 지문의 실제 세부(고치, 산소 소비 감소)를 써서 부분적인 근거가 있다. D는 암모니아를 휴면의 원인으로 잘못 연결한 그럴듯한 오답이다. 지문 내용은 폐어 휴면에 관한 실제 연구와 대체로 일치한다. 중간 난이도에 적합하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-184","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-185","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"For decades, the woodpecker's ability to hammer its beak against tree trunks thousands of times a day without apparent harm has been cited as a model for designing protective helmets. Researchers often pointed to the bird's spongy, trabecular bone near the front of the skull, assuming that this porous tissue cushions the brain much as foam padding does. __However, when biomechanist Sam Van Wassenbergh and colleagues analyzed high-speed video of pecking birds in 2022, they found that the skull decelerates almost as abruptly as the beak, indicating that little impact energy is being absorbed along the way.__ The team argues that the woodpecker's small brain, rather than any built-in cushioning, may explain why the forces involved stay below the threshold for concussion—a conclusion that calls into question helmet designs inspired by the bird.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It describes a structural feature of the woodpecker skull that researchers had previously overlooked.","It presents a finding that challenges a long-held explanation of how woodpeckers avoid injury.","It provides evidence that confirms the protective role of trabecular bone in the woodpecker skull.","It explains why helmet designers first became interested in the woodpecker's pecking behavior."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 'However'로 시작해, 해면골이 충격을 흡수한다는 기존 가정과 달리 두개골이 부리만큼 급격히 감속해 에너지 흡수가 거의 없다는 연구 결과를 제시하므로 B가 정답이다. A는 해면골이 앞 문장에서 이미 언급된 특징이고, 밑줄 문장은 새 구조가 아니라 측정 결과를 다루므로 틀리다. C는 해면골을 언급한다는 점에서 그럴듯하지만, 실제 결과는 그 보호 역할을 확인하는 것이 아니라 의문을 제기하므로 반대이다. D는 헬멧과 관련이 있지만, 헬멧 설계에 대한 관심의 기원은 첫 문장에서 다루며 밑줄 문장의 역할이 아니다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence opens with \"However\" and reports that the skull slows down almost as sharply as the beak. That means very little energy is absorbed, which goes against the earlier idea that spongy bone cushions the brain, so B is correct. A is wrong because the trabecular bone was already introduced in the previous sentence, and the underlined sentence reports a measurement, not a newly noticed structure. C may look right because the sentence relates to the bone's role, but the finding casts doubt on that protective role instead of confirming it. D is about helmets, but the text explains why designers became interested in the first sentence, not in the underlined one.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.605Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"life science — Woodpecker shock-absorbing skull structure and trabecular bone adaptation preventing concussive injury","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 'However'로 전환되어 해면골 완충 가설(기존 설명)에 반하는 2022년 측정 결과를 제시하므로 B가 정확하다. A(새로 발견된 구조), C(보호 역할 확인—정반대), D(헬멧 관심의 기원—첫 문장 내용)는 모두 배제 가능. Van Wassenbergh 2022 Current Biology 연구 내용(두개골이 충격을 흡수하지 않음, 작은 뇌 크기가 뇌진탕 역치 이하 유지 설명)과 부합한다. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 결론과 글자 참조가 일치하고 영어는 자연스러우며 한글 없음. 'However' 신호로 다소 명확하지만 C·D가 지문 요소(해면골, 헬멧)를 활용한 부분적 근거를 지녀 비교가 필요하므로 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"2022년 Van Wassenbergh 등의 Current Biology 연구 내용과 맞음. 오답 C는 내용을 정반대로 뒤집은 선택지이고 A·D는 부분적 근거가 있어 medium 난이도에 적합함.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-185","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-187","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Three-toed sloths descend from the forest canopy about once a week to defecate at the base of their trees, a risky trip that exposes them to predators. Biologist Jonathan Pauli and colleagues proposed that the habit is tied to moths living in sloth fur: female moths ride down with the sloth, lay eggs in its dung, and the new adults fly up to find a sloth host. Pauli's team found that sloths carrying more moths also had more nitrogen in their fur and more algae growing there. __The researchers suggest that the moths, as they die and decompose, act as a fertilizer for the algae, which the sloths may then lick from their fur as a supplement to a diet of nutrient-poor leaves.__ If so, the costly trip to the ground may help keep a cycle of nutrients going that benefits sloth, moth, and alga alike.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It describes a finding that casts doubt on the claim that the moths depend on sloths for reproduction.","It explains why sloths take the risk of coming down to the ground even though the trip makes them easier for predators to catch.","It presents measurements showing that sloths with algae-covered fur are harder for predators to spot.","It offers a possible explanation for the link found between moths, nitrogen, and algae, and points to how sloths might gain from that link."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 친 문장은 앞 문장에서 나온 상관관계(나방이 많을수록 질소와 조류가 많음)를 나방 분해가 조류에 비료 역할을 한다는 가설로 설명하고, 나무늘보가 조류를 섭취해 얻는 이점을 제시하므로 D가 정답이다. A는 틀렸다. 이 문장은 나방의 번식 의존성을 반박하지 않는다. B는 그럴듯하지만, 하강의 이유를 정리하는 것은 마지막 문장이며 밑줄 문장은 그 연결 고리 중 하나만 제시한다. C는 소재인 위장 이야기를 끌어오지만, 지문에는 포식자 탐지에 관한 측정이 없고 밑줄 문장은 측정 결과가 아닌 제안이다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence takes the correlation reported just before it (more moths, more nitrogen, more algae) and proposes a mechanism: decaying moths fertilize the algae. It then suggests sloths benefit by eating that algae, so D is correct. A is wrong because nothing in the sentence questions whether moths rely on sloths to reproduce. B is tempting, but it's the final sentence that connects everything back to the trip to the ground; the underlined sentence supplies only one link in that chain. C is wrong because the text reports no measurements about predators spotting sloths, and the underlined sentence offers a suggestion, not data.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.605Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"life science — Sloth moth symbiosis and algae cultivation in fur providing camouflage and nutrient exchange","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 직전 문장의 상관관계(나방↑→질소·조류↑)에 대한 메커니즘 제안(나방 분해=비료)과 나무늘보의 이득(조류 섭취)을 제시하므로 D가 정확함. B는 지문 전체 결론(마지막 문장)과 혼동을 유도하는 적절한 매력 오답이고, A·C는 지문 소재(나방 번식, 포식자)를 차용하되 밑줄 문장 내용과 불일치해 배제 가능. 내용은 Pauli et al.(2014) 연구와 부합하며 지문은 독자적 서술임. 한·영 해설 모두 결론·글자 참조 일치, 한글 혼입 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B가 강한 함정이다. 밑줄 문장의 기능과 마지막 문장의 기능을 구분해야 풀 수 있다. A와 C는 비교적 쉽게 배제되지만 그럴듯하므로 medium 수준으로 적절하다. 지문 내용은 Pauli et al.(2014) 연구와 맞는다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-187","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-words_in_context-e-190","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Words in Context","difficulty":"easy","skill":"words_in_context","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"When a shark bites a hagfish, glands along the hagfish's body release mucins and protein threads that expand in seawater into a large mass of slime within a fraction of a second. The slime fills the predator's mouth and gills, making it hard for water to flow through. Rather than holding on, the shark usually spits out the hagfish and swims away choking. In this way, the slime ______ the attack, allowing the hagfish to escape unharmed.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["prolongs","conceals","interrupts","encourages"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 점액이 상어의 입과 아가미를 막아 상어가 먹이를 뱉고 떠나며, 그 결과 먹장어가 다치지 않고 도망친다고 설명한다. 따라서 점액은 공격을 '중단시킨다'는 뜻의 C가 가장 논리적이다. A는 공격을 '연장한다'는 뜻이라 상어가 바로 뱉어 낸다는 내용과 반대이다. B는 공격을 '숨긴다'는 뜻인데, 지문은 공격을 감추는 것이 아니라 멈추게 하는 것을 말한다. D는 공격을 '부추긴다'는 뜻이라 먹장어가 탈출한다는 결과와 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The passage says the slime clogs the shark's mouth and gills, so the shark spits out the hagfish and leaves, and the hagfish escapes unharmed. That means the slime stops the attack partway through, which is why C, \"interrupts,\" is the best fit. A, \"prolongs,\" would mean the attack lasts longer, but the shark actually lets go quickly. B, \"conceals,\" would mean the slime hides the attack, but the passage is about the attack ending, not about it being hidden. D, \"encourages,\" would mean the slime makes the shark more eager to attack, which goes against the hagfish getting away.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.605Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"C","seed":"life science — Hagfish slime gland mucin secretion and predator evasion through hydrodynamic drag disruption","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"지문 단서(\"spits out… swims away\", \"escape unharmed\")가 명시적이고, 정답 C(interrupts)가 유일하게 논리적임. 오답은 각각 반대/무관 의미로 규칙을 알면 즉시 배제되나 표면적으로는 그럴듯함. 먹장어 점액 생물학 서술도 사실과 부합. 한·영 해설 모두 정답 및 선택지 글자 참조가 일치하고 자연스러움."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"문맥 단서(spits out, escape unharmed)가 직접 드러나 한 단계로 풀린다. 오답 중 conceals는 slime이 덮는다는 이미지 때문에 그럴듯하고, prolongs·encourages는 결과와 반대라 바로 배제된다. easy 수준에 맞다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-words_in_context-e-190","intendedSkill":"words_in_context","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-191","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"The Loess Plateau of north-central China is blanketed by fine, yellowish silt that in places lies more than 300 meters deep. For decades, geologists assumed that this sediment was carried directly from the nearby Gobi and Taklimakan Deserts by the strong winds that sweep southeastward each spring. Recent studies of the silt's mineral chemistry, however, suggest a more complicated history. Many of the grains turn out to have been ground down by glaciers and mountain erosion in the Tibetan Plateau and surrounding ranges, then washed into river basins such as the upper Yellow River, where they settled as floodplain deposits.\n\nOnly after these deposits dried out and were exposed did the wind pick the particles up again and carry them the final distance to the plateau. According to geochemist Lin Wei and her colleagues, the deserts therefore served mainly as temporary storage areas and launching points rather than as the original source of the silt. In their view, rivers and wind worked in sequence, with each process completing a different stage of the sediment's journey.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Spring winds blowing southeastward from the Gobi and Taklimakan Deserts are strong enough to carry fine silt more than 300 meters into the air above the Loess Plateau.","Glaciers in the Tibetan Plateau have produced most of the silt in northern China, so wind has had little effect on where that sediment ultimately accumulated.","Floodplain deposits along the upper Yellow River contain more silt than the Loess Plateau does, which suggests that rivers are now the region's main sediment sink.","Evidence from mineral chemistry indicates that the plateau's silt reached its location through a multistage process in which rivers moved it before wind delivered it."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 글은 황토가 사막에서 곧바로 바람에 실려 왔다는 기존 가정을 광물 화학 증거로 수정하면서, 빙하와 침식으로 만들어진 입자를 먼저 강이 옮기고 그다음 바람이 고원까지 운반했다는 다단계 과정을 핵심으로 제시하므로 D가 정답이다. A는 300미터라는 수치를 퇴적층의 두께가 아니라 바람에 날린 높이로 잘못 바꾸었고, 글의 중심 내용도 아니다. B는 빙하가 기원이라는 부분은 맞지만, 바람이 마지막 단계를 맡았다는 서술과 어긋나게 바람의 역할을 축소한다. C는 하천 범람원 퇴적물과 고원의 실트 양을 비교하지만, 글에는 그런 비교가 없다.","explanationEn":"The text revises the old assumption that the silt blew straight from the deserts. Using mineral chemistry, it shows that the grains were first carried by rivers and then moved by wind to the plateau, so D is correct. A misuses the 300-meter figure: the passage gives it as the depth of the deposit, not the height the wind carried the silt, and it isn't the central point anyway. B gets the glacial origin right but downplays wind, even though the text says wind completed the final stage. C compares the amount of silt on the floodplains with the amount on the plateau, which the text never does.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.605Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"earth and space science — Loess plateau dust storm formation and aeolian sediment transport mechanisms across northern China Asia","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"지문 전체가 '사막 직송' 가설을 광물 화학 증거로 수정하여 강→바람의 순차적 다단계 운반을 제시하므로 D가 주제문으로 정확하다. A는 300m 수치(퇴적 두께)를 바람 운반 높이로 왜곡한 세부 오용, B는 빙하 기원은 맞으나 바람의 최종 단계 역할을 부정하여 지문과 모순, C는 지문에 없는 양적 비교. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 D를 일관되게 뒷받침하고 선택지 참조가 정확하며 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 황토고원 두께(최대 300m 이상)는 실제 지질 자료와 부합하고, 지문은 독창적 서술로 저작권 우려 없음. 가설 수정 구조 파악 + 두 단락의 정보 연결이 필요하고 B·A가 부분적 근거를 가져 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"D는 기존 가정 수정 + 강→바람의 다단계 과정을 정확히 요약한다. B는 부분적으로 맞는 근거(빙하 기원)를 가진 유력 오답이고, A·C는 글의 세부(300m, 범람원 퇴적물)를 재활용한 그럴듯한 오답이다. medium 난이도에 적합하다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-191","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-192","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Each autumn, crowds gather along China's Qiantang River to watch its tidal bore, a wall of water that can exceed three meters as the incoming tide rushes upstream against the river's flow. For decades, researchers attributed the bore's height almost entirely to the funnel shape of Hangzhou Bay, which narrows sharply and squeezes the advancing tide. Recent field measurements, however, suggest that the funnel tells only part of the story. Sensors placed below the surface recorded internal waves—oscillations along the boundary between denser salt water and lighter river water—moving ahead of and beneath the bore. When these internal waves lined up with the arriving tide, the bore grew noticeably steeper; when they were out of step, it weakened even though the bay's geometry stayed the same.","question":"Based on the text, what did the recent field measurements reveal about the Qiantang River's tidal bore?","options":["Its strength depends partly on how motion beneath the surface coincides with the tide, not solely on the bay's shape.","Its strength depends mainly on the narrowing of Hangzhou Bay, which compresses the tide as it advances.","Its strength depends partly on the density of the river water, which slows the tide as it moves upstream.","Its strength depends mainly on seasonal crowds of observers, who first noticed changes in the bore's height."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 새 측정 결과, 만의 지형이 같아도 내부파가 조석과 맞물리느냐에 따라 해일 높이가 달라졌다고 하므로 지형만으로는 설명되지 않는다는 A가 정답이다. B는 지문에 나온 기존 견해일 뿐, 새 측정은 그것이 '일부'에 불과하다고 했다. C는 밀도가 다른 물을 언급하지만, 지문에서 강물이 조석을 늦춘다고 말하지 않으며 중요한 것은 내부파의 타이밍이다. D는 관람객을 언급하지만, 관람객이 해일 높이를 결정한다거나 변화를 처음 알아챘다는 내용은 없다.","explanationEn":"The new measurements showed that the bore got steeper or weaker depending on whether internal waves lined up with the tide, even though the bay's shape stayed the same. That makes A correct: the bay's shape isn't the whole explanation. B only restates the older view, and the text says the funnel shape \"tells only part of the story.\" C mentions water density, but the text never says river water slows the tide. What matters is the timing of the internal waves. D brings up the crowds, but the text gives them no role in setting or discovering the bore's height.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.605Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"earth and space science — Tidal bore phenomenon in Qiantang River and internal wave dynamics forcing bore propagation","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"정답 A 검산 일치: 지문 마지막 두 문장(내부파가 조석과 맞물리면 가파르고, 어긋나면 지형이 같아도 약화)이 직접 뒷받침. B는 기존 견해를 새 발견으로 오인하게 하는 매력적 오답, C는 '밀도' 어휘를 재활용한 부분적 근거 오답으로 비교 배제가 필요. D는 지문 첫 문장의 관람객을 끌어왔으나 설득력이 약해 네 번째 오답으로는 다소 허술하지만, 기존 견해 vs 새 측정 결과 구분이라는 두 단계 판단이 요구되어 medium에 부합. 한·영 해설 모두 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 중국 첸탕강 조석 해일 3m 초과·항저우만 깔때기 지형은 사실과 부합하며 내부파 연구는 가상 연구 서술로 문제 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"B(기존 견해)와 C(밀도 언급 부분 일치)는 비교해야 배제되는 매력적 오답이다. D는 다소 약하지만 지문 요소(관람객)를 활용해 말은 된다. 중간 난이도에 적합하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-192","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-194","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Earth's magnetosphere usually acts as an effective shield, deflecting most of the charged particles streaming outward from the Sun in the solar wind. For decades, researchers assumed that the strength of a geomagnetic storm depended mainly on how fast and how dense the incoming solar wind was. Observations from spacecraft positioned between Earth and the Sun, however, have shown that even unusually fast, dense streams often produce only minor disturbances. What matters most is the orientation of the magnetic field carried by the solar wind. When that field points southward, opposite to the direction of Earth's field at the dayside boundary of the magnetosphere, the two fields can link together in a process called magnetic reconnection, opening a pathway for solar wind energy to pour into the magnetosphere. When the field points northward, the shield stays largely intact, and even a powerful stream mostly slides around the planet.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Spacecraft positioned between Earth and the Sun have shown that the solar wind is usually too weak to disturb Earth's magnetosphere.","The speed and density of the solar wind determine whether magnetic reconnection occurs at the dayside boundary of Earth's magnetosphere.","The direction of the solar wind's magnetic field, rather than its speed or density, largely determines whether a strong geomagnetic storm develops.","Earth's magnetosphere deflects the solar wind most effectively when the solar wind's magnetic field points in the same direction as Earth's field."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 폭풍의 세기가 태양풍의 속도·밀도로 정해진다는 기존 가정을 뒤집고, 태양풍 자기장의 방향(남향일 때 재결합)이 핵심이라고 주장하므로 C가 정답이다. A는 우주선 관측을 언급하지만, 지문은 빠르고 밀도 높은 흐름도 작은 교란만 일으킨다고 했을 뿐 태양풍이 대체로 약하다고 하지 않았다. B는 재결합의 원인을 방향이 아닌 속도·밀도로 돌려 지문과 반대된다. D는 북향일 때 차폐가 유지된다는 세부 내용과 부분적으로 맞지만 글의 중심 대비(기존 가정 대 방향)를 담지 못한 세부 진술이며, '같은 방향'이 가장 효과적이라는 비교도 지문에 없다.","explanationEn":"The text overturns the old assumption that storm strength depends mainly on solar wind speed and density, and argues that the orientation of the solar wind's magnetic field (southward fields allow reconnection) is what matters most, so C is correct. A mentions the spacecraft observations, but the text only says fast, dense streams often cause minor disturbances; it never says the solar wind is usually weak. B gives speed and density as the cause of reconnection, which is the opposite of the text's point that field direction controls it. D partly matches the detail that a northward field leaves the shield intact, but it is a narrow detail that misses the text's central contrast, and the text never claims a \"same direction\" field is the most effective case.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.605Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"earth and space science — Geomagnetic storm occurrence and solar wind interaction with Earth's magnetosphere deflection","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"지문의 중심 대비(기존 가정: 속도·밀도 → 실제: 자기장 방향)를 C가 정확히 요약함. D는 지문 세부(북향=지구 자기장과 같은 방향일 때 차폐 유지)와 부합하는 진술이라 세부-대-주제 구분을 요구하는 적절한 매력 오답이며, A는 우주선 관측 언급으로 부분 근거를 가짐. B는 인과를 뒤집어 명백히 틀리나 말은 됨. 과학적 내용(남향 IMF 재결합, 주간측 경계에서 지구 자기장 북향)도 정확. 해설 한·영 일치, 한글 혼입 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"D는 북향(지구 자기장과 같은 방향)일 때 차폐가 유지된다는 세부 내용에서 추론할 수 있어 그럴듯한 오답이지만, 중심 생각이 아닌 세부 진술이다. 해설에서 '같은 방향 비교가 지문에 없다'고 한 부분은 다소 엄격한 해석이나 정답 판정에는 영향이 없다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-194","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-197","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In the 1920s, Serbian mathematician Milutin Milankovitch calculated how slow, periodic changes in Earth's orbit—its eccentricity, axial tilt, and the wobble of its axis—alter the amount of sunlight reaching high northern latitudes in summer. He proposed that these variations pace the advance and retreat of continental ice sheets. For decades, the idea could not be tested, because no climate record was long or precisely dated enough to compare with his predicted cycles. __In 1976, however, geologists James Hays, John Imbrie, and Nicholas Shackleton analyzed oxygen isotopes in deep-sea sediment cores spanning roughly 450,000 years and found climate fluctuations recurring at intervals of about 100,000, 41,000, and 23,000 years, closely matching the periods of the orbital changes.__ Even so, puzzles remain: the 100,000-year cycle dominates the record of the past million years, yet changes in eccentricity on that timescale only slightly affect incoming sunlight, suggesting that feedbacks within Earth's climate system must amplify the orbital signal.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It presents a finding that showed that Milankovitch had misidentified which orbital changes affect the amount of sunlight reaching Earth.","It presents a finding that provided the kind of evidence that had previously been unavailable for assessing Milankovitch's proposal.","It presents a finding that explains how feedbacks within Earth's climate system amplify the effects of orbital changes.","It presents a finding that showed that the 100,000-year cycle has dominated the climate record for roughly 450,000 years."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"앞 문장은 기록이 충분히 길거나 정확하게 연대 측정되지 않아 밀란코비치 가설을 검증할 수 없었다고 말하고, 밑줄 문장은 퇴적물 코어에서 예측된 주기와 일치하는 변동을 찾아냈다고 말한다. 따라서 밑줄 문장은 그전까지 없던 검증 증거를 제시하는 기능을 하므로 B가 정답이다. A는 결과가 예측과 '일치'했다는 지문 내용과 반대된다. C에서 말하는 되먹임은 마지막 문장에서 남은 수수께끼로 제시될 뿐, 밑줄 문장이 설명하는 내용이 아니다. D는 100,000년 주기가 지배적이었다는 시기를 '과거 백만 년'에서 밑줄 문장의 450,000년으로 바꿔 섞었고, 이는 밑줄 문장의 요지도 아니다.","explanationEn":"The sentence before the underlined one says Milankovitch's idea couldn't be tested because no climate record was long or precisely dated enough. The underlined sentence then reports sediment-core data whose cycles closely match the orbital periods. So its job is to supply the evidence that had been missing, which makes B correct. A gets it backward: the data matched Milankovitch's predictions instead of contradicting them. C is wrong because feedbacks come up only in the last sentence, as an unsolved puzzle, and the underlined sentence doesn't explain them. D mixes up details: the text says the 100,000-year cycle dominates the past million years, not 450,000 years, and that point isn't the underlined sentence's purpose anyway.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.606Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"earth and space science — Milankovitch orbital cycle variations controlling Quaternary glacial interglacial climate cycles","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 B 검증: 앞 문장(\"could not be tested, because no climate record was long or precisely dated enough\")과 밑줄 문장(\"however... 450,000 years... closely matching\")의 연결이 명확히 B를 뒷받침함. A는 '일치'와 모순, C는 마지막 문장 내용(수수께끼), D는 '과거 백만 년'과 '450,000년'을 뒤섞은 세부사항 혼합. 오답 C·D가 지문 세부(되먹임, 100,000년 주기, 450,000년)를 활용해 부분적 그럴듯함을 가지므로 medium 적합. 역사적 사실(Hays, Imbrie, Shackleton 1976 Science 논문, 주기 값, 100kyr 문제)도 정확. 해설 한·영 결론과 글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"Hays·Imbrie·Shackleton(1976) 연구, 약 45만 년 기록과 10만·4.1만·2.3만 년 주기, 이심률 변화가 일사량에 주는 영향이 작다는 점 모두 사실과 맞다. 정답 B는 앞 문장(검증 불가)과 밑줄 문장을 연결해야 고를 수 있다. C와 D는 지문에 나온 세부 내용을 비틀어 쓴 그럴듯한 오답이다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-197","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-199","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Meteorologists have long linked Europe's winter weather to the North Atlantic Oscillation (NAO), a seesaw in air pressure between Iceland and the Azores. When the pressure difference is large, the jet stream tends to flow fast and fairly straight, steering mild, wet storms into northern Europe. When the difference weakens, the jet stream often slows and bends into wide loops, letting cold Arctic air spill southward. Some researchers have argued that rapid Arctic warming is making these loops more common by weakening the temperature contrast that drives the jet. __Yet a 2022 analysis of seven decades of wind records found that winters with strongly looping jet streams have not become more frequent overall, even as the Arctic has warmed faster than anywhere else on Earth.__ The study's authors suggest that natural swings in the NAO may still explain more of Europe's winter variability than Arctic change does.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It gives an example of the mechanism by which a weakened pressure difference causes the jet stream to bend into loops.","It provides evidence that Arctic warming has weakened the temperature contrast that drives the jet stream.","It explains why researchers first connected the North Atlantic Oscillation to Europe's winter weather.","It presents a finding that complicates a proposed explanation for changes in the jet stream's behavior."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 시작하며, 북극 온난화가 제트기류의 굽이침을 늘린다는 일부 연구자의 주장과 달리 굽이치는 겨울이 늘지 않았다는 자료를 제시하므로 D가 정답이다. A는 앞 문장에 나온 메커니즘을 언급하지만, 밑줄 문장은 그 메커니즘의 사례가 아니라 빈도에 관한 자료이다. B는 북극 온난화를 언급한 점은 맞지만, 밑줄 문장은 온도 대비 약화를 입증하는 것이 아니라 그 주장의 예측을 약화한다. C는 지문 첫 문장의 내용으로, 밑줄 문장의 역할과 무관하다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence begins with \"Yet\" and reports that looping winters have not become more frequent, which cuts against the claim that Arctic warming is making loops more common, so D is correct. A refers to a mechanism the text does describe, but the underlined sentence reports data on how often loops happen, not an example of how they form. B is right that Arctic warming comes up, but the sentence doesn't prove the contrast has weakened; it actually weakens the prediction built on that idea. C points to the text's opening sentence, which has nothing to do with what the underlined sentence does.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.606Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"earth and space science — Jet stream meandering pattern shifts and North Atlantic Oscillation influence on European weather","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 전환하며 북극 온난화→루프 증가 주장(앞 문장)과 상충하는 7십 년 자료를 제시하고, 뒤 문장(NAO 자연 변동이 더 설명력 있음)으로 이어지므로 '제안된 설명을 복잡하게 만드는 발견'인 D가 정확하다. A(메커니즘 사례)·B(온도 대비 약화 증거)는 지문 요소를 재활용해 부분적 매력이 있고, C는 첫 문장 내용으로 그럴듯하지만 밑줄 역할과 무관. 주장→반증 구조 파악과 문맥 연결이 필요해 medium에 적합. 'Yet' 신호가 비교적 명확해 다소 쉬운 편이나 표준 범위 내. 2022 분석·70년 기록 서술은 실제 연구(예: Blackport & Screen 계열)와 부합하는 수준으로 사실 오류 없음. 한·영 해설 모두 D 지지, 글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"'Yet'이라는 신호 덕분에 정답이 비교적 쉽게 보이지만, B와 A는 지문 내용과 겹치는 부분이 있어 비교해야 배제됩니다. 중간 난이도에 적합합니다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-199","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-e-200","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"easy","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"When a large volcano erupts, it can send sulfur dioxide gas high into the stratosphere. There, the gas reacts with water to form tiny droplets called sulfate aerosols, which reflect some incoming sunlight back into space. To track this effect, scientists measure stratospheric optical depth, a number that shows how much the aerosol layer dims sunlight passing through it. __For example, after Mount Pinatubo erupted in the Philippines in 1991, optical depth readings rose sharply, and average global temperatures fell by about half a degree Celsius over the next year.__ Measurements like these help researchers predict how strongly future eruptions might cool the planet.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It gives a specific case that illustrates the process described earlier in the text.","It gives a specific case that challenges the process described earlier in the text.","It gives a specific case that explains why scientists stopped measuring optical depth.","It gives a specific case that introduces the main topic of the text for the first time."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 'For example'로 시작하며, 앞에서 설명한 과정(황산염 에어로졸이 햇빛을 반사해 냉각을 일으키고 광학 깊이로 측정됨)의 실제 사례로 피나투보 화산을 제시한다. 따라서 A가 정답이다. B는 틀렸다. 이 사례는 앞의 설명을 반박하지 않고 뒷받침한다. C도 틀렸다. 지문 마지막 문장은 이런 측정이 계속 유용하다고 말하므로 측정을 그만둔 이유가 아니다. D도 틀렸다. 주제는 이미 첫 문장들에서 소개되었다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence begins with \"For example.\" It uses the Mount Pinatubo eruption as a real case of the process explained earlier: sulfate aerosols reflect sunlight and cause cooling, and scientists measure this with optical depth. That makes A correct. B is wrong because the example supports the earlier explanation instead of challenging it. C is wrong because the last sentence says these measurements are still useful, so the example isn't about why scientists stopped measuring. D is wrong because the first sentences already introduced the topic.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.606Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"A","seed":"earth and space science — Volcanic sulfate aerosol cooling effect and stratospheric optical depth measurement after eruptions","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"정답 A 검증: 밑줄 문장은 \"For example\"로 시작하며 앞서 설명된 에어로졸 냉각·광학 깊이 측정 과정을 피나투보(1991) 사례로 예시함. B(반박), C(측정 중단—마지막 문장과 모순), D(주제 최초 도입—이미 앞에서 소개)는 명확히 배제되나 오개념으로 그럴듯함. 피나투보 1991년 분출 및 약 0.5°C 냉각은 사실과 부합. 한국어·영어 해설 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 'For example'이라는 직접 단서 하나로 풀리므로 easy 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"'For example'라는 직접 단서 하나로 풀리므로 easy에 맞음. 피나투보 화산 이후 약 0.5°C 냉각은 사실과 맞음. C는 지문에 근거가 없어 다소 쉽게 배제되지만 허용 범위임.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-e-200","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-e-201","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"easy","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Before building a wind farm, engineers usually measure average wind speed at a site for a year or more. But average speed alone can be misleading. Near the ground, air moves through the atmospheric boundary layer, where it tumbles and swirls as it passes over hills, trees, and buildings. __At one test site in Oklahoma, for example, two towers recorded nearly the same average wind speed, yet turbines near the rougher, wooded tower produced noticeably less power and needed more repairs.__ For this reason, many researchers now argue that site surveys should also measure how much the wind fluctuates from moment to moment, not just how fast it blows on average.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It introduces a new method engineers use to measure average wind speed at possible wind farm sites.","It gives a specific case showing that average wind speed alone did not predict how well turbines performed.","It presents a finding that challenges the researchers' recommendation stated at the end of the text.","It describes how hills, trees, and buildings form the atmospheric boundary layer near the ground."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 'for example'로 시작하며, 평균 풍속이 같았는데도 거친 지형의 터빈 성능이 낮았던 사례를 들어 앞 문장의 \"평균 풍속만으로는 오해할 수 있다\"는 주장을 뒷받침하므로 B가 정답이다. A는 새로운 측정 방법을 소개하는 것이 아니라 기존 측정의 한계를 보여 주므로 틀리다. C는 이 사례가 마지막 문장의 권고를 반박하지 않고 오히려 뒷받침하므로 틀리다. D는 지형이 경계층을 형성하는 과정을 설명하지 않으며, 그 내용은 앞 문장의 배경일 뿐이다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence begins with \"for example\" and describes two towers with nearly the same average wind speed but different turbine results, which supports the earlier claim that average speed alone can be misleading, so B is correct. A is wrong because the sentence doesn't introduce a new measuring method; it shows a limitation of the usual one. C is wrong because the example supports the researchers' recommendation at the end instead of challenging it. D is wrong because the sentence doesn't explain how the boundary layer forms; that background comes in the sentence before it.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.606Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"B","seed":"earth and space science — Boundary layer turbulence characteristics affecting wind energy resource assessment wind farms","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 'for example'로 명시된 예시이며 앞 문장의 '평균 풍속만으로는 오해 소지' 주장을 구체 사례로 뒷받침함. B 정답 확인. A(새 측정법 소개 아님), C(권고를 반박하지 않고 지지), D(경계층 형성 설명은 앞 문장 내용) 모두 전형적 오개념형 오답으로 적절. 한·영 해설 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 지문은 창작 지문으로 저작권 문제 없음. 단일 규칙(예시 신호어)으로 한 단계 추론, easy 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"'for example'라는 명시적 단서와 바로 앞 주장 사이의 관계를 한 단계만 추론하면 풀린다. 오답 A, C, D는 지문의 어휘를 재활용한 전형적인 오개념 선택지라 easy 난이도에 적합하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-e-201","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-e-202","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"easy","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Most glaciers creep downhill only a few meters each year. Surge glaciers behave differently: after decades of slow movement, they can suddenly speed up and travel many meters in a single day. Scientists think water is a major cause. During warm periods, meltwater from the surface drains down through cracks and gathers where the ice meets the bedrock below. __This trapped water acts like a slippery layer, lifting the ice slightly and reducing the friction that normally holds it in place.__ Once that friction drops, the heavy glacier can slide forward much faster than usual, sometimes until the water finally escapes and the surge ends.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It introduces a surprising fact about how fast surge glaciers move compared with ordinary glaciers.","It presents a claim by some scientists that the text then argues is unlikely to be correct.","It explains how the meltwater described earlier allows a glacier to move more quickly.","It describes the conditions that cause a surge to stop once the water has escaped."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 앞 문장에서 말한 기반암과 얼음 사이에 고인 융빙수가 미끄러운 층이 되어 마찰을 줄인다는 과정을 설명하므로, 융빙수가 빙하를 빠르게 움직이게 하는 방식을 설명한다. 따라서 정답은 C이다. A는 속도 비교를 다루는데, 그 내용은 지문 앞부분에 있고 밑줄 문장의 내용이 아니다. B는 틀렸다. 지문은 이 설명을 반박하지 않고 오히려 뒷받침한다. D는 서지 종료에 관한 내용인데, 이는 마지막 문장에서만 짧게 언급된다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence explains how the meltwater from the previous sentence works: it forms a slippery layer and reduces friction, which lets the glacier move faster. So C is correct. A is about the speed comparison, but that comes earlier in the text, not in the underlined sentence. B is wrong because the text never argues against this idea; it builds on it. D is about how a surge ends, and only the final sentence briefly mentions that.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.606Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"C","seed":"earth and space science — Surge glacier acceleration mechanism and meltwater lubrication at bedrock interface dynamics","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 직전 문장의 융빙수가 마찰을 줄여 빙하를 가속시키는 메커니즘을 설명하며 다음 문장(\"Once that friction drops...\")으로 직접 이어지므로 C가 정답. A(속도 비교)는 1~2문장, D(서지 종료)는 마지막 절의 내용이고 B는 지문에 반박이 없어 배제됨. 오답들은 인접 문장의 내용을 밑줄 문장에 귀속시키는 전형적 오개념으로 적절. 한·영 해설 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 과학 내용(기저 수분에 의한 서지) 타당, 창작 지문으로 저작권 우려 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 앞 문장의 융빙수가 마찰을 줄이는 메커니즘을 설명하므로 C가 정답. 오답 A·D는 지문의 다른 문장 내용을 가져온 전형적 위치 혼동 오답이고, B는 태도 오류 오답이다. 단서가 직접적이고 추론은 한 단계라 easy에 맞다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-e-202","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-203","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Zeolites are crystalline minerals whose aluminosilicate frameworks are riddled with pores of nearly identical width, often less than a nanometer across. Because of this uniformity, zeolites are commonly described as \"molecular sieves\" that admit molecules small enough to enter the pores and exclude larger ones. Yet in one of their most widespread industrial uses, separating nitrogen from oxygen to produce oxygen-enriched air, size plays almost no role: the two molecules are so similar in dimension that both slip easily into the pores of common zeolites. What distinguishes them instead is charge distribution. Nitrogen molecules have a stronger quadrupole moment than oxygen molecules do, so they are drawn more strongly to the positively charged metal ions lining the zeolite's channels. When air is forced through a bed of the material under pressure, nitrogen clings to the pore walls while oxygen passes through, and lowering the pressure later releases the trapped nitrogen so the bed can be reused.","question":"According to the text, what allows zeolites to separate nitrogen from oxygen in the production of oxygen-enriched air?","options":["The pores of common zeolites are narrow enough to block nitrogen molecules while letting the slightly smaller oxygen molecules pass through.","Lowering the pressure on a zeolite bed causes oxygen to be released from the pore walls while nitrogen remains trapped inside.","The positively charged metal ions in zeolite channels react chemically with oxygen, removing it from the air stream.","Nitrogen's electrical properties cause it to be held more strongly by the zeolite's interior than oxygen is, even though both fit in the pores."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 질소와 산소가 크기가 비슷해 둘 다 기공에 들어가지만, 질소의 사중극자 모멘트가 더 강해 채널의 양이온에 더 강하게 끌린다고 설명하므로 D가 정답이다. A는 '분자체'라는 일반적 설명을 이 사례에 잘못 적용한 것으로, 지문은 이 분리에서 크기가 거의 역할을 하지 않는다고 말한다. B는 감압 단계를 언급하지만 감압 시 방출되는 것은 산소가 아니라 붙잡혀 있던 질소이다. C는 금속 이온을 언급하지만 지문은 질소가 이온에 끌린다고 했을 뿐 산소와의 화학 반응은 말하지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The text says nitrogen and oxygen are so similar in size that both enter the pores, but nitrogen's stronger quadrupole moment makes it cling more strongly to the positively charged ions lining the channels, so D is correct. A applies the general \"molecular sieve\" idea to this case, but the text says size plays almost no role in this separation. B mentions the pressure drop, but what lowering the pressure releases is the trapped nitrogen, not oxygen. C mentions the metal ions, but the text says nitrogen is attracted to them and never describes any chemical reaction with oxygen.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.606Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"physical science — Zeolite molecular sieving and selective gas adsorption application in industrial separation processes","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"D는 지문의 \"What distinguishes them instead is charge distribution... drawn more strongly to the positively charged metal ions\"를 정확히 재진술하며, \"both fit in the pores\"도 지문과 일치. A는 '분자체' 일반 설명을 훑어 읽으면 고를 수 있는 매력적 오답, B는 감압 단계에서 기체를 뒤바꾼 오답, C는 금속 이온 세부를 왜곡한 오답으로 모두 지문 근거가 있어 비교가 필요하다. 과학적 사실(PSA 공정에서 N2 사중극자 모멘트 기반 분리)도 정확. 해설 한·영 결론 및 글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스러움."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"D는 '사중극자 모멘트'를 '전기적 성질'로 바꿔 말한 것이라 확인 과정이 한 번 필요하다. A는 '분자체'라는 일반적 설명에 기댄 오답, B는 감압 단계의 순서를 뒤바꾼 오답, C는 금속 이온을 근거로 쓴 그럴듯한 오답이다. 중간 난이도에 맞다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-203","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-205","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Shape memory alloys such as nickel-titanium can recover large deformations because their crystal structure switches between two arrangements: a stiff, high-temperature phase called austenite and a more pliable, low-temperature phase called martensite. When the alloy is held above its transformation temperature and then loaded, stress alone can force austenite into martensite, letting the metal stretch by several percent; once the load is removed, the martensite reverts and the part springs back to its original shape. This behavior, known as pseudoelasticity, has drawn interest from aerospace engineers designing components that must flex repeatedly without permanent damage.\n\nYet engineers at several research centers have found that the same transformation complicates flight hardware. Because the temperature at which the phases switch shifts with each loading cycle, a pseudoelastic part that performs reliably in ground tests may stiffen or soften unpredictably after thousands of cycles in the wide temperature swings of high-altitude flight. Consequently, teams now treat cyclic stability of the transformation temperature, rather than recoverable strain alone, as the key property to qualify before such alloys are installed on aircraft.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Because shape memory alloys can stretch by several percent and still spring back, engineers consider them ready to replace conventional metals in aircraft components that flex repeatedly.","Because the phase change behind shape memory alloys' recoverable flexing drifts over repeated use, engineers now focus on that drift when judging whether the alloys are fit for aircraft.","Because martensite is more pliable than austenite, engineers now design aircraft parts so that shape memory alloys remain in the martensite phase throughout flight.","Because ground tests cannot reproduce high-altitude temperatures, engineers have stopped testing shape memory alloys on the ground and now evaluate them only during flight."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 글은 형상기억합금이 큰 변형에서도 원래 모양으로 돌아오는 이유를 설명한 뒤, 상변태 온도가 하중 주기마다 달라진다는 문제를 제시하고, 그래서 이제는 그 안정성을 핵심 검증 항목으로 삼는다고 결론짓는다. 이 흐름을 그대로 담은 선택지는 B다. A는 첫 단락의 장점만 반영하고, 그 장점을 복잡하게 만드는 둘째 단락의 내용을 무시한다. C는 마르텐사이트가 더 유연하다는 세부를 근거로 삼지만, 글에는 부품을 그 상태로 유지하도록 설계한다는 내용이 없다. D는 지상 시험의 한계를 지나치게 확대한 것으로, 지상 시험을 중단했다는 말은 글에 나오지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The text first explains why shape memory alloys can spring back from large deformations. It then points out a problem: the transformation temperature shifts with each loading cycle. It concludes that engineers now treat the stability of that temperature as the key property to check. Choice B captures this whole line of reasoning. Choice A reflects only the advantage described in the first paragraph and ignores the complication raised in the second. Choice C takes the detail that martensite is more pliable, but the text never says parts are designed to stay in that phase. Choice D stretches the point about ground tests too far, because the text never says ground testing was abandoned.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.606Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"physical science — Shape memory alloy phase transformation and pseudoelastic behavior in aerospace applications","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 B는 1단락(가역 변형의 원리)과 2단락(변태 온도의 주기적 이동 → 순환 안정성을 핵심 검증 항목으로 삼음)을 모두 포괄하는 주제문으로 적절하다. A는 1단락만 반영하고 \"ready to replace\"는 글에 없음, C는 세부(마르텐사이트 유연성)를 과잉 해석, D는 지상 시험 중단은 글에 없음. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 동일 결론·글자 참조, 모순 없음, 영어 자연스러움. 형상기억합금·초탄성·변태 온도의 주기적 이동(cyclic instability)은 과학적으로 타당. 두 단락의 연결을 요구하며 A·C가 부분적 근거를 지녀 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"B는 'drift'라는 말로 지문의 '변태 온도 변화'를 바꿔 말한 것으로 정확하다. 오답 A·C는 첫 단락의 세부 내용에 기대고 있고, D는 지상 시험의 한계를 과장한 것이어서 medium 난이도에 적합하다. 다만 C와 D는 다소 쉽게 배제된다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-205","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-207","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Magnetorheological (MR) fluids are suspensions of tiny iron particles in oil. Under ordinary conditions, the particles drift freely and the fluid pours much like motor oil. When a magnetic field is applied, however, the particles line up into chains along the field lines, and within milliseconds the fluid stiffens into a semisolid that strongly resists flow. Removing the field lets the chains collapse, and the fluid returns to its liquid state just as quickly.\n\nEngineers have used this reversible behavior to build shock absorbers whose resistance can be tuned continuously. In a conventional damper, the thickness of the fluid is fixed at manufacture, so the device is a compromise between comfort on smooth roads and control on rough ones. An MR damper, by contrast, pairs the fluid with sensors and an electromagnet, adjusting the field hundreds of times per second so that the damping matches conditions as they change. The same principle now appears in seismic dampers installed in some buildings and bridges.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Because iron particles in MR fluids form chains under a magnetic field, MR fluids are thicker than the oils used in conventional shock absorbers.","Because conventional dampers balance comfort against control, engineers have replaced them with MR dampers in most vehicles, buildings, and bridges.","Because MR fluids change state within milliseconds, they are mainly valued for allowing seismic dampers to be installed quickly in existing structures.","Because MR fluids can be switched rapidly and reversibly between liquid and semisolid states, they allow dampers whose resistance adjusts to changing conditions."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 첫 단락에서 MR 유체가 자기장에 따라 빠르고 가역적으로 액체와 반고체 사이를 오간다는 성질을, 둘째 단락에서 이 성질 덕분에 조건에 맞춰 저항을 조절하는 댐퍼가 가능하다는 점을 설명하므로 D가 중심 내용이다. A는 사슬 형성이라는 세부는 맞지만, 자기장이 없을 때는 모터오일처럼 흐른다고 했으므로 항상 더 두껍다는 진술은 틀리다. B는 기존 댐퍼의 절충이라는 세부는 맞지만, '대부분'을 대체했다는 내용은 지문에 없다. C는 밀리초 단위 변화를 언급하지만, 그 가치를 빠른 설치와 잘못 연결하고 지진 댐퍼라는 부차적 예시를 중심으로 삼는다.","explanationEn":"The first paragraph explains that MR fluids switch quickly and reversibly between a liquid and a semisolid when a magnetic field is turned on or off. The second paragraph shows how this lets engineers build dampers that adjust to changing conditions, so D states the main idea. A gets the chain formation right, but the text says the fluid pours like motor oil when there's no field, so it isn't always thicker. B correctly mentions the compromise in conventional dampers, but the text never says MR dampers have replaced them in most vehicles or structures. C mentions the millisecond response but wrongly ties its value to quick installation, and it centers on seismic dampers, which are only a passing example.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.606Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"physical science — Magnetorheological fluid viscosity change under magnetic field enabling adaptive damping systems","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"지문·정답 검증: 1문단(빠르고 가역적인 상태 전환) + 2문단(조건에 맞춰 저항이 조절되는 댐퍼)을 종합한 D가 중심 내용으로 정확함. 오답 분석: A는 사슬 형성 세부는 맞으나 '항상 더 두껍다'는 지문과 모순(자기장 없으면 모터오일처럼 흐름), B는 절충 세부는 맞으나 '대부분 대체'는 근거 없음(지문은 'some buildings and bridges'), C는 밀리초 반응은 맞으나 설치 속도와의 연결이 무근거이며 부차적 예시를 중심화. 세 오답 모두 부분적 근거를 가져 비교가 필요하므로 medium에 적합. 한·영 해설 모두 D를 일관되게 지지하고 선택지 글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스러움, 한글 혼입 없음. MR 유체 설명(철 입자, 사슬 형성, 밀리초 반응, 가변 댐퍼, 지진 댐퍼 적용)은 과학적으로 타당. 저작권 의심 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"오답들이 각각 지문 세부(사슬 형성, 절충, 밀리초)를 일부 활용해 비교가 필요함. D가 두 단락을 연결하는 중심 내용으로 명확함. 중간 난이도에 적합.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-207","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-209","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Metal-organic frameworks (MOFs) are crystalline materials built from metal clusters linked by organic molecules, and some contain so many internal pores that a single gram can have a surface area larger than a soccer field. Because hydrogen molecules cling weakly to these surfaces, researchers have long hoped MOFs could store hydrogen fuel compactly for clean-energy vehicles. Early studies focused on maximizing porosity, assuming that more surface area would always mean more stored hydrogen. Chemist Hiroyasu Furukawa and colleagues found, however, that the most porous frameworks often performed poorly at practical temperatures: their pores were so wide that hydrogen drifted away from the walls unless the material was cooled to around -196°C. Frameworks with somewhat smaller pores, tuned so that each pore wall sat close to the trapped molecules, held hydrogen more strongly and retained more of it under less extreme cooling.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Metal-organic frameworks with the greatest surface area are the most promising materials for storing hydrogen in clean-energy vehicles.","Metal-organic frameworks store hydrogen best at practical temperatures when their pore size is matched to the molecules rather than simply maximized.","Metal-organic frameworks can store hydrogen only when they are cooled to around -196°C, which limits their usefulness.","Metal-organic frameworks are unlikely to be used for hydrogen storage because hydrogen molecules bind only weakly to their surfaces."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 처음엔 다공성을 최대화하면 수소 저장이 늘 것이라 여겼지만, 실제로는 기공이 분자에 맞게 조금 작을 때 덜 극단적인 냉각에서도 더 많이 저장된다는 반전을 중심으로 하므로 B가 정답이다. A는 초기 연구의 가정일 뿐이며 지문이 이를 반박한다. C는 가장 다공성인 구조에만 해당하는 세부 내용을 모든 MOF로 일반화했다. D는 약한 결합이라는 사실은 맞지만, 지문은 MOF를 포기하자는 것이 아니라 설계 개선을 제시한다.","explanationEn":"The passage turns on a reversal: researchers first assumed that maximizing porosity would maximize hydrogen storage, but frameworks with somewhat smaller, well-tuned pores actually held more hydrogen at less extreme temperatures, so B is correct. A states the early assumption, which the passage goes on to challenge. C takes a detail that applies only to the most porous frameworks and applies it to all MOFs. D is right that hydrogen binds weakly, but the passage offers a better design, not a reason to give up on MOFs.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.606Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"physical science — Metal organic framework porosity and hydrogen storage capacity for clean energy applications","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"지문의 핵심은 '다공성 최대화 가정 → 기공 크기를 분자에 맞춘 구조가 실용 온도에서 더 우수'라는 반전이며 B가 이를 정확히 요약한다. A는 지문이 반박하는 초기 가정(훑어 읽으면 선택할 함정), C는 가장 다공성인 MOF에만 해당하는 -196°C 세부를 전체로 일반화, D는 약한 결합이라는 사실에 근거하지만 지문의 결론과 반대. 과학적 사실(Furukawa의 MOF 수소 저장 연구, 77K 조건, g당 축구장 크기 표면적)도 타당. 한·영 해설 모두 B를 일관되게 뒷받침하고 선택지 참조가 일치한다. 반전 구조 파악 + 오답 비교가 필요하므로 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"정답 B는 지문의 반전 구조(다공성 최대화 → 기공 크기 맞춤)와 일치한다. A는 반박된 초기 가정, C는 과잉 일반화, D는 맞는 사실(약한 결합)에서 잘못된 결론을 낸다. 오답 각각에 부분적인 근거가 있다. -196°C(약 77 K, 액체질소 온도)는 사실과 맞다. 오답이 다소 쉽게 배제되지만 medium 범위 안이다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-209","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-210","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"When tiny silica or polymer spheres of nearly identical size are suspended in a liquid and allowed to settle slowly, they can arrange themselves into an orderly, repeating lattice known as a colloidal crystal. Because the spacing between the spheres is comparable to the wavelength of visible light, such crystals reflect certain colors strongly while letting others pass, producing an iridescent shimmer similar to that of natural opals. Materials scientists have long hoped to use this effect to make fade-resistant pigments that need no dyes. __In practice, however, even small variations in sphere size create cracks and misaligned regions that scatter light randomly and wash out the color.__ Chemist Lin Okafor and colleagues addressed this problem by adding a soft polymer shell to each sphere, which lets neighboring particles shift slightly during drying and settle into a more uniform arrangement, yielding films with noticeably purer hues.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It explains the physical mechanism by which colloidal crystals reflect some wavelengths of light while transmitting others.","It presents evidence that pigments made from colloidal crystals fade more quickly than pigments made with conventional dyes.","It identifies a practical obstacle that complicates a goal described earlier and that the research mentioned afterward attempts to overcome.","It describes a result of Okafor's team's experiments showing that soft polymer shells reduce the purity of the colors produced."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 'however'로 앞에서 말한 염료 없는 안료 개발 목표를 가로막는 현실적 문제(크기 편차로 인한 균열·색 바램)를 제시하고, 뒤의 Okafor 연구는 이 문제를 해결하려는 시도이므로 C가 정답이다. A는 빛 반사 원리를 설명하는 것이 앞 문장의 역할이므로 틀리다. B는 색이 'wash out'된다는 표현을 기존 염료보다 빨리 바랜다는 비교로 잘못 해석했다. D는 밑줄 문장이 Okafor 팀의 결과가 아니며, 실제로 고분자 껍질은 색 순도를 높였으므로 틀리다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence opens with \"however,\" which tells you it introduces a real-world problem (cracks and misalignment from differences in sphere size) standing in the way of the dye-free pigment goal mentioned just before it. Okafor's team's work, described next, is an attempt to solve that problem, so C is correct. A is wrong because the sentence before the underlined one is the one that explains how light gets reflected. B misreads \"wash out the color\" as a comparison with conventional dyes, but the text never makes that comparison. D is wrong because the underlined sentence isn't one of Okafor's results, and the polymer shells actually made the colors purer.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.607Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"physical science — Colloidal crystal self-assembly and photonic bandgap optical properties in iridescent materials","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 'however'로 앞의 목표(염료 없는 안료)를 가로막는 현실적 장애(크기 편차→균열·색 바램)를 제시하고, 다음 문장이 'addressed this problem'으로 이를 해결하려 하므로 C가 정확함. A는 앞 문장 기능, B는 본문에 없는 염료와의 비교, D는 출처·결과 모두 오류. 한·영 해설 결론 및 글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 가상 연구자·일반 과학 내용으로 저작권 문제 없음. 전환어 파악+앞뒤 연결의 두 단계 판단이 필요하고 A·B가 부분적 근거를 가져 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["too_easy","eliminated:2"],"note":"오답 B·D는 지문과 명백히 모순되고(D는 결과 반대, B는 비교 없음), A도 앞 문장 역할이라 쉽게 배제됨. 부분적 근거로 비교해야 하는 오답이 부족해 medium 기준 미달.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-210","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-213","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Engineers who design plastic pipes, bridge bearings, and other long-lived components cannot rely only on a polymer's stiffness as measured in a quick laboratory test. Because polymers are viscoelastic, their molecular chains slowly slide past and untangle from one another under sustained load. A pipe held at constant stretch therefore gradually loses internal stress, a process called stress relaxation, while a beam carrying a constant weight continues to sag over months or years, a process called creep. __Yet a polymer that passes a one-hour strength test with ease may, after a decade of carrying a far smaller load, deform enough to fail.__ For this reason, designers increasingly use accelerated tests at elevated temperatures, which speed up chain motion, to estimate how a material will behave over its full service life.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It defines the two time-dependent processes, stress relaxation and creep, that were introduced earlier in the text.","It illustrates a practical consequence of the behavior described earlier, which motivates the testing approach mentioned afterward.","It challenges the claim that polymer chains slide past one another by offering evidence from short-term strength tests.","It explains why accelerated tests at elevated temperatures give more reliable results than tests at room temperature."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 앞에서 설명한 크리프·응력 완화 현상이 실제로 낳는 결과(단기 시험 통과 재료도 장기적으로 파손될 수 있음)를 보여 주며, 이것이 마지막 문장의 가속 시험 사용 이유('For this reason')가 된다. 따라서 B가 정답이다. A는 두 현상의 정의가 밑줄 앞 문장에서 이미 이루어졌으므로 틀리다. C는 단기 시험이 언급되긴 하지만 사슬 미끄러짐 주장에 반박하지 않고 오히려 그 결과를 보여 주므로 틀리다. D는 가속 시험을 언급하지만 상온 시험과의 신뢰성 비교는 지문에 없고, 그 시험이 쓰이는 이유를 설명하는 것은 밑줄 문장 자체가 아니라 그다음 문장이다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence shows a real-world consequence of the creep and stress relaxation described just before it: a material can pass a short test and still fail after years under a smaller load. That problem is what the final sentence responds to (\"For this reason\"), so B is correct. A is wrong because the two processes were already defined in the sentence before the underlined one. C is wrong because the sentence doesn't challenge the idea that chains slide past each other; it actually shows what happens because they do. D is wrong because the text never compares accelerated tests with room-temperature tests, and the underlined sentence comes before the testing approach is even mentioned.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.607Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"physical science — Viscoelastic polymer stress relaxation and creep behavior in long-term structural applications","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 앞의 크리프·응력 완화 설명의 실제 결과를 보여 주고, 뒤의 'For this reason'으로 가속 시험 도입을 이끄는 연결 역할을 하므로 B가 명확히 맞다. A(두 현상 언급)와 D(가속 시험 언급)는 지문 요소를 포함해 부분적 근거가 있어 비교가 필요하고 C도 '단기 시험' 언급으로 말이 되므로 medium에 적합. 해설 한·영 모두 B를 일관되게 뒷받침하며 오답 배제 근거가 정확함. 사실관계(점탄성, 사슬 이동, 응력 완화/크리프, 고온 가속 시험)도 정확. 사소한 점: 밑줄 문장 첫 단어 'Yet'이 내용상 결과 제시이므로 대조 연결어가 다소 어색하나 '쉽게 통과'와 '파손'의 대비로 읽힐 수 있어 판정에 영향 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장 앞의 'Yet'은 바로 앞 크리프 설명과의 대조 관계가 약간 어색하다(첫 문장의 단기 시험 강성과 대조되는 것으로 읽힘). 다만 정답 판정에는 영향이 없다. 오답 A·D는 지문 요소를 부분적으로 끌어와 비교가 필요하고, C는 비교적 쉽게 배제된다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-213","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-215","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In capillary electrophoresis, a sample is injected into a narrow glass tube filled with a buffer solution, and a strong voltage is applied across the tube's ends. Charged molecules in the sample then migrate toward the electrode of opposite charge, each at a speed determined by its electrophoretic mobility, a property that depends largely on the ratio of the molecule's charge to its size. A small, highly charged ion therefore outpaces a large, weakly charged one, and molecules that entered the tube together emerge at the far end at different times. __One might expect neutral molecules, which feel no electrical pull, to remain stranded near the injection point, yet they too reach the detector, carried along by a bulk flow of buffer that the voltage generates along the charged inner wall of the tube.__ Because this flow moves every component in the same direction, analysts can detect positive, negative, and neutral species in a single run, distinguishing them by their arrival times.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It presents an exception to the principle that charge-to-size ratio governs migration speed, suggesting that this principle is unreliable for most samples.","It identifies a limitation of capillary electrophoresis that prevents analysts from detecting uncharged molecules in a sample.","It offers an additional illustration of how differences in charge-to-size ratio cause molecules to arrive at the detector at different times.","It addresses an apparent gap in the mechanism described earlier by introducing a process that explains a result the text goes on to discuss."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"앞 문장들은 전하를 띤 분자가 전기적 인력으로 이동한다고 설명하므로, 전하가 없는 분자는 움직이지 않을 것이라는 의문이 생긴다. 밑줄 문장은 이 예상을 제시한 뒤 완충액의 전체 흐름이라는 과정을 소개해 이를 해소하고, 마지막 문장은 이 흐름 덕분에 모든 종을 한 번에 검출할 수 있다는 결과를 논의한다. 따라서 D가 정답이다. A는 '예외'라는 점은 일부 맞지만 원리가 신뢰할 수 없다고 말하지 않는다. B는 중성 분자도 검출기에 도달한다는 내용과 정반대이며, C는 중성 분자에는 전하 대 크기 비가 적용되지 않으므로 같은 원리의 추가 예시가 아니다.","explanationEn":"The earlier sentences explain that charged molecules move because of electrical pull, which leaves open the question of what happens to uncharged molecules. The underlined sentence raises that expectation and then answers it by introducing the bulk flow of buffer, and the final sentence discusses the result: all species can be detected in one run. That makes D correct. A is partly right that neutral molecules are an exception, but the text never says the charge-to-size principle is unreliable. B is the opposite of what the sentence says, since neutral molecules do reach the detector, and C is wrong because neutral molecules move by flow, not because of charge-to-size differences.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.607Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"physical science — Capillary electrophoresis separation mechanism using electric field and differential ion mobility","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 '중성 분자는 멈춰 있을 것'이라는 예상(앞 문장들의 메커니즘이 남긴 공백)을 제기한 뒤 전기삼투 흐름(bulk flow)을 도입하고, 마지막 문장이 이 흐름 덕분에 모든 종을 한 번에 검출한다는 결과를 논의하므로 D가 정확히 부합한다. A는 '예외'라는 부분적 근거가 있으나 '신뢰할 수 없다'는 평가가 본문에 없고, C는 '도착 시간 차이'라는 부분적 근거가 있으나 중성 분자의 이동 원리가 다르며, B는 본문과 정반대다. 전기삼투 흐름의 과학적 설명도 정확하다. 한·영 해설 모두 정답과 선택지 참조가 일치하며 영어 해설은 자연스럽고 한글이 없다. 두 문장 간 연결과 비교 판단이 필요해 medium에 적합하다."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"전기삼투류 설명이 과학적으로 정확하다. A는 일부 맞는 내용을 담은 그럴듯한 오답이다. B는 지문과 정반대여서 쉽게 배제되고, C는 중간 정도로 그럴듯하다. 정답 D를 고르려면 앞 문장과 뒤 문장을 연결해야 하므로 medium 난이도에 적합하다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-215","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-217","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Graphene aerogels, made by freeze-drying a suspension of graphene oxide sheets and then chemically reducing the resulting scaffold, are among the lightest solids ever produced, with some samples weighing less than the air they displace. Because more than 99 percent of their volume is empty space, many engineers assumed they would be excellent thermal insulators, since heat travels poorly through gas-filled pores. __Yet early measurements by materials scientist Hu Liang's team showed that their aerogels conducted heat noticeably better than expected for their density.__ The team traced the problem to the graphene sheets themselves: graphene carries heat extremely well along its plane, so wherever sheets touched and formed continuous walls, heat flowed quickly through the solid network. By adjusting the freezing rate to produce thinner, more fragmented walls with fewer sheet-to-sheet contacts, the researchers lowered the material's conductivity to levels rivaling the best commercial insulators.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It presents a measurement that confirms the engineers' reasoning about how heat moves through gas-filled pores.","It presents a finding that runs counter to an expectation and sets up the explanation and remedy that follow.","It presents a finding that shows graphene aerogels are unsuitable for insulation, a conclusion the rest of the text supports.","It presents a finding that explains why freeze-drying produces some of the lightest solids ever made."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 시작해 기공이 많으니 단열이 뛰어날 것이라는 기대와 달리 열전도가 예상보다 높았다는 결과를 제시하고, 이어지는 문장들이 그 원인(그래핀 시트 접촉)과 해결책(동결 속도 조절)을 설명하므로 B가 정답이다. A는 측정이 기대를 확인한 것이 아니라 뒤집었으므로 틀리다. C는 문제 제기라는 점은 맞지만, 글 후반에서 상용 단열재 수준으로 개선했으므로 '부적합하다'는 결론을 뒷받침하지 않는다. D는 가벼움을 다룬 첫 문장과 관련 있을 뿐, 밑줄 문장은 열전도에 관한 것이다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence begins with \"Yet.\" It reports that the aerogels conducted heat better than expected, which goes against the assumption that all those gas-filled pores would make them excellent insulators. The rest of the text then explains the cause (graphene sheets touching each other) and the fix (changing the freezing rate), so B is correct. A is wrong because the measurement contradicts the engineers' reasoning instead of confirming it. C correctly sees that the sentence raises a problem, but the text ends with the conductivity brought down to the level of top commercial insulators, so it never concludes that the aerogels are unsuitable. D links the sentence to the first sentence about lightness, but the underlined sentence is about heat conduction, not about why the material is so light.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.607Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"physical science — Graphene aerogel synthesis and ultra-low density thermal insulation material properties characterization","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 기대(우수한 단열)와 상반되는 결과(예상보다 높은 열전도)를 제시하고, 이후 원인 규명과 해결책이 이어지므로 B가 정확하다. A는 '확인'이 아닌 '반박'이라 틀리고, C는 문제 제기는 맞지만 글 결말(상용 단열재 수준 달성)과 모순되며, D는 밑줄 문장의 주제(열전도)와 무관하다. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 동일한 결론과 선택지 참조를 가지며 영어는 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 그래핀 에어로겔의 제조법·초경량성·면내 열전도 특성 설명은 과학적으로 타당하며 연구자명은 가상으로 보여 저작권 우려 없음. 담화 표지 파악 + 후속 문맥(원인·해결) 연결의 두 단계 판단이 필요하고 C가 부분적 근거를 가져 medium에 적합하다."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"C가 그럴듯한 오답이고, A·D도 지문에 나오는 요소(기공을 통한 열 이동, 가벼움)를 사용해 함정 역할을 한다. 'Yet'이라는 단서가 다소 노골적이지만 중간 난이도로 볼 수 있다. 일부 표본이 자신이 밀어낸 공기보다 가볍다는 주장은 대체로 실제 보고와 맞는다(공기를 제외하고 잰 밀도 기준). Hu Liang은 가상 인물일 가능성이 있다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-217","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-words_in_context-m-218","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Words in Context","difficulty":"medium","skill":"words_in_context","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Conventional lithium-ion batteries rely on organic liquid electrolytes that begin to break down when the voltage across them climbs too high, which limits how much energy a cell can store. Ionic liquids—salts that remain liquid at room temperature—have drawn attention because many of them resist decomposition across a much wider voltage range. Researchers caution, however, that this advantage is not unconditional: even trace amounts of water absorbed from the air can ______ an ionic liquid's stability, narrowing its usable voltage window so much that it performs little better than the conventional electrolytes it was meant to replace.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["disguise","regulate","undermine","reveal"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 미량의 수분이 이온성 액체의 전압 창을 좁혀 기존 전해질보다 나을 게 없게 만든다고 말하므로, 빈칸에는 안정성을 '약화시키다'라는 뜻이 필요하고 C(undermine)가 이에 맞습니다. A(disguise)는 안정성을 숨긴다는 뜻이라 실제로 성능이 떨어진다는 내용과 맞지 않습니다. B(regulate)는 수분이 안정성에 영향을 준다는 점은 담지만, 조절한다는 중립적인 의미일 뿐 안정성이 떨어진다는 방향은 담지 못합니다. D(reveal)는 수분이 숨어 있던 한계를 드러낸다고 읽을 수도 있지만, 지문은 수분이 안정성을 직접 떨어뜨린다고 말하므로 맞지 않습니다.","explanationEn":"The text says trace water narrows the ionic liquid's voltage window until it performs little better than conventional electrolytes, so the blank needs a word meaning \"weaken.\" That makes C (undermine) the answer. A (disguise) means to hide the stability, but the text describes performance actually getting worse. B (regulate) captures that water affects stability, but it's a neutral word meaning \"control,\" so it misses the direction of harm. D (reveal) could suggest water exposes a hidden limit, but the text says water directly reduces stability rather than uncovering it.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.607Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"physical science — Ionic liquid electrolyte stability and electrochemical window expansion for battery applications","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 C(undermine) 검증: \"narrowing its usable voltage window\"가 안정성 약화를 직접 뒷받침. A/D는 숨기기/드러내기로 방향 불일치, B는 중립적 '조절'로 부정적 결과와 불일치. 해설 한·영 결론 및 글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 과학적 배경(이온성 액체의 넓은 전기화학 창, 수분 오염에 의한 창 축소)도 사실과 부합. 난이도: 'however… not unconditional'의 대비 구조와 결과절을 연결해야 하고 B·D가 부분적 매력을 지녀 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"수분이 이온성 액체의 전기화학 창을 좁힌다는 내용은 사실에 부합함. undermine이 유일하게 맞음. regulate와 reveal은 매력 오답으로 적절해 medium 수준으로 볼 수 있음. disguise는 비교적 약한 오답임.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-words_in_context-m-218","intendedSkill":"words_in_context","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-words_in_context-m-220","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Words in Context","difficulty":"medium","skill":"words_in_context","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"When a circuit board repeatedly heats up and cools down, its solder joints are strained because the copper pads and the silicon chip expand at different rates. Materials engineer Priya Venkataraman found that the first microscopic cracks in such joints do not appear at random. Instead, they consistently ______ at the corners of the joint, where stress concentrates most sharply, and only later spread inward along the boundaries between metal grains.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["originate","propagate","accumulate","dissipate"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 균열이 '처음' 나타나는 위치(모서리)와 '나중에' 안쪽으로 퍼지는 과정을 대비하므로, 빈칸에는 '시작되다'라는 뜻의 A가 들어가야 한다. B는 균열을 다룰 때 자주 쓰이는 단어지만 '퍼지다'라는 뜻이어서, 퍼짐은 나중 단계라는 'only later spread' 부분과 맞지 않는다. C는 응력이 모서리에 집중된다는 점과 어울려 보이지만, 처음 생겨나는 미세 균열을 '쌓인다'고 표현하는 것은 정확하지 않다. D는 '흩어져 사라지다'라는 뜻이어서 균열이 생겨나고 자란다는 흐름과 반대된다.","explanationEn":"The text contrasts where the cracks first appear (the corners) with how they later spread inward, so the blank needs a word meaning \"begin,\" which makes A correct. B is a common word for cracks, but it means \"spread,\" and the text saves spreading for the later stage (\"only later spread\"). C might seem to fit because stress concentrates at the corners, but saying the first tiny cracks \"pile up\" there doesn't precisely describe how they start. D means \"fade away,\" which is the opposite of cracks forming and growing.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.608Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"physical science — Solder joint fatigue crack initiation and propagation under thermal cycling stress conditions","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 A 검산: 'first microscopic cracks', 'do not appear at random. Instead... at the corners', 'only later spread inward'의 대비 구조상 '시작되다(originate)'가 유일하게 논리적. B propagate는 균열 관련 전문어로 매력적이지만 '퍼지다'는 later 단계와 충돌해 배제됨(강한 오답). C accumulate는 응력 집중과 연결돼 부분적 그럴듯함을 가지나 미세 균열의 최초 발생을 기술하기엔 부정확. D dissipate는 반대 의미로 말은 되나 명확히 배제. 두 단계 판단(시간 대비 파악 + propagate와의 변별) 요구로 medium 적합. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 글자 참조 일치, 결론 동일, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 선택지 뒤 '<- 정답' 표기는 감사용 메타 표기로 판단. 지문은 가상의 연구자를 사용한 창작 지문으로 저작권 우려 없음. 열팽창 계수 차이로 인한 솔더 접합부 응력·모서리 응력 집중·입계 균열 전파는 사실관계상 타당."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"'first cracks'와 'only later spread'의 대비를 읽어야 하고, propagate(균열 관련 용어)와 accumulate(응력 집중)가 그럴듯한 오답 역할을 해 medium에 적합하다. dissipate는 비교적 쉽게 배제된다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-words_in_context-m-220","intendedSkill":"words_in_context","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-words_in_context-m-221","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Words in Context","difficulty":"medium","skill":"words_in_context","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"A quartz crystal used in a wristwatch is cut so that it vibrates at 32,768 times per second when voltage is applied, a property known as piezoelectric resonance. This frequency is not perfectly fixed, however: as temperature rises or falls, the crystal's vibration rate drifts slightly. Engineers designing precision clocks for laboratories therefore enclose the crystal in a small heated chamber that holds its temperature steady, a technique that does not remove the crystal's sensitivity to heat but ______ its effects, keeping the frequency stable enough that the clock loses less than a second over many years.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["eliminates","neutralizes","intensifies","reveals"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 가열 챔버가 수정의 열 민감성 자체를 '없애지는 않지만' 그 영향을 막아 주파수를 안정시킨다고 말하므로, 영향을 상쇄해 무력화한다는 B(neutralizes)가 정답이다. A(eliminates)는 효과를 줄인다는 방향은 맞아 보이지만, 'does not remove ... but' 구조에서 '제거하다'는 앞 절과 같은 의미라 대조가 성립하지 않는다. C(intensifies)는 온도 변화가 영향을 준다는 점과는 연결되지만, 주파수를 안정시킨다는 결과와 반대된다. D(reveals)는 실험실 맥락에선 그럴듯하지만, 영향을 드러내는 것은 시계 안정성을 설명하지 못한다.","explanationEn":"The text says the heated chamber does not remove the crystal's sensitivity to heat, yet it keeps the frequency stable. So the chamber must cancel out the effects of that sensitivity, which makes B (neutralizes) correct. A (eliminates) points the right way, but it means the same thing as \"remove,\" so the \"does not remove ... but\" contrast falls apart. C (intensifies) ties in with the idea that temperature affects the crystal, but it contradicts the stable frequency. D (reveals) sounds natural in a lab setting, but showing the effects would not explain why the clock stays accurate.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.608Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"physical science — Quartz oscillator frequency stability and piezoelectric resonance in precision timekeeping applications","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B(neutralizes)는 '민감성은 남지만 영향을 상쇄한다'는 문맥에 가장 정밀하게 부합한다. 다만 A(eliminates)가 '그 영향을 제거한다'로 읽혀 상당히 변론 가능한 수준이어서 정답 유일성이 다소 약하다(지문 말미의 미세 오차 언급이 유일한 배제 근거). C·D는 명확한 오답. 수정 발진 32,768 Hz, 항온조(OCXO) 기법 등 사실 관계는 정확. 형식 양호."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B가 가장 적절하다. A는 그럴듯한 오답으로 비교 판단이 필요해 medium 난이도에 맞는다. 다만 A를 배제하는 근거는 '오차가 남는다'는 점, 즉 완전 제거라는 과장을 짚는 쪽으로 보강하는 것이 바람직하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-words_in_context-m-221","intendedSkill":"words_in_context","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-words_in_context-m-222","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Words in Context","difficulty":"medium","skill":"words_in_context","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In a ferromagnetic crystal such as cobalt, the magnetization does not point in just any direction with equal ease. Because of interactions between electron orbitals and the crystal lattice, certain crystallographic axes, called \"easy axes,\" require less energy to magnetize along than others. This energy difference, known as magnetocrystalline anisotropy, means that in the absence of an external field, the magnetization of each domain will tend to ______ one of these easy axes, settling there rather than wandering among the many orientations that the lattice permits but does not favor.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["rotate away from","fluctuate around","align with","be indifferent to"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 쉬운 축이 자화에 필요한 에너지가 적어서 자화가 그 축에 \"자리 잡는다(settling there)\"고 말하므로, 자화가 쉬운 축과 같은 방향을 향한다는 뜻의 C가 정답이다. A는 회전이라는 물리적 움직임은 맞지만 방향이 반대라서, 에너지가 낮은 축에서 멀어진다는 의미가 된다. B는 쉬운 축 근처에 머문다는 점은 일부 맞지만, 계속 흔들린다는 뜻이 이어지는 \"settling there rather than wandering\"과 충돌한다. D는 자화 방향이 어느 쪽이든 쉽지 않다는 첫 문장과 정면으로 모순된다.","explanationEn":"The text says easy axes take less energy to magnetize along and that the magnetization ends up \"settling there,\" so it must point along an easy axis. That makes C the answer. A does involve rotation, but it goes the wrong way: it would move the magnetization away from the low-energy direction. B partly works because it keeps the magnetization near the easy axis, but constant fluctuation clashes with \"settling there rather than wandering.\" D directly contradicts the opening claim that magnetization does not point in just any direction with equal ease.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.608Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"physical science — Magnetocrystalline anisotropy energy and preferred magnetization direction in ferromagnetic materials","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 C 검산 완료: \"require less energy to magnetize along\" + \"settling there rather than wandering\"의 두 단서를 연결해야 하며, B(근처에 머묾)와 A(회전 동작)는 부분적 근거가 있어 비교가 필요하고 D도 훑어 읽으면 그럴듯함. 자기결정 이방성·쉬운 축 설명은 물리적으로 타당(코발트는 단축 이방성이지만 \"such as\"로 일반 서술이므로 오류 아님). 영어 해설은 한국어 해설과 같은 결론·글자 참조를 가지며 한글 없음. 한국어 해설의 첫 문장 요약 표현만 소폭 부정확."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B만 실질적으로 경쟁력 있는 오답이고, A와 D는 비교적 쉽게 배제된다. 다만 \"settling there rather than wandering\"을 근거로 B를 배제해야 하므로 두 단계 판단이 필요해 medium으로는 적합하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-words_in_context-m-222","intendedSkill":"words_in_context","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-words_in_context-m-223","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Words in Context","difficulty":"medium","skill":"words_in_context","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Because glass bends short wavelengths of light more sharply than long ones, a single lens brings blue and red light to focus at slightly different points, fringing images with color. In the 1750s, optician John Dollond found that pairing a converging lens of crown glass with a weaker diverging lens of flint glass, whose dispersion is much greater, could largely solve the problem: the flint element spreads colors in the opposite direction by just enough to ______ the crown element's color error, while still leaving the pair with enough overall bending power to form an image.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["magnify","reveal","replicate","offset"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"플린트 렌즈는 색을 '반대 방향'으로 퍼뜨려 크라운 렌즈의 색수차를 '대부분 해결'하므로, 오차를 상쇄한다는 D가 정답이다. A는 '렌즈가 확대한다'는 광학적 연상과는 맞지만, 오차를 키우면 문제가 해결되지 않는다. B는 오차가 드러난다는 의미여서 과학 맥락과는 어울리지만, 반대 방향 분산이 하는 일인 교정을 나타내지 못한다. C는 같은 오차를 다시 만든다는 뜻이라 '반대 방향'과 모순된다.","explanationEn":"The flint lens spreads colors \"in the opposite direction,\" and this \"largely solves\" the problem, so it must cancel out the crown lens's color error. That makes D the answer. A fits the general idea that lenses magnify things, but magnifying the error would make the problem worse. B suggests the error is exposed, which sounds scientific but doesn't describe a correction. C means reproducing the same error, which contradicts \"opposite direction.\"","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.608Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"physical science — Chromatic aberration correction in optical systems through lens element material selection","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"'opposite direction' + 'largely solve' 두 단서를 연결하면 '상쇄(offset)'가 유일한 정답. 돌런드 색지움 렌즈(크라운 수렴+플린트 발산, 플린트의 큰 분산) 서술은 사실과 부합. 오답 A(렌즈=확대 연상), B(과학적 어조)는 표면적 매력이 있어 비교 필요하나 정독 시 명확히 배제됨. 한·영 해설 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 수정 불필요."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"Dollond의 무색수차 렌즈(1758)에 관한 서술은 사실에 맞음. 'opposite direction'과 'largely solve'라는 단서를 연결해야 풀리고, magnify(렌즈 연상)와 reveal 같은 그럴듯한 오답이 있어 medium에 적합함.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-words_in_context-m-223","intendedSkill":"words_in_context","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-words_in_context-m-225","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Words in Context","difficulty":"medium","skill":"words_in_context","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"When liquid helium-4 is cooled below about 2.17 kelvins, part of it becomes a superfluid, a quantum state in which the liquid flows with no measurable viscosity. Experimenters have found that this superfluid can pass through channels so narrow that ordinary liquids, and even gases, are blocked entirely. Yet the same liquid does not behave this way under every condition: if it is forced to move faster than a certain critical velocity, small swirling vortices form and friction comes back. The superfluid's ability to flow without resistance is therefore ______: it holds only while the flow stays below that speed limit.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["immeasurable","conditional","temporary","exaggerated"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"콜론 뒤 문장은 저항 없는 흐름이 유속이 임계 속도보다 낮을 '때만' 유지된다고 설명하므로, 그 능력이 특정 조건에 달려 있다는 뜻의 B \"conditional\"이 정답이다. A \"immeasurable\"은 지문의 'no measurable viscosity'와 표현이 비슷해 끌리지만, 측정할 수 없는 것은 점성이지 흐르는 능력이 아니고 속도 한계라는 내용과도 맞지 않는다. C \"temporary\"는 그 성질이 사라질 수 있다는 점은 맞지만, 지문은 시간이 지나서가 아니라 속도 조건 때문에 사라진다고 말하므로 정확하지 않다. D \"exaggerated\"는 그 능력이 과장되었다는 뜻이 되는데, 지문은 실험으로 확인된 사실이라고 말하며 범위가 제한될 뿐이라고 하므로 맞지 않다.","explanationEn":"The sentence after the colon says resistance-free flow holds \"only while\" the flow stays below a critical speed, so the ability depends on a condition. That makes B, \"conditional,\" the answer. A, \"immeasurable,\" may tempt you because the text mentions \"no measurable viscosity,\" but it's the viscosity that can't be measured, not the ability, and the word ignores the speed limit. C, \"temporary,\" gets right that the property can disappear, but the text ties its loss to speed, not to the passing of time. D, \"exaggerated,\" would mean the ability has been overstated, yet the text treats it as confirmed by experiments and only limited in scope.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.608Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"physical science — Superfluid helium quantum fluid properties and zero viscosity flow phenomena near absolute zero","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"콜론 뒤 'only while ... below that speed limit'가 조건을 명시하므로 B가 유일하게 정확. A는 'no measurable viscosity'와의 표면적 유사성으로 유인, C는 성질이 사라진다는 점에서 부분적으로 타당하나 시간 vs 조건의 구분이 필요, D도 문맥상 말이 됨. 물리 사실(람다점 2.17K, 초유체 누출, 임계속도·양자 소용돌이) 정확. 한·영 해설 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"사실관계(He-4 람다점 약 2.17 K, 임계 속도 초과 시 양자 소용돌이 생성)가 정확하다. temporary와 immeasurable 오답은 부분적으로 그럴듯해 보이는 함정이라 medium 난이도에 맞다. 다만 exaggerated는 비교적 쉽게 배제된다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-words_in_context-m-225","intendedSkill":"words_in_context","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-229","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"medium","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- Composite laminates are made by stacking thin layers, or plies, of strong fibers held in a polymer matrix.\n- Delamination is a failure in which neighboring plies separate from one another.\n- In one common pathway, small cracks first form in the matrix within a ply when the laminate is bent or struck.\n- These matrix cracks grow until they reach the boundary between plies, where they turn and run along the layer interface.\n- Delamination spreads more easily when the bond between the fibers and the surrounding matrix is weak.\n- Engineers sometimes stitch plies together with through-thickness fibers to slow delamination.","question":"The student wants to explain the sequence by which delamination develops in a laminate. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Delamination, in which neighboring plies separate, spreads more easily when the bond between the fibers and the surrounding matrix is weak.","Delamination can begin with small matrix cracks inside a ply that grow until they reach the boundary between plies and then turn to run along that interface.","Delamination, a separation of neighboring plies, can be slowed when engineers stitch the plies together with through-thickness fibers.","Delamination occurs in composite laminates, which are made by stacking plies of strong fibers held in a polymer matrix."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"목표는 박리가 어떤 순서로 진행되는지 설명하는 것이다. B는 기지 균열이 생기고, 층 경계까지 자라고, 그다음 경계면을 따라 방향을 트는 단계를 차례대로 제시하므로 목표를 이룬다. A는 박리를 더 쉽게 만드는 조건(약한 섬유-기지 결합)을 말할 뿐 진행 순서는 다루지 않는다. C는 박리를 늦추는 방법을 말하고, D는 적층판의 구조만 설명하므로 둘 다 과정의 순서를 보여 주지 못한다.","explanationEn":"Your goal is to explain the order in which delamination develops. B does this: it lays out the stages in sequence, with matrix cracks forming, growing to the ply boundary, and then turning to run along the interface. A gives a condition that helps delamination spread (a weak fiber-matrix bond), but it doesn't describe any sequence. C describes a way to slow delamination, and D only describes how laminates are built, so neither one shows the steps of the process.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.608Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"physical science — Composite laminate delamination failure through matrix cracking and fiber-matrix interface weakness","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 B가 노트 3·4번의 단계(기지 균열 발생 → 층 경계까지 성장 → 경계면을 따라 진행)를 순서대로 정확히 종합함. A는 '확산(spreads)'이라는 발전 관련 어휘로 부분적 매력을 갖고, D는 박리 발생 맥락(적층 구조)을 언급해 비교가 필요하며, C도 노트 기반으로 말이 됨. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 B를 일관되게 뒷받침하고 선택지 글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 복합재 박리 메커니즘 서술도 공학적으로 타당. 난이도는 표준 SAT 수사적 종합 중간 수준에 부합(다소 쉬운 편에 가까운 경계선)."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["too_easy","eliminated:3"],"note":"'sequence' 목표에 맞는 단계 서술은 B뿐이라 키워드만 맞춰도 바로 풀린다. A·C·D는 모두 순서 요소가 전혀 없어 부분 근거를 갖춘 오답이 없다. 예를 들어 순서를 일부만 담거나 순서가 틀린 오답이 없으므로 medium 기준(오답 2개 이상이 비교를 요구할 것)에 못 미친다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-229","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-230","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"medium","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- Some organic compounds glow after absorbing light; this glow can take two forms, fluorescence and phosphorescence.\n- In fluorescence, an excited molecule returns from a singlet state to its ground state, emitting light within nanoseconds.\n- In phosphorescence, the excited molecule first crosses into a triplet state, from which the return to the ground state is \"spin-forbidden\" and therefore slow.\n- As a result, phosphorescent emission can persist for milliseconds to several seconds after the light source is removed.\n- In 2015, chemist Zhenguo Chi and colleagues reported organic crystals whose afterglow lasted more than a second at room temperature.\n- Oxygen and molecular vibrations can drain energy from triplet states, so many organic compounds phosphoresce only when frozen or tightly packed.","question":"The student wants to explain why the light from the second type of emission lingers longer than the light from the first. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Fluorescent emission occurs within nanoseconds, whereas phosphorescent emission can last for milliseconds to several seconds after the light source is removed.","Because oxygen and molecular vibrations can drain energy from triplet states, many organic compounds phosphoresce only when frozen or tightly packed.","Because phosphorescent molecules must return to the ground state from a triplet state, a \"spin-forbidden\" and therefore slow process, their glow persists far beyond fluorescence's nanosecond-scale emission.","In 2015, Zhenguo Chi and colleagues reported organic crystals whose phosphorescent afterglow lasted more than a second at room temperature, much longer than typical fluorescence."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"목표는 인광이 형광보다 오래 지속되는 '이유'를 설명하는 것이다. C는 삼중항 상태에서 바닥 상태로의 복귀가 스핀 금지되어 느리다는 메커니즘(원인)과 형광의 나노초 방출을 연결해 이유를 제시한다. A는 두 방출의 지속 시간 차이를 정확히 대조하지만 왜 그런지는 설명하지 않는다. B는 인광이 약해지는 조건을 다룰 뿐 지속 시간 차이의 원인이 아니다. D는 긴 잔광의 구체적 사례를 들지만 역시 원인을 설명하지 않는다.","explanationEn":"Your goal is to explain why phosphorescence lasts longer than fluorescence, so the answer has to give a cause. C does this: it names the mechanism (the return from the triplet state is \"spin-forbidden\" and therefore slow) and links it to the gap with fluorescence's nanosecond emission. A correctly contrasts the two durations, but it only describes the difference and never explains it. B covers the conditions under which phosphorescence gets weakened, which is not the reason for the longer duration. D gives a striking example of a long afterglow, but an example is not an explanation of the cause.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.608Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"physical science — Phosphorescence delayed light emission and triplet state relaxation in organic luminescent compounds","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"목표(이유 설명)에 맞는 유일한 선택지는 C(삼중항→바닥 상태 복귀가 스핀 금지·느림 → 지속). A는 지속 시간 대조만(원인 없음), D는 사례만, B는 인광이 억제되는 조건으로 목표와 무관. 노트 내용(단일항/삼중항, 스핀 금지, 산소·진동에 의한 소광)은 화학적으로 정확하며 2015 Chi 그룹의 실온 유기 인광 결정 보고도 실제 사실과 부합. 한·영 해설 모두 C를 일관되게 뒷받침하고 선택지 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. A·D가 부분적으로 그럴듯해 '무엇'과 '왜'를 구분해야 하므로 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"'second type'를 인광으로 연결하는 단계와 원인 대 기술 구분이 필요하다. A와 D는 부분적으로 맞는 매력적 오답이다. B는 'Because'로 인과 형식을 갖췄지만 엉뚱한 원인을 제시한다. 중간 난이도에 적합하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-rhetorical_synthesis-m-230","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-e-231","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"easy","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"When a slice of cucumber is placed in salty water, it soon becomes limp. This change is caused by osmosis, the movement of water across a semipermeable membrane, a barrier that lets water pass through but blocks many dissolved substances, such as salt. Water tends to move from the side where dissolved substances are less concentrated to the side where they are more concentrated. __Because the salty water outside the cucumber's cells holds more dissolved salt than the fluid inside them, water flows out of the cells, and the slice loses its firmness.__ The same process works in reverse when a wilted stalk of celery is placed in plain water and becomes crisp again.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It introduces a new process that differs from the one defined earlier in the text.","It describes an exception to the general pattern of water movement stated earlier in the text.","It presents a claim about cucumbers that the following sentence calls into question.","It uses the general principle stated earlier in the text to account for the change described in the first sentence."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 앞에서 설명한 원리(물은 용질 농도가 낮은 쪽에서 높은 쪽으로 이동한다)를 적용해 첫 문장의 현상(오이 조각이 흐물흐물해지는 것)이 왜 일어나는지 설명하므로 D가 정답이다. A는 틀렸다. 밑줄 문장은 새로운 과정이 아니라 앞서 정의한 삼투를 그대로 다룬다. B도 틀렸다. 물의 이동이 일반 규칙을 그대로 따르므로 예외가 아니다. C도 틀렸다. 다음 문장은 같은 과정이 반대 방향으로도 일어남을 보여 줄 뿐, 밑줄 문장에 의문을 제기하지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence takes the rule given earlier (water moves toward the side with more dissolved substances) and uses it to explain why the cucumber slice goes limp, the change described in the first sentence, so D is correct. A is wrong because the sentence doesn't introduce a new process; it's still talking about osmosis, which was already defined. B is wrong because the water moves just as the general rule predicts, so this isn't an exception. C is wrong because the next sentence shows the same process working in reverse, and it doesn't challenge the underlined sentence at all.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.608Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"D","seed":"physical science — Osmosis water transport mechanism across semipermeable membranes driven by solute concentration gradient","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"지문은 원리 제시 → 적용(밑줄) → 역방향 사례의 명확한 구조. 밑줄 문장은 \"Because...\" 로 앞의 일반 원리를 첫 문장의 현상에 적용하므로 D가 유일한 정답. A(새 과정), B(예외), C(다음 문장이 반박)는 구조를 알면 즉시 배제되지만 그럴듯한 전형적 오답. 삼투 설명은 과학적으로 정확. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 일치하고 자연스러움. 오리지널 지문으로 저작권 우려 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"원리를 사례에 적용하는 기능이 지문에 직접 드러나며, 오답은 전형적 오개념(새 과정, 예외, 반박)이다. 과학적 서술도 정확하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-e-231","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-cross_text_connections-e-232","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Cross-Text Connections","difficulty":"easy","skill":"cross_text_connections","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Text 1\nMetamaterials are engineered structures built from tiny repeating units, such as metal rings and wires, arranged in patterns. Because these units resonate with incoming waves, some metamaterials bend light in the \"wrong\" direction, giving them a negative refractive index. Many writers predict that such materials will soon make practical invisibility cloaks for everyday objects.\n\nText 2\nNegative refraction in metamaterials is real and well tested, but it usually works only in a narrow band of wavelengths, near the frequency where the structures resonate. Outside that band, the effect fades, and the materials also absorb much of the energy passing through them. For now, a cloak that hides an object from ordinary visible light, which spans many wavelengths, remains far beyond reach.","question":"Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the prediction described in Text 1?","options":["By arguing that the prediction is too hopeful because the effect it depends on works only over a limited range of wavelengths","By arguing that the prediction is mistaken because metamaterials have never actually been shown to bend light in a negative direction","By arguing that the prediction is too cautious because metamaterials already hide objects from all kinds of visible light","By arguing that the prediction is irrelevant because metamaterials are made from natural crystals rather than engineered units"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"Text 2는 음의 굴절이 실제로 있다고 인정하지만, 공명 주파수 근처의 좁은 파장대에서만 작동하므로 가시광선 전체를 가리는 투명 망토는 아직 먼 이야기라고 말한다. 따라서 Text 1의 예측이 지나치게 낙관적이라고 볼 것이므로 A가 정답이다. B는 Text 2가 이 효과를 '실제로 있고 충분히 검증되었다'고 한 것과 어긋난다. C는 Text 2의 조심스러운 태도와 정반대이다. D는 메타물질이 인공 구조물이라는 두 지문의 설명과 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"Text 2 agrees that negative refraction is real, but it says the effect works only in a narrow band of wavelengths near resonance, so a cloak for visible light, which covers many wavelengths, is still far off. That means the author would see Text 1's prediction as too hopeful, so A is correct. B is wrong because Text 2 says the effect is \"real and well tested.\" C is wrong because it's the opposite of Text 2's cautious view. D is wrong because both texts describe metamaterials as engineered structures, not natural crystals.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.608Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"A","seed":"physical science — Metamaterial negative refractive index engineering through structural resonance and wave manipulation","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"Text 2 explicitly concedes negative refraction is \"real and well tested\" but limited to a narrow wavelength band, making a visible-light cloak \"far beyond reach\" — directly supports A. B contradicts \"real and well tested\"; C reverses Text 2's stance; D contradicts both texts' description of engineered units. Single-step inference with explicit textual cues; distractors are plausible misreadings (overlooking the concession, inverting tone, confusing natural vs. engineered). Korean and English explanations align in conclusion and letter references; English is natural and contains no Hangul. Original, non-copyrighted content; science is accurate."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"정답 A는 지문에 직접 근거가 있다. C와 D는 다소 쉽게 배제되지만 easy 난이도로는 적합하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-cross_text_connections-e-232","intendedSkill":"cross_text_connections","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-words_in_context-e-233","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Words in Context","difficulty":"easy","skill":"words_in_context","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"When certain crystals such as quartz are crushed or split, they give off brief flashes of light, an effect called triboluminescence. Because these flashes appear only at the moment a crystal breaks, engineers at some mining plants have placed light sensors inside grinding machines. The faint glow the sensors detect is a ______ sign that rock is actually being fractured, letting operators confirm that the machines are working as intended without stopping them to look inside.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["misleading","reliable","decorative","delayed"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 빛이 결정이 깨지는 순간에만 나타난다고 하고, 운영자가 이 빛으로 기계가 제대로 작동하는지 확인한다고 말한다. 그러므로 이 빛은 파쇄가 일어나고 있음을 믿을 수 있게 알려 주는 신호이며, B가 정답이다. A는 빛이 정확한 확인 수단으로 쓰인다는 내용과 반대된다. C는 '장식적'이라는 뜻으로, 빛이 감시라는 실용적 목적에 쓰인다는 내용과 맞지 않는다. D는 빛이 파쇄 순간에 바로 나타난다는 설명과 어긋난다.","explanationEn":"The passage says the flashes appear only at the moment a crystal breaks, and operators use them to confirm that the machines are working. That means the glow is a dependable sign that fracturing is happening, so B is correct. A doesn't fit because the glow is used to confirm things accurately, not to mislead anyone. C means \"ornamental,\" but the light has a practical monitoring purpose. D contradicts the point that the flashes show up right when the rock breaks.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.608Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"B","seed":"physical science — Triboluminescence light emission from mechanical fracture of crystalline minerals and industrial grinding application monitoring","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"정답 B 검증: \"appear only at the moment a crystal breaks\" + \"letting operators confirm\" → 믿을 수 있는 신호 = reliable. 오답 A(반대), C(실용적 용도와 불일치), D(즉시성과 모순)는 모두 지문 단서로 바로 배제되며, 단서가 명시적이고 한 단계 추론으로 해결 가능해 easy에 적합. 한국어·영어 해설 결론 및 선택지 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 트라이보루미네선스(석영 파쇄 시 발광) 사실 관계 문제 없음. 원문 지문으로 보이며 저작권 의심 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"'only at the moment a crystal breaks'와 'confirm'이라는 직접 단서로 한 단계 추론하면 reliable이 나온다. 다만 decorative 선택지는 그럴듯함이 약간 떨어진다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sw-words_in_context-e-233","intendedSkill":"words_in_context","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-234","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Engineers have long been intrigued by the idea of embedding piezoelectric materials beneath road surfaces. These crystals and ceramics generate a small electric charge when they are squeezed, so every passing car could, in principle, become a tiny power source. Early field trials seemed promising: sensors installed under a busy highway lane in Israel produced measurable current with each axle that rolled over them. Yet when researchers at several universities compared the output of such systems with their installation and maintenance costs, the picture changed. A single lane fitted with piezoelectric modules typically yields only enough electricity to run a few streetlights, and the modules tend to crack under years of heavy loads, requiring replacement long before they repay their expense. For this reason, many engineers now argue that the technology is best suited not to supplying the power grid but to powering the very sensors that monitor traffic and pavement conditions, devices that need only trickles of energy and would otherwise depend on batteries.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Field trials of piezoelectric pavements have shown that the technology produces more electricity on busy highways than engineers originally expected.","Piezoelectric pavements generate power efficiently, but the modules must be redesigned so that they no longer crack under heavy vehicle loads.","Piezoelectric pavements appear too costly to serve as a major electricity source, so their most practical use may be supplying small amounts of power to roadside monitoring devices.","Piezoelectric pavements should replace batteries in streetlights, since a single lane can generate enough electricity to light an entire highway."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 글은 압전 도로가 비용 대비 발전량이 적어 전력망 공급에는 부적합하며, 적은 에너지만 필요한 교통·노면 센서 전원으로 쓰는 것이 가장 적합하다는 주장으로 마무리되므로 C가 정답이다. A는 초기 실험이 유망했다는 세부 내용만 반영했고, 예상보다 많았다는 내용은 글에 없다. B는 균열 문제를 언급하지만 글은 발전 효율이 좋다고 말하지 않으며 재설계를 결론으로 제시하지도 않는다. D는 가로등과 배터리를 언급하지만 한 차로는 가로등 몇 개분의 전력만 낸다는 글의 내용과 모순된다.","explanationEn":"The text ends by arguing that because piezoelectric pavements produce little power relative to their cost, they are best used to power low-energy traffic and pavement sensors instead of supplying the grid, so C is correct. A builds on the detail that early trials looked promising, but the text never says the output was higher than expected. B mentions the cracking problem, but the text doesn't say the pavements generate power efficiently, and it doesn't conclude that the modules need to be redesigned. D brings up streetlights and batteries, but it contradicts the text, which says that one lane powers only a few streetlights.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.608Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"technology and engineering — Piezoelectric energy harvesting in roadway pavements converting vehicle vibration to electrical power storage","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 C는 글의 양보 구조(유망한 초기 실험 → 비용 대비 저출력·균열 → 센서 전원용이 최적)를 정확히 요약함. A는 '초기 실험 유망' 세부에, B는 '균열' 세부에 기대어 부분적 근거를 가지며, D는 가로등·배터리 어휘를 재활용하되 '가로등 몇 개분'과 모순되어 배제됨. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 결론과 선택지 참조가 일치하고 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 압전 도로 관련 사실(이스라엘 고속도로 시험, 저출력·내구성 문제, 센서 전원 활용 제안)은 일반적으로 알려진 내용과 부합. 난이도 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"C는 글의 전환(비용 대비 낮은 발전량)과 결론(저전력 센서용)을 모두 담고 있다. A와 B는 글의 세부 내용(초기 실험의 유망한 결과, 균열 문제)에 기대고 있어 비교해 봐야 배제된다. D는 명백히 틀렸지만 그럴듯하게 들린다. 난이도는 중간 수준에 맞다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-234","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-235","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Packaging made from mycelium, the threadlike root network of fungi, is often promoted as a direct substitute for polystyrene foam. To make it, manufacturers mix fungal spores with agricultural waste such as hemp stalks, let the mycelium bind the fibers into a mold-shaped mass over several days, and then heat the material to stop growth. The result decomposes in soil within weeks rather than centuries. Yet engineers note that the material absorbs moisture readily and is heavier than foam, and its multiday growing period makes rapid, high-volume production difficult. For these reasons, mycelium packaging has so far gained ground mainly in protecting sturdy, high-value goods such as wine bottles and electronics, where shipping volumes are modest and a company's environmental image justifies a higher cost per unit.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Mycelium packaging breaks down far faster than polystyrene foam, which is why it has displaced foam across most kinds of shipping.","Mycelium packaging is made by growing fungi on agricultural waste, a process engineers have recently shortened so that it can match foam production.","Mycelium packaging is too heavy and moisture-sensitive to be practical, so companies that adopt it do so only to improve their public image.","Mycelium packaging offers a clear environmental benefit, but its physical and production limits have so far confined it to particular uses rather than making it a general foam replacement."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 균사체 포장재가 몇 주 만에 분해된다는 장점을 소개한 뒤, 흡습성·무게·긴 성장 기간이라는 한계 때문에 고가·소량 제품에만 주로 쓰인다고 말하므로 D가 정답이다. A는 빠른 분해라는 사실은 맞지만 대부분의 운송에서 폼을 대체했다는 내용은 지문과 반대이다. B는 제조 과정 설명은 맞지만, 성장 기간이 단축되었다는 내용은 지문에 없고 오히려 성장 기간이 한계로 제시된다. C는 단점과 이미지 요소를 언급하지만 '비실용적'이라거나 '이미지 때문에만'이라고 과장하여 실제 쓰이는 틈새 용도를 무시한다.","explanationEn":"The text first presents mycelium packaging's advantage (it decomposes in weeks) and then explains how moisture absorption, weight, and slow growth have limited it mostly to sturdy, high-value goods, so D is correct. A gets the fast decomposition right, but the text says the material has not replaced foam widely, which is the opposite of what A claims. B describes the manufacturing process correctly, but the text never says growth time has been shortened; it actually treats the slow growth as a limitation. C picks up on the drawbacks and the image factor, but it overstates them by calling the material impractical and saying image is the only reason, which ignores the niche where the material genuinely works.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.608Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"technology and engineering — Mycelium-based biodegradable packaging material grown from fungal networks replacing petroleum plastics","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"D correctly synthesizes the benefit + limits + niche-use structure. A (fast decomposition true, \"displaced foam\" false), B (process true, \"shortened\" fabricated), C (drawbacks/image true but overstated) each have partial textual grounding and require comparison; requires linking benefit, limitations, and resulting niche. Mycelium packaging facts (hemp substrate, heat to stop growth, moisture absorption, wine/electronics use) are accurate. Original text, no copyright concern. Explanations in both languages are consistent, accurate, and natural."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"D가 장점+한계+틈새 용도를 종합함. A·B는 부분적으로 맞는 근거가 있고 C는 과장형 오답으로 그럴듯함. D가 가장 길고 종합적이어서 다소 눈에 띄지만 medium 난이도로 적절함.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-central_ideas_details-m-235","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-238","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"For decades, engineers building aircraft fuselages avoided welding high-strength aluminum alloys, because melting these metals and letting them resolidify tends to leave brittle, porous seams. Instead, panels were joined with thousands of rivets, which add weight and create holes where cracks can begin. Friction stir welding, developed in the early 1990s, offered an alternative: a rotating tool is plunged into the joint line and dragged along it, generating enough frictional heat to soften the metal so that the tool can stir the two edges together. __Crucially, the metal never reaches its melting point, so the seam cools without forming the gas pockets and coarse crystal structures that weaken conventionally welded aluminum.__ As a result, several aerospace manufacturers now use the process to join large fuselage sections, reducing both part counts and overall weight.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It describes a limitation of friction stir welding that has prevented manufacturers from abandoning rivets entirely.","It explains the mechanical steps by which the rotating tool moves along the joint line to combine the panels.","It identifies why the new process avoids the defect that had long discouraged welding these alloys, setting up its adoption.","It contrasts the weight savings of friction stir welding with the added weight of riveted fuselage panels."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 금속이 녹지 않으므로 기존 용접의 결함(기공, 거친 결정)이 생기지 않는다고 설명하며, 이는 첫 문장의 문제(취약하고 다공성인 이음매)에 대한 해결 근거이고 다음 문장의 채택(As a result)으로 이어진다. 따라서 C가 정답이다. A는 한계를 말한다고 하지만 문장은 장점을 제시한다. B는 공구의 작동 과정을 다룬 앞 문장의 기능이다. D의 무게 비교는 리벳 설명과 마지막 문장의 내용이지 밑줄 문장의 역할이 아니다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence explains that because the metal never melts, the seam avoids the gas pockets and coarse crystals that weaken conventional welds. That answers the problem raised in the first sentence (brittle, porous seams), and it leads into the adoption described next (\"As a result\"), so C is correct. A is wrong because the sentence presents an advantage, not a limitation. B describes what the previous sentence does, since that's where the tool's motion is explained. D is wrong because the weight comparison comes from the rivet discussion and the final sentence, not from the underlined sentence.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.608Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"technology and engineering — Friction stir welding technique joining aluminum alloys without melting for aerospace fuselage construction","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 '녹지 않음 → 기공·거친 결정 없음'으로 첫 문장의 문제(취약·다공성 이음매)를 해결하는 이유를 제시하고 'As a result'로 채택을 뒷받침하므로 C가 정확. A는 장점을 한계로 뒤집은 오답, B는 앞 문장 기능, D는 리벳 설명·마지막 문장 내용으로 지문에 근거가 있어 비교가 필요함. 해설(한/영) 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 마찰교반용접 1991년 TWI 개발, 고강도 알루미늄 용융용접 기피 등 사실 관계 문제 없음. 두 정보(문제 제기+결과 연결)를 묶어야 하는 구조로 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"오답 B·D는 지문 내 인접 정보를 차용해 그럴듯하고, A는 방향이 반대라서 쉽게 배제된다. 문장 간 연결(첫 문장의 문제 → 해결 → As a result)을 파악해야 하므로 medium에 적합하다. 마찰교반용접(FSW) 관련 사실(1991년 TWI 개발, 고상 접합)도 정확하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sw-text_structure_purpose-m-238","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-h-241","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"hard","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Perovskite solar cells can convert sunlight into electricity cheaply, but their efficiency depends heavily on the ratio of halide ions, such as iodide and bromide, in the crystal lattice. At a laboratory in Lausanne, materials chemist Hye-jin Park and her team spent two years adjusting that ratio in thin films deposited on glass substrates. Having tested more than four hundred compositions under simulated sunlight, ______ a mixture containing roughly 15 percent bromide that pushed power conversion efficiency above 24 percent while resisting the phase separation that usually degrades such films.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["the thin films revealed to Park's team","Park's team identified","the Lausanne laboratory produced for Park's team","the simulated sunlight helped Park's team identify"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"정답 B. 분사구문 \"Having tested more than four hundred compositions\"의 의미상 주어는 실제로 조성을 시험한 행위자, 즉 Park의 연구팀이다. 따라서 주절의 주어 자리에 \"Park's team\"이 와야 수식어가 매달리지 않는다(dangling modifier 방지).\nA: 앞 문장에 나오는 무생물 명사 thin films를 주어로 삼았다. 박막은 조성을 시험할 수 없으므로 수식어가 잘못 연결된다.\nC: 앞부분 배경에 나오는 장소 명사 Lausanne laboratory를 주어로 삼았다. 실험실은 장소일 뿐이고, 시험을 한 행위자는 아니다.\nD: 수식어구 바로 안에 나오는 simulated sunlight를 주어로 삼았다. Park's team이 문장에 들어 있기는 하지만 목적어 자리에 있어서, 문법상으로는 햇빛이 조성을 시험한 것이 된다.","explanationEn":"The answer is B. The opening modifier, \"Having tested more than four hundred compositions,\" has to describe whoever did the testing, and that is Park's team. So \"Park's team\" needs to be the subject of the main clause, or the modifier dangles.\nA makes the thin films the subject. The films are objects that got tested, so they can't be the ones testing.\nC makes the Lausanne laboratory the subject. That noun only gives the setting, and a lab is a place, not the one doing the testing.\nD makes the simulated sunlight the subject, which is the noun right next to the modifier. Park's team does appear in this choice, but only as an object. Grammatically, the sentence would then say the sunlight did the testing.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.608Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["dangling_modifier_subject_matching"],"note":"문두 분사구문 \"Having tested...\"의 의미상 주어는 실제 시험 행위자인 Park's team이며, B만이 이를 주절 주어로 둔다. A(thin films), C(Lausanne laboratory), D(simulated sunlight)는 모두 비행위자 명사를 주어로 삼아 dangling modifier를 만든다. 특히 D는 정답 명사 \"Park's team\"을 목적어 자리에 포함시켜 '명사의 존재'만 보고 고르는 수험생을 걸러내는 장치로, 문법적 주어 판별을 실제로 요구하므로 medium 이상. 체크리스트 3번은 오답 순서상 D가 인접 명사(simulated sunlight) 함정에 해당하며, 번호 순서는 다르나 기능적으로 충족. 해설은 각 오답의 오류 이유를 정확히 기술하고 모순 없음. 사실·저작권 문제 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["dangling_modifier_subject_matching"],"note":"오답 A, C, D에 모두 Park's team이 들어 있어 '팀이 보인다'는 이유만으로는 고를 수 없고, 문법상 주어 자리를 따로 확인해야 한다. 특히 D는 행위자 Park's team을 목적어 자리에 둔 함정이다. 다만 3번 항목은 느슨하게 충족한다. 수식어구 바로 옆 명사는 D의 simulated sunlight이고, A의 thin films는 앞 문장에 나오는 명사다. 그래도 전체적으로는 충족으로 본다. 어려움이 계산량에서 오는 것이 아니라 의미상 주체를 추적하는 데서 오므로 medium보다 다소 어렵다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"batch2-D-cross","gid":"sw-form_structure_sense-h-241","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":"form_structure_sense_dangling_modifier_agent_trace","recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":"recipe","difficultyStatus":"provisional_ai","review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-inferences-m-000","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Inferences","difficulty":"medium","skill":"inferences","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"The following text is adapted from a short story. Twelve-year-old Greta spends her summer afternoons at her grandfather's allotment garden in Berlin.\n\nAll July, Herr Brandt and Frau Kessler argued about the fence between their plots: whether it stood ten centimeters too high, whether the club rules allowed it, whether it threw a shadow across Frau Kessler's beans. They measured it with folding rulers, wrote letters to the committee, and read the bylaws aloud to anyone who would listen. Meanwhile, a tomato plant that nobody had planted had pushed up through a crack in the roof of Herr Brandt's shed and now hung heavy with red fruit above both their heads. Greta watched the two neighbors stand beneath it for an hour, pointing at the fence, and neither once looked up. She began to suspect that what the adults actually cared about was ______","question":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","options":["the dispute itself rather than anything the garden might actually produce.","the shade that the fence cast on Frau Kessler's crop of beans.","the unusual tomato plant, which they were secretly competing to claim.","the committee's rules, which they hoped to have rewritten that summer."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"이웃들은 몇 시간씩 울타리 문제로 다투면서도 머리 위에 열매가 주렁주렁 달린 토마토는 한 번도 올려다보지 않는다. 이 두 사실을 함께 보면, 그들이 진짜 신경 쓰는 것은 정원의 수확이 아니라 다툼 그 자체라는 결론이 나오므로 A가 정답이다. B는 지문에 나온 콩의 그늘 문제를 가져왔지만, 콩을 정말 걱정하는 사람이 눈앞의 열매를 무시한다는 점과 맞지 않는다. C는 두 사람이 토마토를 전혀 보지 않았다는 서술과 모순된다. D는 규정을 읽는 행동에 근거하지만, 규정을 바꾸려 한다는 내용은 지문에 없고 그레타가 관찰한 대비도 설명하지 못한다.","explanationEn":"The neighbors argue about the fence for hours, yet neither one looks up at the tomato plant full of ripe fruit hanging right above them. When you put those two facts together, it's clear they care about the argument itself, not about anything the garden grows, so A is correct. B uses the detail about shade on the beans, but someone who truly cared about crops wouldn't ignore ripe fruit right over their head. C contradicts the text, which says neither neighbor ever looked up at the tomato. D builds on the neighbors reading the bylaws aloud, but the text never says they want the rules changed, and that idea doesn't explain the contrast Greta notices.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.609Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Twelve-year-old Greta notices that her Berlin allotment neighbors spend hours arguing about fence height while ignoring the tomato plant that has spontaneously grown through the shed roof.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 A는 '울타리 논쟁에 몰두' + '머리 위 열매를 한 번도 보지 않음'이라는 두 정보를 연결해야 도출되는 추론으로 타당함. B(콩 그늘)와 D(규정 낭독)는 지문의 세부에 근거한 부분 정답형 오답이라 비교가 필요하고, C는 지문과 모순되지만 토마토를 언급해 그럴듯함. 지문은 원작 인용 흔적 없는 창작 각색으로 보임. 해설의 \"몇 시간씩/for hours\" 표현만 지문의 \"an hour\"와 미세하게 다름."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"울타리 다툼과 아무도 올려다보지 않은 토마토라는 두 단서를 연결해야 A가 나옴. B와 D는 지문 세부(콩 그늘, 규약 낭독)에 기대고 있어 그럴듯함. C는 비교적 쉽게 배제됨. 중간 난이도에 적합함.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-inferences-m-000","intendedSkill":"inferences","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-inferences-m-001","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Inferences","difficulty":"medium","skill":"inferences","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"On the dock at Húsavík, the January wind came off the bay sharp enough to numb Bjorn's fingers through his gloves, so he worked bare-handed, as his father did. The torn net lay across his knees. His father had shown him the knot only once: loop, pass under, draw tight until the mesh square matched its neighbors exactly. Bjorn had tied hundreds that morning, quickly, pleased with his speed. Then his father lifted the section to the light, and water-heavy gaps sagged open wherever Bjorn had pulled a knot unevenly. \"A cod finds the loose one,\" his father said, and handed the net back without another word. Bjorn untied every knot he had made. Working again, he counted each pass under his breath and measured each square against the one beside it before moving on. By dusk he had mended less than a third of what he had finished before noon, yet when he raised the net himself, he found that he ______","question":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","options":["could finally tie the knots as fast as his father had tied them earlier that day","was looking for uneven squares with the same eye his father had turned on his morning's work","regretted throwing away his morning's work, since most of those knots had been sound","was now sure his father would praise how much of the net he had finished"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"비욘은 오전에 속도를 자랑했지만 아버지가 그물을 빛에 비춰 처진 틈을 찾아냈고, 이후 비욘은 칸 하나하나를 옆 칸과 비교하며 묶었습니다. 그래서 그가 직접 그물을 들어 올렸다는 것은 아버지처럼 고르지 않은 칸을 살펴보는 눈을 갖게 되었다는 뜻이므로 B가 정답입니다. A는 오후에 작업한 양이 오전의 3분의 1도 안 되었다는 내용과 맞지 않습니다. C는 매듭이 고르지 않아 틈이 벌어졌다는 내용과 모순됩니다. D는 아버지가 작업한 양이 아니라 정확성을 중시했다는 점을 놓쳤습니다.","explanationEn":"In the morning Bjorn was proud of how fast he worked, but his father held the net up to the light and found the gaps where knots were pulled unevenly. After that, Bjorn checked each square against the one next to it. So when he lifts the net himself, the logical conclusion is that he now inspects it the way his father did, which is choice B. Choice A doesn't fit, because he finished less than a third as much by dusk, so he hadn't gotten faster. Choice C contradicts the text, which says the morning's knots left gaps. Choice D misses the point that his father cared about precision, not how much got done.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.609Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Bjorn, a fishing boat captain's son, learns to mend nets on an Icelandic winter dock, each knot requiring a precision that exposes his previous carelessness.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 B는 '아버지가 그물을 빛에 비춰 살핌' → '비욘이 직접 그물을 들어 올림'이라는 두 장면의 연결과 'yet'의 대조(양은 줄었으나 눈을 얻음)를 읽어야 도출되어 medium에 적합. A·D는 '3분의 1도 못 미침'으로 배제되고, C는 지문의 분위기·결과와 어긋남. 다만 A는 '아버지가 그날 매듭을 묶었다'는 전제 자체가 지문에 없어 다소 약한 오답. 창작 지문으로 저작권 문제 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"B는 아버지가 그물을 빛에 비춰 살핀 장면과 비욘이 칸마다 옆 칸과 비교한 장면을 연결해야 고를 수 있으므로 타당한 추론입니다. A와 D는 비교적 쉽게 배제되고, C는 그럴듯한 오답입니다. medium 난이도의 하한선 수준입니다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-inferences-m-001","intendedSkill":"inferences","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-command_of_evidence_text-m-003","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Command of Evidence (Textual)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"command_of_evidence_text","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"The following is adapted from a scene in a 1950s novel set in Paris.\n\nOn the last Thursday of October 1952, Monsieur Aubert, who had come into Lucien Ferrand's bookshop every week for eleven years, set a parcel on the counter and left without his usual remark about the weather. Inside was a copy of Montaigne's Essays, its spine cracked, its corners soft as felt, a coffee ring blooming across the title page. Lucien turned it over twice. To give a bookseller a ruined book, he thought, was to tell him that his trade was worth nothing more than this. He slid the volume beneath the counter and did not look at it again that day.\n\nDiscussing this scene, literary scholar Hélène Marchetti argues that the novel invites readers to see what Lucien cannot: that the book's battered condition is itself the message, evidence of a devotion that Aubert built over many years and connected directly to Lucien.","question":"Which finding, if true, would most directly support Marchetti's argument?","options":["In a later chapter, Lucien realizes he misjudged Aubert and visits his apartment to say sorry, but finds that Aubert has moved away from Paris.","In a later chapter, Lucien remembers that his own father, also a bookseller, believed that no customer should ever give a used book as a gift.","In a later chapter, Lucien learns that Aubert first bought the volume at a different shop across the Seine before he started visiting Lucien's store.","In a later chapter, Lucien opens the volume and finds Aubert's dated notes in its margins, many responding to passages Lucien had recommended to him over the years."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"Marchetti의 주장에는 두 부분이 있다. 책이 낡은 것은 Aubert가 오랜 세월 쌓아 온 헌신의 증거라는 점, 그리고 그 헌신이 Lucien과 직접 이어져 있다는 점이다. D는 여러 해에 걸쳐 날짜가 적힌 메모(오랜 반복 독서)를 보여 주고, 그 메모가 Lucien이 추천한 구절에 대한 응답(Lucien과의 연결)임을 보여 주므로 두 조건을 모두 충족한다. A는 Lucien이 자신의 오해를 깨닫는다는 내용이지만, 책의 상태가 무엇을 뜻하는지는 설명하지 못한다. B는 오히려 선물을 모욕으로 본 Lucien의 해석에 배경을 줄 뿐이다. C는 책의 내력을 알려 주지만 Lucien과 무관한 곳에서 산 책이므로 헌신이 Lucien과 연결된다는 점을 뒷받침하지 못한다.","explanationEn":"Marchetti's argument has two parts: the book's worn condition is evidence of devotion Aubert built up over many years, and that devotion is tied directly to Lucien. D satisfies both. Notes dated across many years show long, repeated reading, and the fact that they respond to passages Lucien recommended links the wear to Lucien himself. A shows that Lucien realizes he was wrong, but it says nothing about what the book's condition means. B only gives background for Lucien's view that the gift was an insult. C tells you where the book came from, but because Aubert bought it somewhere unrelated to Lucien, it actually fails to connect the book to him.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.609Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — A Parisian bookseller in 1952 misinterprets a regular customer's gift of a worn volume, believing it an insult rather than an act of devotion.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"Marchetti의 주장은 (1) 낡은 상태 = 오랜 헌신의 증거, (2) 그 헌신이 Lucien과 직접 연결, 두 조건으로 구성됨. D만이 두 조건을 모두 충족(여러 해에 걸친 날짜 메모 + Lucien 추천 구절에 대한 응답). A는 '오해 깨달음'이라는 부분적 근거가 있으나 책 상태의 의미를 설명하지 못하고, C는 책의 내력(오랜 소유)을 주지만 Lucien과의 연결을 끊음. B는 Lucien의 해석을 뒷받침하는 쪽. 오답 2개가 부분적 근거를 가지므로 medium에 적합. 한국어·영어 해설 결론 및 선택지 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 가상 소설 발췌로 저작권 우려 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"두 조건(오랜 헌신 + Lucien과의 연결)을 모두 확인해야 하는 구조임. A와 C는 일부 근거만 갖춘 오답이어서 medium 난이도에 맞음. 정답 D가 유일하게 두 조건을 모두 충족함.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-command_of_evidence_text-m-003","intendedSkill":"command_of_evidence_text","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-cross_text_connections-m-004","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Cross-Text Connections","difficulty":"medium","skill":"cross_text_connections","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Text 1\nIn Margarethe Lind's novel The Fourth Zone, the boarder Frau Keller spends three days crossing postwar Vienna to recover a single letter left at her old address. Critics usually praise how closely Lind shows the city split among four occupying powers: the checkpoints, the ruined tram lines, the guards' changing languages. That divided city is the book's real subject. The letter itself is little more than a pretext, a device that keeps Keller moving so that readers can see Vienna's divisions.\n\nText 2\nNo reader can forget Lind's checkpoints, and they have earned their praise. But the city takes its shape from Keller's errand. At each barrier she silently repeats the name of her brother, who wrote the letter, and she judges every delay by how much it postpones the moment she will hold his words. The British sector feels hostile to her not because of its soldiers but because its detours cost her an afternoon. Take away the letter and Lind's Vienna loses the urgency that makes it vivid.","question":"Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the claim in Text 1 about the role of the letter in Lind's novel?","options":["By agreeing that the divided city is powerfully portrayed while maintaining that Keller's attachment to the letter governs how that city is experienced","By agreeing that the letter is incidental to the plot while maintaining that Keller's brother is the novel's true central concern","By disputing that the city is powerfully portrayed while maintaining that the checkpoints are less memorable than critics suggest","By disputing that Keller ever reaches the letter while maintaining that her journey is ultimately left unfinished"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"Text 2의 저자는 검문소 묘사가 칭찬받을 만하다고 인정하면서도(\"No reader can forget... earned their praise\"), 도시가 편지라는 용무를 통해 형태를 갖는다고 주장한다. 따라서 편지가 단순한 구실이라는 Text 1의 주장을 반박하고, 편지가 도시 경험을 좌우한다고 볼 것이므로 A가 정답이다. B는 오빠를 중요하게 본다는 점은 맞지만, 편지가 부수적이라는 데 동의한다는 부분이 Text 2의 핵심 주장과 반대된다. C는 Text 2가 도시 묘사를 칭찬하므로 틀렸다. D는 Text 2에 Keller가 편지를 찾는지에 대한 언급이 없으므로 근거가 없다.","explanationEn":"The author of Text 2 grants that Lind's checkpoints \"have earned their praise,\" but argues that the city \"takes its shape from Keller's errand,\" meaning that the letter controls how she experiences each delay and sector. So this author would accept Text 1's praise of the divided city while rejecting the idea that the letter is a mere pretext, which is choice A. Choice B is partly right because the brother does matter in Text 2, but it says the author agrees the letter is incidental, and Text 2 argues the opposite. Choice C is wrong because Text 2 praises the city's portrayal rather than questioning it. Choice D has no support, since neither text discusses whether Keller actually gets the letter.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.609Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Frau Keller, a postwar Vienna boarder, takes a three-day journey across the fractured city to retrieve a single letter she fears may have been lost forever.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"Text 2 explicitly concedes the checkpoints \"have earned their praise\" and then argues the city \"takes its shape from Keller's errand,\" directly contradicting Text 1's \"pretext\" claim—A is the only choice capturing both the concession and the rebuttal. B is a strong partial-credit distractor (brother does matter, but \"letter is incidental\" reverses Text 2's thesis); C inverts the concession; D is unsupported but surface-plausible. Korean and English explanations match in conclusion and letter references, with no Hangul in the English version. Fictional novel/author, no copyright concern. Two-step reasoning (identify concession + identify counterclaim) suits medium."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["too_easy","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 A는 타당하다. 그러나 부분적으로 맞는 근거를 가진 오답은 B 하나뿐이다. C는 Text 2 첫 문장(\"earned their praise\")과 정면으로 모순되고, D는 두 지문 어디에도 근거가 없어 훑어 읽어도 바로 걸러진다. 'medium' 기준인 '오답 3개 중 최소 2개가 부분적으로 맞는 근거를 가질 것'을 충족하지 못한다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-cross_text_connections-m-004","intendedSkill":"cross_text_connections","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-boundaries-m-006","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"On the last morning of the term, Teacher Mateo did not speak of sheep. He stood at the window of the one-room schoolhouse, where the wind off the Patagonian steppe rattled the tin roof like loose coins, and pointed upward at the wide, colorless sky that the ranch children had long ago stopped noticing ______ it was, he told them quietly, the only thing on the estancia that no one would ever own.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":[",","and,",";","(no punctuation)"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"빈칸 앞 \"He stood ... noticing\"은 긴 관계절과 수식어가 붙어 있지만 하나의 독립절이고, 빈칸 뒤 \"it was ... own\"도 주어와 동사를 가진 독립절이다. 두 독립절을 연결하려면 세미콜론이 필요하므로 C가 정답이다. A는 뒤에 나오는 삽입구 \"he told them\" 주변의 쉼표들과 비슷해 보이지만, 쉼표만으로 두 독립절을 이으면 쉼표 오류(comma splice)가 된다. B는 접속사 and를 쓴 점은 맞지만, 쉼표를 and 앞이 아니라 뒤에 두어 문장부호 위치가 잘못되었다. D는 아무 문장부호 없이 두 절을 붙여 무종지문(run-on)이 된다.","explanationEn":"The words before the blank, \"He stood ... noticing,\" make up one independent clause, even though long relative clauses and modifiers are attached to it. The words after the blank, \"it was ... own,\" form a second independent clause with its own subject and verb. To join two independent clauses, you need a semicolon, so C is correct. A might look right because it matches the commas around \"he told them,\" but a comma alone between two independent clauses is a comma splice. B correctly uses the conjunction \"and,\" but the comma goes after \"and\" instead of before it, so the punctuation is in the wrong place. D puts no punctuation between the clauses at all, which makes a run-on sentence.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.609Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Teacher Mateo delivers his final lesson to ranch children on the Patagonian steppe, speaking not of sheep but of the sky they are learning to ignore.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"빈칸 앞 \"He stood ... stopped noticing\"은 관계절·수식어가 길게 붙은 하나의 독립절이고, 뒤 \"it was ... own\"도 독립절이므로 세미콜론(C)이 유일한 정답. A는 comma splice, B는 and 뒤 쉼표로 위치 오류, D는 run-on(단, \"noticing it was...\"가 명사절처럼 읽혀 유혹적임). 긴 문장 구조에서 절 경계를 찾아야 하고 A·D가 부분적 근거를 가지므로 medium에 적합. 한·영 해설 모두 정답 및 선택지 참조가 일치하고 오류 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"관계절이 길어 절의 경계가 가려지고, 뒤 절의 삽입구 쉼표가 A를 그럴듯하게 만든다. 그래서 중간 난이도에 대체로 맞는다. 다만 B와 D는 비교적 쉽게 배제된다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-boundaries-m-006","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-boundaries-m-007","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"For eleven years, Carlos and Eduardo had refused to share so much as a thermos of coffee at the San Isidro depot. But on the night a rockslide trapped both of their buses on the switchbacks above the village, Eduardo, the driver who had once reported Carlos for leaving three minutes early, did something no one at the depot would have predicted ______ walked down the dark road to Carlos's stalled bus, a coil of tow rope over his shoulder, and asked where to tie it.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":[", he","; and he","he",": he"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"긴 동격구(the driver who...)를 걷어내면 'Eduardo did something no one would have predicted'가 완전한 독립절이고, 뒤의 'he walked...'도 독립절이며 그 '예측 못 한 일'을 구체적으로 설명한다. 앞 절이 완결되고 뒤 절이 그 내용을 풀어 설명하므로 콜론을 쓰는 D가 정답이다. A는 독립절 두 개를 쉼표만으로 이어 쉼표 오용(comma splice)이 된다. B는 세미콜론 뒤에 등위접속사 and를 붙여 쓴 비표준 형태이다. C는 두 독립절을 아무 문장부호 없이 붙여 무종지문(run-on)이 된다.","explanationEn":"If you set aside the long appositive (the driver who...), \"Eduardo did something no one at the depot would have predicted\" is a complete independent clause. \"He walked...\" is also an independent clause, and it spells out what that unexpected act was. A colon is the right mark when a complete clause is followed by an explanation of it, so D is correct. A joins two independent clauses with only a comma, which makes a comma splice. B puts the conjunction \"and\" after a semicolon, which is not standard. C runs the two clauses together with no punctuation at all.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.609Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Two rival bus drivers at a Mexican mountain depot—Carlos and Eduardo—develop grudging respect after a shared crisis forces them to help one another.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"검산: 'Eduardo ... did something no one at the depot would have predicted'는 완전한 독립절, 'he walked ... and asked ...'도 독립절이며 앞 절의 '예측 못 한 일'을 구체화하므로 콜론(D)이 적절. A는 comma splice, B는 세미콜론+and 비표준, C는 run-on. 긴 삽입 동격구와 부사절이 주절 경계 파악을 요구해 두 단계 판단이 필요하며, A·B가 부분적 타당성을 갖는 오답으로 기능하므로 medium 적합. 한·영 해설 결론 및 선택지 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"긴 동격구 때문에 주절의 구조를 다시 파악해야 하고, 그다음 콜론의 설명 기능을 확인해야 하는 두 단계 판단이 필요해 medium 난이도에 맞다. B(세미콜론+and)를 비표준으로 본 해설은 엄밀히 따지면 논란의 여지가 있지만 SAT 관례에는 부합한다. 다만 뒤 절이 앞 절을 구체화한다는 점에서 콜론이 가장 적절하다는 근거를 덧붙이면 더 좋겠다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-boundaries-m-007","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-boundaries-m-008","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Every morning the school boat left Tagbac before the tide turned, and the children, crowded beneath its patched blue canopy, made up games to fill the hour. The newest game, invented by Lorna Dimaculangan, a quiet girl who swore she had dreamed it during the last typhoon______ that anyone walking between the island's villages at midday must never once step on his or her own shadow. By the time the boat reached the pier, even the boatman was squinting at the sun and planning his route home.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":[", required","required","; required","—required"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장의 주어는 \"The newest game\"이고 동사는 \"required\"이다. 그 사이에 \"invented by ...\"라는 수식어와 \"a quiet girl who ... typhoon\"이라는 동격구가 끼어 있다. 동격구가 쉼표로 시작했으므로 같은 쉼표로 닫아야 하고, 그래서 A가 정답이다. B는 닫는 쉼표가 없어서 \"typhoon required\"가 관계절 속 동사처럼 읽혀 버린다. C의 세미콜론은 주어와 동사를 갈라놓아 앞부분이 독립절이 되지 못한다. D의 대시는 쉼표로 연 삽입구를 다른 부호로 닫는 것이라 짝이 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this sentence is \"The newest game,\" and its verb is \"required.\" Between them sit the modifier \"invented by ...\" and the appositive \"a quiet girl who ... typhoon.\" That appositive opens with a comma, so it has to close with a comma too, and that makes A correct. B leaves out the closing comma, so \"typhoon required\" reads as if the verb belonged inside the \"who\" clause. C puts a semicolon between the subject and its verb, and that's a problem because the words before a semicolon must form an independent clause, which they don't here. D closes with a dash even though the interruption opened with a comma, so the punctuation doesn't match.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.609Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On a Philippine island school boat, children invent a game where neighbors must navigate between villages without stepping on their own shadow.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"주어 \"The newest game\"과 동사 \"required\" 사이에 긴 삽입 수식어(분사구 + 동격구 + 관계절)가 끼어 있고, 삽입은 쉼표로 열렸으므로 쉼표로 닫는 A가 유일한 정답. B는 닫는 부호 누락, C는 세미콜론 앞이 독립절이 아님, D는 여는 부호(쉼표)와 닫는 부호(대시)가 불일치. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 같은 결론과 글자 참조를 가지며 정확하고 자연스러움. 긴 삽입구 속 중첩 구조를 추적해야 하므로 medium에 적합. 지문은 창작 원문으로 저작권 우려 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"주어-동사 사이에 긴 삽입구(분사구+동격구+관계절)가 있어 짝 쉼표를 찾아야 하는 2단계 판단이 필요하다. 표준 medium 수준이다. 엄밀히 보면 삽입 요소는 'invented' 앞의 쉼표로 열리지만, 해설이 동격구 기준으로 설명해도 결론은 같다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-boundaries-m-008","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-boundaries-m-010","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Jin and Sora had surfaced side by side for forty years, their breath-whistles rising together over the cold swells off Jeju. Now, as Sora coiled her rope on the black rocks and talked about her aching knees, about her granddaughter in Seoul, about the blue gate she would finally have time to repaint______ said nothing, and for the first time the silence between them felt less like comfort than like a door being slowly closed.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["; Jin",": Jin",", Jin",", and Jin"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"'as Sora coiled... repaint'는 'as'로 시작하는 종속절이고, 주절은 'Jin said nothing'입니다. 도입 종속절과 주절 사이에는 쉼표 하나를 쓰므로 C가 정답입니다. A의 세미콜론은 앞뒤가 모두 독립절일 때만 쓸 수 있는데, 앞부분은 길어도 종속절이라 혼자 문장이 될 수 없습니다. B의 콜론도 앞에 완전한 독립절이 있어야 하므로 같은 이유로 틀립니다. D는 쉼표+and로 종속절을 주절과 대등하게 연결해 버려서, 'as' 절이 수식할 주절이 사라집니다.","explanationEn":"The part starting with \"as Sora coiled... repaint\" is a dependent clause, and the main clause is \"Jin said nothing.\" When an introductory dependent clause comes before the main clause, you separate them with a single comma, so C is correct. A doesn't work because a semicolon has to join two independent clauses, and even though the opening is long, it's a dependent clause that can't stand alone. B fails for the same reason, since a colon needs a complete independent clause before it. D adds \"and,\" which links the dependent clause to the main clause as if they were equal, so the \"as\" clause no longer has a main clause to modify.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.609Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Divers Jin and Sora have been haenyeo partners for forty years, but as one plans to retire, their comfortable silence begins to feel like goodbye.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"'Now, as Sora coiled ... repaint' is a long introductory subordinate clause (with an internal 'about...' series that invites misreading it as independent); the main clause is 'Jin said nothing'. Only a comma (C) correctly separates them. A and B require an independent clause before the mark; D's ', and' leaves the 'as' clause with no main clause. Both explanations match the answer and letter references and are accurate; English is natural with no Hangul. Two-step judgment (identify clause type despite length/internal commas, then apply punctuation rule) suits medium."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"'Now, as ... repaint'라는 긴 종속절이 있고, 그 안에 about 병렬 구문이 들어가 있어서 종속절이 어디서 끝나는지 파악하기 어렵습니다. 그래서 훑어 읽으면 세미콜론이나 콜론을 고르는 오답을 유도하므로 medium 난이도에 적합합니다. D도 'and'가 있으니 그럴듯해 보이는 오답입니다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-boundaries-m-010","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-boundaries-m-015","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Captain Elias Merrow had spent three nights at the chart table drawing the river from Cairo to Natchez, marking every sandbar and snag he had learned in twenty years of piloting. When his brother Tobias finally came up to the pilothouse, Elias pushed the folded sheet across the wheel without a word. Tobias, who had not spoken to him since their father's funeral and who had boarded the boat only because no other passage south was ______ the map open slowly, as if it might tear.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["available; unfolded","available, and unfolded","available unfolded","available, unfolded"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장의 주어는 Tobias이고 본동사는 unfolded이며, 그 사이의 'who had not spoken... available'은 앞쪽 쉼표로 열린 비필수 관계절이다. 따라서 이 삽입절을 닫는 쉼표 하나가 필요하므로 D가 정답이다. A의 세미콜론은 앞뒤에 독립절이 있어야 하는데, 앞부분은 주어만 있고 동사가 없는 불완전한 절이다. B의 'and'는 unfolded를 관계절 속 동사(had boarded)와 나란히 묶어 버려 주어 Tobias에게 본동사가 남지 않는다. C는 삽입절을 닫는 쉼표가 빠져 있어 'available unfolded'가 잘못 붙어 읽힌다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this sentence is Tobias and its main verb is unfolded. Between them sits a nonessential relative clause (\"who had not spoken... available\") that opens with a comma, so it needs a matching comma to close it, which makes D correct. A uses a semicolon, but a semicolon needs an independent clause on each side, and the part before it has a subject with no main verb. B adds \"and,\" which pairs unfolded with the verb inside the relative clause (had boarded), so Tobias ends up with no main verb. C leaves out the closing comma, so the clause never ends and \"available unfolded\" runs together.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.609Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On a nineteenth-century riverboat, a steamboat captain gives his estranged brother a hand-drawn map, a gesture neither can quite articulate.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"검산: 주어 Tobias + 쉼표로 열린 비필수 관계절(who... and who... available) + 본동사 unfolded 구조이므로 닫는 쉼표가 필요한 D가 유일하게 옳음. A는 세미콜론 앞이 독립절이 아님, B는 'and'가 본동사를 관계절에 흡수시켜 주절 동사 소실, C는 닫는 쉼표 누락. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 동일 결론·글자 참조로 정확하며 자연스러움. 긴 삽입절과 두 개의 who절을 추적해야 하므로 medium에 적합. 원창작 지문으로 저작권 우려 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"긴 비필수 관계절 안에 다시 'who ... and who' 병렬 구조가 들어 있다. 그래서 수험생은 주어-동사를 찾은 뒤 삽입절을 닫는 쉼표가 필요하다는 것까지 두 단계로 판단해야 한다. B는 관계절 안의 병렬 구조 때문에 그럴듯하게 보이는 매력적인 오답이다. medium 난이도에 적합하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-boundaries-m-015","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-boundaries-m-016","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Amara had assumed the stranger sharing the narrow ledge beneath the rooftop water tank was just another office clerk caught by the monsoon without an umbrella. But when Dev mentioned the salt-stung cashew groves and the crooked lighthouse at the edge of his childhood town, a place neither of them had returned to in more than a decade______ realized that they had once lived only a few lanes apart.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":[", she","; she",", and she",". She"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장은 \"when\"으로 시작하는 종속절이 \"a place ... decade\"라는 긴 동격어구로 끝나고, 그 뒤에 주절 \"she realized...\"가 온다. 문장 앞에 오는 종속절과 주절은 쉼표로 연결하므로 A가 정답이다. B의 세미콜론은 앞뒤가 모두 독립절이어야 쓸 수 있는데, 앞부분은 \"when\" 때문에 종속절이다. C의 \", and\"도 앞부분을 독립절로 잘못 본 것이다. 종속절에 주절을 등위접속사로 이을 수는 없다. D는 앞부분을 \"But when...\"으로 시작하는 문장 조각(fragment)으로 남긴다.","explanationEn":"The sentence opens with a dependent clause beginning with \"when,\" and that clause ends with a long appositive (\"a place ... decade\"). After it comes the main clause \"she realized....\" A comma is the standard way to join an introductory dependent clause to a main clause, so A is correct. B uses a semicolon, which needs an independent clause on both sides, but \"when\" makes the first part dependent. C uses \", and,\" which also wrongly treats the first part as an independent clause, and a coordinating conjunction can't join a dependent clause to a main clause. D leaves \"But when...\" standing alone as a sentence fragment.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.609Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Amara and Dev, strangers sheltering from monsoon rain on a Mumbai rooftop, discover they both fled the same coastal town years ago.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"검산: \"But when Dev mentioned ... town, a place ... decade\" 전체가 when 종속절(동격어구 포함)이고 주절은 \"she realized...\"이므로 쉼표(A)가 유일한 정답. B(세미콜론)·C(, and)는 앞부분을 독립절로 오인한 것이고 D는 조각문을 만든다. 긴 동격어구가 구조를 가려 훑어 읽으면 B/C에 끌리도록 설계되어 medium에 적합. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 정답과 선택지 글자 참조가 일치하고 오류 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"긴 동격어구 때문에 종속절 경계를 찾기 어려워 medium 수준에 맞음. 오답 B, C, D 모두 그럴듯함.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-boundaries-m-016","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-boundaries-m-017","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Rolf turned the brass key over in his palm. It belonged to his parents' apartment on Wiedner Hauptstraße, a place of high ceilings and a piano no one had played since 1945______ he slept on a narrow cot in the Hubers' kitchen, wedged between the stove and a wardrobe that smelled of camphor.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":[", meanwhile,","; meanwhile,",", meanwhile","; meanwhile"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"빈칸 앞 \"It belonged ... since 1945\"는 긴 동격구로 끝나는 독립절이고, 빈칸 뒤 \"he slept ...\"도 독립절이다. 두 독립절을 접속부사 meanwhile로 이으려면 앞에 세미콜론, 뒤에 쉼표를 써야 하므로 B가 정답이다. A와 C는 쉼표만으로 두 독립절을 이어 comma splice가 된다(meanwhile은 등위접속사가 아니다). D는 세미콜론은 맞지만 문장 앞머리 접속부사 meanwhile 뒤에 쉼표가 빠져 있다.","explanationEn":"The part before the blank, \"It belonged ... since 1945,\" is an independent clause, even though it ends with a long appositive. The part after the blank, \"he slept ...,\" is also an independent clause. If you join two independent clauses with the conjunctive adverb \"meanwhile,\" you need a semicolon before it and a comma after it, so B is correct. A and C use only a comma to join the two clauses, which makes a comma splice, because \"meanwhile\" is not a coordinating conjunction. D has the correct semicolon, but it leaves out the comma that should follow \"meanwhile\" at the start of the clause.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.609Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Rolf, a postwar Vienna boarder, must decide whether to remain in the comfortable, cramped room he shares or reclaim the family apartment standing empty.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"빈칸 앞뒤 모두 독립절이므로 세미콜론+접속부사+쉼표(B)가 표준 정답이며, A·C는 comma splice로 명확히 배제된다. 다만 B와 D의 유일한 차이가 접속부사 meanwhile 뒤 쉼표 유무인데, 이는 실제 용법에서 선택적(특히 짧은 부사)으로 취급되는 경우가 많아 D를 '오류'로 단정하기 약하다. 실제 디지털 SAT는 세미콜론 뒤 접속부사의 쉼표 유무만으로 정오를 가르는 설계를 피하는 경향이 있으므로, 변별 근거의 견고성 측면에서 주의가 필요하다(판정 범위 내에서는 B가 최선의 선택임은 인정). 긴 동격구 뒤에 절 경계를 숨긴 점은 medium 난이도에 부합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"세미콜론 + 접속부사 + 쉼표를 묻는 표준 문항이다. 앞 독립절이 긴 동격구로 끝나서 절 경계를 찾기가 조금 어려워지고, 이 점이 medium 난이도에 맞다. D는 SAT 관례상 오답으로 처리하는 전형적인 선택지다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-boundaries-m-017","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-boundaries-m-018","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Marcus had been counting the cars of the approaching Ravenswood train when he saw it. The man beside him on the elevated platform, a tall figure in a gray overcoat who had been checking his wristwatch every few seconds______ the gold band from his finger and let it slip into his coat pocket. No one else on the crowded platform seemed to notice.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["; twisted","— twisted",", twisted"," twisted"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"주어 \"The man beside him on the elevated platform\" 뒤에 쉼표로 시작하는 동격어구(a tall figure ... every few seconds)가 삽입되어 있고, 그 뒤에 본동사 twisted가 온다. 쉼표로 열린 비필수 삽입구는 쉼표로 닫아야 하므로 C가 정답이다. A의 세미콜론은 주어와 동사를 끊어 앞부분을 독립절이 아닌 조각으로 만든다. B의 대시는 삽입구를 닫는 데 쓸 수 있지만 쉼표로 연 삽입구를 대시로 닫으면 부호가 일치하지 않는다. D는 닫는 부호가 없어서 seconds twisted가 한 덩어리처럼 읽히고, 삽입구가 어디서 끝나는지 알 수 없다.","explanationEn":"The subject, \"The man beside him on the elevated platform,\" is followed by an appositive that opens with a comma (\"a tall figure ... every few seconds\"), and then the main verb \"twisted\" comes next. A nonessential phrase that opens with a comma has to close with a comma, so C is correct. A uses a semicolon, which cuts the subject off from its verb and leaves a fragment before the semicolon. B uses a dash, which can close an interruption, but only when a dash opened it; closing a comma-opened phrase with a dash mixes the punctuation. D has no closing punctuation, so \"seconds twisted\" runs together and the reader can't tell where the appositive ends.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.609Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On a 1960s Chicago elevated platform, ten-year-old Marcus watches a man slip a wedding ring into his coat pocket, a gesture no one else seems to notice.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"주어 \"The man beside him on the elevated platform\" 뒤에 쉼표로 열린 동격 삽입구가 \"every few seconds\"까지 이어지고 본동사 twisted가 뒤따르므로 쉼표로 닫는 C가 유일하게 옳다. A(세미콜론)는 주어와 동사를 분리해 조각을 만들고, B(대시)는 쉼표로 연 삽입구와 부호가 불일치하며, D는 경계가 사라진다. 해설(한·영) 결론과 글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 삽입구 시작점을 역추적해 부호 짝을 맞추는 두 단계 판단이 필요하고 B·A가 부분적 타당성을 가져 medium 적합. 지문은 창작물로 저작권 문제 없음. D 선택지의 공백 두 칸은 사소한 표기 차이."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"동격어구 안에 관계절(who had been checking...)이 길게 들어 있어서 동사 twisted를 찾으려면 앞뒤를 연결해 읽어야 하므로 중간 난이도에 맞는다. B와 D는 부분적으로 그럴듯한 오답이다. D 선택지 앞에 공백이 두 칸 들어간 것은 사소한 표기 문제다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-boundaries-m-018","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-m-019","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Every weekday at 7:40, the Johnsons climbed to the Garfield Boulevard platform in the same order: Mr. Johnson first, then his wife, then nine-year-old Della with her lunch pail. But on the cold Tuesday that a gaunt brown dog appeared beneath the platform bench, ribs showing through its matted coat, Della knelt beside it and would not move. As the southbound train rattled in and out without them, the routine of the household, built over years of punctual departures and carefully pressed shirts, ______ apart in a single stubborn refusal to stand up.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["were coming","having come","to come","came"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 절의 주어는 단수 명사 'the routine'이고, 삽입된 수식어구 'built over years of ... shirts' 다음에 정동사가 와야 절이 완성된다. D의 'came'은 단수 주어와 맞는 정동사이며, 앞 문장들의 과거 시제와도 일치한다. A의 'were coming'은 정동사이긴 하지만 수식어구 안의 복수 명사(departures, shirts)에 맞춘 복수형이라 단수 주어 'routine'과 일치하지 않는다. B의 'having come'과 C의 'to come'은 비정형(분사·부정사)이어서 주어 'routine'에 정동사가 없게 되므로 문장이 성립하지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this clause is the singular noun \"the routine,\" and after the modifier \"built over years of ... shirts,\" the clause still needs a main verb to be complete. Choice D, \"came,\" is a main verb that agrees with the singular subject and also fits the past tense used in the rest of the passage. Choice A, \"were coming,\" is a main verb, but it's plural: it agrees with the nouns inside the modifier (\"departures,\" \"shirts\"), not with the singular subject \"routine.\" Choices B (\"having come\") and C (\"to come\") are nonfinite forms (a participle and an infinitive), so \"routine\" would be left with no main verb and the sentence wouldn't work.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.609Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — The Johnsons' orderly 1960s Chicago household transforms when a half-starved dog appears on their elevated train platform and their daughter refuses to leave it.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"주어 'the routine of the household'(단수) 뒤에 긴 분사 수식어구 'built over years of punctual departures and carefully pressed shirts'가 삽입되어 있으며, 빈칸에는 정동사가 필요하다. D 'came'은 단수·과거 정동사로 정답이 맞다. A는 수식어구 내 복수 명사에 이끌린 수 일치 오류, B·C는 비정형으로 문장이 성립하지 않는다. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 동일한 결론과 선택지 참조를 갖고 정확하다. 수식어구를 건너뛰어 주어를 찾는 단계와 정동사/비정형 판별 단계가 결합되어 있어 medium에 적합하다. 지문은 독창적으로 보이며 저작권 의심 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"'household'의 주어는 단수 'routine'이고 그 뒤에 수식어구가 끼어 있다. 'came'은 정동사이자 과거 시제여서 옳다. A는 복수 명사에 끌린 수 일치 함정이고, B와 C는 비정형이라 정동사가 없어진다. 두 단계로 판단해야 해서 중간 난이도에 맞는다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-m-019","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-m-020","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Kamau had ridden the same green matatu into Nairobi every morning for nineteen years, but today he was riding it out of the city, toward the village where he had promised his daughter he would scatter her ashes. Clutching the small cedar box against his chest as the minibus lurched past the Kenyatta Avenue stage, ______ the conductor calling out destinations he had heard a thousand times before.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["Kamau barely heard","Kamau's ears barely caught","there was barely any notice by Kamau of","the words barely reached Kamau from"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장은 분사구 'Clutching the small cedar box…'로 시작하므로, 바로 뒤에 오는 주어가 상자를 움켜쥔 사람이어야 한다. A는 주어가 Kamau라서 수식 관계가 맞고, 뒤의 목적어 'the conductor calling out…'과도 자연스럽게 이어진다. B는 Kamau라는 이름이 들어 있어 맞아 보이지만, 실제 주어는 'Kamau's ears'여서 귀가 상자를 움켜쥔 꼴이 된다. C는 주어 자리에 허사 there가 있어 분사구가 꾸밀 대상이 없다. D는 주어가 'the words'라서 말이 상자를 움켜쥔 꼴이 된다.","explanationEn":"The sentence opens with the participial phrase \"Clutching the small cedar box…,\" so the subject that comes right after it has to be the person holding the box. Choice A makes Kamau the subject, so the modifier attaches correctly, and the object \"the conductor calling out…\" follows naturally. Choice B looks right because it includes Kamau's name, but its actual subject is \"Kamau's ears,\" which would mean his ears were clutching the box. Choice C puts the placeholder \"there\" in the subject position, so the opening phrase has nothing to modify. Choice D makes \"the words\" the subject, which would mean the words were clutching the box.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.609Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Kamau boards the same Nairobi matatu each morning, today carrying his daughter's ashes to the village where he promised to scatter them.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"분사구 'Clutching the small cedar box…'의 수식 대상이 주어여야 하므로 Kamau가 주어인 A만 정답. B('Kamau's ears'), C(허사 there), D('the words')는 모두 현수 분사 오류. B는 이름이 포함되어 훑어 읽으면 매력적인 오답이고 D도 의미상 그럴듯하여 비교가 필요하므로 medium 적합. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 선택지 글자 참조와 결론이 일치하며 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 독창적 서사로 저작권 우려 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"현수 수식어 문항. B의 소유격 함정이 비교를 요구하고, D도 문법적으로는 성립해 보여 medium 수준에 맞음. C는 상대적으로 쉽게 배제됨.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-m-020","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-m-021","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Halfway across the channel, the old fisherman spread the torn sail over his knees and motioned for Iris to sit beside him. He spoke slowly, as if each instruction might be the last he would ever give. The rhythm of his hands, pulling the waxed twine through the canvas in loops as even as the waves slapping against the hull, ______ her more than his words did, and by the time the island came into view, she could close a seam on her own.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["were teaching","taught","teaching","have taught"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장의 주어는 단수 명사 \"The rhythm\"이고, 콤마 사이의 긴 분사구(pulling ... hull)는 삽입된 수식어일 뿐이다. 따라서 단수 주어와 맞으면서 지문의 과거 시제(spoke, did, came, could)와도 맞는 정동사가 필요하므로 B \"taught\"가 정답이다. A는 과거 시제는 맞지만 복수형이어서, 가까이 있는 \"hands\"나 \"waves\"에 잘못 맞춘 것이다. C는 분사라서 문장에 정동사가 없게 된다. D는 복수형인 데다 현재완료여서 서술 시제와도 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this sentence is the singular noun \"The rhythm.\" The long phrase between the commas (pulling ... hull) only modifies it. So you need a main verb that is singular and also matches the passage's past tense (spoke, did, came, could). That makes B, \"taught,\" the answer. A is in the past tense, but it's plural, so it wrongly agrees with nearby nouns like \"hands\" or \"waves.\" C is a participle, which leaves the sentence without a main verb. D is plural and in the present perfect, so it doesn't match the narration's tense either.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.610Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On a Caribbean ferry crossing, Iris learns traditional sail-mending from an elderly fisherman who speaks as though teaching her for the last time.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"주어 \"The rhythm\"(단수)과 긴 삽입 분사구(pulling ... hull)를 건너뛴 뒤 과거 시제 서술(spoke, did, came, could)에 맞춰야 하므로 B \"taught\"가 유일하게 수·시제가 모두 맞는 정동사다. A는 시제는 맞지만 복수, C는 비정형, D는 복수+현재완료로 모두 배제됨. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 동일 결론과 글자 참조를 가지며 오류 없음. 삽입구에 \"hands\", \"waves\" 등 복수 명사가 가까이 있어 훑어 읽으면 A로 유인되는 구조이며, 주어 식별+시제 확인의 두 단계 판단이 필요해 medium에 적합하다."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"긴 삽입구가 끼어 있어 주어-동사 수일치를 판단해야 하고, 시제도 함께 확인해야 하는 두 단계 문항이다. 근처 복수 명사(hands, waves)가 함정 역할을 하며 medium 난이도에 적합하다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-m-021","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-m-024","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Min-jun had cooked all afternoon for his sister and her husband, and he had told no one else about the dinner. Yet when the doorbell rang a second time, the voice in the hallway was one he had not heard in six years. Setting down the platter of japchae in the center of the table, ______ the chair nearest the window, her coat still buttoned as though she might leave at any moment.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["Min-jun saw that his mother had already claimed","his mother, Min-jun saw, had already claimed","the eyes of Min-jun saw that his mother had already claimed","Min-jun seeing that his mother had already claimed"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"분사구 'Setting down the platter...'의 의미상 주어는 바로 뒤 주절의 주어여야 하고, 문맥상 요리를 해서 접시를 내려놓는 사람은 Min-jun이다. A는 Min-jun을 주어로 두고 정동사 saw를 갖춰 주어와 서술어가 모두 맞는다. B는 동사 claimed가 있어 완전한 문장이지만, 접시를 내려놓은 사람이 어머니가 되어 수식어가 잘못 연결된다. C는 Min-jun이라는 이름은 들어 있지만 문법상 주어가 'the eyes'여서 눈이 접시를 내려놓은 것이 된다. D는 주어가 맞아 보이지만 seeing이 분사라서 정동사가 없는 불완전한 문장(fragment)이다.","explanationEn":"The opening phrase \"Setting down the platter...\" describes whoever comes right after the comma, and the context tells you Min-jun cooked and served the meal. Choice A makes Min-jun the subject and gives him a finite verb, \"saw,\" so the modifier and the clause both work. Choice B is a complete sentence, but it says his mother set down the platter, so the modifier is attached to the wrong person. Choice C mentions Min-jun, but the grammatical subject is \"the eyes,\" so his eyes would be setting down the platter. Choice D has the right subject, but \"seeing\" is a participle, which leaves the sentence without a main verb, so it is a fragment.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.610Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Min-jun's Seoul apartment fills with tension when his estranged mother appears unannounced at a family dinner he did not invite her to.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"A를 넣으면 'Setting down the platter..., Min-jun saw that his mother had already claimed the chair...'로 분사구 수식 대상과 정동사가 모두 갖춰진 완전한 문장이 된다. B는 완전한 문장이지만 어머니가 접시를 내려놓은 것이 되어 수식어 오류, C는 'the eyes'가 주어가 되어 수식어 오류, D는 정동사 부재로 fragment. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 선택지 글자 참조가 일치하고 결론이 같다. 수식어 규칙 적용 + 문맥(요리한 사람) 확인 + 정동사 여부 판단의 두 단계 추론이 필요하고 B·D가 부분적으로 타당한 오답이어서 medium에 적합하다."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"현수 수식어(dangling modifier) 문항이며 형식이 표준적이다. B는 삽입구가 있는 완전한 문장이라 그럴듯하고, D는 주어는 맞지만 문장이 성립하지 않는다. 그래서 오답 두 개가 부분적인 근거를 갖춰 medium 난이도에 맞는다. C는 비교적 쉽게 배제된다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-m-024","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-m-025","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"At the edge of the cove on Jeju, the haenyeo were already floating beyond the breakers, their orange buoys bobbing like scattered fruit. The older woman, who had come to the rocks every morning since her daughter's funeral and who now sat in silence beside the two young divers drying their masks, ______ the beginner's trembling hand and pressed it flat against the cold, seaweed-slick stone. \"Breathe here first,\" she said. \"The sea can wait.\"","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["were taking","took","taking","having taken"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장의 주어는 단수 'The older woman'이고, 그 뒤에 이어지는 두 개의 who 관계절은 수식어일 뿐이므로 빈칸에는 단수 주어에 맞는 정동사가 와야 한다. 또한 빈칸 뒤의 'pressed'와 and로 병렬되므로 과거시제 정동사 B 'took'이 알맞다. A는 정동사이긴 하지만 바로 앞의 복수명사 'divers'에 수를 맞춘 것이라 단수 주어와 일치하지 않는다. C와 D는 분사형이라 문장에 주동사가 없게 되고, 'pressed'와의 병렬도 깨진다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this sentence is the singular noun \"The older woman.\" The two \"who\" clauses after it are just modifiers, so the blank needs a finite verb that agrees with a singular subject. The blank is also joined by \"and\" to the past-tense verb \"pressed,\" so B, \"took,\" is correct. A is a finite verb, but it agrees with the nearby plural noun \"divers\" instead of the singular subject. C and D are participles, which would leave the sentence without a main verb and break the parallel with \"pressed.\"","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.610Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Two strangers meet by chance at a Korean haenyeo cove—one grieving a lost daughter, one learning to dive—their brief conversation changing everything.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"주어 'The older woman'(단수) + 두 개의 긴 who 관계절 뒤 정동사 필요, 'and pressed'와 병렬 → B 'took' 정답 확인. A는 인접 복수명사 'divers'에 수 일치시킨 함정으로 그럴듯하고, C/D는 관계절 연속으로 오독 시 선택 가능. 두 단계 판단(주어 식별 + 병렬 시제 확인) 요구로 medium 적합. 해설 한·영 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 창작 지문으로 저작권 문제 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"긴 관계절 두 개가 주어와 동사를 떼어 놓는 구조라, 정동사인지 확인하고 단수 주어와 수를 맞추는 두 단계 판단이 필요하다. 오답 A는 바로 앞 복수명사 divers에 이끌리게 만든 함정이고, C와 D는 그럴듯해 보이는 분사형이다. 표준 SAT 중간 난이도에 맞는다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-m-025","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-m-026","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"By noon the neighbors had begun arriving in wagons and dusty Fords, and Joanne stood at the edge of the yard to greet each of them. Then, halfway down the first row of wheat, the combine coughed, shuddered, and fell silent. The long tables that she had spread with her mother's embroidered cloths, along with the rhubarb pie cooling on the porch rail, ______ suddenly foolish to her, like decorations for a party no one could afford.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["looks","looking","looked","having looked"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장의 주어는 복수 명사 'tables'이며, 'that she had spread...' 관계절과 'along with...' 삽입구는 주어 수에 영향을 주지 않는다. 따라서 주어에 맞는 정동사가 필요하고, 지문 전체가 과거 시제로 서술되므로 C 'looked'가 맞다. A 'looks'는 정동사이긴 하지만 바로 앞의 'pie'나 'rail'에 맞춘 단수 현재형이어서 복수 주어와 맞지 않고 과거 시제와도 어긋난다. B 'looking'과 D 'having looked'는 분사라서 문장에 정동사가 없게 되어 완전한 문장이 되지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this sentence is the plural noun \"tables.\" The relative clause \"that she had spread...\" and the phrase \"along with...\" don't change whether the subject is singular or plural. So the sentence needs a main verb that agrees with \"tables,\" and because the whole passage is told in the past tense, C, \"looked,\" is correct. A, \"looks,\" is a main verb, but it's singular and present tense, which makes it seem to match the nearby nouns \"pie\" or \"rail.\" It doesn't agree with \"tables,\" and it breaks from the past tense. B, \"looking,\" and D, \"having looked,\" are participles, so the sentence would be left without a main verb and wouldn't be complete.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.610Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On a 1930s Great Plains farm, Joanne's wheat-threshing festival celebration falters when the combine breaks down, revealing the family's true financial desperation.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"주어 'tables'(복수)와 관계절·'along with' 삽입구 뒤의 정동사 자리. 과거 시제 서술이므로 'looked'가 유일한 정답. A는 인접 단수 명사(pie/rail)에 끌리는 함정, B는 'cooling'과의 표면적 평행으로 그럴듯하며, D도 문법 형태상 말이 됨. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 결론과 선택지 참조가 일치하고 오류 없음. 지문은 독창적 서사로 저작권 의심 없음. 긴 삽입구 넘어 주어 찾기 + 시제 확인의 두 단계 판단이 요구되어 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"복수 주어와 동사의 일치, 삽입구 무시, 과거 시제 일관성을 함께 따져야 하므로 medium 난이도에 맞음. 비정동사 오답 두 개는 다소 쉽게 배제됨.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-m-026","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-m-027","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"At the junction below the Nuwara Eliya road, where the morning bus paused just long enough for pickers to climb aboard, Ravi noticed the young woman before she noticed him. Her sandals, caked with red mud that could only have come from the lower switchbacks, ______ far too thin for a night on the ridge, and the canvas bag she clutched looked as though it had been packed in a hurry.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["was clearly","being clearly","clearly to be","were clearly"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 절의 주어는 복수 명사 'sandals'이고, 'caked with ... switchbacks'는 주어와 동사 사이에 끼어든 수식어구이므로, 빈칸에는 복수 주어와 일치하는 정동사가 필요하다. D는 복수 과거 정동사로 뒤의 'looked'와 시제도 맞으므로 정답이다. A는 정동사이고 과거 시제지만, 가까이 있는 단수 명사 'mud'에 맞춘 단수형이라 주어와 일치하지 않는다. B의 분사와 C의 부정사는 의미상 말이 되는 듯하지만, 정동사가 아니어서 'Her sandals'로 시작하는 절에 본동사가 없게 된다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this clause is the plural noun \"sandals.\" The phrase \"caked with ... switchbacks\" is a modifier that sits between the subject and its verb, so the blank needs a finite verb that agrees with a plural subject. D supplies a plural past-tense finite verb that also matches the tense of \"looked\" later in the sentence, so it is correct. A is a finite past-tense verb, but it is singular because it agrees with the nearby noun \"mud\" instead of the real subject. B (a participle) and C (an infinitive) may seem to make sense, but neither is a finite verb, so the clause beginning with \"Her sandals\" would have no main verb.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.610Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Ravi, a tea estate supervisor, encounters a runaway from the city at a Sri Lankan mountain junction and becomes unexpectedly entangled in her escape.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"주어 'Her sandals'(복수)와 동사 사이에 'caked with red mud that ... switchbacks' 수식어구가 끼어 있어, 정동사 필요 여부 판단 + 복수 일치 확인의 두 단계가 요구됨. D 'were clearly'가 유일하게 복수 정동사이며 뒤의 'looked'와 시제 일관. A는 인접 명사 'mud'에 이끌리는 단수형 오답(부분적 근거), B·C는 비정형 동사로 절에 본동사가 없게 됨. 해설(한·영) 모두 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 지문은 창작 서사로 저작권 문제 없음. 표준 SAT medium 수준에 부합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"주어와 동사 사이에 수식어구가 끼어든 수 일치 문항으로, 끌림 요소(mud)가 있어 medium 난이도에 적합하다. B와 C는 쉽게 배제된다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-m-027","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-m-029","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Every morning Samuel squeezed into the same green matatu on Jogoo Road, his knees pressed against the seat in front of him and his lunch wrapped in newspaper on his lap. The saw that he had lent to his cousin Peter months earlier, along with the two chisels that had once belonged to Samuel's father, ______ untouched in Peter's workshop in Kariobangi, and as the matatu lurched through traffic, Samuel quietly practiced the words he might use to ask for it back.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["were sitting","was sitting","are sitting","sitting"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장의 주어는 단수 명사 'The saw'이다. 'along with the two chisels...'는 삽입된 수식어구일 뿐 주어를 복수로 만들지 않으므로 단수 동사가 필요하다. 또한 지문 전체가 과거 시제(squeezed, lurched, practiced)로 서술되므로 B가 정답이다. A는 시제는 맞지만 바로 앞의 'chisels'에 맞춘 복수 동사이고, C는 복수인 데다 현재 시제라 문맥과 맞지 않는다. D는 분사일 뿐이어서 주어 'The saw'에 정동사가 없게 된다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this sentence is the singular noun \"The saw.\" The phrase \"along with the two chisels...\" is just an interrupting modifier, and it doesn't make the subject plural, so you need a singular verb. The whole passage is also told in the past tense (squeezed, lurched, practiced), so B is correct. A has the right tense, but its plural verb matches the nearby word \"chisels\" instead of the real subject. C is plural and also switches to the present tense, which doesn't fit the context. D is only a participle, so the subject \"The saw\" would be left without a main verb.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.610Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Samuel rides the Nairobi matatu daily, his borrowed carpentry saw never returned, each morning wondering if he should finally ask for it back.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"주어 'The saw'(단수)는 관계절 'that he had lent...'와 'along with the two chisels...' 삽입구로 동사와 분리되어 있으며, 'along with'는 주어의 수를 바꾸지 않으므로 단수 동사 필요. 지문 전체 과거 시제(squeezed, lurched, practiced)와 뒤의 'ask for it back'의 단수 대명사 'it'도 B를 뒷받침. A는 인접 명사 'chisels'에 이끌린 복수 함정, C는 수·시제 모두 불일치, D는 정동사 부재로 문장 파편. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 동일 결론·글자 참조이며 정확함. 주어 식별 + 시제 확인의 두 단계 판단이 요구되어 medium에 적합. 원창작 지문으로 저작권 문제 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"단수 주어와 삽입구로 수 일치를 묻고, 시제 확인까지 해야 하는 두 단계 문항이다. 'ask for it back'의 it도 단수 saw를 가리켜 정답 B와 맞는다. A는 근처 명사 chisels에 끌리게 만든 그럴듯한 오답이다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-m-029","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-m-030","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"For eleven years, Ferhan had boarded the 6:10 ferry from Kadıköy with the same thermos and the same folded newspaper, timing his steps so that he reached the upper deck's starboard bench before anyone else. That morning, however, a sudden squall over the Bosphorus sent every passenger scrambling below, where the windows streamed with rain and the floor tilted beneath their feet. Pressed shoulder to shoulder with strangers in the stale cabin, ______","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["Ferhan's carefully rehearsed sequence of steps, thermos, and bench seemed to have become meaningless.","the thermos and newspaper that had anchored his eleven years of mornings seemed to Ferhan to have become meaningless.","Ferhan realized that his carefully rehearsed sequence of steps, thermos, and bench had become meaningless.","it became clear to Ferhan that his carefully rehearsed sequence of steps, thermos, and bench had become meaningless."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"문장 첫머리의 분사구 \"Pressed shoulder to shoulder with strangers in the stale cabin\"은 바로 뒤에 오는 주어를 꾸미므로, 그 주어는 낯선 사람들과 어깨를 맞대고 끼어 있던 사람, 즉 Ferhan이어야 한다. C는 주어 자리에 Ferhan을 두므로 수식 관계가 바르게 성립한다. A는 Ferhan이 소유격으로 들어가 있지만 실제 주어는 \"sequence\"라서 일련의 습관이 사람들 사이에 끼어 있었다는 뜻이 된다. B는 \"thermos and newspaper\"가 주어여서 보온병과 신문이 끼어 있었다는 말이 되고, D는 가주어 \"it\"이 수식을 받게 된다. A·B·D는 모두 Ferhan을 문장 안에 언급하기는 하지만 주어 자리에는 두지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The opening phrase \"Pressed shoulder to shoulder with strangers in the stale cabin\" modifies whatever comes right after it, so the subject that follows has to be the person who was pressed among strangers: Ferhan. Choice C puts Ferhan in the subject position, so the modifier attaches correctly. In choice A, Ferhan appears only as a possessive; the real subject is \"sequence,\" which means his routine was the thing pressed among strangers. In choice B, the subject is \"thermos and newspaper,\" and in choice D, the placeholder \"it\" receives the modifier. Choices A, B, and D all mention Ferhan, but none of them makes him the subject, so each creates a dangling modifier.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.610Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Ferhan commutes on the Istanbul ferry each dawn, but when a sudden storm traps passengers belowdecks, he discovers the routine he mastered has become entirely useless.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"분사구 \"Pressed shoulder to shoulder...\"의 수식 대상은 Ferhan이어야 하며, C만 Ferhan을 주어로 둔다. A(소유격 Ferhan's + 주어 sequence), D(가주어 it)는 Ferhan을 언급해 부분적으로 그럴듯한 함정으로 기능하고, B도 문법적으로는 성립하는 문장이라 비교가 필요하다. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 정답 및 선택지 글자 참조가 일치하고 모순 없음. 중간 난이도 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"현수 수식어 문항. 오답 A·B·D가 모두 Ferhan을 언급하고 있어 훑어 읽으면 끌릴 수 있게 설계되어 있다. medium에 적합하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-m-030","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-m-031","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"medium","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Captain Josiah had expected a bill of lading, not a gift. Yet the ornate wooden compass, together with the two brass hinges that held its carved lid and the folded note from Silas Marrow tucked beneath them, ______ waiting on his chart table when he returned from the pilothouse that evening. Josiah turned the instrument over in his hands, unable to decide whether his old rival meant it as a treasure or as a quiet jab at the sandbar that had grounded him the previous week.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["were","have been","being","was"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장의 주어는 단수 명사 'compass'이다. 'together with ... beneath them'은 삽입된 수식어구일 뿐 주어를 복수로 만들지 않는다. 또한 이야기가 과거 시제('returned')로 서술되므로 단수 과거 동사 D가 알맞다. A는 시제는 맞지만 바로 앞의 복수 명사 'hinges'나 'them'에 잘못 일치시킨 복수형이다. B는 복수형인 데다 현재완료여서 과거 시점인 'when he returned'와 어울리지 않는다. C는 분사라서 문장에 정동사가 없게 된다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this sentence is the singular noun \"compass.\" The phrase \"together with ... beneath them\" is just an interrupting modifier, so it doesn't make the subject plural. The narration is also in the past tense (\"returned\"), which means the sentence needs a singular past-tense verb, D. A is in the right tense, but it's plural, as if it agreed with the nearby words \"hinges\" or \"them.\" B is plural too, and its present perfect form doesn't fit the past moment set by \"when he returned.\" C is a participle, so it leaves the sentence with no main verb.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.610Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Captain Josiah receives an ornate wooden compass from a riverboat rival on the Mississippi, uncertain whether it is a treasure or a taunt about his failing navigation.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"주어 'compass'(단수)와 'together with ...' 삽입구 구조 확인 + 과거 시제('returned') 확인의 두 단계 판단이 필요한 표준 SAT 주어-동사 일치 문항. 'was'가 유일하게 단수·과거·정동사 조건을 모두 충족. A는 시제만 맞고 'hinges/them'에 끌린 복수형, B는 복수+현재완료, C는 정동사 부재로 모두 타당하게 배제됨. 한·영 해설 결론 및 선택지 참조 일치, 영어 해설 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 원작 소설 지문으로 저작권 우려 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"'together with' 삽입구로 주어와 동사 사이를 길게 떼어 놓은 주어-동사 일치 문항으로, 중간 난이도에 맞다. 다만 'the two brass hinges that held its carved lid and the folded note ... tucked beneath them'은 경첩이 뚜껑과 쪽지를 함께 고정한 것으로도 읽힐 수 있어 구문이 다소 모호하다. 정답 판정에는 영향이 없다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-m-031","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-rhetorical_synthesis-m-032","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"medium","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- \"The Third Cup\" is a 2019 short story by the fictional Ethiopian writer Hirut Bekele.\n- In the story, Desta hosts a traditional coffee ceremony for her family in Addis Ababa, roasting the green beans herself.\n- Desta has secretly bought a one-way ticket to Toronto and plans to tell her family once the first cup is poured.\n- Before the first cup is served, Almaz, a woman Desta has not seen since leaving her childhood village, knocks at the door.\n- Almaz was the person who taught Desta to roast coffee when Desta was a girl.\n- By the time Desta pours the third cup, known as the baraka, or blessing, she still has not shared her news.","question":"The student wants to explain how the visitor's appearance relates to the timing of Desta's intentions. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Desta plans to reveal her one-way ticket to Toronto as soon as the first cup is poured, but before that moment comes, Almaz, a woman from her childhood village, knocks at the door.","Desta roasts the green beans herself for the ceremony, a skill she learned as a girl from Almaz, a woman from her childhood village who later knocks at the door.","Desta plans to reveal her one-way ticket to Toronto during the ceremony, but even after the third cup, the baraka, is poured, she has not shared her news.","Desta hosts a traditional coffee ceremony for her family in Addis Ababa in \"The Third Cup,\" a 2019 short story by Hirut Bekele."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"목표는 손님의 등장이 데스타의 계획 시점과 어떻게 맞물리는지 설명하는 것이다. A는 첫 잔을 따른 뒤 알리려던 계획과, 그 순간이 오기 전에 알마즈가 문을 두드리는 장면을 함께 보여 주어 목표를 이룬다. B는 알마즈와 데스타의 과거 인연을 강조할 뿐 데스타의 계획은 다루지 않는다. C는 계획과 그 계획이 실현되지 않은 결과를 말하지만 손님의 등장을 빠뜨려 둘 사이의 관계를 보여 주지 못한다. D는 작품과 배경을 소개할 뿐 계획도 손님도 언급하지 않는다.","explanationEn":"Your goal is to show how the visitor's arrival lines up with the timing of Desta's plan. Choice A does this: it states that Desta meant to make her announcement after the first cup and that Almaz knocks before that moment comes. Choice B focuses on Desta's past connection to Almaz but never mentions Desta's plan. Choice C gives the plan and the fact that it doesn't happen, but it leaves out the visitor, so it can't show how her arrival relates to the plan. Choice D only introduces the story and its setting.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.610Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — At an Ethiopian coffee ceremony, Desta's unexpected guest—a woman from her village's past—arrives just as Desta was preparing to announce she is leaving forever.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 A 검산 일치: 계획 시점(첫 잔 후 발표)과 손님 등장(그 전에 노크)을 함께 연결하는 유일한 선택지. C는 계획·시점·결과를 담지만 손님 누락, B는 손님과 과거 인연만 담고 계획 누락으로 비교가 필요한 강한 오답이며 D도 문맥상 말이 됨. 해설 한/영 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 가상 작가·작품 명시로 저작권 문제 없음. 에티오피아 커피 의식의 세 번째 잔 'baraka' 명칭도 사실에 부합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B와 C가 각각 요소 하나씩(방문자 / 계획 시점)만 담고 있어서 둘을 비교해야 오답으로 걸러진다. 그래서 medium 난이도에 맞다. D는 너무 쉽게 배제되지만 허용 범위다. 'as soon as'는 노트의 'once'를 바꿔 쓴 표현으로 볼 수 있다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-rhetorical_synthesis-m-032","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-rhetorical_synthesis-m-034","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"medium","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- \"The Borrowed Net\" is a 2016 short story by Egyptian writer Nadia Fawzy.\n- The story is set on a rooftop in Cairo's Shubra district, where many residents keep pigeon lofts.\n- The narrator, Hassan, lends his favorite pigeon-catching net to his childhood friend Karim.\n- Hassan watches from the rooftop as Karim carries the net into the crowded streets below; Karim never returns it.\n- By the story's last page, Hassan and Karim have stopped speaking to each other.\n- Critics have noted that Fawzy uses the lost net to stand for the fading bond between the two boys.","question":"The student wants to explain what the lending episode means within the story as a whole. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["In Fawzy's \"The Borrowed Net,\" Hassan lends his net on a Shubra rooftop, a neighborhood where many Cairo residents keep pigeon lofts.","In Fawzy's \"The Borrowed Net,\" Hassan lends his favorite net to Karim, who carries it into the crowded streets and never returns it.","In Fawzy's \"The Borrowed Net,\" the net Hassan watches disappear with Karim into Cairo's streets comes to represent the friendship that quietly dissolves between them.","In Fawzy's \"The Borrowed Net,\" a 2016 story by an Egyptian writer, Hassan lends a pigeon-catching net to his childhood friend Karim."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"목표는 그물을 빌려준 일이 이야기 전체에서 어떤 의미를 갖는지 설명하는 것이다. C는 그물이 거리로 사라지는 장면과, 그물이 두 소년의 우정을 상징한다는 비평가의 해석을 연결한다. 그래서 정답이다. A는 배경인 슈브라 지역의 비둘기 사육장만 언급할 뿐 의미는 다루지 않는다. B는 줄거리를 정확하게 요약하지만 그 사건이 무엇을 상징하는지 설명하지 않는다. D는 작가와 출간 연도 같은 기본 정보와 사건만 소개하므로 목표에서 벗어난다.","explanationEn":"Your goal is to explain what lending the net means within the story as a whole. C does this by linking the net vanishing into the streets to the critics' reading that the net represents the boys' fading friendship. A only describes the setting, the pigeon lofts of Shubra, and never addresses meaning. B accurately retells the plot but never says what the event stands for. D just introduces the author, the date, and the basic event, so it also misses the goal.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.610Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On a Cairo rooftop, Hassan lends his favorite pigeon-catching net to his childhood friend and watches it disappear into the city, along with their friendship.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 C만이 비평가의 상징 해석(그물=사라지는 우정)과 사건을 연결해 '의미'를 설명하므로 옳음. B·D는 노트 정보를 정확히 사용하지만 의미 설명이 없어 비교 후 배제되고, A는 배경만 언급해 가장 약한 오답. 가상의 작품으로 저작권 문제 없음. 표준 SAT rhetorical synthesis 중간 난이도에 부합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"C만 상징적 의미(노트 6)를 사건과 연결하므로 정답이 맞다. B와 D는 대여 사건을 정확히 다루어 그럴듯한 오답이고, A는 배경만 다룬다. 'represent'가 단서가 되어 다소 쉬운 편이지만 표준 SAT medium 범위 안에 든다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-rhetorical_synthesis-m-034","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-transitions-m-037","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"medium","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"By the third week of the monsoon, the rooftop of the Shanti Niwas building had become a battlefield of clotheslines. When Rajesh stretched a blue tarp above his shirts and declared it \"a scientific advantage,\" Anaya told her sister that she refused to sink to his level; the contest, she insisted, would be won by patience and good wringing alone. ______ by Thursday she had hauled her mother's pedestal fan up four flights of stairs, run an extension cord through the stairwell window, and aimed the whirring blades squarely at her damp dupattas.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Consequently,","Nevertheless,","Similarly,","For example,"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"앞 문장에서 Anaya는 Rajesh처럼 장비를 쓰지 않고 인내와 손빨래 짜기만으로 이기겠다고 다짐한다. 그런데 다음 문장에서 그녀는 선풍기를 옥상까지 끌고 올라가 정반대 행동을 하므로, 다짐과 실제 행동이 어긋나는 대조를 나타내는 B가 맞다. A는 Rajesh의 방수포가 그녀의 대응을 불렀다고 볼 수 있어 그럴듯하지만, 바로 앞 문장의 핵심은 '그와 같은 수준으로 내려가지 않겠다'는 다짐이고, 이 다짐에서 선풍기 사용이 결과로 나올 수는 없다. C는 두 사람 모두 장비를 동원했다는 점에서 유사해 보이지만, 이 문장의 초점은 Anaya 자신의 말과 행동이 어긋난다는 데 있다. D는 선풍기 사용을 인내 전략의 한 예로 만들어 버리므로 논리에 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"In the previous sentence, Anaya vows to win with patience and wringing alone instead of copying Rajesh's gadgets. Then the next sentence shows her doing the opposite by dragging a fan up to the roof, so B is correct because it signals a contrast between her vow and what she actually does. A may seem reasonable, since Rajesh's tarp could have provoked her. But the key point of the sentence right before the blank is her promise not to sink to his level, and using a fan can't be a result of that promise. C picks up on the fact that both neighbors end up using equipment, but this sentence is about Anaya's own words clashing with her actions. D doesn't work because it would make the fan an example of her patience-only strategy.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.611Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Anaya and her neighbor Rajesh wage an increasingly absurd rooftop monsoon contest to see whose laundry dries fastest during Mumbai's heaviest rains.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"앞 문장의 '인내와 짜기만으로' 다짐과 뒤 문장의 선풍기 동원이 명확히 대조되어 B(Nevertheless)가 정답. A는 Rajesh의 방수포→대응이라는 인과로 읽힐 수 있어 유혹적이고, C도 '둘 다 장비 사용'이라는 부분 근거가 있어 비교가 필요함. D는 말이 되나 논리상 배제됨. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 동일 결론과 글자 참조, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 창작 지문으로 저작권 문제 없음. 지문 길이와 두 단계 판단(다짐 파악+행동 대조, 인과 유혹 배제)이 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"다짐과 실제 행동이 반대로 가는 대조라서 정답 B가 명확하다. A(방수포가 대응을 촉발)와 C(두 사람 모두 장비 사용)는 부분적으로 그럴듯해 오답으로 기능한다. 표준 medium 수준이다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-transitions-m-037","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-transitions-m-038","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"medium","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"On the houseboat drifting through the Kerala backwaters, Deepak turned his grandmother's sandalwood box over in his hands. His aunts had made it clear that they expected him to open it that evening, and he had even pressed his thumb against the brass latch until it gave a small click. ______ he set the box on the shelf beside her old prayer lamp, the latch closed again, deciding that whatever she had kept inside could stay hers a little longer.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Moreover,","As a result,","Instead,","For instance,"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"앞 문장은 가족의 기대와 걸쇠를 누른 행동으로 상자를 열 것 같은 방향을 제시하고, 빈칸 뒤에서는 상자를 닫은 채 선반에 두기로 한다. 예상된 행동 대신 다른 행동을 택한 것이므로 대안·반전을 나타내는 C가 정답이다. A는 같은 방향의 정보를 덧붙이는 표현인데, 뒤 문장은 앞의 흐름을 뒤집는다. B는 걸쇠를 누른 것이 상자를 닫아 두는 결과로 이어진 것처럼 만들어 인과 방향이 맞지 않는다. D는 뒤 문장을 앞 내용의 예시로 만들지만, 상자를 열지 않는 것은 열려는 기대의 예가 아니다.","explanationEn":"The earlier sentence leans toward opening the box: his aunts expect it, and Deepak even clicks the latch. The next sentence goes the other way, because he puts the box away still closed. He chooses a different action from the one that was expected, so the reversal word in C fits. A adds information that continues in the same direction, but this sentence reverses the earlier one. B treats closing the box as a result of pressing the latch, which gets the cause and effect wrong. D presents the sentence as an example, but leaving the box closed is not an example of the expectation that he would open it.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.611Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Deepak inherits his grandmother's small sandalwood box on the Kerala houseboat and must decide whether to open it or preserve it unopened.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"앞 문장(열 것이라는 기대·걸쇠 클릭)과 뒤 문장(닫은 채 선반에 둠)의 관계는 예상 행동의 대체·반전이므로 'Instead'가 유일하게 성립한다. 뒤 문장의 절대구문(\"the latch closed again\")도 문법적으로 자연스럽다. A(Moreover)는 앞 문장이 행동 나열이라 훑어 읽으면 선택할 수 있고, B(As a result)는 걸쇠를 눌렀다는 직전 행동과 표면적 인과를 만들어 부분적 근거가 있다. D는 명백히 어긋나지만 말은 된다. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 C를 지지하며 글자 참조와 논리가 일치하고, 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 독창적 서사 지문으로 저작권 문제 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"기대·걸쇠를 누른 행동 → 닫힌 채 보관으로 이어지는 반전 구조라 Instead가 유일하게 맞다. 걸쇠를 누른 행동이 표면적인 인과 연결을 만들어 B가 그럴듯한 오답이 된다. 중간 난이도의 하단에 해당한다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-transitions-m-038","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-boundaries-e-042","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"easy","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"For twenty years, Amaan and Karim had worked side by side at the tannery on the riverbank, dipping hides into the dye pits each morning. Lately, the two partners spoke only about leather______ man could say exactly when the silence between them had begun.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":[", neither"," neither","; neither",", which neither"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"빈칸 앞 'the two partners spoke only about leather'와 뒤 'neither man could say ...'는 각각 독립절이다. 접속사 없이 두 독립절을 잇는 데는 세미콜론이 맞으므로 C가 정답이다. A는 쉼표만으로 두 독립절을 이어 쉼표 스플라이스가 된다. B는 문장부호 없이 이어 붙인 융합문(run-on)이다. D는 'which'로 관계절을 만들지만 뒤 내용이 관계절 구조에 맞지 않아 비문이 된다.","explanationEn":"The text before the blank (\"the two partners spoke only about leather\") and the text after it (\"neither man could say...\") are both independent clauses. When you join two independent clauses without a conjunction, a semicolon works, so C is correct. A uses only a comma, which makes a comma splice. B has no punctuation at all, which makes a run-on sentence. D adds \"which\" to start a relative clause, but the words after it don't fit that structure, so the sentence becomes ungrammatical.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.611Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Amaan and Karim, tannery partners at the Moroccan riverside for twenty years, have stopped speaking except to discuss leather, and neither knows when it began.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"빈칸 앞뒤 모두 독립절('the two partners spoke only about leather' / 'neither man could say ... begun')이므로 세미콜론(C)이 유일하게 맞음. A는 쉼표 스플라이스, B는 융합문, D는 'which'가 이끄는 관계절이 뒤 구조와 맞지 않아 비문. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 정답과 선택지 참조가 일치하고 결론이 동일함. 단일 규칙(독립절 연결 부호)으로 풀리고 오답이 전형적 오개념이라 easy에 적합. 사소하게 선택지 B 앞 공백이 두 칸인 점만 표기상 미세한 흠."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"독립절 두 개를 세미콜론으로 잇는 단일 규칙 문항이다. 오답은 쉼표 스플라이스, 융합문, 관계절 오용으로 전형적인 오개념들이다. 선택지 B에 공백이 두 칸 들어간 것은 표시상의 사소한 문제다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sv-boundaries-e-042","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-e-044","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"easy","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Kamau sits by the window of the crowded matatu as it lurches down Ngong Road toward the city center. On his wrist is his father's watch, the same one his father carried home from a war many years ago. A jeweler in Nairobi has just finished restoring it. Now the watch, with its newly polished hands, ______ the afternoon light each time the vehicle turns, and the strangers beside him lean closer to study its mended face.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["catches","catch","are catching","have caught"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"빈칸에 들어갈 동사의 주어는 단수 명사 'the watch'이고, 'with its newly polished hands'는 주어와 동사 사이에 끼어든 수식어일 뿐이다. 따라서 단수 현재형 동사가 필요하며, 지문 전체가 현재 시제(sits, lean)로 서술되므로 A가 정답이다. B, C, D는 모두 복수 주어에 맞는 동사형으로, 수식어 속 복수 명사 'hands'를 주어로 착각하게 만드는 오답이다. 문장의 실제 주어는 단수인 'watch'이므로 B, C, D는 수 일치가 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The subject of the verb in the blank is the singular noun \"the watch.\" The phrase \"with its newly polished hands\" is just a modifier that sits between the subject and the verb. That means you need a singular present-tense verb, and the passage is told in the present tense (\"sits,\" \"lean\"), so A is correct. B, C, and D are all verb forms that go with plural subjects, and they trick you into treating the plural noun \"hands\" inside the modifier as the subject. Since the real subject, \"watch,\" is singular, B, C, and D don't agree with it in number.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.611Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On a Nairobi matatu, Kamau carries his father's restored watch—the same watch his father carried home from a war—and watches strangers study its repaired face.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"주어 'the watch'(단수) + 끼어든 수식어 'with its newly polished hands' 구조. 현재 시제 서술(sits, lean)에 맞춰 단수 현재형 'catches'(A)만 적합. B/C/D는 모두 복수형으로 'hands'에 이끌리는 전형적 오개념 오답. 한·영 해설 모두 정답 및 선택지 참조 일치, 한글 혼입 없음. 단일 규칙(수 일치)으로 해결되어 easy 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"주어 'the watch'(단수)와 동사의 수 일치를 묻는 문항이다. 끼어든 'with its newly polished hands'가 오답을 유도한다. 판단 규칙이 하나뿐이라 easy 수준에 맞다. 오답 B·C·D는 모두 복수형이라 규칙만 알면 바로 걸러진다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-e-044","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-e-045","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"easy","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In the Kyoto pottery district, Akiko and Tomoe once shared a single wheel, laughing as wet clay spun between their hands. Now their two studios face each other across a narrow alley that neither woman ever crosses. Each morning, the row of glazed bowls in Akiko's window ______ in the early light, and each morning Tomoe pretends not to notice them.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["shine","shines","are shining","have shone"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장의 주어는 단수 명사 \"row\"이고, \"of glazed bowls in Akiko's window\"는 주어를 꾸미는 수식어일 뿐이다. 따라서 단수 동사가 필요하고, 같은 문장의 \"pretends\"와 같은 현재 시제여야 하므로 B \"shines\"가 정답이다. A, C, D는 모두 복수 동사(shine, are, have)를 써서 바로 앞의 복수 명사 \"bowls\"에 수를 맞춘 오류이다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this clause is the singular noun \"row\"; the phrase \"of glazed bowls in Akiko's window\" only modifies it. So you need a singular verb in the present tense, which matches \"pretends\" later in the sentence. That makes B, \"shines,\" correct. A, C, and D all use plural verb forms (shine, are, have), which wrongly agree with the nearby plural noun \"bowls\" instead of the actual subject.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.611Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — In the Kyoto pottery district, Akiko and Tomoe once threw clay together, but now their studios face each other across an alley they never cross.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"주어 \"row\"(단수) + 수식어구 \"of glazed bowls in Akiko's window\"에 의한 전형적 주어-동사 일치 문항. \"each morning ... pretends\"가 현재 시제 단서로 작동하여 B \"shines\"만 적합. A/C/D는 모두 인접 복수 명사 \"bowls\"에 끌린 복수형 오답으로 오개념 기반 매력도 적절. 해설(한·영) 결론·글자 참조 일치, 한글 혼입 없음. 지문 창작물로 저작권 문제 없음. easy 난이도 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"단수 주어 row와 수식어 of glazed bowls 사이의 주어-동사 수일치 문항으로, 규칙 하나만 알면 풀 수 있다. 오답 A, C, D는 모두 가까운 복수 명사 bowls에 동사를 맞춘 전형적인 오개념이라 easy 난이도에 맞다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-e-045","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-e-046","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"easy","skill":"form_structure_sense","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"On the night of his final concert with the Bavarian brass band, Ernst lifted the trumpet his grandfather had repaired decades earlier. He ran his thumb along the bell, feeling each small hollow in the brass. The dents on the old instrument ______ reminders of stories that no one in the band could remember anymore, yet Ernst felt them all as he raised the trumpet to play.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["was","is","were","has been"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 문장의 주어는 복수 명사 \"The dents\"이며, \"on the old instrument\"는 주어를 꾸미는 전치사구일 뿐이다. 또한 이야기가 과거 시제(lifted, ran, felt)로 서술되므로 복수 과거형 동사가 필요하다. 따라서 C \"were\"가 정답이다. A \"was\"와 D \"has been\"은 단수 동사여서 수가 맞지 않으며, 바로 앞의 단수 명사 \"instrument\"에 이끌려 고르기 쉬운 오답이다. B \"is\"는 단수인 데다 현재 시제라서 수와 시제가 모두 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The subject of this sentence is the plural noun \"The dents.\" The phrase \"on the old instrument\" only describes the subject. The story is also told in the past tense (lifted, ran, felt), so you need a plural past-tense verb. That makes C, \"were,\" the correct answer. A (\"was\") and D (\"has been\") are singular verbs, so they don't agree with the subject. They're easy to pick by mistake because the singular noun \"instrument\" comes right before the blank. B (\"is\") is wrong on both counts: it's singular, and it's in the present tense.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.611Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Ernst, the Bavarian brass band's trumpet player, plays his final concert with an instrument his grandfather repaired, the dents telling stories no one remembers.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"주어 \"The dents\"(복수) + 과거 시제 서술 → \"were\"가 유일하게 맞음. 오답 3개 모두 단수형으로, 직전 명사 \"instrument\"에 의한 근접 일치 오개념을 겨냥한 전형적 오답. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 정답 C와 글자 참조가 일치하고 모순 없음. 단일 규칙·한 단계 추론으로 easy에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"주어-동사 수 일치 문제로, 주어와 동사 사이에 전치사구가 끼어 있음. 복수 주어 \"dents\"와 과거 시제 문맥이 맞으므로 정답은 were. 함정이 하나뿐인 전형적인 easy 문항임.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sv-form_structure_sense-e-046","intendedSkill":"form_structure_sense","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-transitions-e-047","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"easy","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"At the fish camp on Bayou Lafourche, Chet kept his cypress netting needle in his shirt pocket at all times, and for thirty years he had refused to let anyone else use it, not even his own sons. ______ when his cousin Remy, visiting from Texas for only one night, asked to borrow it to mend a torn cast net, Chet handed it over without a word, already suspecting that Remy might leave before dawn and never come back.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Similarly,","For example,","Therefore,","Yet"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"첫 문장은 Chet이 30년 동안 아무에게도, 아들에게조차 바늘을 빌려주지 않았다고 말하고, 두 번째 문장은 그가 사촌에게 아무 말 없이 바늘을 건넸다고 한다. 두 문장은 예상과 반대되는 대조 관계이므로 D가 정답이다. A는 비슷한 행동을 덧붙일 때 쓰는데, 바늘을 건넨 행동은 거절하던 습관과 정반대이다. B는 앞 내용의 예시를 들 때 쓰지만, 바늘을 건넨 것은 거절하는 습관의 예가 될 수 없다. C는 결과를 나타내는데, 늘 거절해 왔다는 사실에서 바늘을 건넸다는 결과가 나오지는 않는다.","explanationEn":"The first sentence tells you that Chet refused for thirty years to let anyone use his needle, not even his sons. The second sentence says he handed it to his cousin without a word. That is the opposite of what you would expect, so the sentences are in contrast, and D is correct. A is for adding a similar action, but handing over the needle goes against his habit of refusing. B introduces an example, but giving the needle away can't be an example of always refusing. C signals a result, and his long refusal doesn't lead to him handing the needle over.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.611Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — At a Louisiana bayou fish camp, Chet lends his favorite net-weaving tool to a visiting kinsman and realizes he may never see the man again.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"첫 문장(30년간 아무에게도 빌려주지 않음)과 둘째 문장(사촌에게 말없이 건넴)은 명백한 대조 관계로, 유일한 대조 전환어 D \"Yet\"이 정답임을 직접 검산함. \"Yet when ..., Chet handed it over\"는 문법적으로도 자연스러움. 오답 A(유사), B(예시), C(결과)는 전형적 오개념 선택지로 적절. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 D를 일관되게 뒷받침하며 글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 단일 규칙·한 단계 추론으로 easy 난이도에 부합. 원작 지문은 창작으로 보이며 저작권 의심 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"명확한 대조 관계. 'Yet' 뒤 쉼표 없음은 SAT 관례상 허용. 오답들은 전형적인 오개념이다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sv-transitions-e-047","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-transitions-e-048","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"easy","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Sophia stood at the ferry kiosk on the island of Naxos, holding a ticket she had not yet decided to use. Thirty years earlier, she had promised an old sailor named Stavros that she would come back every summer to wait for his boat at this very dock. She had kept that promise for exactly one summer. ______ she had moved to Athens, married, and let the island fade into a story she rarely told.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["After that,","For example,","In contrast,","Similarly,"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"빈칸 앞 문장은 소피아가 약속을 단 한 번의 여름 동안만 지켰다고 말하고, 뒤 문장은 그 이후 그녀가 아테네로 이사하고 결혼한 일을 말하므로 시간 순서를 잇는 A가 정답이다. B는 예시를 나타내지만, 이사와 결혼은 한 번 약속을 지킨 일의 예가 아니다. C는 대조를 나타내는데, 뒤 문장은 앞 문장과 맞서는 내용이 아니라 그다음에 일어난 일이다. D는 비슷한 내용을 나타내지만 두 문장은 비슷한 행동을 말하고 있지 않다.","explanationEn":"The sentence before the blank says Sophia kept her promise for only one summer. The sentence after it tells what happened next: she moved to Athens and got married. Since these events come one after another in time, A is correct. B signals an example, but moving and marrying aren't examples of keeping the promise once. C signals a contrast, but the second sentence doesn't oppose the first; it simply continues the story in time. D signals similarity, but the two sentences don't describe similar actions.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.611Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — On a Greek island ferry kiosk, Sophia remembers she once promised an old sailor she would return to wait for his boat, a vow she abandoned thirty years ago.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"앞 문장(한 번의 여름 동안 약속 이행) → 뒤 문장(아테네 이주·결혼·섬을 잊음)은 명백한 시간적 순서이므로 'After that,'(A)이 유일하게 논리적임. B(예시)·D(유사)는 관계 불일치, C(대조)는 뒤 문장이 앞 문장과 맞서는 내용이 아니므로 배제됨. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 A를 일관되게 지지하고 선택지 글자 참조가 정확하며 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 서술은 창작 지문으로 저작권 우려 없음. 시간 순서 전환어라는 단일 개념으로 한 단계 추론만 필요해 easy에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"The answer depends on one clue that sits right next to the blank: \"for exactly one summer\" leads into what happened next, so the time-sequence transition is correct. C is a believable wrong answer because keeping the promise and then dropping it can look like a contrast, but the sequence reading fits better. Overall the item suits the easy level.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sv-transitions-e-048","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-rhetorical_synthesis-e-049","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"easy","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- \"The Dented Bell\" is a 2019 short story by the German writer Lena Haubrich.\n- The story is set in a small Bavarian village, at a weekly rehearsal of the local brass band.\n- Its main character is Anton, the band's elderly tuba player.\n- Anton arrives late to rehearsal because his tuba was damaged when it fell from his bicycle.\n- When he plays the damaged tuba, its tone is softer and warmer than the band has ever heard before.\n- The story was translated into English in 2022.","question":"The student wants to describe the surprising event at the center of the story. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["In Lena Haubrich's 2019 short story \"The Dented Bell,\" a brass band in a small Bavarian village holds its weekly rehearsal.","In Lena Haubrich's short story \"The Dented Bell,\" Anton's tuba, damaged in a fall from his bicycle, produces a softer and warmer tone than the band has ever heard.","In Lena Haubrich's short story \"The Dented Bell,\" which was translated into English in 2022, the main character is an elderly tuba player named Anton.","In Lena Haubrich's short story \"The Dented Bell,\" Anton's tuba is repaired after a fall from his bicycle so that it sounds the same as it always did."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"목표는 이야기 중심의 놀라운 사건을 묘사하는 것이다. B는 망가진 튜바가 오히려 밴드가 들어 본 적 없는 부드럽고 따뜻한 소리를 낸다는 점을 전해 목표에 맞는다. A는 배경(마을, 연습)만 소개하고 놀라운 사건이 없다. C는 번역 연도와 주인공 소개일 뿐 사건을 다루지 않는다. D는 튜바가 수리되어 예전과 같은 소리를 낸다고 해 메모 내용과 어긋나는 부정확한 진술이다.","explanationEn":"Your goal is to describe the surprising event at the heart of the story. B does this: it explains that Anton's tuba, damaged in a fall, makes a softer and warmer tone than the band has ever heard. A only gives the setting (the village and the rehearsal) and doesn't mention anything surprising. C tells you the translation date and introduces the main character, but it doesn't describe an event. D is inaccurate, because the notes never say the tuba is repaired or that it sounds the same as before.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.611Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — At a Bavarian village brass band rehearsal, the tuba player arrives with a malfunctioning instrument that somehow sounds more beautiful broken than it ever did whole.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"B가 \"놀라운 사건\"(망가진 튜바가 더 좋은 소리를 냄)을 메모 그대로 정확히 전달한다. A·C는 목표(사건 묘사)와 무관한 배경·메타 정보, D는 메모에 없는 내용(수리, 동일한 소리)으로 부정확하여 배제된다. 한·영 해설 모두 B를 일관되게 뒷받침하며 선택지 참조가 일치하고 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 단일 규칙(목표에 맞는 관련 정보 선택)으로 풀리고 단서가 명시적이어서 easy 적합. 가상의 작가·작품으로 저작권 문제 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"목표와 일치하는 단서가 명확하고, 오답은 배경만 소개하거나 사건을 다루지 않거나 메모 내용과 어긋나는 전형적 유형이다. D는 메모에 없는 내용이라 쉽게 배제되지만 easy 수준에서는 허용된다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sv-rhetorical_synthesis-e-049","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-rhetorical_synthesis-e-050","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"easy","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- \"The Extra Bowl\" is a short story by a Vietnamese American writer.\n- It is set in a street-food alley in Hanoi at dawn.\n- Its main character is Tuan, a seven-year-old boy who helps at his aunt's noodle stall.\n- Every morning, an old man orders two bowls of soup but eats only one.\n- Tuan finally asks the adults why no one seems to notice the untouched bowl.","question":"The student wants to tell readers who the main character of the story is and where the story takes place. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["\"The Extra Bowl\" is a short story by a Vietnamese American writer about an old man who orders two bowls of soup.","In \"The Extra Bowl,\" an old man orders two bowls of soup every morning but eats only one of them.","\"The Extra Bowl\" follows Tuan, a seven-year-old boy who helps at a noodle stall in a Hanoi street-food alley at dawn.","In \"The Extra Bowl,\" a boy finally asks the adults why no one notices a bowl of soup that is never eaten."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"목표는 주인공이 누구인지와 이야기의 배경을 함께 밝히는 것이다. C는 주인공(일곱 살 소년 Tuan)과 배경(새벽의 하노이 길거리 음식 골목)을 모두 담고 있다. A는 작가와 노인 손님 이야기만 하고 주인공과 배경은 빠져 있다. B는 노인의 행동만 설명하며 주인공도 배경도 나오지 않는다. D는 소년의 질문을 언급하지만 이름도 배경도 밝히지 않는다.","explanationEn":"Your goal is to say who the main character is and where the story takes place. C does both: it names Tuan, a seven-year-old boy, and places the story in a Hanoi street-food alley at dawn. A gives the author and the old customer but leaves out the main character and the setting. B only describes what the old man does, so it has neither the main character nor the setting. D mentions a boy's question but doesn't give his name or say where the story happens.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.611Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — In Hanoi's dawn street-food alley, seven-year-old Tuan notices a customer always orders extra soup but leaves it untouched—and finally asks why no one else sees it.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 C만 주인공(Tuan)과 배경(하노이 골목, 새벽)을 모두 포함. A·B는 노인 중심, D는 소년을 언급하나 이름·배경 없음 — 전형적 오답. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 일치하고 정확함. 가상의 작품으로 저작권 문제 없음. 두 요소 매칭만으로 풀리는 easy 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"정답은 C 하나뿐이다. 오답 선택지들은 이야기의 다른 사실을 담고 있어 그럴듯해 보이지만, 주인공과 배경을 둘 다 담고 있는지만 확인하면 바로 지울 수 있다. 조건 하나만 확인하면 풀리므로 쉬움(easy) 난이도에 맞다. D는 소년을 언급하지만 이름과 배경이 빠져 있다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sv-rhetorical_synthesis-e-050","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-052","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Around 1415, the Florentine architect Filippo Brunelleschi painted a small panel of the Baptistery of San Giovanni as seen from the doorway of the cathedral opposite it. He drilled a hole through the panel so that a viewer could stand where he had stood, look through the back, and check the painted image against the real building reflected in a handheld mirror. Brunelleschi's skill had come from years of measuring ruined Roman buildings and drawing plans for builders, work that required him to turn three-dimensional spaces into exact lines on a flat surface.\n\nBrunelleschi never wrote down his method, however. What we know of the demonstration comes mostly from a biography written decades later by Antonio Manetti. It was the humanist Leon Battista Alberti who, in his 1435 treatise On Painting, explained linear perspective as a set of geometric steps that any painter could follow. Historians therefore credit Brunelleschi with showing that a single fixed viewpoint could produce a convincing image, and they credit Alberti with turning that demonstration into a method that could be taught.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Brunelleschi showed through a hands-on experiment, drawing on his architectural training, that a fixed-viewpoint image could look convincing, but another writer was the one who made the technique teachable.","Brunelleschi's panel of the Baptistery shows that his training in measuring Roman ruins was more important to his career than his work as a painter.","Brunelleschi wrote down linear perspective as a set of geometric steps, and Alberti later spread those steps to painters across Florence.","Brunelleschi's demonstration is known mainly through Manetti's biography, which suggests that historians doubt the experiment ever happened."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"A가 정답이다. 첫 단락은 건축 측량 경험에 바탕을 둔 브루넬레스키의 시연을, 둘째 단락은 그가 방법을 글로 남기지 않았고 알베르티가 이를 가르칠 수 있는 방법으로 정리했다는 점을 말하므로, A가 두 단락을 함께 아우른다. B는 측량 훈련이라는 세부 내용을 다루지만, 지문은 그 훈련이 화가로서의 일보다 더 중요했다고 비교하지 않는다. C는 알베르티의 역할을 언급하지만 브루넬레스키가 방법을 기록했다고 하여 지문의 'never wrote down'과 모순된다. D는 마네티의 전기라는 세부 사항을 가져오지만, 역사가들이 시연 자체를 의심한다는 내용은 지문 어디에도 없다.","explanationEn":"A is correct. The first paragraph describes Brunelleschi's demonstration, which grew out of his experience measuring buildings. The second paragraph explains that he never recorded his method and that Alberti turned it into steps painters could learn, so A is the only choice that covers both paragraphs. B picks up the detail about his surveying training, but the text never says that training mattered more than his painting. C mentions Alberti's role, but it claims Brunelleschi wrote down the method, which contradicts the text's statement that he \"never wrote down his method.\" D draws on the detail about Manetti's biography, but nothing in the text says historians doubt the experiment happened.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.611Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — The development of perspectiva artificialis in Filippo Brunelleschi's architectural treatises and panel painting","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"지정 정답 A 검산 결과 옳음: 1단락(건축 측량 경험에 기반한 고정 시점 시연)과 2단락(기록 부재, 알베르티가 가르칠 수 있는 방법으로 정리, 역사가들의 공로 배분)을 모두 포괄한다. B는 '화가로서의 일보다 중요'라는 비교가 지문에 없음, C는 'never wrote down his method'와 직접 모순, D는 역사가들의 의심이 지문에 없음(지문은 오히려 역사가들이 공로를 인정한다고 서술). 한국어·영어 해설 모두 같은 결론과 선택지 참조를 가지며 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 역사적 사실(1415년경 시연, 마네티 전기, 알베르티 1435년 On Painting) 문제 없음. 지문은 창작문으로 저작권 의심 없음. 난이도: 두 단락의 정보를 연결해야 하고 B·C·D가 각각 지문 세부(측량 훈련·알베르티·마네티)를 부분적으로 차용하여 비교가 필요하므로 medium에 적합. 다만 정답 A가 다른 선택지보다 눈에 띄게 길어 길이 단서가 될 수 있는 점은 참고."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"정답 A는 두 단락을 모두 아우르는 진술이다. 오답 B·C·D는 각각 지문의 세부 내용 하나를 붙잡고 왜곡하는 방식이라 그럴듯하게 읽힌다. 다만 C는 'never wrote down'과 정면으로 모순되어 쉽게 배제된다. A는 다른 선택지보다 눈에 띄게 길어 길이가 단서가 될 수 있지만, 이것만으로 판정을 바꿀 정도는 아니다. 역사적 사실(1415년경 시연, 1435년 『회화론』, 마네티의 전기)은 통설과 맞는다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-052","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-053","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In his 1880 essay \"The Experimental Novel,\" Émile Zola argued that the novelist should work like a physiologist, placing characters in carefully observed conditions and recording how heredity and environment shape their behavior. Critics often mocked this analogy, pointing out that a novelist, unlike a scientist, invents both the experiment and its outcome. Yet Zola's working notebooks suggest that the analogy guided his practice more than his critics assumed. Before drafting Germinal (1885), he spent a week in the mining region near Anzin, descending into a pit, interviewing workers, and sketching the layout of miners' cottages; for other novels he compiled files of newspaper clippings, railway timetables, and department-store catalogs. Literary historians who have examined these files note that Zola rarely altered the documented details to suit his plots. Instead, he frequently revised plot events that conflicted with what he had recorded, letting the gathered evidence constrain what his imagined characters could plausibly do.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Zola's critics were correct that his fiction was not truly scientific, because his notebooks show that he invented the outcomes of his characters' lives.","Although Zola's comparison of novelists to scientists was ridiculed, his habit of letting collected documentation limit his storytelling shows that the comparison shaped how he actually wrote.","Zola's visit to the Anzin mining region was the primary reason that Germinal became more widely read than his other novels.","Although Zola gathered extensive documentation for his novels, he regularly changed recorded details whenever they interfered with the plots he had already planned."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 비평가들이 졸라의 과학자 비유를 조롱했지만, 노트를 보면 그가 수집한 증거에 맞춰 줄거리를 고쳤으므로 그 비유가 실제 창작을 이끌었다는 것을 말한다. 따라서 B가 정답이다. A는 비평가의 지적을 언급하지만, 지문은 그 비판을 반박하는 방향으로 전개된다. C는 지문에 있는 안쟁 방문을 다루지만, 작품의 인기는 언급되지 않는다. D는 자료를 많이 모았다는 점은 맞지만, 졸라가 세부를 고친 것이 아니라 줄거리를 고쳤다는 지문 내용과 반대이다.","explanationEn":"The text says critics mocked Zola's scientist analogy, but his notebooks show he revised plots to fit the evidence he had gathered, so the analogy really did guide how he wrote. That makes B correct. A brings up the critics' objection, but the text goes on to challenge that objection rather than support it. C mentions the Anzin visit, which is in the text, but the text never says anything about how popular Germinal was. D is right that Zola gathered a lot of documentation, but it reverses the key detail: he changed his plots, not the details he had recorded.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.611Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — Émile Zola's naturalist literary theory and documentary evidence collection method in novel composition","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B는 지문의 'Yet' 전환 이후 핵심 주장(자료가 줄거리를 제약 → 비유가 실제 창작을 이끔)을 정확히 요약. A는 비평가 입장(지문이 반박), C는 인기 언급 없음, D는 세부/줄거리 수정 관계를 뒤집음. 한·영 해설 모두 B를 일관되게 뒷받침하며 글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 1880 에세이·1885 Germinal·Anzin 방문 등 사실 관계 정확. 두 정보(비판+노트 증거) 연결이 필요하고 D가 강한 오답이므로 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"A와 D는 지문 일부에 근거가 있어 비교가 필요하고, C는 그럴듯하지만 근거가 없는 오답이다. 졸라의 1880년 에세이, 1885년 Germinal, 안쟁 방문 등 사실관계도 정확하다. 중간 난이도에 맞다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-053","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-054","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Before 1908, even the most chromatic Western music still relied on an underlying hierarchy: dissonant chords, however lush, were heard as tensions that would eventually resolve to a stable tonic. In works such as his Second String Quartet and the piano pieces of Op. 11, Arnold Schoenberg abandoned that expectation. Critics at the time often described the results as chaotic, assuming that without a home key the music lacked any organizing logic. Yet Schoenberg's scores reveal a different kind of coherence. Rather than treating dissonances as unstable sounds requiring resolution, he let them stand as independent sonorities, and he unified passages by repeating and transforming small groups of intervals, so that a brief melodic cell might reappear as a chord, in inversion, or at a new pitch level. What listeners perceived as disorder was, in this view, a shift from organization by key to organization by intervallic motive.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Schoenberg's early atonal works were initially criticized as chaotic, but later audiences came to prefer them to the chromatic music that preceded them.","Schoenberg's early atonal works intensified the chromatic dissonance of earlier music while still resolving those dissonances to a stable tonic.","Schoenberg's early atonal works replaced the key-based hierarchy of tonal music with a structure built from recurring, transformed interval patterns.","Schoenberg's early atonal works lacked a home key, which is why critics concluded that the pieces had no organizing logic at all."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 글은 쇤베르크가 조성의 위계(불협화음이 으뜸음으로 해결되는 원리)를 버렸지만, 작은 음정 묶음을 반복·변형해 새로운 통일성을 만들었다고 주장하므로 C가 정답이다. A는 당시 비평이 혼란스럽다고 했다는 사실은 맞지만, 후대 청중이 더 선호하게 되었다는 내용은 지문에 없다. B는 불협화음이 강조되었다는 점은 비슷하지만, 해결되었다는 부분이 지문과 정반대이다. D는 으뜸조가 없었고 비평가들이 논리가 없다고 봤다는 세부 사항은 맞지만, 그 견해를 반박하는 글의 핵심 주장을 놓치고 있다.","explanationEn":"The text argues that Schoenberg gave up the tonal hierarchy, where dissonances resolve to a tonic, but built coherence in a new way by repeating and transforming small interval groups, so C is correct. A is right that critics called the music chaotic, but the text never says later audiences came to prefer it. B gets the heightened dissonance right, but the text says the dissonances were not resolved, which is the opposite of what B claims. D accurately reports that the music had no home key and that critics saw no logic in it, but it misses the text's main point, which is to argue against that critical view.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.611Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — The harmonic innovations of Arnold Schoenberg's early atonal works challenging tonal functionality principles","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"지문의 핵심 주장(조성 위계 → 음정 동기에 의한 조직으로의 전환)을 C가 정확히 요약함. A·D는 지문의 세부 사실(당시 비평의 '혼란' 평가, 으뜸조 부재)을 부분적으로 포함해 비교가 필요하고, B는 '해결'이라는 핵심 전제에서 지문과 정반대이나 훑어 읽으면 그럴듯함. 역사적 사실(제2현악4중주 1908, Op. 11 1909)도 정확. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 선택지 참조와 결론이 일치하며 자연스러움."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"C는 '조성 위계 포기'와 '음정 동기를 통한 조직'을 모두 담고 있어 핵심 주장과 정확히 맞는다. D는 지문 세부 사항을 정확히 담았지만 글이 반박하는 비평가 견해에 머물러 있어 훑어 읽으면 고르기 쉬운 매력적 오답이다. A와 B도 각각 부분적 근거가 있다. 2판 Op.10(1908), Op.11(1909) 연대는 사실과 맞는다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-054","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-055","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Modern readers often assume that Sappho's poems survive only in tatters because ancient readers found her expressions of desire for women too troubling to preserve. The evidence of transmission, however, points elsewhere. Classicist Camille Hardwick notes that Sappho wrote in the Aeolic dialect of Lesbos, whose unfamiliar vowels and word forms made her verses increasingly difficult for later Greek scribes and schoolteachers to read. As literary education across the Greek-speaking world came to favor Attic and Ionic authors, copies of Sappho were made less often, and her collected books gradually fell out of circulation.\n\nHardwick points out that this explanation also fits what does survive. Many of the fragments, including lines frankly describing longing for a woman, were preserved because grammarians and critics quoted them to illustrate rare Aeolic words or admirable meter, and others turned up on discarded papyri in Egyptian rubbish heaps. If ancient copyists had been purging erotic content, Hardwick argues, such passages would hardly be among the pieces that reached us.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Ancient grammarians and critics valued Sappho's poems mainly for their rare Aeolic words and skillful meter rather than for their descriptions of desire.","Sappho's poems about desire for women were less widely copied than her other works because later Greek scribes found them hard to read.","Fragments of Sappho recovered from Egyptian papyri give a fuller picture of her poetry than the lines quoted by ancient writers.","The survival of Sappho's poetry in fragments likely owes more to changing tastes in language and education than to discomfort with its subject matter."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 사포 시가 단편으로만 남은 이유가 동성 욕망에 대한 거부감이 아니라 아이올리스 방언의 난해함과 교육 선호의 변화 때문이라는 Hardwick의 주장, 그리고 남은 단편이 이를 뒷받침한다는 근거를 제시하므로 D가 정답이다. A는 문법학자들이 단편을 인용한 이유라는 세부 근거일 뿐 중심 생각이 아니다. B는 방언 문제를 언급하지만 욕망을 다룬 시만 덜 필사되었다고 주제와 섞어 왜곡한다. C는 파피루스와 인용 단편을 비교하는데, 지문에는 그런 비교가 없다.","explanationEn":"The text presents Hardwick's argument that Sappho's poems survive only in fragments because her Aeolic dialect was hard to read and education came to favor other dialects, not because readers objected to her desire for women. The surviving erotic fragments are then used as support, so D is correct. A describes why grammarians quoted certain lines, but that's only a supporting detail, not the main idea. B mentions the dialect problem but wrongly claims that the poems about desire in particular were copied less, which mixes the two explanations together. C compares papyrus finds with quoted lines, and the text never makes that comparison.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.612Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — Sappho's lyric fragments and ancient Greek homoerotic desire representation in archaic poetry transmission","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"지문 전체(1문단의 대안 설명 + 2문단의 뒷받침 근거)를 종합해야 D가 중심 생각임을 확인할 수 있다. A는 2문단의 세부 근거를 중심 생각으로 과장한 오답, B는 방언 설명과 욕망 주제를 뒤섞은 왜곡 오답으로 각각 부분적 근거를 가지며, C는 지문에 없는 비교지만 파피루스·인용 언급으로 표면상 그럴듯하다. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 D를 일관되게 뒷받침하고 선택지 참조가 일치한다. 사포가 아이올리스 방언으로 썼다는 사실과 방언 난해성이 전승 단절의 원인이라는 설명은 실제 학설과 부합한다. 지문 자체는 창작으로 보이며 저작권 문제 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"A·B는 부분 근거가 있어 비교가 필요하고, C도 그럴듯하다. 중간 난이도에 적합하다. Hardwick는 가상의 인물로 보이지만 문제없다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-055","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-056","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In the 1940s, the architect Le Corbusier introduced the Modulor, a system of measurements derived from the height of a standing man with a raised arm and subdivided according to the golden ratio. Le Corbusier promoted it as a rational tool that would bring universal harmony to building design, and he applied it to projects such as the Unité d'Habitation in Marseille, where ceiling heights, window bands, and balcony depths all follow its intervals. Yet architectural historians who have examined his working drawings note that Le Corbusier frequently departed from the Modulor's figures when they conflicted with site conditions, construction budgets, or simply his own visual judgment. In their view, the system functioned less as a strict generator of form than as a flexible vocabulary that lent his intuitive choices the appearance of mathematical necessity.","question":"Based on the text, what have architectural historians concluded about Le Corbusier's use of the Modulor?","options":["Le Corbusier treated the Modulor as an adaptable framework that gave a rational look to decisions he often made on other grounds.","Le Corbusier treated the Modulor as a binding standard whose intervals determined nearly every dimension of his completed buildings.","Le Corbusier treated the Modulor as a theoretical exercise that he discussed in writing but seldom applied to actual projects.","Le Corbusier treated the Modulor as a cost-saving method chiefly intended to reduce construction budgets on large housing projects."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"역사가들은 르 코르뷔지에가 부지·예산·시각적 판단에 따라 모듈로르 수치에서 자주 벗어났고, 이 체계가 직관적 선택에 수학적 필연성의 외관을 부여하는 유연한 어휘였다고 보므로 A가 정답이다. B는 마르세유 사례만 보고 엄격한 적용으로 오해한 것으로, 역사가들의 견해와 반대된다. C는 실제 프로젝트(위니테 다비타시옹)에 적용했다는 지문 내용과 모순된다. D는 예산이 언급되긴 하지만 수치에서 벗어난 이유일 뿐, 체계의 목적이 비용 절감이었다는 근거는 없다.","explanationEn":"A is correct because the historians found that Le Corbusier often departed from the Modulor's figures because of site conditions, budgets, or his own taste. They saw the system as a flexible vocabulary that made his intuitive choices look mathematically necessary. B comes from reading only the Marseille example as strict application, which is the opposite of what the historians concluded. C contradicts the text, since he did apply the system to real buildings such as the Unité d'Habitation. D twists a detail: the text mentions budgets only as one reason he departed from the system, not as its purpose.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.612Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — The architectural rationalism of Le Corbusier's modular proportional system in modernist building design","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"마지막 두 문장(수치에서 자주 이탈 + \"flexible vocabulary that lent his intuitive choices the appearance of mathematical necessity\")이 A를 직접 뒷받침한다. B는 지문 전반부(르 코르뷔지에 자신의 홍보·마르세유 사례)만 훑으면 선택하기 쉬운 매력적 오답이고, D는 '예산' 세부를 왜곡한 오답, C는 적용 사실과 모순되지만 '엄격 적용 아님'을 과장 해석하면 말이 되는 오답이다. 역사가 견해와 건축가 자신의 주장을 구분해야 하므로 medium에 적합. 모듈로르 관련 사실(1940년대, 팔 든 사람 신장, 황금비, 위니테 다비타시옹)도 정확. 한·영 해설 모두 글자 참조와 결론이 일치한다."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"정답 A는 마지막 문장을 바꿔 쓴 것이다. B는 마르세유 세부를, D는 예산 언급을 근거로 삼아 그럴듯하게 꾸몄다. C는 다소 약하지만 말은 된다. 중간 난이도에 맞다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-056","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-057","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Literary historians have often described the inward turn of early twentieth-century Japanese fiction as an import, a technique borrowed from European modernists. Natsume Soseki's novel Kusamakura (1906), however, complicates that account. Its narrator, a painter wandering through mountain villages, records drifting associations of memory, half-formed aesthetic judgments, and sudden shifts of attention in a manner that resembles what would later be called stream of consciousness. __Yet Soseki drew this loosely linked, digressive style less from Western novels than from haikai prose and classical Chinese travel writing, forms he had studied closely for years before he went to London.__ For this reason, some scholars now argue that Kusamakura should be read not as an early imitation of modernism but as evidence that similar narrative experiments could arise independently from different literary traditions.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It explains why the painter-narrator of Kusamakura shifts abruptly between memories and aesthetic judgments.","It offers a detail about the sources of Soseki's technique that undercuts the account presented at the beginning of the text.","It presents evidence that Soseki's stay in London shaped the style of Kusamakura more than critics have acknowledged.","It introduces a scholarly claim that Kusamakura is the earliest example of stream-of-consciousness writing in any language."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 소세키의 기법이 서양 소설보다 하이카이 산문과 한문 기행문에서 나왔다고 밝혀, 첫 문장의 '유럽에서 수입된 기법'이라는 통설을 약화시키고 마지막 문장의 '독자적 발생' 주장의 근거가 되므로 B가 정답이다. A는 서술자의 연상 전환을 언급한다는 점에서 일부 관련이 있지만, 밑줄 문장은 서술자의 심리가 아니라 기법의 출처를 다룬다. C는 런던을 언급한다는 점만 맞을 뿐, 지문은 소세키가 런던에 가기 전에 그 형식들을 연구했다고 말하므로 정반대다. D는 지문에 없는 '최초'라는 주장이며, 학자들의 주장은 밑줄 문장이 아니라 마지막 문장에 나온다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence says Soseki's style came mainly from haikai prose and classical Chinese travel writing, not from Western novels. That detail weakens the opening claim that this inward turn was imported from Europe, and it sets up the final sentence's argument about independent development, so B is correct. A is somewhat related because the narrator's shifts of attention are mentioned, but the sentence is about where the technique came from, not why the narrator thinks the way he does. C gets London from the text but reverses the point: Soseki studied these forms before he went there. D claims Kusamakura was the \"earliest\" example, which the text never says, and the scholars' argument shows up only in the last sentence.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.612Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — Natsume Soseki's stream-of-consciousness narrative technique in early twentieth-century Japanese fiction","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 기법의 출처(하이카이 산문·한문 기행문)를 제시해 첫 문장의 '유럽 수입' 통설을 약화시키고 마지막 문장의 '독자적 발생' 주장을 뒷받침하므로 B가 정확하다. A(서술자 심리 설명), C(런던 영향—지문과 정반대), D(최초 사례·학자 주장 위치 오류)는 모두 지문 요소를 일부 차용해 비교가 필요한 적절한 오답이다. 소세키의 런던 체류(1900–02), Kusamakura(1906) 등 사실관계도 문제없음. 한·영 해설 모두 정답 및 선택지 참조가 일치하며 자연스럽다."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B는 첫 문장의 '수입' 통설과 연결해야 고를 수 있다. A는 서술자 묘사와 겹치고, C는 런던 언급을 이용한 함정이라 비교가 필요하다. D는 비교적 쉽게 배제된다. 사실관계(1906년 작, 1900~02년 런던 체류)도 맞다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-057","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-058","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In 1964, philosopher Arthur Danto encountered Andy Warhol's Brillo Box, a plywood sculpture that looked almost exactly like the cardboard cartons of soap pads stacked in any supermarket stockroom. The experience convinced Danto that no visible property could explain why one object was art and its twin was not. __Earlier theorists had assumed that art could be identified by looking, whether by its beauty, its skill of execution, or its resemblance to the world.__ Danto argued instead that what makes something an artwork is its place within an \"artworld\": a surrounding atmosphere of theory and a knowledge of art history that lets an object be interpreted as being about something. On this view, Warhol's box counts as art not because of how it looks but because it embodies a meaning that viewers familiar with that context can read in it.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It gives evidence that Warhol's sculpture was visually different from ordinary soap-pad cartons.","It presents the main claim of Danto's theory, which the rest of the text then puts to the test.","It describes an older assumption that the Brillo Box challenged and that Danto's account replaces.","It describes a criticism of Danto's theory, which the text goes on to reject as mistaken."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 미술을 눈으로 보고 식별할 수 있다는 이전 이론가들의 가정을 소개한다. 바로 앞 문장은 그 가정이 Brillo Box 때문에 흔들렸음을 보여 주고, 뒤 문장의 \"instead\"는 Danto가 그 가정을 대체한다는 점을 보여 주므로 C가 정답이다. A는 Warhol의 작품을 언급하지만, 지문은 두 물체가 거의 똑같아 보인다고 하므로 사실과 반대이다. B는 이론을 다룬다는 점은 맞지만, 밑줄 문장은 Danto의 주장이 아니라 그가 반대한 견해이다. D는 대립 관계를 다룬다는 점은 맞지만, 이 견해는 Danto에 대한 비판이 아니라 Danto보다 앞선 가정이다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence sums up what earlier theorists assumed: that you can identify art just by looking at it. The sentence before it shows the Brillo Box undermining that assumption, and the word \"instead\" in the next sentence shows Danto replacing it, so C is correct. A mentions Warhol's work, but the text says the two objects look almost exactly alike, so A gets the facts backward. B is right that the sentence deals with theory, but the sentence describes a view Danto argued against, not his own claim. D is right that two views are opposed, but this view is an earlier assumption that came before Danto, not a criticism of his theory.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.612Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — The philosophical aesthetics of Arthur Danto's institutional theory defining contemporary artwork status","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 C 검증: 밑줄 문장은 \"Earlier theorists had assumed...\"로 과거의 가정을 제시하며, 앞 문장(Brillo Box로 시각적 속성 기준이 무너짐)과 뒤 문장(\"Danto argued instead\")이 각각 '도전'과 '대체'를 뒷받침한다. A는 지문 사실(거의 똑같아 보임)과 반대, B는 밑줄이 Danto의 주장이 아님, D는 Danto에 대한 비판이 아니라 선행 가정이므로 오답. 사실관계(Danto 1964 \"The Artworld\", Warhol Brillo Box) 정확. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 C로 일치하고 선택지 참조 정확, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 난이도: 밑줄 문장이 Danto의 견해인지 반대 견해인지를 \"instead\"와 앞뒤 문맥으로 판별해야 하며 B·D가 부분적으로 그럴듯해 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"C가 옳다. 앞 문장과 'instead'를 연결해야 풀 수 있어 두 단계 판단이 필요하다. B·D는 일부 맞는 근거가 있어 비교해야 배제된다. A는 지문과 직접 모순되어 비교적 쉽게 지워지지만 그럴듯하게는 읽힌다. Danto의 1964년 'The Artworld'와 합판으로 만든 Brillo Box 관련 사실 관계에는 문제가 없다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-058","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-059","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Art historians have long linked Caravaggio's tenebrism—his practice of setting brightly lit figures against near-total darkness—to the goals of the Counter-Reformation Church, which urged painters to make sacred stories emotionally gripping for ordinary worshippers. In The Calling of Saint Matthew (1599–1600), a single shaft of light cuts across a dim tax office and falls on Matthew at the instant Christ summons him. __Yet technical studies of Caravaggio's canvases suggest that this effect began less as a theological program than as a studio habit: he often posed models in a darkened room lit by one high window or lamp.__ Some scholars therefore argue that the painting's spiritual intensity grew out of a practical working method that patrons later found well suited to devotional aims, rather than from a deliberate plan to illustrate Church doctrine.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It offers an example of how the Counter-Reformation Church instructed painters to arrange the lighting in their studios.","It describes a feature of The Calling of Saint Matthew that supports the long-standing view that Caravaggio designed tenebrism to serve doctrine.","It identifies the specific religious moment that Caravaggio chose to emphasize with light in The Calling of Saint Matthew.","It introduces evidence that complicates a widely held explanation of where Caravaggio's lighting technique came from."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 시작하며, 테네브리즘이 반종교개혁의 목표에서 나왔다는 오랜 견해와 달리 작업실 습관에서 비롯되었다는 기술적 연구 결과를 제시하므로 D가 정답이다. A는 교회와 작업실 조명이라는 두 요소를 섞었지만, 교회가 작업실 조명을 지시했다는 내용은 지문에 없다. B는 그림의 특징을 언급한다는 점은 맞지만, 이 문장은 기존 견해를 뒷받침하는 것이 아니라 그 견해에 의문을 제기한다. C에서 말하는 소명의 순간은 밑줄 문장이 아니라 그 앞 문장에서 묘사된다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence starts with \"Yet\" and brings in technical findings that the effect came from a studio habit. That challenges the long-held view that tenebrism grew out of Counter-Reformation goals, so D is correct. A mixes up two things in the text, the Church and studio lighting, but the passage never says the Church told painters how to light their studios. B is right that the sentence relates to the painting, but the sentence questions the traditional view instead of supporting it. C describes the moment of the calling, which appears in the sentence before the underlined one, not in the underlined sentence itself.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.612Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — Caravaggio's tenebrism lighting technique and psychological drama intensity in Counter-Reformation religious painting","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 D 검증: 밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 기존 통설(반종교개혁 기원)에 반하는 기술적 연구 증거를 도입하고, 다음 문장의 대안적 결론으로 이어지므로 '널리 받아들여진 설명을 복잡하게 만드는 증거 도입'이 정확함. B·C는 지문 내 다른 문장의 내용을 차용한 부분적 근거가 있어 비교가 필요하고, A도 표면적으로 그럴듯함. 연대(1599–1600) 및 작품명 사실 관계 문제 없음. 'Yet' 신호어로 비교적 명확하지만 통설 vs 반론 구조 파악의 두 단계가 필요하여 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"D가 명확한 정답이다. 'Yet'의 역접 기능과 '오랜 견해 → 반박 증거'라는 구조를 함께 파악해야 하므로 medium에 맞다. B는 방향만 뒤집은 매력적 오답이다. A와 C는 지문 요소를 끌어다 쓴 오답이며, 비교적 쉽게 배제된다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-059","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-boundaries-m-062","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Metaphysical poets often borrowed the memento mori, a reminder of death, from devotional writing and turned it to secular ends. In \"To His Coy Mistress,\" Andrew Marvell's speaker builds a three-part argument, conceding first that, with endless time, he would praise his beloved slowly for centuries. The poem's second section, which opens with the famous image of \"Time's wingèd chariot hurrying ______ that leisure is impossible: the grave, the speaker warns, offers no embraces. Only in the final section does he urge immediate pleasure as the logical conclusion.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["near,\" and insists","near\"; insists","near,\" insists","near\"—and it insists"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"주어 \"The poem's second section\" 뒤에 쉼표로 시작한 비필수 관계절(which opens ... near)이 끼어 있으므로, 관계절을 닫는 쉼표 뒤에 바로 본동사 insists가 와야 한다. 그래서 C가 정답이다. A는 and 때문에 insists가 관계절 안의 두 번째 동사(opens and insists)가 되어 주절에 본동사가 남지 않는다. B는 세미콜론 앞부분이 동사 없는 불완전한 절이 되고, 닫는 쉼표도 빠져 있다. D는 대명사 it이 주어를 한 번 더 써서 원래 주어가 동사를 잃고, 대시로 연 삽입도 쉼표와 짝이 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The subject \"The poem's second section\" is interrupted by a nonessential relative clause that begins with a comma (\"which opens ... near\"). That clause has to close with a comma, and then the main verb, \"insists,\" comes right after it. That's why C is correct. A adds \"and,\" which makes \"insists\" a second verb inside the relative clause (\"opens and insists\"), so the sentence ends up with no main verb. B puts a semicolon after a subject that has no verb, so the part before the semicolon isn't a complete clause, and the closing comma is missing too. D adds the pronoun \"it,\" which repeats the subject and leaves the original subject without a verb; it also mixes a dash with the opening comma, so the interruption isn't punctuated consistently.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.612Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — The literary memento mori tradition in Metaphysical poetry and Andrew Marvell's carpe diem argumentation","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"문장 구조 검산: 주어 \"The poem's second section\" + 비필수 관계절(\"which opens ... near,\") + 본동사 \"insists\" → C만 완전한 주절을 만든다. A는 and로 insists가 관계절에 묶여 본동사 부재, B는 세미콜론 앞이 단편, D는 it이 주어를 중복하고 쉼표–대시 짝이 불일치. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 C를 지지하며 글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음. Marvell 시의 인용구와 3부 구조 서술은 사실에 부합. 삽입구 닫기 + 본동사 확인의 두 단계 판단이 필요하고 A·D가 그럴듯한 오답이라 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"C로 넣으면 \"The poem's second section, which opens with ... near,' insists that...\"가 되어 문법적으로 맞다. 인용된 짧은 구절은 퍼블릭 도메인이다. A는 관계절 안에 동사를 하나 더 붙이는 그럴듯한 함정이고, 나머지 오답도 말이 된다. 중간 난이도에 맞는다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-boundaries-m-062","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-boundaries-e-063","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"easy","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Early copies of the Quran were often written in Kufic, a script known for its angular, horizontal letterforms. By the tenth century, however, many copyists had begun to favor Naskh, a rounded script that was easier to read and faster to ______ it eventually became one of the most widely used scripts for manuscripts across the Islamic world.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["write,","write","write, and,","write, and"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"빈칸 앞 'By the tenth century ... faster to write'와 뒤 'it eventually became ...'는 모두 독립절이다. 두 독립절은 쉼표와 등위접속사로 이어야 하므로 'write, and'인 D가 정답이다. A는 쉼표만으로 독립절을 이어 쉼표 스플라이스가 된다. B는 아무 부호 없이 두 절을 붙인 무종지문(run-on)이다. C는 'and' 뒤에 불필요한 쉼표를 넣어 접속사와 뒤 절을 부당하게 끊는다.","explanationEn":"The text before the blank (\"By the tenth century ... faster to write\") and the text after it (\"it eventually became ...\") are both independent clauses. To join two independent clauses, you need a comma followed by a coordinating conjunction, so D, \"write, and,\" is correct. A joins the clauses with only a comma, which creates a comma splice. B puts no punctuation between the clauses, which creates a run-on sentence. C adds an extra comma after \"and\" that wrongly separates the conjunction from the clause it introduces.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.612Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"D","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — Islamic calligraphic script evolution from Kufic angular to Naskh rounded letterforms across manuscript periods","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"빈칸 앞(\"many copyists had begun to favor Naskh ... faster to write\")과 뒤(\"it eventually became ...\")가 모두 독립절임을 직접 확인함. D(쉼표+and)만 올바르게 두 독립절을 연결하며, A는 쉼표 스플라이스, B는 무종지문, C는 'and' 뒤 불필요한 쉼표로 배제됨. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 D를 가리키고 글자 참조·논리가 일치하며 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 쿠파체(각진 형태)·나스크체(둥근 형태, 10세기 보급)에 관한 배경 서술은 사실과 부합. 지문은 독창적 서술로 저작권 우려 없음. 단일 규칙(독립절 연결: 쉼표+등위접속사)으로 한 단계 추론으로 풀리고 오답은 전형적 오개념(쉼표 스플라이스, 융합문, 접속사 뒤 쉼표)이므로 easy 난이도에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"독립절 두 개를 쉼표+등위접속사로 잇는 규칙 하나만 쓰는 문항이다. 오답은 쉼표 스플라이스, 무종지문, 불필요한 쉼표로 모두 전형적인 오개념이다. 사실 관계(쿠픽체에서 나스크체로의 이행, 10세기 무렵)도 대체로 맞다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sv-boundaries-e-063","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-boundaries-e-064","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"easy","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In the 1970s, German choreographer Pina Bausch developed Tanztheater, a form that blends theatrical storytelling with contemporary dance. Her performers often repeated ordinary gestures, such as brushing hair or embracing, until the movements took on new emotional ______ audiences found these repetitions both unsettling and deeply moving.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["weight, and","weight,","weight","weight, and,"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"빈칸 앞 \"Her performers ... new emotional weight\"와 뒤 \"audiences found ... moving\"은 각각 독립절이다. 두 독립절은 쉼표와 등위접속사로 연결할 수 있으므로 A가 정답이다. B는 쉼표만으로 두 독립절을 이은 쉼표 스플라이스이다. C는 문장부호나 접속사 없이 두 독립절을 붙인 무종지문이다. D는 접속사 and 뒤에 쓸데없는 쉼표가 있어 틀렸다.","explanationEn":"The text before the blank (\"Her performers ... new emotional weight\") and the text after it (\"audiences found ... moving\") are both independent clauses. You can join two independent clauses with a comma plus a coordinating conjunction, so A is correct. B is a comma splice, because a comma alone can't join two independent clauses. C is a run-on sentence, since it puts the two clauses together with no punctuation or conjunction. D adds an extra comma after \"and\" that doesn't belong there.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.612Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"easy","targetLetter":"A","seed":"arts and humanities nonfiction — Pina Bausch's Tanztheater movement merging theatrical narrative with contemporary dance body expression innovation","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"빈칸 앞(\"Her performers ... emotional weight\")과 뒤(\"audiences found ... moving\")가 모두 독립절임을 직접 확인했다. A(쉼표+and)만 올바르며, B는 쉼표 스플라이스, C는 무종지문(fused sentence), D는 and 뒤 불필요한 쉼표로 오답이다. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 정답 및 선택지 참조가 일치하고 모순이 없다. Pina Bausch·Tanztheater·1970년대 등 사실 관계도 정확하다. 독립절 연결 규칙 하나로 풀 수 있고 오답이 전형적 오개념이므로 easy 난이도에 적합하다."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"독립절 두 개를 쉼표+등위접속사로 잇는 규칙 하나만 쓰는 문항. 오답은 쉼표 스플라이스, 무종지문, 불필요한 쉼표로 학생들이 흔히 틀리는 유형이다. Bausch와 Tanztheater 설명은 사실에 맞다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-easy","gid":"sv-boundaries-e-064","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-067","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In the 1960s and 1970s, developmental psychologist Mary Ainsworth designed the Strange Situation, a laboratory procedure in which a one-year-old is briefly separated from its mother, left with a stranger, and then reunited with the mother. Many observers assumed the most revealing moment would be the separation itself, since an infant who cries loudly when the mother leaves seems to be the most strongly attached. Ainsworth, however, paid closest attention to the reunion. Some infants who had cried hard calmed quickly once the mother came back and went back to exploring the room, and Ainsworth classified them as securely attached. Others who had cried just as hard pushed the mother away or would not be comforted, and some infants who had shown no distress at all avoided the mother when she returned. Ainsworth had also watched these families at home earlier, and she found that the infants classified as secure usually had mothers who responded promptly and sensitively to their signals there.","question":"According to the text, what did Ainsworth treat as the clearest evidence of how an infant was attached to its mother?","options":["How intensely the infant cried when the mother left the room, since this showed how much the infant depended on her","How the infant responded to the stranger during the separation, since this showed whether the infant trusted unfamiliar adults","How promptly the mother answered the infant's signals at home, since this alone determined the infant's classification","How the infant behaved when the mother came back, since infants who had shown similar distress could react very differently then"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 Ainsworth가 분리 순간보다 재회 장면에 가장 주목했다고 말하고, 똑같이 심하게 울었던 아기들도 재회할 때는 서로 아주 다르게 반응했다는 근거를 든다. 그러므로 정답은 D이다. A는 지문이 소개하는 '다른 관찰자들'의 가정일 뿐이며, Ainsworth는 바로 이 관점과 반대 입장이다. B는 낯선 사람이 절차에 등장하기는 하지만, 지문은 낯선 사람에 대한 아기의 반응을 판단 근거로 제시하지 않는다. C는 가정 내 반응성이 '안정 애착'으로 분류된 아기들과 관련이 있다고만 했을 뿐, 그것만으로 분류가 결정되었다고 하지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The text says Ainsworth paid closest attention to the reunion, not the separation. It supports this by showing that infants who cried equally hard could react in completely different ways when the mother returned, so D is correct. A describes what other observers assumed, and the text sets Ainsworth's view against that assumption. B mentions the stranger, who is part of the procedure, but the text never says the infant's reaction to the stranger was used to classify attachment. C goes too far: the text says home responsiveness was linked to the secure classification, not that it alone decided the classification.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.612Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"social science research — Mary Ainsworth's Strange Situation procedure measuring infant attachment security and maternal responsiveness behavioral classification","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"지문이 \"Ainsworth, however, paid closest attention to the reunion\"라고 명시하고, 같은 강도로 울었던 아기들이 재회 시 다르게 반응했다는 근거를 제시하므로 D가 정답임을 직접 확인함. A는 '다른 관찰자들'의 가정(훑어 읽으면 고르기 쉬운 함정), C는 가정 관찰이 분류와 '관련'된다는 서술을 '단독 결정'으로 과장한 오답으로 비교 판단이 필요하며, B는 절차에 등장하는 낯선 사람을 이용한 그럴듯한 오답. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 동일 결론과 선택지 참조를 가지며 영어 해설에 한글 없음. Ainsworth의 Strange Situation(1960~70년대) 서술은 사실과 부합. 원문 창작 지문으로 저작권 의심 없음. 난이도 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"A는 관찰자들의 가정이라 훑어 읽으면 고르기 쉬운 매력적 오답이고, C는 'alone'이 과한 진술이라 배제된다. B는 비교적 약한 오답이지만 말은 된다. medium 난이도에 맞다. Ainsworth와 Strange Situation 관련 사실도 정확하다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-067","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-069","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In the 1960s and 1970s, British sociologist Basil Bernstein proposed that children from different social classes tend to develop distinct ways of using language. He described a \"restricted code,\" which relies on meanings shared within a close-knit group and leaves much unstated, and an \"elaborated code,\" which spells out meanings explicitly so that listeners unfamiliar with the speaker's context can follow. Bernstein observed that working-class children often favored the restricted code, while middle-class children were more practiced in both. Critics sometimes read his work as claiming that working-class speech was deficient, but Bernstein rejected that interpretation. His central argument concerned schools: because British classrooms rewarded the explicit, context-independent style of the elaborated code, children who arrived already fluent in it were advantaged, and the resulting gaps in achievement reflected the expectations built into schooling rather than differences in children's linguistic or intellectual ability.","question":"According to the text, what did Bernstein see as the main source of the achievement differences he discussed?","options":["Working-class children used a code that left too much unstated to express complex ideas.","Schools favored one style of speech, which benefited children already accustomed to it.","Middle-class children were trained to switch between codes, which raised their intellectual ability.","Critics misread his theory, which led schools to lower expectations for working-class pupils."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문 마지막 문장에서 Bernstein은 학교가 정교화 코드의 명시적 스타일을 보상했기 때문에 그 코드에 익숙한 아이들이 유리했고, 성취 격차는 아이들의 능력이 아니라 학교의 기대에서 비롯되었다고 주장하므로 B가 정답이다. A는 제한 코드가 많은 것을 말하지 않는다는 설명은 맞지만, 그것을 결함으로 보는 것은 Bernstein이 거부한 해석이다. C는 중산층 아이들이 두 코드 모두에 능숙했다는 점은 맞지만, 지문은 격차가 지적 능력 차이 때문이 아니라고 명시한다. D는 비평가들의 오독을 언급하지만, 그 오독이 학교의 기대를 낮췄다는 내용은 지문에 없다.","explanationEn":"B is correct because the last sentence says British classrooms rewarded the explicit style of the elaborated code. That gave an advantage to children who already spoke that way, and Bernstein linked the achievement gaps to what schools expected, not to children's ability. A gets the restricted code's reliance on unstated meaning right, but calling that a weakness is the \"deficient\" reading that Bernstein rejected. C is right that middle-class children were practiced in both codes, but the text says plainly that the gaps did not come from differences in intellectual ability. D mentions the critics' misreading, but the text never says that misreading caused schools to lower their expectations.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.612Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"social science research — Basil Bernstein's restricted versus elaborated code theory linking social class to linguistic patterns and educational outcomes Britain","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"정답 B는 마지막 문장(\"because British classrooms rewarded... the resulting gaps in achievement reflected the expectations built into schooling\")에 직접 근거함. A는 제한 코드 묘사는 정확하나 결함론 해석을 Bernstein이 거부했다는 문장과 충돌, C는 중산층이 두 코드에 능숙하다는 사실은 맞지만 '지적 능력 향상'은 지문이 명시적으로 부정, D는 지문에 없는 인과. 한·영 해설 모두 동일 결론·글자 참조, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. Bernstein의 코드 이론 및 결함론 거부에 대한 서술은 사실과 부합. 정답이 지문 말미에 비교적 명시되어 있으나 오답 A·C가 부분적 근거를 갖춰 비교가 필요하므로 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B는 지문 마지막 문장을 바꿔 쓴 것이고 근거가 분명하다. A와 C는 지문 내용을 일부 담고 있어서 지문의 결론과 대조해 봐야 걸러진다. D도 그럴듯하게 들리지만 지문에 근거가 없다. 중간 난이도에 맞다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-069","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-070","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In the 1970s, anthropologist Barbara Myerhoff spent several years at a senior center in Venice, California, whose members were mostly elderly Jewish immigrants from Eastern Europe. Many observers had described such communities as remnants, groups simply waiting out the end of a vanishing way of life. Myerhoff noticed something else: the members kept inventing ceremonies, such as a graduation for a class of elderly students and a birthday celebration for a ninety-five-year-old man, that mixed religious forms with entirely secular content. __Few of these events followed any traditional script, and some participants openly admitted that they no longer believed in the religious teachings the ceremonies borrowed from.__ For Myerhoff, this was exactly what made the rituals revealing. Because the members could not count on inherited meaning, they had to build meaning themselves, and their improvised ceremonies showed a community actively deciding who it was rather than passively fading away.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It gives evidence supporting the observers' view that the community was a remnant of a disappearing way of life.","It explains why Myerhoff eventually concluded that the ceremonies held little real significance for their participants.","It points out features of the ceremonies that might seem to weaken their importance but that Myerhoff treated as central to her interpretation.","It describes a disagreement among the center's members about whether the ceremonies should follow religious tradition."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 의식이 전통 형식을 따르지 않고 참여자들이 종교적 가르침을 믿지 않았다는 점을 제시하는데, 언뜻 보면 의식의 가치를 깎는 듯한 특징이다. 하지만 바로 다음 문장에서 Myerhoff는 바로 이 점이 의식을 의미 있게 만든다고 보았으므로 C가 정답이다. A는 '사라져 가는 공동체'라는 관찰자들의 견해와 연결되지만, 이 글은 그 견해를 반박한다. B는 밑줄 문장만 보면 그럴듯하지만, Myerhoff의 결론은 정반대이다. D는 구성원 사이의 의견 차이를 언급하지만, 지문에는 그런 논쟁이 나오지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence says the ceremonies didn't follow tradition and that some participants didn't believe the teachings behind them. At first glance, those details seem to make the rituals less important. But the very next sentence tells you that Myerhoff saw exactly this as what made them revealing, so C is correct. A ties in with the observers' \"remnant\" view, but the text pushes back against that view instead of supporting it. B might sound reasonable if you read the sentence on its own, but Myerhoff actually concluded the opposite. D mentions a disagreement among the members, and the text never describes one.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.612Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"social science research — Barbara Myerhoff's ethnographic study of elderly Jewish immigrants creating secular rituals and meaning-making in Venice Beach community","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장(비전통적·불신 참여자)이 언뜻 의식의 가치를 약화시키는 듯하나, 바로 다음 문장 \"this was exactly what made the rituals revealing\"이 Myerhoff가 이를 해석의 핵심으로 삼았음을 명시하므로 C가 정확. A는 관찰자 견해(remnant)와 표면적으로 연결되고 B는 밑줄 문장만 읽으면 그럴듯해 비교가 필요하며, D는 구성원 간 논쟁이 지문에 없어 배제됨. Myerhoff의 Number Our Days(졸업식, 95세 생일 의식, 세속적 의식 논의) 내용과 사실 일치. 해설 한·영 결론과 글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스러움, 한글 혼입 없음. 밑줄 문장과 다음 문장을 연결하는 두 단계 판단이 필요해 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"Myerhoff의 'Number Our Days' 연구를 바탕으로 새로 쓴 지문이며 사실관계에 문제가 없다. 정답을 고르려면 두 단계가 필요하다. 먼저 밑줄 문장이 의식의 가치를 깎는 것처럼 보이는 특징임을 파악하고, 이어서 다음 문장이 그 특징을 오히려 핵심 근거로 뒤집는다는 점을 확인해야 한다. 오답 A와 B는 밑줄 문장만 따로 읽으면 그럴듯해서 매력적인 오답 역할을 하고, D는 상대적으로 약하지만 말은 된다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-070","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-071","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"For centuries, philosophers treated categories the way Aristotle did: a thing belongs to a category if it meets a fixed list of necessary and sufficient conditions, and every member belongs equally. In the early 1970s, psychologist Eleanor Rosch tested this assumption with the Dani people of New Guinea, whose language has only two basic color terms, roughly \"dark\" and \"light.\" Rosch found that Dani participants learned and remembered new names more easily when the names were attached to certain \"focal\" colors, such as a particular vivid red, than when they were attached to colors falling between those focal points. __Because the Dani had no word for red, they could not have picked up this preference from their vocabulary, so the advantage seemed to come from how human perception organizes color itself.__ Rosch went on to argue that categories are built around such best examples, or prototypes, with other members belonging more or less strongly depending on how closely they resemble the center.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It introduces a weakness in Rosch's study design that later researchers would use to cast doubt on her findings about focal colors.","It describes the Dani color vocabulary in order to show that Aristotle's view of categories fits some languages better than others.","It summarizes the experimental procedure Rosch used to compare how quickly Dani participants learned names for different colors.","It rules out an alternative explanation for Rosch's result, which supports the claim that leads into her broader theory."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 다니족에게 '빨강'이라는 단어가 없으므로 초점 색 선호가 어휘에서 왔을 수 없다고 말해, 언어 학습이라는 대안 설명을 배제하고 지각 자체에서 온다는 결론을 지지한다. 이 결론이 원형 이론으로 이어지므로 D가 정답이다. A는 '약점'을 제시한다고 하지만 문장은 오히려 결과를 강화한다. B는 다니족 어휘를 언급하는 점은 맞지만, 아리스토텔레스 견해를 지지하려는 목적이 아니다. C는 실험 절차가 아니라 결과의 해석에 관한 문장이라는 점에서 틀렸다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence points out that the Dani have no word for red, so their preference for focal colors could not have come from their vocabulary. That rules out a language-based explanation and supports the idea that perception itself organizes color, and this idea is what leads into the prototype theory. That makes D correct. A is wrong because the sentence makes Rosch's result stronger instead of pointing out a weakness. B is wrong because, although the sentence does mention Dani vocabulary, it isn't used to support Aristotle's view. C is wrong because the sentence interprets the result instead of describing how the experiment was done.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.612Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"social science research — Eleanor Rosch's prototype theory of categorization challenging Aristotelian definition logic through color naming cross-cultural experiments","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 '어휘에서 왔을 수 없다'(대안 설명 배제) → '지각이 원인'(결론) → 원형 이론으로 연결되는 구조로, D가 정확히 기능을 기술함. A(약점)는 방향이 반대, B(아리스토텔레스 지지)는 지문 전체 논지와 반대, C(절차 요약)는 앞 문장의 내용이지 밑줄 문장이 아님. 다니족 2개 기본 색채어·Rosch(Heider) 1970년대 초 연구 등 사실관계도 정확. 한·영 해설 모두 D를 일관되게 뒷받침하며 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 밑줄 문장의 논리 역할 파악 + 지문 전체 흐름(원형 이론으로의 연결) 확인이라는 두 단계 판단이 필요하고, B·C가 부분적으로 지문 내용과 맞아 비교가 필요하므로 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"D는 정답이 맞다. 밑줄 문장은 어휘에서 왔다는 설명을 배제하고, 그 결과 얻은 지각 기반 결론이 원형 이론으로 이어진다. 오답 B(다니족 어휘 언급)와 C(실험과의 관련성)는 부분적으로 맞는 근거를 갖고 있다. A는 비교적 쉽게 배제되지만 그럴듯하게 읽힌다. 다니족 색 연구에 관한 사실 서술은 실제 Rosch(Heider) 연구와 부합한다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-071","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-072","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Sociologist Erving Goffman argued that everyday interaction resembles a theatrical performance: people manage the impressions others form of them, maintaining a \"front stage\" demeanor before audiences and relaxing in \"backstage\" regions. Many readers have taken this to mean that Goffman saw social life as fundamentally deceptive, with individuals cynically manipulating one another. __Yet Goffman stressed that most performers are taken in by their own acts, sincerely believing in the roles they play, and that sustaining \"face\" is a cooperative effort in which audiences tactfully overlook slips to spare everyone embarrassment.__ On this reading, his dramaturgy describes less a world of con artists than a shared moral order, one that participants jointly uphold even in rigid institutional settings such as hospitals and schools.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It presents aspects of Goffman's account that undercut a common interpretation of his work and prepare the text's alternative reading.","It presents an example of cynical manipulation that supports a common interpretation of Goffman's view of social life.","It presents a criticism of Goffman's theatrical model that the text goes on to show applies mainly to institutional settings.","It presents the distinction between front stage and backstage regions that the text treats as the core of Goffman's theory."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 시작해 고프먼이 사회생활을 기만으로 보았다는 흔한 해석을 반박하는 근거(진실한 역할 수행, 협력적 체면 유지)를 제시하고, 이어지는 '공유된 도덕 질서'라는 대안적 해석으로 연결되므로 A가 정답이다. B는 냉소적 조작이라는 소재는 맞지만 밑줄 문장은 그 해석을 지지하지 않고 약화시킨다. C는 기관 환경이 지문에 나오지만 밑줄 문장은 고프먼 모델에 대한 비판이 아니라 그의 주장 자체이다. D는 전무대/후무대 구분이 첫 문장에서 소개된 내용이지 밑줄 문장의 기능이 아니다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence opens with \"Yet\" and points to parts of Goffman's account (performers sincerely believing in their roles, face being kept up cooperatively) that challenge the common view that he saw social life as deceptive. It also sets up the next sentence's alternative reading of a \"shared moral order,\" so A is correct. B mentions cynical manipulation, but the sentence weakens that interpretation instead of supporting it. C picks up on institutional settings, but the sentence isn't a criticism of Goffman's model; it states his own position. D refers to the front stage/backstage distinction, which comes from the first sentence and isn't what the underlined sentence does.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.613Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"social science research — Erving Goffman's dramaturgy analysis of self-presentation and face-work in everyday social interactions institutional settings","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 흔한 해석(기만적 사회생활)을 반박하고 다음 문장의 '공유된 도덕 질서' 대안 해석을 준비하므로 A가 정확. B는 소재(냉소적 조작)는 겹치나 방향이 반대, C는 '비판'이 아닌 고프먼 자신의 주장이며 기관 환경은 마지막 문장 소재, D는 첫 문장 내용으로 매력적 오답 구성이 적절. 고프먼의 '자기 연기에 빠진 수행자', 협력적 체면 유지(face-work), 병원·학교 등 기관 연구는 사실과 부합. 한국어·영어 해설 결론과 글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스러움. 두 단계 판단(전환어 인식 + 후속 문장과의 연결)이 필요해 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"정답 A가 명확함. B·C·D는 지문 소재(냉소적 조작, 기관 환경, 전무대/후무대)를 각각 끌어와 부분적 근거를 갖추고 있어 medium 난이도에 맞음. 다만 C는 '비판'이라는 표현 때문에 비교적 쉽게 배제됨. 'Goffman stressed that most performers are taken in by their own acts'는 『자아 연출의 사회학』 내용과 일치하나, 마지막 문장의 '경직된 기관 환경에서도'는 『수용소(Asylums)』를 다소 단순화한 서술로 문항 판정에는 영향 없음.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-072","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-073","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In the 1920s and 1930s, Swiss psychologist Jean Piaget questioned children individually rather than giving them standardized tests. In a typical conservation task, a child watched as water was poured from a short, wide glass into a tall, thin one and was then asked whether the amount had changed. Many five-year-olds insisted that the tall glass held more. __Piaget, however, was less interested in whether a child answered correctly than in the reasoning the child offered when he pressed with follow-up questions such as \"How do you know?\"__ Those explanations showed him that younger children tended to focus on a single visible dimension, such as height, while older children reasoned that nothing had been added or taken away. From such patterns, Piaget argued that children's thinking moves through distinct stages.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It presents a common error made by young children that the rest of the text treats as evidence against Piaget's stage theory.","It identifies the aspect of the children's responses that made possible the observations described in the following sentence.","It explains why Piaget chose to replace the conservation task with standardized tests in his later research.","It provides the result of the water-pouring task that leads directly to Piaget's conclusion in the final sentence."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 피아제가 정답 여부보다 아이들이 내놓는 추론(설명)에 주목했다는 점을 밝히고, 바로 다음 문장은 그 설명들을 통해 연령별 사고 차이를 발견했다고 이어지므로 B가 정답이다. A는 아이들의 오류가 앞 문장에 나오긴 하지만 밑줄 문장은 오류 자체를 제시하지 않으며, 지문은 그것을 이론에 반하는 증거로 다루지도 않는다. C는 지문 첫 문장에서 피아제가 표준화 검사를 쓰지 않았다고 했으므로 반대 방향이다. D는 밑줄 문장이 과제의 결과가 아니라 연구자의 관심 초점을 말하며, 결론과 바로 연결되는 것은 그 다음 문장의 관찰이므로 틀렸다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence says Piaget cared more about children's reasoning than about whether their answers were correct, and the very next sentence explains what those explanations showed him, so B is correct. A is wrong because the children's error actually appears in the sentence before, not in the underlined one, and the text never treats it as evidence against Piaget's theory. C contradicts the text, which says Piaget avoided standardized tests. D is wrong because the underlined sentence describes Piaget's focus, not the task's result; the observations that lead to his conclusion come in the sentence after it.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.613Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"social science research — Jean Piaget's clinical interview method revealing cognitive development stages through children's conservation task performance Switzerland","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 피아제가 정답 여부가 아닌 아이들의 추론(설명)에 주목했음을 밝히고, 다음 문장 \"Those explanations showed him...\"이 그 설명을 토대로 한 관찰을 제시하므로 B가 정확히 맞다. A는 오류가 앞 문장에 있고 이론 반증으로 쓰이지 않음, C는 첫 문장과 모순, D는 밑줄이 과제 결과가 아님. 한·영 해설 모두 B를 일관되게 뒷받침하며 글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 피아제 보존 과제·단계 이론 서술은 사실에 부합. 오답 A·D가 지문 인접 내용에 부분 근거를 가져 비교가 필요하고 C도 표면상 그럴듯하여 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B가 정답으로 옳다. A와 D는 근거가 일부 맞아 보여 서로 비교해야 배제되지만, C는 첫 문장과 정면으로 모순되어 쉽게 배제된다. 사소한 점: 보존 과제 연구는 주로 1940년대에 출간되어 시기 서술이 약간 느슨하고, 밑줄 문장의 'he pressed'는 지시 대상이 조금 모호하다. 판정에는 영향이 없다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-073","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-074","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Before the 1960s, many linguists treated language as a system of grammatical rules that could be described apart from the situations in which people spoke. Anthropologist Dell Hymes argued that this approach missed something essential: knowing a language also means knowing when, where, and with whom particular ways of speaking are appropriate. To study this knowledge, Hymes proposed analyzing \"speech events,\" such as a storytelling session or a council meeting, by attending to features like the setting, the participants, and the norms governing who may speak. __In his work with Chinookan narratives from the Pacific Northwest, for instance, Hymes showed that tellers organized stories into patterned groupings of lines and verses that shifted depending on audience and occasion, structures that earlier transcribers, focused only on vocabulary and grammar, had flattened into ordinary prose.__ For Hymes, such findings demonstrated that the meaning of speech cannot be fully recovered without the context in which it is performed.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It describes a limitation of Hymes's method that later researchers working with Chinookan narratives sought to correct.","It explains why linguists before the 1960s preferred to study grammatical rules rather than features of speech events.","It presents a specific case illustrating the kind of insight that Hymes's approach to studying speech could yield.","It introduces a point of disagreement between Hymes and other anthropologists about how stories should be transcribed."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 \"for instance\"로 시작하며, 맥락(청중·상황)에 주목하는 Hymes의 분석이 치누크 서사에서 문법 중심 전사가 놓친 구조를 드러냈다는 구체적 사례를 제시하므로 C가 정답이다. A는 Chinookan 서사를 언급하지만 Hymes 방법의 한계가 아니라 성과를 보여 주므로 틀리다. B는 이전 언어학자들이 언급되긴 하나 그들이 문법을 선호한 이유를 설명하지 않는다. D는 전사 방식에 대한 대비가 있긴 하지만 다른 인류학자와의 논쟁이 아니라 Hymes 접근의 유용성을 보여 주는 예시이므로 틀리다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence opens with \"for instance\" and gives a concrete case: by paying attention to audience and occasion, Hymes found structure in Chinookan narratives that grammar-focused transcribers had missed. That makes C correct. A mentions Chinookan narratives, but the sentence shows something Hymes's method achieved, not a weakness that others had to fix. B is wrong because, although the text mentions earlier linguists, it never explains why they preferred grammar. D picks up on the contrast about transcription, but the sentence isn't describing a debate with other anthropologists. It's an example of how useful Hymes's approach was.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.613Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"social science research — Dell Hymes's ethnography of communication framework analyzing speech events and contextual variation in Native American language use","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 C 검증: 밑줄 문장은 \"for instance\"로 도입된 구체 사례이며, 청중·상황에 따라 달라지는 서사 구조를 Hymes가 밝혀냈다는 점에서 그의 접근이 낳은 통찰을 예시함. A(한계), B(이전 언어학자의 선호 이유), D(인류학자 간 논쟁)는 모두 지문에 근거 없음. A·D는 지문 요소(Chinookan, 전사 대비)를 차용해 그럴듯하고 B도 첫 문장과 연결되어 말이 됨. 사실관계(Hymes의 speech event/ethnography of speaking, Chinookan 서사의 verse 분석)도 정확. 해설 한·영 결론 및 글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스러움. 난이도 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"\"for instance\"라는 신호어 때문에 다소 쉬워지지만, D(전사자와의 대비)와 A(Chinookan 언급)가 부분 근거를 가져 비교가 필요하므로 medium에 적합. Hymes의 ethnopoetics 작업과 사실관계 부합.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-074","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-075","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"When European diplomats gathered in Berlin in 1884 to settle competing claims in Africa, no African ruler or representative was invited. Popular accounts often say the conference carved up the continent on a map, but historians point out that the delegates actually drew few borders there. Instead, they agreed on procedures: a power claiming coastal territory had to notify the other signatories, and a claim would be recognized only if the power showed \"effective occupation,\" meaning enough administrative presence to protect trade and maintain order. Those rules turned out to matter more than any line drawn in the meeting hall. Because recognition now depended on showing control on the ground, European states rushed to sign treaties with local leaders, set up outposts, and send military expeditions into the interior, so the partition sped up sharply in the years after the conference. In this way, the agreement in Berlin, made without any African participants, set off a scramble whose effects African societies would feel for generations.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["The Berlin Conference drew most of Africa's colonial borders, and those borders were later enforced through treaties and military expeditions.","The Berlin Conference failed to settle European rivalries in Africa because its delegates could not agree on where borders should be placed.","The Berlin Conference is remembered mainly for excluding African representatives, which historians consider more significant than any decision the delegates made.","The Berlin Conference shaped Africa's partition less by drawing borders than by setting rules for claiming land, which pushed European powers to rapidly extend their control."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 회의가 국경을 많이 긋지 않았다는 점을 바로잡은 뒤, '실효적 점령' 같은 절차 규칙이 조약 체결과 원정 경쟁을 불러 분할을 가속했다고 설명하므로 D가 정답이다. A는 군사 원정과 조약이라는 세부 내용은 맞지만, 지문이 반박하는 통념(회의가 국경을 그었다는 주장)을 그대로 따른다. B는 국경이 거의 그어지지 않았다는 사실을 합의 실패로 잘못 해석한 것으로, 실제로 대표들은 절차에 합의했다. C는 아프리카 대표가 배제되었다는 사실을 언급하지만, 지문은 그것이 결정 사항보다 더 중요하다고 평가하지 않으며 글의 초점은 규칙이 미친 영향에 있다.","explanationEn":"The text corrects the popular idea that the conference drew borders, then explains that procedural rules such as \"effective occupation\" set off a race for treaties and expeditions that sped up partition, so D is correct. A gets the treaties and expeditions right, but it repeats the very myth the text rejects, that the conference drew most borders. B misreads the lack of borders as a failure to agree, when in fact the delegates did agree on procedures. C mentions that African representatives were excluded, but the text never says this mattered more than the conference's decisions; its focus is on the effects of the rules.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.613Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"history and civics — The 1884 Berlin Conference partitioning of Africa and European colonial powers' territorial claims without African representation","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"지문의 핵심(국경을 그은 것이 아니라 '실효적 점령' 규칙이 분할을 가속)을 D가 정확히 요약. A는 세부(조약·원정)는 맞으나 지문이 반박한 통념을 전제, C는 배제 사실을 과대평가, B는 절차 합의를 실패로 오독하여 모두 비교 후 배제 가능. 역사적 사실(1884 베를린 회의, 실효적 점령 원칙, 아프리카 대표 부재) 정확. 한·영 해설 결론 및 글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"역사적 사실(실효적 점령, 해안 영유 통보, 아프리카인 불참)이 정확함. A는 통념을 따르는 함정, B·C는 부분적 근거가 있는 오답으로 적절한 중간 난이도.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-075","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-078","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Many accounts of the 1956 Suez Crisis treat it as the moment Britain's imperial decline became visible to the world. When Egyptian President Gamal Abdel Nasser nationalized the Suez Canal Company in July of that year, Britain, together with France and Israel, launched a military intervention to regain control of the waterway. Within weeks, financial pressure from the United States forced a humiliating British withdrawal. __Yet historian Wm. Roger Louis has argued that the crisis did less to cause Britain's retreat from empire than to expose a weakness that officials in London had privately acknowledged for years.__ In his reading, the canal episode mattered chiefly because it stripped away the public pretense that Britain could still act as a great power independent of Washington.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It presents evidence that the British withdrawal from Egypt was caused mainly by American financial pressure.","It explains why Nasser chose to nationalize the canal company at that particular moment in 1956.","It introduces a scholar's view that qualifies the common account of the crisis's significance described earlier.","It concludes that the Suez Crisis had little effect on how Britain was perceived internationally."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 시작해 앞의 통설(수에즈 위기가 영국 쇠퇴가 드러난 순간)을 소개한 뒤, Louis가 위기는 쇠퇴의 원인이라기보다 이미 알려진 약점을 드러냈다고 본다는 수정적 견해를 제시하므로 C가 정답이다. A는 미국의 재정 압박이 앞 문장에 나오지만 밑줄 문장은 철수 원인의 증거를 제시하지 않는다. B는 나세르의 국유화 동기를 다루지 않으므로 틀리다. D는 마지막 문장이 위기가 영국의 '공적 가식'을 벗겨냈다고 하므로 국제적 인식에 큰 영향이 있었다는 내용과 모순된다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence begins with \"Yet,\" which signals a turn away from the common account given earlier (that Suez was the moment Britain's decline became visible). It then presents Louis's more nuanced view: the crisis exposed a weakness instead of causing it. That makes C correct. A is wrong because American financial pressure is mentioned in the previous sentence, and the underlined sentence offers no evidence about why Britain withdrew. B is wrong because the sentence never discusses Nasser's motives. D is wrong because the final sentence says the crisis stripped away Britain's public pretense, so it clearly did change how Britain was seen.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.613Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"history and civics — The 1956 Suez Crisis and Egyptian nationalization of the canal challenging British imperial decline","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 통설과 대비되는 Louis의 수정적 견해를 도입하므로 C가 정확함. A(미국 재정 압박 언급)와 D(인식 변화 관련)는 지문 내용에 부분적 근거가 있어 비교가 필요하고, B는 가장 약하나 지문 소재상 말이 됨. 한·영 해설 모두 동일 결론·글자 참조, 모순 없음. Wm. Roger Louis의 입장 서술도 실제 학계 견해와 어긋나지 않음. 다만 통설 자체가 '쇠퇴가 가시화된 순간'이라 Louis 견해와의 대비가 다소 미묘한 편이나 '원인 vs. 노출' 구도로 충분히 성립함."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"지문 논리에 미세한 약점이 있다. 통설은 위기를 '쇠퇴가 가시화된 순간'으로 기술할 뿐 '원인'으로 보지는 않는데, Louis는 '원인이라기보다'라고 반박한다. 'qualifies'라는 표현이 이 약점을 덮어 주므로 정답 C는 유효하다. A와 D는 부분적인 근거가 있지만 B는 쉽게 배제되어, medium 난이도의 하단에 해당한다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-078","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-080","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Historians have long described Britain's Great Reform Act of 1832 as the moment the middle class entered political life. The act did extend the vote to many householders in towns, raising the electorate from roughly 400,000 to about 650,000 men. __Yet historian Philip Salmon argues that the act's most lasting effect came not from who could vote but from a new requirement that voters register in advance.__ Because registration could be challenged in annual courts, local party associations formed to sign up supporters and dispute opponents' claims, and these associations became permanent organizations that drew middle-class men into politics between elections.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It introduces a view that moves attention from the act's expansion of the electorate to a procedural feature that the rest of the text then explains.","It introduces a view that rejects the claim that the act increased the number of voters, which the rest of the text then disproves.","It introduces a view that summarizes the statistics on voters given earlier, which the rest of the text then expands with further figures.","It introduces a view that explains why historians first called the act a turning point, which the rest of the text then defends."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 시작해 선거권 확대라는 기존 초점에서 사전 등록 요건이라는 절차적 특징으로 관심을 옮기고, 이어지는 문장이 등록 법정과 정당 조직 형성으로 그 영향을 설명하므로 A가 정답이다. B는 문장이 대조를 이룬다는 점은 맞지만, Salmon은 유권자 수 증가를 부정하지 않고 다른 효과가 더 지속적이었다고 말할 뿐이다. C는 앞 문장의 수치와 연결되는 듯하지만 밑줄 문장은 수치를 요약하지 않으며 뒤에도 추가 수치가 없다. D는 '전환점'이라는 앞 내용과 이어지지만, 밑줄 문장은 기존 평가의 이유를 설명하는 것이 아니라 다른 해석을 내놓는다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence begins with \"Yet\" and moves attention from the act's widening of the vote to a procedural feature, advance registration. The next sentence then explains how registration courts led to permanent party associations, so A is correct. B gets the contrast right, but Salmon never denies that the electorate grew; he only argues that another effect lasted longer. C ties the sentence to the earlier figures, but the sentence doesn't summarize those numbers, and no new figures come after it. D links to the \"turning point\" idea, but the sentence offers a different interpretation rather than explaining the traditional one.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.613Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"history and civics — The 1832 Great Reform Act expanding English voting franchise and middle-class political participation mechanisms","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 선거권 확대(앞 문장)에서 사전 등록 요건(절차적 특징)으로 초점을 옮기고, 마지막 문장이 그 요건의 결과(등록 법정→정당 조직)를 설명하므로 A가 정확함. B는 Salmon이 유권자 증가를 부정하지 않으므로 오답, C는 수치 요약·추가 수치 없음, D는 기존 평가의 이유 설명이 아니라 대안 해석 제시이므로 오답. 1832년 개혁법 유권자 수(약 40만→65만)와 Philip Salmon의 등록제 중심 해석은 실제 학설과 부합. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 동일 결론과 선택지 참조로 일관되며 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 오답 세 개 모두 지문의 일부 요소(대조, 수치, '전환점')와 연결되는 부분적 근거를 가져 medium 난이도에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"유권자 수 약 40만→65만은 통설 수치(약 43.5만→65.2만)와 대체로 맞는다. 등록 요건과 정당 조직 형성에 관한 Salmon의 논지도 실제 연구(Electoral Reform at Work)와 일치한다. B와 D는 일부만 맞는 근거를 갖고 있어 비교해야 배제된다. C는 다소 약한 오답이지만 말은 된다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-080","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-081","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Lloyd's of London is often described as an insurance company, but it is better understood as a marketplace. Rather than a single firm setting prices, dozens of independent syndicates—groups of investors backing a specialist underwriter—compete to take on portions of a given risk. When a shipowner seeks coverage for a vessel crossing a hazardous strait, a broker carries the proposal from one syndicate to another. A \"lead\" underwriter, typically one with recognized expertise in that type of voyage, examines the ship's age, cargo, route, and crew record and proposes a premium; other syndicates may then accept a share of the risk on those terms or decline.\n\nEconomic historians argue that this arrangement allowed maritime risk to be priced more accurately than a single insurer could manage. Because each underwriter staked capital on its own judgment, poorly reasoned quotes were quickly exposed when other syndicates refused to follow them, while a lead underwriter whose assessments proved reliable attracted more followers over time. The market's prices, in this view, reflected the pooled scrutiny of many specialists rather than the estimate of any one of them.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Lloyd's of London relied on lead underwriters with recognized expertise because individual syndicates lacked the capital to assess maritime voyages on their own.","Lloyd's of London's structure, in which competing syndicates each risked capital on their own assessments, is credited with producing more accurate prices for shipping risks.","Lloyd's of London's brokers determined the premiums for shipping risks by comparing the quotes of many syndicates and selecting the most reliable one.","Lloyd's of London's syndicates tended to decline risks involving hazardous straits unless a lead underwriter had first evaluated the ship's crew record."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 Lloyd's가 단일 회사가 아닌 시장이며, 각 신디케이트가 자기 판단에 자본을 걸고 경쟁하기 때문에 해상 위험 가격이 더 정확해졌다고 주장하므로 B가 정답이다. A는 리드 언더라이터가 등장한다는 점은 맞지만, 신디케이트의 자본 부족이라는 이유는 지문에 없다. C는 브로커가 제안서를 전달한다는 점은 맞지만, 프리미엄을 제안하는 것은 리드 언더라이터이지 브로커가 고르는 것이 아니다. D는 지문의 세부 예시(해협, 선원 기록)를 과도하게 일반화한 것으로 중심 내용이 아니다.","explanationEn":"The text says Lloyd's works as a marketplace in which syndicates compete and each puts capital behind its own judgment, and it claims this produced more accurate pricing of maritime risk, so B is correct. A gets it right that lead underwriters exist, but the text never says syndicates lacked capital. C correctly says brokers carry proposals, but the lead underwriter proposes the premium; brokers don't choose among quotes. D takes details from the example (the strait, the crew record) and turns them into a general rule the text never states.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.613Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"economics and business — Lloyds of London insurance market and individual underwriter syndicates pricing maritime risk assessment mechanisms","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B를 직접 검산: 1문단(경쟁 신디케이트가 각자 자본을 걸고 위험 분담)과 2문단(경제사학자들이 이 구조 덕분에 더 정확한 가격 책정이 가능했다고 주장)을 결합한 진술로 중심 내용에 정확히 부합한다. A는 리드 언더라이터의 존재는 맞으나 \"자본 부족\"이라는 인과가 지문에 없고, C는 브로커 역할은 맞으나 프리미엄 제안 주체(리드 언더라이터)를 왜곡했으며, D는 예시 세부(해협·선원 기록)를 일반 규칙으로 과도하게 확장한 세부 사항이다. 두 문단 정보를 연결해야 하고 오답 2개가 부분적 근거를 가지므로 medium에 적합. 한·영 해설 모두 B를 일관되게 뒷받침하며 글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음. Lloyd's의 신디케이트·리드 언더라이터·브로커 구조 서술은 실제와 부합하며 사실 오류 없음. 지문은 독창적 서술로 보여 저작권 의심 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B는 구조 설명과 경제사가들의 평가(is credited with)를 함께 담고 있다. A와 C는 지문에 나온 세부 사항(리드 언더라이터, 브로커)에 근거하지만 메커니즘을 왜곡한다. D는 예시를 지나치게 일반화했다. 중간 난이도에 적합하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-081","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-082","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In the Democratic Republic of the Congo, a large share of cobalt is dug by hand rather than by industrial firms, and in 2019 the government created a state company, Entreprise Générale du Cobalt (EGC), with exclusive rights to buy and export this artisanal output. Officials argued that a single buyer would let them trace the metal, enforce safety rules, and capture revenue that had been lost to middlemen. Economist Raphaël Kabeya, however, found that most hand-dug cobalt never reached EGC. Diggers kept selling to independent trading depots, which paid cash on the spot and accepted ore in any quantity, while EGC paid only after the ore had been tested and graded. Kabeya argues that the monopoly failed not because miners rejected regulation itself but because the official channel could not match the speed and flexibility that cash-poor diggers depended on.","question":"Based on the text, what does Kabeya conclude about why artisanal miners went around EGC?","options":["Miners stayed with independent depots mainly because the depots paid higher prices per ton than EGC offered.","Miners stayed with independent depots mainly because they opposed the safety and tracing rules that EGC was created to enforce.","Miners stayed with independent depots mainly because the depots' immediate, flexible payments suited the miners' financial needs better than EGC's slower process did.","Miners stayed with independent depots mainly because EGC lacked the legal authority to require that artisanal cobalt be sold to it."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"C가 정답이다. Kabeya는 현금이 부족한 광부들이 의존하는 속도와 유연성을 공식 경로가 따라가지 못해 독점이 실패했다고 보며, 이는 즉시 현금 지급, 소량 매입, 검사 후 지급이라는 세부 내용과 연결된다. A는 그럴듯하지만 지문은 가격 차이를 전혀 언급하지 않는다. B는 지문에 규제가 언급되지만 Kabeya가 실패 원인이 규제 거부가 아니라고 분명히 밝혔으므로 정반대다. D는 EGC가 독점권을 가졌다는 지문 내용과 모순된다.","explanationEn":"C is correct. Kabeya says the monopoly failed because the official channel couldn't match the speed and flexibility that cash-poor diggers relied on, and that matches the details about cash on the spot, any quantity accepted, and EGC paying only after testing. A sounds plausible, but the text never mentions a price difference. B picks up on the regulation the text discusses, but Kabeya says outright that miners did not reject regulation itself, so B states the opposite of his view. D contradicts the text, which says EGC was given exclusive rights.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.613Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"economics and business — Congolese cobalt mining artisanal sector and informal supply chains bypassing official export monopoly controls","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 C는 마지막 문장(\"could not match the speed and flexibility that cash-poor diggers depended on\")과 중간의 세부(현금 즉시 지급, 소량 매입 vs 검사 후 지급)를 연결해야 확정되므로 2단계 판단에 해당. A는 지문이 언급하지 않은 가격 차이를 끌어들여 그럴듯하게 설계됨, B는 지문의 규제 언급을 활용하되 Kabeya가 명시적으로 부정한 내용, D는 '배타적 권리' 서술과 모순. 해설(한/영) 모두 정답 및 선택지 참조가 일치하고 모순 없음. EGC가 2019년 DRC 정부에 의해 설립되어 수공 코발트 독점 구매·수출권을 가진다는 배경은 사실과 부합하며, 경제학자는 SAT 관행대로 가상의 연구자로 제시됨."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"EGC(2019) 설립은 사실이다. Kabeya는 가상의 인물로 보이지만 문제는 없다. B는 지문의 'not because' 구문을 비틀어 만든 매력적인 오답이다. A는 그럴듯하지만 지문에 근거가 없다. D는 쉽게 배제된다. medium 난이도에 적합하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-082","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-083","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In the seventeenth century, the Dutch Republic controlled much of northern Europe's trade in preserved herring, a position historians often credit simply to the Dutch fleet's size. Economic historian Jan de Vries and others point to a more specific combination of innovations. Dutch crews gutted and salted herring aboard large decked vessels called busses, so the fish could be packed in barrels at sea rather than spoiling on the way to port. The fluyt, a cargo ship developed in the 1590s, then moved those barrels cheaply across the Baltic and beyond: its rounded hull held unusually large cargoes, and its simple rigging let it sail with roughly half the crew that rival ships of similar size needed. Because preservation at sea kept the product's quality steady and the fluyt cut the cost of shipping each barrel, Dutch merchants could sell reliable herring at prices competitors struggled to match.","question":"According to the text, what accounted for the Dutch advantage in the preserved herring trade?","options":["The Dutch fleet's sheer size allowed it to catch more herring than any rival nation could catch.","The fluyt's large rounded hull allowed Dutch crews to gut and salt herring while still at sea.","The busses' small crews made it inexpensive for Dutch merchants to carry herring across the Baltic.","The pairing of at-sea processing with a low-cost cargo ship allowed Dutch merchants to offer dependable fish cheaply."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 두 가지 혁신을 함께 제시한다. 버스선에서 바다 위에 가공해 품질을 유지한 것과, 플루이트선으로 운송비를 낮춘 것이 결합해 우위를 만들었다고 하므로 D가 정답이다. A는 지문이 흔한 설명으로 소개한 뒤 더 구체적인 설명으로 대체하는 견해다. B는 바다 위 가공을 플루이트선의 일로 잘못 연결했는데, 실제로 가공은 버스선에서 이루어졌다. C는 적은 선원 수라는 특징을 플루이트선이 아닌 버스선에 잘못 붙였다.","explanationEn":"The text names two innovations that worked together: processing fish at sea on busses kept quality steady, and the fluyt lowered the shipping cost per barrel. Because the Dutch combined these two, D is correct. A states the common explanation, which the text brings up only to replace it with a more specific one. B attaches at-sea gutting and salting to the fluyt, but that work happened on the busses. C gives the busses the small-crew feature, but the text says that belonged to the fluyt.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.613Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"economics and business — Dutch Golden Age herring fishery and the fluyt ship design enabling preserved fish export market dominance","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"정답 D는 지문 마지막 문장(\"Because preservation at sea kept the product's quality steady and the fluyt cut the cost... reliable herring at prices competitors struggled to match\")을 정확히 종합한다. A는 지문이 반박하는 통념, B·C는 버스선/플루이트선의 특징을 서로 바꿔 붙인 세부 혼동형 오답으로, 두 선박의 역할을 각각 확인해야 배제되므로 medium 2단계 판단 요건에 부합한다. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 D를 지지하고 글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 역사적 사실(버스선 선상 가공, 1590년대 플루이트, 적은 선원 수, de Vries)도 통설과 부합하며 서술 자체는 독창적 산문으로 저작권 우려 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"B와 C는 지문 속 두 배의 특징을 서로 바꿔 붙인 오답이라 정독해야만 걸러낼 수 있다. A는 지문이 흔한 통념으로 소개한 견해라 그럴듯하게 읽힌다. 정답 D는 지문의 마지막 문장을 바꿔 말한 것이다. medium 난이도에 맞는다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-083","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-084","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Economists studying Bangladesh's garment industry have long described it as a textbook case of a buyer-driven supply chain: large Western retailers set prices and delivery deadlines, and factories compete fiercely to win orders by keeping labor costs low. Researcher Nazia Rahman argues that this picture, while accurate at the top of the chain, obscures what happens below it. In her surveys of Dhaka's industrial suburbs, many registered factories that accepted orders from international buyers did not complete the work themselves. __Instead, they quietly passed portions of each order to smaller, unregistered workshops, which were paid per piece and absorbed sudden spikes in volume when deadlines tightened.__ Because these workshops fall outside inspection regimes, Rahman contends, the cost pressure that retailers apply is not simply borne by the visible factories; it is pushed downward to the least protected workers in the network.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It specifies a practice that supports the researcher's claim that the conventional account leaves out part of the chain's operation.","It specifies a practice that explains why retailers are able to set prices and deadlines for registered factories.","It specifies a practice that the researcher offers as a solution to the problem of weak inspection regimes.","It specifies a practice that challenges the researcher's conclusion about where cost pressure ultimately falls."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 등록 공장이 주문 일부를 비등록 작업장에 넘긴다는 구체적 관행을 제시하며, 이는 기존 설명이 공급망 하층을 가린다는 Rahman의 주장을 뒷받침하므로 A가 정답이다. B는 소매업체의 가격 결정력이 지문 첫 문장에 나오지만 밑줄 문장은 그 원인을 설명하지 않는다. C는 검사 제도가 언급되긴 하나 하도급은 해결책이 아니라 문제의 일부로 제시된다. D는 밑줄 문장이 비용 압력이 하층 노동자에게 전가된다는 결론을 반박하는 것이 아니라 오히려 그 근거가 되므로 틀리다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence describes a concrete practice: registered factories handing parts of orders to unregistered workshops. This backs up Rahman's claim that the standard buyer-driven account hides what happens lower in the chain, so A is correct. B is wrong because the text mentions retailers' power to set prices, but the underlined sentence doesn't explain where that power comes from. C is wrong because inspection regimes do come up, but subcontracting is presented as part of the problem, not as a solution. D is wrong because the sentence supports Rahman's conclusion that cost pressure is pushed down to the least protected workers. It doesn't challenge it.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.613Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"economics and business — Bangladeshi garment factory subcontracting networks and buyer-driven global supply chain labor cost competition","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 \"Instead\"로 앞 문장(등록 공장이 직접 작업하지 않음)을 받아 하도급 관행을 구체화하며, 이는 \"기존 설명이 하층을 가린다\"는 Rahman의 주장을 뒷받침함 → A 정답 확인. B(소매업체 가격 결정력의 원인), C(해결책), D(결론 반박)는 모두 지문과 불일치. B·C는 지문 속 요소(소매업체, 검사 제도)를 차용해 부분적 타당성을 가지며, D는 방향 반전 오답으로 비교적 쉽게 배제되지만 말은 됨. 두 단계 판단(문장 내용 파악 + Rahman 주장과의 연결) 요구로 medium 적합. 해설 한·영 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음, 자연스러움. 가상의 연구자 인용으로 사실 오류·저작권 문제 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 A가 맞다. 선택지 모두 'It specifies a practice that…'로 시작하는 평행 구조라서 기능을 구분해 읽어야 한다. B와 C는 지문 속 요소(가격 결정력, 검사 제도)를 끌어와 그럴듯하게 만들었고, D는 방향을 뒤집은 오답이다. medium 난이도에 맞다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-084","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-085","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In nineteenth-century Australia, colonial governments leased vast inland tracts to pastoralists rather than selling them outright, and many historians have treated these pastoral leases chiefly as a tool for controlling who could occupy land. Economic historian Lena Marchetti argues that the leases also shaped how meat reached growing coastal cities. Because leaseholders lacked secure long-term title, they had little incentive to build costly fencing or local slaughter facilities; instead, they relied on drovers who walked mobs of cattle hundreds of kilometers along stock routes to urban saleyards. __Marchetti notes that stock routes thickened noticeably in districts where leases were shortest, while regions granted longer tenures developed more on-station infrastructure and fewer droving corridors.__ In her view, then, the droving networks that fed Sydney and Melbourne were not simply a response to distance but partly a product of land policy.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It presents a view held by many historians that Marchetti ultimately rejects as unsupported by the evidence.","It offers a pattern that supports Marchetti's claim that lease conditions influenced how cattle were moved to cities.","It explains why drovers preferred to walk cattle along stock routes rather than use on-station slaughter facilities.","It offers a pattern that suggests distance alone, rather than lease conditions, determined where droving corridors formed."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 임차 기간이 짧은 지역일수록 가축 이동로가 많고 긴 지역일수록 현지 시설이 많았다는 패턴을 제시해, 임대 정책이 육류 공급 방식을 형성했다는 Marchetti의 주장을 뒷받침하므로 B가 정답이다. A는 역사가들의 일반적 견해가 첫 문장에 나오지만 밑줄 문장은 그 견해가 아니라 Marchetti의 근거이므로 틀렸다. C는 투자 유인 부족을 설명한 것은 앞 문장이며, 밑줄 문장은 드로버의 선호를 설명하지 않는다. D는 '패턴 제시'라는 틀은 맞지만 결론이 정반대로, 지문은 거리만이 원인이 아니라고 말한다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence describes a pattern: stock routes were denser where leases were shortest, and longer tenures brought more on-station infrastructure. That pattern backs Marchetti's claim that land policy shaped how meat reached cities, so B is correct. A is wrong because the historians' view appears in the first sentence, and the underlined sentence is Marchetti's evidence, not that view. C is wrong because the sentence before it gives the reasoning about incentives, and the underlined sentence says nothing about what drovers preferred. D describes the sentence's form correctly (it offers a pattern) but gets the conclusion backward, since the text says droving was not simply a response to distance.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.613Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"economics and business — Australian cattle station pastoral lease system and long-distance droving networks supplying colonial urban meat demand","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 짧은 임차 지역에 가축 이동로가 많고 긴 임차 지역에 현지 시설이 많다는 상관 패턴을 제시하며, 이는 '임대 정책이 육류 유통 방식을 형성했다'는 Marchetti 주장의 근거로 기능하므로 B가 정답임을 직접 확인. A(역사가 견해는 첫 문장), C(유인 설명은 직전 문장이며 드로버 선호를 다루지 않음), D(결론이 정반대)는 모두 지문 근거로 배제 가능. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 B 결론과 선택지 참조가 일치하고 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 가상의 역사가·일반적 역사 배경으로 저작권·사실 오류 우려 없음. 패턴 식별 + 주장과의 연결이라는 두 단계 판단이 필요하고 C·D가 부분적으로 맞는 근거를 가져 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B가 명확한 정답. A는 첫 문장의 역사가 견해를 이용한 함정이고, C는 앞 문장의 인과를 이용한 함정이며, D는 형식은 맞지만 결론이 반대인 함정이다. 오답이 부분적 근거를 가지므로 medium 난이도에 적합하다. 다만 A는 Marchetti가 기존 견해를 '거부'하지 않고 '또한(also)'으로 보완한다는 점에서 배제가 비교적 쉽다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-085","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-086","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Tardigrades, microscopic animals often called water bears, can survive almost complete drying by entering a state known as anhydrobiosis. As water leaves their bodies, they pull in their legs and contract into a compact form called a tun, and their metabolism slows to levels that can barely be detected. For years, researchers assumed that tardigrades, like brine shrimp and some nematodes, protected their cells mainly by filling them with the sugar trehalose, which turns into a glassy solid that holds delicate structures in place. However, many tardigrade species produce little or no trehalose. In 2017, biologist Thomas Boothby and colleagues reported that tardigrades instead rely on a family of proteins found only in their group, called tardigrade-specific intrinsically disordered proteins (TDPs). When genes for these proteins were silenced, the animals no longer survived drying well, and when the proteins were added to yeast and bacteria, those organisms became more tolerant of desiccation. Like trehalose, the proteins appear to form a glass-like matrix as cells dry, which suggests that tardigrades arrived at a familiar protective strategy by using a very different molecule.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Tardigrades survive drying mainly by contracting into a tun and slowing their metabolism, which makes the chemical makeup of their cells less important than researchers once believed.","Tardigrades protect their cells during drying by producing larger amounts of trehalose than brine shrimp and nematodes do, which explains why they tolerate harsher conditions.","Tardigrades appear to protect their cells during drying with proteins unique to their group, which seem to work much as trehalose does in other animals.","Tardigrade proteins have been shown to make yeast and bacteria more tolerant of drying, which suggests the proteins may soon be widely used to preserve other organisms."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 지문은 트레할로스가 주된 보호 수단이라는 기존 가정을 소개한 뒤, 타디그레이드는 고유 단백질(TDP)에 의존하며 이 단백질이 트레할로스처럼 유리 같은 기질을 만든다는 점을 제시하므로 C가 정답이다. A는 툰 형성과 대사 저하라는 지문의 세부 내용을 다루지만, 화학적 보호가 덜 중요하다는 주장은 지문에 없다. B는 트레할로스를 언급하지만, 지문은 많은 종이 트레할로스를 거의 만들지 않는다고 말하므로 지문과 모순된다. D는 효모·세균 실험이라는 근거 하나만 보고 지문에 없는 미래 응용까지 추론한 것이다.","explanationEn":"C is correct. The passage first describes the old assumption that trehalose was the main protection, then reports that tardigrades rely on their own unique proteins (TDPs), which seem to form a glassy matrix the same way trehalose does. A uses real details from the passage, the tun and the slowed metabolism, but the passage never says that cell chemistry matters less. B mentions trehalose, but it contradicts the passage, which says many species make little or no trehalose. D takes one supporting detail, the yeast and bacteria experiment, and adds a prediction about future uses that the passage never makes.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.613Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"life science — Tardigrades' cryptobiosis mechanism and anhydrobiosis survival strategy enabling extreme environmental stress tolerance","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"지문은 Boothby et al. 2017(Molecular Cell)의 TDP 연구를 정확히 반영함(RNAi 침묵 시 생존율 저하, 효모·세균 발현 시 내건성 증가, 유리화). 정답 C는 '기존 가정(트레할로스) → 새로운 발견(고유 단백질) → 유사한 보호 전략'이라는 지문 구조를 정확히 요약. A는 실제 세부(툰·대사 저하)를 쓰되 지문에 없는 주장을 덧붙였고, D는 실험 세부를 근거로 지문 밖 응용을 추론해 둘 다 비교·배제가 필요한 오답. B는 지문과 직접 모순되지만 트레할로스 언급으로 표면상 그럴듯함. 한·영 해설 모두 글자 참조와 논리가 일치하며 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 오리지널 작성 지문으로 보이며 저작권 의심 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"Boothby et al. 2017 실제 연구와 부합. 오답 A·D는 지문 세부를 부분적으로 활용해 비교가 필요하고, B는 명백한 모순이지만 그럴듯함. medium 적합.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-086","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-088","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Many mammals, from rats to rhesus monkeys, eat the placenta shortly after giving birth, a behavior known as placentophagy. A long-standing explanation holds that the placenta replenishes iron and protein lost during delivery. Yet biologist Mark Kristal and colleagues observed that rats fed placenta did not show meaningfully better nutrient levels than rats fed ordinary meat of equal weight. What the placenta-fed rats did show was a stronger natural pain-relieving response during and after birth, an effect that ordinary meat did not produce. Kristal's team traced this effect to a substance in placental tissue and amniotic fluid that appears to amplify the body's own opioid system. Building on such findings, some researchers now suspect that placentophagy is valuable less as a meal than as a source of chemical signals, possibly including ones that influence oxytocin release and early maternal care, though this link has not yet been firmly established.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Evidence from rats suggests that eating the placenta may benefit mammal mothers mainly through its biochemical effects rather than its nutritional value.","Evidence from rats suggests that eating the placenta benefits mammal mothers mainly by restoring the iron and protein lost during birth.","Evidence from rats suggests that eating the placenta triggers oxytocin release that directly strengthens early maternal care in mammals.","Evidence from rats suggests that eating the placenta offers mammal mothers no measurable advantage over eating ordinary meat."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 글은 영양 회복 가설이 쥐 실험 결과로 약해졌고, 진통 효과와 화학 신호가 더 중요한 이점일 수 있다고 말하므로 정답은 A이다. B는 글에서 소개만 하고 반박하는 기존 가설을 그대로 주장한다. C는 글 마지막에 나오지만 아직 확인되지 않았다고 밝힌 옥시토신 연결을 확정된 사실처럼 말한다. D는 영양 면에서는 맞지만, 일반 고기에는 없던 진통 효과를 무시한다.","explanationEn":"The text says the rat findings weakened the nutrient-recovery hypothesis and points instead to pain relief and chemical signals as the likely benefits, so A is correct. B states the older hypothesis, which the text brings up only so it can challenge it. C treats the oxytocin link as fact, but the text says that link has not yet been firmly established. D holds up only for nutrition, since it ignores the pain-relieving effect that ordinary meat did not produce.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.614Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"life science — Placentophagy in mammals and postpartum maternal nutrient recovery oxytocin hormone secretion hypothesis","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 A 검산 일치: 글은 영양 가설(B)을 소개 후 쥐 실험으로 약화시키고, 진통 효과·화학 신호를 핵심 이점으로 제시하며, 옥시토신 연결은 미확정이라고 명시(C 배제). D는 영양 비교에서만 맞고 진통 효과를 무시하여 부분 정답형 오답으로 기능. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 글자 참조와 결론이 일치하고 자연스러움. Kristal의 POEF 연구는 실존하며 서술이 그 취지와 부합해 사실 오류 없음. 지문은 자체 작성된 원문으로 저작권 우려 없음. 반박된 가설 식별 + 마지막 문장의 유보 표현 확인이라는 두 단계 판단이 필요하고, C·D가 부분적 근거를 갖춘 오답이어서 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"Kristal의 POEF(placental opioid-enhancing factor) 연구와 사실이 일치한다. 오답 B·C·D는 각각 지문의 일부(기존 가설, 미확정 옥시토신 연결, 영양 차이 없음)에 근거한 그럴듯한 함정이어서 medium 난이도에 적합하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-088","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-089","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Three-toed sloths descend from the forest canopy about once a week to defecate at the base of their trees, a trip that exposes them to predators and burns precious energy. Ecologist Jonathan Pauli and colleagues proposed that the habit is tied to moths living in the sloths' fur: female moths leave the sloth during these descents to lay eggs in the dung, and the emerging adults fly up to colonize sloths in the canopy. The moths, in turn, appear to deposit nitrogen and other nutrients into the fur, fueling the growth of algae there. __Notably, the researchers found that sloths carrying more moths also had higher concentrations of inorganic nitrogen and greater algal biomass in their fur.__ Because sloths have been observed licking algae from their coats, and because the algae are rich in digestible carbohydrates and lipids, the team suggested that this greenish growth may supplement the sloths' notoriously low-nutrient diet of leaves, in addition to helping camouflage them among the foliage.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It presents a finding that challenges the claim that sloths descend from the canopy in order to aid the moths' reproduction.","It provides evidence for a proposed link between the moths and algal growth that the text goes on to connect to a possible benefit for sloths.","It introduces a finding that explains why sloths choose to defecate at the base of their trees rather than in the canopy.","It offers an observation suggesting that algae, rather than moths, are the main source of nitrogen in sloths' fur."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 나방이 많을수록 털 속 질소와 조류가 많다는 결과로, 바로 앞 문장의 '나방이 영양분을 공급해 조류 성장을 돕는다'는 주장을 뒷받침하고, 이후 문장은 이 조류가 나무늘보의 영양·위장에 도움이 될 수 있다고 연결하므로 B가 정답이다. A는 이 결과가 연구진의 가설을 반박하는 것이 아니라 오히려 지지한다는 점에서 틀렸다. C는 나무늘보의 하강 행동이 지문에서 다뤄지긴 하지만, 밑줄 문장은 하강의 이유가 아니라 털 속 성분을 다룬다. D는 질소의 원천을 거꾸로 서술하고 있는데, 지문은 나방이 영양분을 공급한다고 말한다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence reports that sloths with more moths had more nitrogen and algae in their fur. This backs up the previous sentence's claim that moths supply nutrients that help algae grow, and the next sentence then ties those algae to possible nutrition and camouflage benefits for sloths, so B is correct. A is wrong because the finding supports the researchers' hypothesis instead of challenging it. C is wrong because the text does discuss the descents, but the underlined sentence is about what is in the fur, not about why sloths come down to defecate. D reverses the source of the nitrogen, since the text says the moths supply the nutrients.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.614Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"life science — Sloth moth symbiosis and algal growth on fur providing camouflage and nutritional benefits","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 '나방→질소→조류' 가설을 뒷받침하는 상관관계 결과이며, 다음 문장이 조류를 나무늘보의 영양·위장 이익과 연결하므로 B가 정확하다. A(반박)·D(원천 역전)는 지문과 반대이고, C는 하강 행동이 지문의 큰 틀이라는 점에서 부분적 근거가 있으나 밑줄 문장 자체는 털 성분을 다루므로 배제 가능. 앞뒤 문장을 연결해 기능을 판단해야 하므로 medium에 적합. Pauli et al.(2014) 연구 내용과 사실관계 일치, 지문은 독자적 서술로 저작권 의심 없음. 한·영 해설 결론과 선택지 참조 일치."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"Pauli et al. 2014 연구를 바탕으로 한 문항이며 내용이 정확하다. B는 앞 문장(근거)과 뒤 문장(이점)을 모두 연결해야 고를 수 있다. A, C, D는 각각 지문의 요소(가설, 하강, 질소)를 활용하므로 그럴듯한 오답이다. 다만 D는 비교적 쉽게 배제된다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-089","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-090","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Remoras are fish that ride on sharks, whales, and sea turtles, clinging to their hosts with a flattened disc on top of the head. The disc is a modified dorsal fin whose rows of bony plates, called lamellae, can be raised to create pockets of low pressure against the host's skin. For decades, researchers assumed that remoras attached wherever they could grip and simply endured the turbulent water rushing past. __However, when biologist Brooke Flammang and colleagues attached tags to blue whales and filmed the remoras riding on them, they found that the fish gathered mostly in a few areas, such as behind the blowhole, where the flow of water over the whale's body is slower.__ In these sheltered zones, a remora experiences far less drag than it would in open water, letting it hitch a ride while spending little energy, and its disc lets it slide across the skin to feed without fully letting go.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It explains how the lamellae on a remora's disc produce the low pressure that holds the fish against a host.","It presents evidence that remoras on blue whales face stronger turbulence than researchers had previously estimated.","It presents a finding that challenges an earlier assumption and sets up the explanation of how remoras limit the drag they experience.","It presents a finding that resolves a disagreement among researchers about which host species remoras prefer."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 'However'로 시작해 '아무 데나 붙어 난류를 견딘다'는 기존 가정과 반대되는 관찰(흐름이 느린 특정 부위에 모임)을 제시하고, 이어지는 문장이 그 부위에서 항력이 줄어드는 이유를 설명하므로 C가 정답이다. A는 흡착판 원리를 다루지만 그것은 밑줄 이전 문장의 내용이다. B는 난류라는 단어를 공유하지만 연구 결과는 오히려 난류가 약한 곳을 고른다는 것이다. D는 연구 결과를 언급하나 숙주 종에 대한 연구자 간 논쟁은 지문에 없다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence opens with \"However\" and reports an observation (remoras cluster in slow-flow areas) that contradicts the earlier assumption that they grip anywhere and endure turbulence, and the next sentence explains how those zones reduce drag, so C is correct. A describes the disc mechanism, but that is the job of the sentence before the underlined one. B borrows the word turbulence, yet the finding shows remoras avoid strong flow rather than face more of it. D correctly treats the sentence as a finding, but the text never mentions a debate about preferred host species.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.614Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"life science — Remora fish suction disc attachment mechanism and hydrodynamic drag reduction in host swimming behavior","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 'However'로 앞 문장의 가정(아무 데나 붙어 난류를 견딤)을 뒤집는 관찰을 제시하고, 다음 문장이 항력 감소 원리를 설명하므로 C가 정확함. A는 지문 내 실제 내용(흡착판 원리)이지만 밑줄 앞 문장의 기능, B는 '난류' 어휘를 공유하나 방향이 반대, D는 '연구 결과'라는 틀은 맞으나 숙주 종 논쟁은 없음. 한·영 해설 모두 동일 결론·글자 참조, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. Flammang 연구팀의 대왕고래 리모라 관찰(분수공 뒤 등 저유속 구역 집중)은 실제 연구 내용과 일치. 지문은 독창적 서술로 저작권 의심 없음. 가정-반전-설명의 두 단계 연결이 필요하고 오답들이 부분적 근거를 가져 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"Flammang 연구진의 대왕고래 빨판상어 연구(2020)와 일치한다. 'However' 단서가 뚜렷해 다소 쉬운 편이지만, B·D가 부분적으로 그럴듯해서 medium 범위에 든다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-090","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-093","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Satellite images taken since the 1960s show that the open water of Lake Chad, on the southern edge of the Sahara, shrank by roughly 90 percent within a few decades. The shrinkage was often presented as a textbook case of climate-driven desertification across the Sahel. More recent analyses that combine satellite gravity measurements with long-term rainfall records make the picture more complicated. These studies find that the lake's northern basin did largely dry out during the severe droughts of the 1970s and 1980s, but that the southern basin has been fairly stable since the 1990s, and groundwater beneath the region has even increased slightly. Researchers argue that the lake's decline reflects a shift in rainfall patterns followed by partial recovery, along with heavy irrigation withdrawals, rather than a steady, ongoing march of the desert.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Satellite images confirm that Lake Chad has lost about 90 percent of its water, showing that desertification across the Sahel continues to speed up.","Newer data suggest that Lake Chad's decline came mostly from past droughts and water use and has partly leveled off, not from continuous desertification.","Irrigation withdrawals, not changes in rainfall, are the only reason Lake Chad's northern basin dried out in the 1970s and 1980s.","Groundwater beneath the Lake Chad region has increased enough that the lake's open water is expected to return to its 1960s extent."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"이 글은 처음에는 차드호 축소를 기후로 인한 사막화의 대표 사례로 소개한 뒤, 새로운 자료가 그런 시각을 수정한다고 설명한다. 축소의 원인은 과거의 가뭄과 관개였고 이후 어느 정도 안정되었다는 것이 핵심이므로 B가 정답이다. A는 90% 감소라는 수치는 맞지만, 글이 반박하는 '계속되는 사막화' 해석을 그대로 받아들이고 있다. C는 관개가 언급되었다는 점은 맞지만, 강우 변화를 원인에서 빼고 '유일한 원인'이라고 지나치게 단정한다. D는 지하수 증가라는 세부 내용을 1960년대 수준으로의 회복 예측으로 부풀렸는데, 글에는 그런 예측이 없다.","explanationEn":"The text first presents Lake Chad's shrinkage as the classic example of climate-driven desertification, then explains how newer data revise that view. Its main point is that the decline came from past droughts and irrigation and has partly stabilized, so B is correct. A gets the 90 percent figure right, but it accepts the \"ongoing desertification\" interpretation that the text argues against. C is right that irrigation is mentioned, but it leaves out the shift in rainfall and goes too far by calling irrigation the only cause. D takes the detail about rising groundwater and stretches it into a prediction that the lake will return to its 1960s size, which the text never makes.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.614Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"earth and space science — Lake Chad shrinkage over fifty years satellite monitoring Sahel climate desertification documented change","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"지문은 '기존 해석(기후 사막화) → 새 자료로 수정(과거 가뭄+관개, 부분 안정)' 구조이며 B가 이를 정확히 요약함. A는 90% 수치는 맞으나 글이 반박하는 '가속되는 사막화'를 주장해 틀림, C는 '유일한 원인'·강우 배제로 지문과 모순, D는 지하수 소폭 증가를 1960년대 수준 회복 예측으로 과장. 한·영 해설 모두 정답과 선택지 글자 참조가 일치하고 모순 없음. 차드호 약 90% 축소, GRACE 중력 관측 기반 지하수 증가 등 사실관계도 실제 연구(예: Pham-Duc et al. 2020)와 부합. 전체 구조 파악 + 세부 정보 대조라는 두 단계 판단이 필요하고 오답 3개가 모두 지문의 일부 사실에 근거하므로 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"B는 기존 해석을 수정하는 구조와 원인(가뭄·관개)·부분 안정을 모두 담는다. A는 앞부분만 읽으면 끌리는 오답이고, C·D는 세부 내용을 과장했다. medium 수준에 맞다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-093","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-094","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"On most days, air near the ground is warmer than the air above it, so pollutants released by cars and furnaces rise and disperse as the warm air lifts. During winter in mountain valleys such as Utah's Salt Lake Valley, however, cold, dense air can settle on the valley floor beneath a layer of warmer air that has moved in overhead. This arrangement, called a thermal inversion, acts like a lid: the cold surface air cannot rise through the warmer layer, and the surrounding mountains block it from flowing out sideways. Researchers tracking fine-particle pollution in the valley have found that daily emissions during inversion episodes are roughly the same as on clear days. Yet particle concentrations climb steadily the longer an inversion persists, sometimes exceeding federal health limits within a few days, and then drop sharply once a passing storm mixes the layers apart.","question":"Based on the text, what accounts for the worsening air quality in the Salt Lake Valley during inversion episodes?","options":["Cold air on the valley floor causes vehicles and furnaces to release more fine particles than they do on clear days.","Warm air arriving overhead carries pollutants into the valley from distant sources beyond the mountains.","Pollutants that would ordinarily disperse accumulate because the cold surface air is held in place by the warm layer and the mountains.","Storms passing through the valley stir up particles that then remain suspended near the ground for several days."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 역전 기간에도 배출량은 맑은 날과 비슷하지만, 따뜻한 상층이 뚜껑처럼 작용하고 산이 옆으로 빠져나가는 것을 막아 오염물질이 쌓인다고 설명하므로 C가 정답이다. A는 겨울철 연소와 그럴듯하게 연결되지만 배출량이 거의 같다는 진술과 모순된다. B는 따뜻한 공기가 위로 들어온다는 점은 맞지만, 그 공기가 오염물질을 실어 온다는 내용은 지문에 없다. D는 폭풍을 언급하지만 지문에서 폭풍은 층을 섞어 농도를 낮추는 역할을 한다.","explanationEn":"C is correct. The text says emissions during inversions are about the same as on clear days, but the warm layer acts as a lid and the mountains block sideways flow, so pollutants build up. A sounds reasonable because furnaces burn more in winter, but it contradicts the statement that emissions stay roughly the same. B is right that warm air moves in overhead, but the text never says that air brings pollution with it. D mentions storms, but in the text storms mix the layers apart and lower concentrations.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.614Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"earth and space science — Thermal inversion atmospheric layers trapping pollution in mountain valleys urban air quality degradation","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 C는 지문의 '배출량 동일 + 뚜껑/산에 의한 갇힘' 설명과 정확히 일치. A는 배출량 동일 진술과 모순, B는 지문에 없는 외부 유입 가정, D는 폭풍 역할 반전. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 두 정보(배출량 불변 + 갇힘 메커니즘) 연결이 필요해 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"정답을 고르려면 배출량이 같다는 진술과 뚜껑 및 산이라는 메커니즘을 연결해야 함. A와 B는 부분적으로 그럴듯한 오답이고 D도 지문 요소를 활용함. medium 수준에 적합.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-094","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-095","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In a handful of estuaries worldwide, such as the Qiantang in China and the Severn in Britain, the incoming tide arrives not as a gradual rise but as a single wall of water called a tidal bore. Researchers have long attributed bores mainly to the funnel shape of these estuaries: as the channel narrows and shallows upstream, the energy of the tidal wave is squeezed into a smaller cross section, steepening its front. __Yet funneling alone cannot explain why some narrow estuaries produce towering bores while others of similar shape produce none.__ Hydrologists now argue that resonance is also crucial. When the time a tidal wave takes to travel the length of an estuary and reflect back roughly matches a fraction of the tidal period, successive waves reinforce one another, amplifying the tidal range enough for a bore to form.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It presents evidence that the funnel-shaped explanation of tidal bores is mistaken and should be replaced by the resonance account that follows.","It explains how the narrowing of an estuary steepens the front of an incoming tidal wave, which the text then illustrates with examples.","It summarizes the conditions under which the resonance described later in the text is most likely to produce a bore.","It identifies a gap in a long-standing account of tidal bores, which motivates the additional factor introduced afterward."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 깔때기 모양만으로는 비슷한 하구 간 차이를 설명할 수 없다고 지적해 기존 설명의 한계를 드러내고, 이어서 공명이라는 추가 요인을 도입하므로 D가 정답이다. A는 '또한(also) 중요하다'는 표현과 어긋나게 기존 설명을 폐기·대체한다고 과장한다. B는 앞 문장의 내용(깔때기의 파도 가파르게 하기)을 밑줄 문장의 기능으로 착각한 것이다. C는 공명 조건을 요약하는 것은 마지막 문장이며 밑줄 문장은 공명을 언급하지도 않는다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence points out that funneling can't account for why similarly shaped estuaries differ, exposing a limit of the established explanation; the text then adds resonance as another factor, so D is correct. A overstates things: the text says resonance is \"also\" crucial, so funneling is supplemented, not rejected. B describes the previous sentence, not the underlined one. C fits the final sentence, which lays out resonance conditions; the underlined sentence doesn't mention resonance at all.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.614Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"earth and space science — Tidal bore phenomenon in funnel-shaped estuaries and resonance amplification of tidal wave height","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 기존 깔때기 설명의 한계를 지적하고 공명 요인 도입을 유도하므로 D가 정확. 'also crucial'로 A의 '대체' 주장 배제 가능. B·C는 각각 앞·뒤 문장의 기능을 차용한 적절한 오답. 해설 한·영 일치, 사실 오류 없음(Qiantang·Severn 보어, 공명 설명 타당). 난이도 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"A는 '한계 지적'이라는 부분적 근거를 가진 그럴듯한 오답이다. 'also'와 대조해야 배제할 수 있다. C도 뒤 내용과 연결되어 있어 그럴듯하다. 중간 난이도에 적합하다. 공명 설명은 과학적으로 타당하다(고유 주기가 조석 주기의 약 1/4).","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-095","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-096","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Most tsunamis are generated when an undersea earthquake abruptly lifts or drops a section of seafloor, displacing the water column above it. Some tsunamis, however, originate when sediment piled on a continental slope gives way and slides downhill, pushing water ahead of it. Geologists have long assumed that such slope failures need a strong earthquake to set them off. __Yet cores drilled from the Storegga slide area off Norway contain thin, weak layers of clay that apparently lost strength gradually as overlying sediment built up and trapped water in their pores.__ This finding suggests that some slopes may become so fragile that even a minor tremor, or none at all, could start a slide, which would make the resulting tsunamis much harder to predict from seismic monitoring alone.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It presents evidence that challenges a long-held assumption, which the text then uses to draw a conclusion about forecasting.","It presents evidence that confirms a long-held assumption, which the text then uses to explain why seismic monitoring is reliable.","It presents evidence that contrasts earthquake-generated tsunamis with slide-generated tsunamis, which the text then uses to show that slides are more common.","It presents evidence that explains how a slide pushes water ahead of it, which the text then uses to describe the size of the resulting tsunami."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 시작해, 사면 붕괴에는 강한 지진이 필요하다는 기존 가정과 달리 점토층이 서서히 약해졌다는 시추 증거를 제시한다. 이어지는 문장은 이 증거를 바탕으로 쓰나미를 지진 관측만으로 예측하기 어렵다는 결론을 내리므로 A가 정답이다. B는 증거가 가정을 확인한다고 하고 지진 관측이 믿을 만하다고 하여 지문과 정반대이다. C는 두 종류의 쓰나미가 지문에 언급되기는 하지만, 밑줄 문장은 둘을 대조하지 않으며 어느 쪽이 더 흔한지도 말하지 않는다. D는 물을 밀어내는 과정이 앞 문장에 나오기는 하지만, 밑줄 문장은 붕괴가 왜 일어나는지를 다룰 뿐 쓰나미 규모는 다루지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence begins with \"Yet.\" It offers core-sample evidence that the clay layers weakened gradually, which goes against the long-held view that slope failures need a strong earthquake. The next sentence uses this evidence to conclude that such tsunamis are hard to predict from seismic monitoring alone, so A is correct. B says the evidence confirms the assumption and that seismic monitoring is reliable, which is the opposite of what the text says. C names two types of tsunamis that do appear in the text, but the underlined sentence doesn't compare them, and the text never says which type is more common. D points to the water-pushing process from an earlier sentence, but the underlined sentence explains why slopes fail, not how big the tsunami gets.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.614Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"earth and space science — Submarine landslide-triggered tsunami generation and offshore sediment slope stability failure mechanisms","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 'Yet'으로 기존 가정(강진 필요)에 반하는 시추 증거를 제시하고, 다음 문장이 이를 근거로 예측 어려움이라는 결론을 도출하므로 A가 정확하다. B는 정반대, C·D는 지문의 다른 문장 내용(두 유형 대조, 물 밀어냄)을 차용한 부분적 근거가 있어 비교가 필요하며, '더 흔하다'·'규모'는 지문에 없다. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 동일 결론·글자 참조로 일관되고 영어 자연스러움. Storegga 사면의 약한 점토층·간극수압 관련 서술은 지질학 문헌과 부합하며 'apparently'로 완화되어 사실 오류 없음. 원창작 지문으로 저작권 문제 없음. 대조 파악 + 전체 글에서의 기능 연결이라는 두 단계 판단이 필요해 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["too_easy","eliminated:3"],"note":"정답 A는 맞다. 다만 오답의 오류가 너무 뻔하다. B는 'Yet'과 정면으로 어긋나는 '가정을 확인한다'를 내세우고, C는 지문에 없는 '어느 쪽이 더 흔한가'를, D는 지문에 없는 '쓰나미 규모'를 근거로 삼는다. 그래서 'Yet' 하나만 보거나 지문을 훑어 읽기만 해도 바로 배제된다. 부분적으로 맞는 근거를 비교해야만 걸러지는 오답이 사실상 없어 medium으로 보기에는 쉽다. 예를 들어 '가정에 도전한다'는 부분은 맞지만 결론의 방향이나 대상이 다른 오답이 있어야 medium에 맞는다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-096","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-097","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"When a liquid is blasted with intense sound waves, tiny gas bubbles form, swell, and then collapse violently, a process called acoustic cavitation. In 1990, physicist Felipe Gaitan found a way to trap a single bubble at the center of a flask of water, where it expanded and collapsed tens of thousands of times per second, giving off a faint flash of blue light with every collapse. This effect, known as sonoluminescence, had been seen in clouds of bubbles since the 1930s, but isolating one bubble let researchers measure it precisely. They found that each flash lasts less than a billionth of a second and that the gas inside the bubble may reach thousands of degrees as the bubble shrinks. Still, how the light is actually produced is debated. Some researchers credit heating from shock waves converging inside the bubble, while others argue that the hot gas simply glows the way any very hot material does, and so far no experiment has clearly ruled out either explanation.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Gaitan's single-bubble experiment showed that sonoluminescence is caused by shock waves converging inside a collapsing bubble.","Trapping a single bubble allowed sonoluminescence to be studied in detail, but the process that creates its light is still unresolved.","Trapping a single bubble showed that sonoluminescence flashes are far hotter and briefer than flashes produced by clouds of bubbles.","Trapping a single bubble allowed researchers to observe sonoluminescence for the first time after decades of failed attempts."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 단일 기포를 가두는 방법 덕분에 소노루미네선스를 정밀하게 측정할 수 있게 되었지만, 빛이 생기는 원리는 여전히 논쟁 중이라고 말하므로 B가 정답이다. A는 여러 가설 중 하나인 충격파를 확정된 결론처럼 말하지만, 지문은 어느 설명도 배제되지 않았다고 한다. C는 지문에 나온 수치를 활용하지만 기포 무리에서 나는 빛과 비교한 내용은 지문에 없다. D는 이 현상이 1930년대부터 이미 관찰되었다는 사실과 어긋난다.","explanationEn":"The text says that isolating one bubble let researchers measure sonoluminescence precisely, but scientists still argue over how the light is produced, so B is correct. A treats one competing hypothesis, shock waves, as proven, while the text says neither explanation has been ruled out. C uses details from the measurements, but the text never compares single-bubble flashes with flashes from bubble clouds. D contradicts the text, which says the effect had already been seen in clouds of bubbles since the 1930s.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.614Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"physical science — Sonoluminescence phenomenon and acoustic cavitation bubble collapse generating light emission mechanism","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"지문은 '단일 기포 포획 → 정밀 측정 가능' + '발광 메커니즘은 미해결'의 두 축으로 구성되어 있고 B가 이를 정확히 요약함. A는 두 가설 중 하나(충격파)를 확정으로 단정해 마지막 문장과 충돌, C는 지문의 수치(10억분의 1초, 수천 도)를 차용하지만 기포 무리와의 비교는 지문에 없음, D는 1930년대부터 관찰됐다는 문장과 모순. 오답 A·C가 지문 세부를 활용한 부분적 근거를 가져 비교가 필요하고, D도 훑어 읽으면 그럴듯하므로 medium 적합. 사실관계(Gaitan 1990 단일 기포 소노루미네선스, 1930년대 다중 기포 관찰, 피코초급 섬광, 메커니즘 논쟁)도 정확함. 한·영 해설 결론 및 선택지 참조 일치, 영어 해설에 한글 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 B가 지문의 두 축(단일 기포로 정밀 측정 가능 + 발광 원리 미해결)을 모두 담는다. A·C·D는 지문의 세부를 부분적으로 활용한 그럴듯한 오답이라 medium 수준에 적합하다. 사실관계(Gaitan 1990, 1930년대 관찰)도 맞다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-097","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-101","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Metal-organic frameworks (MOFs) are crystalline materials built from metal clusters linked by organic molecules, forming networks riddled with tiny pores. Because chemists can choose the linkers, they long assumed that making pores as large and numerous as possible would yield the best materials for capturing gases such as carbon dioxide from industrial exhaust. Some MOFs do have enormous internal surface areas: a single gram can contain more surface than a soccer field. Yet chemist Omar Farha and colleagues found that several of the highest-surface-area frameworks performed poorly at pulling carbon dioxide out of mixtures that also contained nitrogen. In those wide pores, both gases drifted in and out with little preference.\n\nThe more successful frameworks in the team's tests had narrower pores lined with chemical groups that interact strongly with carbon dioxide molecules but only weakly with nitrogen. Shrinking pores reduced the total amount of gas a material could hold, but it greatly increased how selectively the material held carbon dioxide. For separation tasks, the researchers concluded, tailoring pore size and chemistry to the target molecule matters more than maximizing open space.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Research shows that MOFs with very large surface areas can store more carbon dioxide than any other known material, which makes them well suited to cleaning industrial exhaust.","Research suggests that a MOF's ability to separate one gas from another depends less on how much empty space it has than on how well its pores are matched to the desired gas.","Research indicates that narrowing the pores of MOFs improves both the total amount of gas they hold and their preference for carbon dioxide over nitrogen.","Research reveals that MOFs are unable to tell carbon dioxide from nitrogen, so chemists must look for other materials to capture gases from exhaust."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 기공을 최대한 크게 만들면 좋다는 기존 가정을 소개한 뒤, 기체 분리에는 열린 공간을 최대화하기보다 목표 분자에 맞게 기공 크기와 화학적 성질을 조정하는 것이 더 중요하다는 결론으로 끝나므로 B가 정답이다. A는 표면적이 넓다는 세부 내용은 맞지만, 그런 MOF가 분리 성능이 떨어졌다는 핵심 내용과 어긋난다. C는 선택성이 높아졌다는 점은 맞지만, 기공을 좁히면 총 저장량은 오히려 줄었다고 했으므로 틀렸다. D는 일부 넓은 기공의 MOF에만 해당하는 내용을 모든 MOF로 일반화했고, 좁은 기공의 MOF는 성공했다는 점과 모순된다.","explanationEn":"The text starts with the old assumption that bigger pores are better. It then concludes that for separating gases, matching pore size and chemistry to the target molecule matters more than maximizing open space, so B is correct. A gets the large surface areas right, but it ignores the key finding that those high-surface-area MOFs did a poor job at separation. C correctly says selectivity went up, but the text says narrowing the pores actually lowered the total amount of gas a MOF could hold. D takes what happened with some wide-pore MOFs and applies it to all MOFs, which contradicts the success of the narrow-pore frameworks.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.614Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"physical science — Metal-organic framework porosity engineering for selective gas adsorption and separation applications","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 B는 지문 마지막 문장의 결론(열린 공간 최대화보다 목표 분자에 맞춘 기공 크기·화학이 중요)을 정확히 재진술한다. A는 '다른 어떤 물질보다 많이 저장'이라는 근거 없는 과장이자 분리 성능 저하라는 핵심과 어긋나고, C는 총 저장량이 '줄었다'는 지문과 반대이며, D는 일부 넓은 기공 MOF의 결과를 전체로 일반화해 좁은 기공 MOF의 성공과 모순된다. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 같은 결론과 글자 참조를 가지며 영어는 자연스럽고 한글이 없다. Omar Farha는 실제 MOF 연구자이나 지문은 독창적으로 구성된 것으로 보이며, 1g당 축구장 넓이의 표면적 등 사실 관계도 일반적으로 통용되는 수준이다. 기존 가정 vs 새 발견을 연결해야 하고, A·C가 부분적으로 맞는 세부를 담고 있어 비교가 필요하므로 medium에 적합하다."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"C는 절반만 맞는 강한 오답이다. A와 D는 지문 세부 내용을 왜곡했지만 그럴듯하게 읽힌다. 중간 난이도에 적합하다. 다만 Omar Farha라는 실명을 연구 서술에 넣은 점은 확인이 필요하다(허구일 수 있음).","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-101","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-102","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Photochromic eyeglass lenses darken outdoors and clear indoors because of molecules embedded in their plastic. In many lenses, these are spirooxazine molecules, which normally hold a folded, colorless shape. When ultraviolet light strikes one, a chemical bond breaks and the molecule unfolds into a flat form that absorbs visible light, tinting the lens. __Yet the flat form is not stable on its own: once ultraviolet exposure stops, heat from the surroundings gradually pushes the molecules back into their folded shape.__ This reversal is why wearers notice that their lenses fade more slowly on a cold day than on a warm one, since lower temperatures supply less of the energy needed to refold the molecules.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It describes the step by which ultraviolet light gives the molecules a form that tints the lens.","It presents an exception showing that some lenses keep their tint after ultraviolet exposure ends.","It explains a process that the text then uses to account for an effect wearers observe.","It introduces a disagreement about whether heat or light controls how the lenses change."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 자외선이 사라진 뒤 주변의 열이 분자를 다시 접힌 형태로 되돌린다는 과정을 설명하고, 다음 문장은 이를 근거로 추운 날 렌즈가 더 천천히 맑아지는 현상을 설명하므로 C가 정답이다. A는 자외선이 분자를 펼치는 단계를 말하는데, 그것은 밑줄 앞 문장의 내용이고 밑줄 문장은 반대 방향의 과정을 다룬다. B는 'Yet'을 예외 제시로 잘못 읽은 것이며, 실제로는 착색이 사라진다는 내용이다. D는 열과 빛이 모두 언급된 점에 기댄 것이지만, 지문에는 어떤 논쟁도 없고 두 요인이 각각 다른 단계를 맡는다고 설명할 뿐이다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence explains how heat refolds the molecules once ultraviolet light is gone, and the next sentence uses that process to explain why lenses fade more slowly on cold days, so C is correct. A describes ultraviolet light unfolding the molecules, but that happens in the sentence before the underlined one, while the underlined sentence covers the reverse process. B misreads \"Yet\" as signaling an exception, when the sentence actually says the tint goes away. D picks up on the fact that both heat and light are mentioned, but the text describes no disagreement; it just shows each factor driving a different step.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.614Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"physical science — Photochromic lens molecular isomerization and reversible light-induced color change mechanism","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 열에 의한 재접힘(역과정)을 설명하고, 바로 다음 문장이 \"This reversal is why...\"로 이를 착용자가 관찰하는 현상(추운 날 더 느리게 맑아짐)의 근거로 사용하므로 C가 정확하다. A는 앞 문장(자외선에 의한 펼침)의 내용, B는 'Yet'을 오독한 예외 해석, D는 지문에 없는 논쟁을 상정한 오답으로 모두 배제 가능. 스피로옥사진의 UV 개환·열적 복귀 및 저온에서 퇴색이 느려지는 현상은 과학적으로 타당하다. 한·영 해설 결론 및 선택지 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 두 단계 판단(밑줄 내용 파악 + 다음 문장과의 연결)이 요구되어 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 C는 밑줄 문장이 설명하는 과정과 그다음 문장이 설명하는 착용자 관찰 현상을 연결해야 고를 수 있어 두 단계 판단이 필요하다. 오답 A는 앞 문장 내용, B는 'Yet'을 잘못 읽은 경우, D는 열과 빛이 함께 언급된 점에 기댄 경우로, 모두 그럴듯한 함정이다. 스피로옥사진의 광변색 원리와 온도 의존성에 대한 설명도 과학적으로 맞다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-102","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-104","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In petroleum refining, catalytic cracking breaks long hydrocarbon chains into the smaller molecules that make up gasoline. Many refineries rely on zeolites, crystalline aluminosilicates riddled with pores less than a nanometer wide, to speed this process. Because reactions occur mainly inside these micropores, the pore dimensions determine which molecules can enter, which transition states can form, and which products can escape. __One might therefore expect that the zeolite with the widest pores would always be preferred, since it admits the greatest variety of feedstock molecules.__ Yet engineers often favor zeolites with narrower channels: by excluding bulky branched molecules and preventing the formation of large intermediates that tend to produce coke, these tighter pores yield a more predictable product mixture and extend the catalyst's working life.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It presents a seemingly reasonable assumption that the text then shows to be incomplete.","It presents a finding that the text then uses to explain how coke forms inside zeolites.","It presents a conclusion that the text then supports with evidence about catalyst lifespan.","It presents a definition that the text then applies to the selection of refinery feedstocks."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 'One might therefore expect'로 시작하여, 기공 크기가 중요하다는 앞 내용에서 자연스럽게 나올 법한 예상(가장 넓은 기공이 최선)을 제시하고, 바로 다음 'Yet' 문장이 더 좁은 기공이 선호되는 이유를 들어 그 예상이 불충분함을 보여 준다. 따라서 A가 정답이다. B는 코크 형성이 뒤에 언급되기는 하지만 밑줄 문장은 연구 결과가 아니라 가정이며 코크 설명의 근거로 쓰이지 않는다. C는 촉매 수명이 뒤에 나오지만 그것은 밑줄 문장을 뒷받침하는 것이 아니라 반박한다. D는 밑줄 문장이 정의가 아니고, 글은 원료 선택이 아니라 촉매 선택을 다룬다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence begins with \"One might therefore expect,\" which offers a prediction that seems to follow from the earlier point about pore size: the widest pores should always be best. The next sentence opens with \"Yet\" and explains why narrower pores are often chosen, which shows that the expectation is incomplete. That makes A the answer. B doesn't work because the sentence is an assumption, not a finding, and it isn't used to explain how coke forms, even though coke comes up later. C doesn't work because the point about catalyst lifespan argues against the underlined sentence instead of supporting it. D doesn't work because the sentence isn't a definition, and the text is about choosing a catalyst, not choosing feedstocks.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.615Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"physical science — Zeolite catalytic cracking of hydrocarbons and micropore selectivity in petroleum refining","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 'One might therefore expect'로 제시된 예상이며, 바로 뒤 'Yet' 문장이 좁은 기공을 선호하는 이유(부피 큰 분자 배제, 코크 생성 억제, 수명 연장)를 들어 이를 반박·보완하므로 A가 정답임을 직접 확인함. B·C는 본문 후반에 등장하는 세부(코크, 촉매 수명)를 차용해 부분적 그럴듯함을 갖고 있어 비교 배제가 필요하고, D도 문장 성격(정의 아님)과 글의 초점(촉매 선택)으로 배제 가능해 medium에 적합. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 결론과 선택지 참조가 일치하며 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 제올라이트가 1nm 미만 미세기공을 가진 결정성 알루미노규산염이라는 서술 및 형상 선택성 설명은 과학적으로 타당하며, 지문은 창작 설명문으로 저작권 의심 없음. 다만 'One might expect… Yet' 신호어가 매우 뚜렷해 medium 중에서는 다소 쉬운 편."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"'One might expect… Yet' 구조라서 정답을 찾을 수 있음. B와 C는 뒤 문장에 나오는 코크·촉매 수명을 끌어와 부분 근거를 갖춘 오답이고, D는 상대적으로 약함. medium 난이도에 적합함.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-104","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-words_in_context-m-105","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Words in Context","difficulty":"medium","skill":"words_in_context","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"When a suspension of identical silica microspheres is left to settle slowly, the particles can arrange themselves into a highly ordered lattice without any external guidance. Materials scientist Hyun-Woo Baek notes that this process is remarkably ______: even a small fraction of spheres that differ in size disrupts the packing, introducing defects that scatter light randomly and prevent the lattice from reflecting the single, vivid color associated with a photonic bandgap.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["spontaneous","sensitive","efficient","reversible"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"콜론 뒤 내용은 크기가 다른 입자가 조금만 섞여도 배열이 무너진다는 점, 즉 공정이 작은 변화에 쉽게 영향을 받는다는 것을 설명하므로 B(sensitive)가 정답이다. A(spontaneous)는 첫 문장의 '외부 유도 없이'와 맞아 보이지만 콜론 뒤의 결함 설명을 뒷받침하지 못한다. C(efficient)는 질서 있는 격자 형성과 연결될 듯하나 지문은 효율이 아닌 취약성을 강조한다. D(reversible)는 침강·배열 과정과 그럴듯하게 어울리지만 되돌릴 수 있다는 내용은 지문에 없다.","explanationEn":"The text after the colon explains that even a few spheres of a different size disrupt the packing, so the process is easily affected by small variations, which makes B (\"sensitive\") correct. A (\"spontaneous\") seems to fit the first sentence's \"without any external guidance,\" but it doesn't set up the explanation about defects that follows the colon. C (\"efficient\") might seem to go with forming an ordered lattice, but the text stresses how fragile the process is, not how efficient it is. D (\"reversible\") sounds plausible for a settling process, but nothing in the text says the arrangement can be undone.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.615Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"physical science — Colloidal crystal self-assembly and photonic bandgap formation in optical interference structures","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"콜론 뒤 '소량의 크기 차이만으로 배열이 무너진다'는 설명이 '작은 변화에 쉽게 영향받음(sensitive)'을 명확히 뒷받침한다. A(spontaneous)는 첫 문장의 'without any external guidance'와 호응해 훑어 읽으면 고르기 쉬운 강력한 오답이며, C·D도 문맥상 그럴듯해 비교가 필요하다. 콜로이드 결정의 자기조립과 다분산성에 의한 결함, 광결정 밴드갭 색상 등 과학적 내용도 타당하다. 한·영 해설 모두 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 중간 난이도에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"콜론 뒤 내용이 '작은 변동에도 무너짐'을 설명하므로 sensitive가 유일한 정답이다. spontaneous는 첫 문장과 맞아 보이는 강한 오답이고, efficient와 reversible도 그럴듯해서 medium 난이도에 맞다. 콜로이드 결정과 광자 밴드갭 관련 과학 내용도 정확하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-words_in_context-m-105","intendedSkill":"words_in_context","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-words_in_context-m-106","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Words in Context","difficulty":"medium","skill":"words_in_context","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"When a circuit board repeatedly heats up and cools down, its lead-free solder joints are squeezed and stretched because the solder and the board expand at different rates. Materials engineer Priya Raman found that cracks in tin-silver-copper joints rarely begin at random points. Instead, they tend to ______ at the boundaries between tiny grains of the alloy, where strain builds up during each cycle, and only later spread across the rest of the joint.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["propagate","terminate","originate","accumulate"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 균열이 \"무작위 지점에서 시작되지 않고\" 결정립 경계에서 생기며 \"나중에야\" 접합부 전체로 퍼진다고 말하므로, 빈칸에는 '시작되다'라는 뜻의 C(originate)가 들어가야 한다. A(propagate)는 균열과 자주 쓰이는 단어지만 '퍼지다'라는 뜻이어서, 퍼짐을 나중 단계로 따로 언급한 문장과 맞지 않는다. D(accumulate)는 같은 위치에 변형률이 쌓인다는 내용과 비슷해 보이지만, 쌓이는 것은 변형률이지 균열 자체가 아니다. B(terminate)는 균열이 '끝난다'는 뜻이라 '시작'을 대비시키는 문맥과 반대된다.","explanationEn":"The text says cracks \"rarely begin at random points\" and form at grain boundaries, and that they \"only later spread,\" so the blank has to mean \"start.\" That makes C (originate) the answer. A (propagate) is a common word for cracks, but it means \"spread,\" and the text saves spreading for the later stage. D (accumulate) sounds right because strain builds up at those boundaries, but strain is what accumulates there, not the cracks. B (terminate) means \"end,\" which is the opposite of the idea of where cracks begin.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.615Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"physical science — Solder joint fatigue crack initiation in lead-free alloys under thermal cycling stress conditions","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"\"rarely begin at random points. Instead, they tend to ______ ... and only later spread\" → '시작되다'가 유일하게 논리적. C(originate) 정답 확인. A(propagate)는 균열 관련 빈출어로 강한 매력 오답이며 \"only later spread\"와 충돌해 배제됨; D(accumulate)는 \"strain builds up\"과 연결되는 부분 근거가 있음; B(terminate)는 반대 의미로 그럴듯한 오답. 두 단계 판단(대비 구조 + 시간 순서) 필요하여 medium 적합. 해설 한·영 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 과학적 내용(SAC 솔더, 열피로, 결정립 경계 균열 개시) 사실관계 문제 없음. 가상의 연구자 인용으로 저작권 우려 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"'rarely begin'과 'only later spread'의 대비로 정답이 originate로 분명히 정해진다. propagate는 균열과 자주 쓰이는 단어이고 accumulate는 strain이 쌓인다는 내용과 겹쳐서 둘 다 그럴듯한 오답이 된다. 중간 난이도에 맞다. 다만 지문에 나오는 Priya Raman이 실존 연구자인지는 확인하지 못했다. 가상 인물이라면 문제 될 것은 없다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-words_in_context-m-106","intendedSkill":"words_in_context","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-words_in_context-m-107","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Words in Context","difficulty":"medium","skill":"words_in_context","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Magnetorheological fluids consist of tiny iron particles suspended in oil. With no magnetic field present, the particles drift freely and the fluid pours much like motor oil. When a field is applied, however, the particles snap into chains aligned with the field lines, and within milliseconds the fluid stiffens into a near-solid. Because engineers can strengthen or weaken the field continuously, the fluid's resistance to flow is not simply switched on or off but can be ______ to any level between those extremes, a property that makes it useful in seat suspensions that respond to each bump in the road.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["reversed","maximized","concealed","calibrated"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 자기장을 연속적으로 세게 하거나 약하게 할 수 있어서 유체의 저항이 켜짐/꺼짐 둘 중 하나가 아니라 두 극단 사이의 어떤 수준으로든 맞춰질 수 있다고 말합니다. 따라서 원하는 정확한 수준으로 맞춘다는 뜻의 D가 정답입니다. A는 자기장을 끄면 유체가 다시 흐른다는 점에서 그럴듯하지만, '되돌린다'는 말은 중간 수준으로 맞춘다는 뜻을 담지 못합니다. B는 유체가 거의 고체로 굳는다는 내용과 연결되지만, 지문이 강조하는 것은 최대치가 아니라 '어떤 수준이든'이라는 범위입니다. C는 저항이 사라진다는 뜻으로 오해할 수 있지만, 숨긴다는 뜻이라 맥락에 맞지 않습니다.","explanationEn":"The passage says the field can be strengthened or weakened continuously, so the fluid's resistance isn't just on or off—it can be set to any level between the two extremes. That's why D, meaning adjusted precisely to a chosen level, is correct. A seems reasonable because turning off the field lets the fluid flow again, but \"reversed\" doesn't express setting the resistance to an in-between level. B connects to the fluid stiffening into a near-solid, but the passage stresses \"any level,\" not just the highest one. C might suggest the resistance disappearing, but \"concealed\" means hidden, which doesn't fit the context.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.615Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"physical science — Magnetorheological fluid behavior modulation and magnetic field-responsive viscosity applications","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"\"not simply switched on or off but can be ______ to any level between those extremes\" clearly requires a word meaning 'adjusted/set precisely'; D 'calibrated' fits ('tuned'/'adjusted' would be slightly more idiomatic but 'calibrated to any level' is acceptable). A (reversed) and B (maximized) each have partial textual support (field removal restores flow; near-solid stiffening) but are ruled out by the 'any level' contrast; C is weak but coherent. Two-step reasoning (contrast structure + 'continuously') matches medium. MR fluid description is scientifically accurate. Korean and English explanations agree in conclusion and letter references; English is natural with no Hangul."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["too_easy","eliminated:2"],"note":"'to any level between those extremes'라는 단서가 너무 직접적이고, 'continuously' 같은 단서도 겹쳐 있음. 오답 중 C(concealed)는 처음부터 말이 안 되고, B(maximized)는 'any level'과 정면으로 충돌하며, A(reversed)만 조금 그럴듯함. 비교해야만 배제되는 오답이 2개 이상이어야 한다는 기준을 충족하지 못함.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-words_in_context-m-107","intendedSkill":"words_in_context","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-words_in_context-m-108","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Words in Context","difficulty":"medium","skill":"words_in_context","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"When engineers first examined carbon-fiber laminates that had failed under repeated bending, they assumed the cracks between layers had begun in the resin itself. Microscopy by materials scientist Lena Okafor complicated that view: the earliest damage appeared not within the resin but along the thin boundary where resin meets fiber, and only after these tiny separations joined together did a visible crack spread between plies. Okafor's findings thus ______ the earlier assumption, showing that it described a later stage of failure rather than its origin.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","options":["qualified","confirmed","overturned","anticipated"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 Okafor의 연구가 기존 가정을 \"복잡하게 했다\"고 하고, 그 가정이 틀린 것이 아니라 파손의 기원이 아닌 후기 단계를 설명한다고 보여 주었다고 한다. 따라서 가정을 부분적으로 제한·수정했다는 뜻의 A(qualified)가 가장 정확하다. B는 연구가 가정을 그대로 지지한다는 뜻이어서 기원이 다르다는 발견과 맞지 않는다. C는 '완전히 뒤집었다'는 뜻인데, 지문은 가정이 후기 단계에 대해서는 여전히 유효하다고 하므로 너무 강하다. D는 연구가 가정보다 먼저 나왔다는 뜻이 되어 시간 순서와 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The text says Okafor's microscopy \"complicated\" the earlier view and showed that the assumption described a later stage of failure instead of its origin. So her findings limited or refined the assumption without throwing it out, and that is what A (\"qualified\") means. B doesn't work because the findings did not simply support the assumption, since they located the origin somewhere else. C goes too far: \"overturned\" means rejecting the assumption completely, but the text says it still holds for the later crack stage. D would mean the findings came before the assumption, which reverses the order of events.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.615Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"physical science — Composite laminate delamination propagation and matrix-fiber interface failure mechanism analysis","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"\"complicated that view\" + \"later stage rather than its origin\" 두 단서를 연결해야 'qualified'를 고를 수 있고, 'overturned'은 훑어 읽으면 고르기 쉬운 매력적 오답, 'confirmed'도 부분적 근거(가정이 후기 단계에는 맞음)가 있어 medium 기준에 부합. 해설 양쪽 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 과학적 내용(복합재 층간 박리가 섬유-수지 계면에서 시작)도 타당. 지문은 창작물로 저작권 의심 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"C(overturned)는 그럴듯한 오답이고, 'later stage rather than origin'이라는 단서로 배제된다. 지문은 기존 가정이 처음에는 수지 내부의 균열을 말했다는 점과 그 가정이 후기 단계를 설명했다는 점을 약간 느슨하게 연결하지만, 정답을 정하는 데는 문제가 없다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-words_in_context-m-108","intendedSkill":"words_in_context","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-boundaries-m-111","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In 1955, chemists Malcolm Williams, Robert Landel, and John Ferry published what is now called the WLF equation, a formula describing how far a polymer's relaxation-modulus curve slides along the time axis when the material is heated or cooled by a given number of ______ applying it, engineers can stitch together brief laboratory measurements taken at several temperatures into a single master curve predicting decades of stress decay.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["degrees, by","degrees by","degrees, which, by","degrees; by"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"빈칸 앞은 \"chemists ... published ... the WLF equation\"이라는 독립절에 긴 동격어구가 붙은 형태이고, 빈칸 뒤 \"by applying it, engineers can stitch...\"도 주어와 동사를 갖춘 독립절이다. 두 독립절은 세미콜론으로 연결해야 하므로 D가 정답이다. A는 쉼표만으로 두 독립절을 이은 쉼표 오용(comma splice)이다. B는 문장부호 없이 이어 붙인 비문이며, \"by applying\"이 앞의 \"degrees\"를 수식하는 것처럼 잘못 읽힌다. C는 관계사 which를 넣어 종속절처럼 보이게 했지만, 절 안에 이미 \"it\"이 있어 which가 맡을 문법적 역할이 없으므로 비문이 된다.","explanationEn":"Before the blank you have an independent clause (\"chemists ... published ... the WLF equation\") followed by a long appositive. After the blank comes another full independent clause, \"by applying it, engineers can stitch...,\" which has its own subject and verb. Two independent clauses can be joined by a semicolon, so D is correct. A joins them with only a comma, which makes a comma splice. B runs the clauses together with no punctuation and makes \"by applying\" seem to modify \"degrees.\" C adds \"which\" to make the second part look like a relative clause, but the clause already contains \"it,\" so \"which\" has no grammatical role and the sentence breaks down.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.615Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"physical science — Viscoelastic polymer relaxation modulus decay and time-temperature superposition principle validation","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"빈칸 앞은 독립절+긴 동격구, 뒤는 \"by applying it, engineers can stitch...\"라는 독립절이므로 세미콜론(D)이 유일하게 적법. A는 comma splice, B는 run-on, C는 which가 절 내에서 문법적 역할이 없어 비문. 해설(한/영) 모두 정답과 선택지 참조가 일치하고 모순 없음. WLF 방정식(1955, Williams–Landel–Ferry, 시간-온도 중첩) 사실관계도 정확. 긴 동격구로 독립절 경계를 가리고 C가 그럴듯한 오답 역할을 하므로 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"WLF 방정식의 연도(1955)와 저자(Williams, Landel, Ferry), 시간-온도 중첩으로 마스터 곡선을 만든다는 설명은 사실과 맞는다. 긴 동격어구 때문에 앞 절의 경계가 잘 드러나지 않고, \"by applying it\" 같은 도입 구가 있어 쉼표 오용 함정이 효과적이다. medium 난이도로 적절하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-boundaries-m-111","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-rhetorical_synthesis-m-113","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"medium","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- Photocatalytic water splitting uses light energy to break water molecules into hydrogen and oxygen gas.\n- In 1972, Japanese researchers Akira Fujishima and Kenichi Honda showed that titanium dioxide (TiO2) could split water when exposed to ultraviolet light.\n- TiO2 is inexpensive, nontoxic, and resists corrosion in water, so it can be used for long periods.\n- However, TiO2 absorbs only ultraviolet light, which makes up about 4 percent of the energy in sunlight.\n- Because of this, TiO2 systems running on ordinary sunlight convert only a small fraction of incoming solar energy into hydrogen.","question":"The student wants to present both an advantage and a drawback of using titanium dioxide for this process. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Titanium dioxide is inexpensive and nontoxic, and in 1972 Fujishima and Honda showed that it could split water into hydrogen and oxygen under ultraviolet light.","Titanium dioxide is inexpensive and resists corrosion in water, but because it absorbs only ultraviolet light, it converts just a small fraction of sunlight's energy into hydrogen.","Titanium dioxide absorbs only ultraviolet light, which makes up about 4 percent of sunlight's energy, so it converts just a small fraction of incoming solar energy into hydrogen.","Titanium dioxide uses light energy to break water into hydrogen and oxygen, and it resists corrosion in water, so it can be used for long periods."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"정답은 B이다. B는 저렴하고 부식에 강하다는 장점과, 자외선만 흡수해 태양에너지의 일부만 수소로 바꾼다는 단점을 'but'으로 함께 제시한다. A와 D는 정확한 메모를 쓰지만 장점이나 일반적 사실만 담고 단점이 없다. C는 단점을 원인과 결과까지 자세히 설명하지만 장점이 빠져 있어 목표의 절반만 달성한다.","explanationEn":"The answer is B. Choice B gives an advantage (TiO2 is inexpensive and resists corrosion) and a drawback (it absorbs only ultraviolet light, so it converts little of sunlight's energy into hydrogen), linking the two with \"but.\" Choices A and D use accurate notes, but they give only advantages or general facts, with no drawback. Choice C explains the drawback carefully, cause and effect included, but it leaves out any advantage, so it meets only half of the goal.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.615Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"physical science — Photocatalytic water splitting using titanium dioxide under ultraviolet radiation for hydrogen production","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B는 장점(저렴·내부식)과 단점(자외선만 흡수→전환율 낮음)을 모두 제시하는 유일한 선택지. A·D는 장점/일반 사실만, C는 단점만 담아 목표의 절반만 충족. 1972 Fujishima–Honda 실험, 자외선 약 4% 비중 등 사실 관계 문제 없음. 한·영 해설 모두 정답 및 글자 참조 일치, 자연스러운 영어, 한글 혼입 없음. 두 요소 결합 판단이 필요하고 오답들이 각각 부분적 근거를 지녀 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"A·D는 장점만, C는 단점만 담고 있어 각각 부분적으로만 맞으므로 비교해야 배제할 수 있음. 정답은 B 하나로 명확하고, 사실관계(Fujishima-Honda 1972, 자외선 약 4%)도 정확함. 표준 medium 수준.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-rhetorical_synthesis-m-113","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-114","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"medium","skill":"central_ideas_details","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Electrospinning is a method for drawing polymer solutions into fibers far thinner than a human hair. A droplet of solution sits at the tip of a needle, and when a high voltage is applied, electric charge builds up on the droplet's surface until it stretches into a cone and ejects a thin jet toward a grounded collector. Engineers once assumed that the final fiber diameter depended mainly on how viscous the solution was. Work by materials scientist Elena Varga and colleagues suggests a more complicated picture: as the jet travels, charges on its surface repel one another and cause the jet to whip in rapid loops, stretching it far more than a straight path would. By adjusting the shape of the electric field between needle and collector, Varga's team was able to lengthen this whipping phase and produce fibers less than half as thick as those made from the same solution under a standard setup.","question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","options":["Electrospinning produces fibers thinner than a human hair because a high voltage causes a droplet to form a cone and release a jet toward a collector.","Varga's team showed that solution viscosity has no effect on fiber diameter, since electric charges alone determine how thin an electrospun fiber becomes.","Varga's team found that fiber thickness in electrospinning can be reduced by modifying the electric field to extend the stage in which the jet loops and stretches.","Varga's team found that electrospun fibers become thinner when engineers increase the voltage applied to the needle so that more charge builds on the droplet."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"지문은 기존 가정(점도가 굵기를 결정)을 소개한 뒤, Varga 팀이 전기장 형태를 조절해 제트가 휘며 늘어나는 단계를 연장하여 섬유를 더 가늘게 만들었다는 발견을 중심으로 전개되므로 C가 정답이다. A는 도입부의 공정 설명만 담은 세부 사항일 뿐 글의 핵심 발견을 놓친다. B는 지문이 점도의 영향을 '더 복잡하다'고 했을 뿐 영향이 없다고 하지 않았으므로 과장이다. D는 전압 증가를 원인으로 제시하지만, 지문에서 팀이 조절한 것은 전압의 크기가 아니라 전기장의 형태이다.","explanationEn":"The text introduces an old assumption (viscosity controls diameter) and then centers on Varga's finding that reshaping the electric field lengthens the whipping, stretching phase of the jet and yields much thinner fibers, so C is correct. A only restates the opening description of the process and misses the study's central finding. B overstates the text: it calls the picture \"more complicated\" but never says viscosity has no effect. D credits increased voltage, but the team changed the shape of the electric field, not the voltage level.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.615Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"technology and engineering — Electrospinning polymer nanofiber production and ultrafine fiber diameter control through electric field manipulation","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 C는 지문의 핵심 발견(전기장 형태 조절→휘핑 단계 연장→섬유 굵기 감소)을 정확히 요약. A(도입부 세부), B(점도 '영향 없음' 과장), D(전압 크기 vs 전기장 형태 혼동)는 각각 부분적 근거가 있어 비교 배제 필요. 해설 한/영 모두 일관되고 정확하며 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 전기방사 원리 설명(테일러 콘, 휘핑 불안정)도 사실과 부합. 연구자는 가상 인물로 저작권 문제 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"C가 지문 핵심(전기장 형태 조절→휘핑 단계 연장→섬유 굵기 절반 이하)을 정확히 담고 있음. D는 '전압 크기'와 '전기장 형태'를 구분해야 걸러지는 그럴듯한 오답이고, A는 지문 내용 중 일부만 담은 오답, B는 지문 내용을 과장한 오답임. medium 난이도에 맞음.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-central_ideas_details-m-114","intendedSkill":"central_ideas_details","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-116","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Thermoelectric modules convert heat directly into electricity through the Seebeck effect: when one side of a semiconductor junction is hotter than the other, charge carriers drift toward the cooler side, producing a voltage. Because the devices have no moving parts, engineers have long hoped to attach them to car exhausts and factory chimneys to recover energy that would otherwise be lost. __Yet the very materials that conduct electricity well tend to conduct heat well too, so the temperature difference the module depends on quickly evens out.__ For this reason, most commercial modules convert less than ten percent of the heat passing through them. Researchers at several laboratories are now designing semiconductors laced with nanoscale grain boundaries that scatter heat-carrying vibrations while letting electrons pass, an approach that could loosen this trade-off.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It identifies a physical obstacle that accounts for a limitation described later and motivates the research discussed at the end.","It explains the mechanism by which the Seebeck effect generates a voltage across a semiconductor junction.","It presents evidence that thermoelectric modules are unsuitable for use on car exhausts and factory chimneys.","It describes how nanoscale grain boundaries allow electrons to pass while blocking heat-carrying vibrations."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 전기를 잘 통하는 물질이 열도 잘 통해 온도차가 사라진다는 물리적 장애를 제시하며, 이것이 다음 문장의 낮은 변환 효율(10% 미만)의 원인이 되고 마지막 문장의 나노 구조 연구의 동기가 되므로 A가 정답이다. B는 Seebeck 효과의 작동 원리를 다루는데, 이는 첫 문장의 역할이다. C는 밑줄 문장이 응용을 제약하는 것은 맞지만 부적합하다고 단정하지 않으며, 글은 오히려 해결 노력을 소개한다. D는 마지막 문장의 내용으로, 밑줄 문장은 해결책이 아니라 문제를 제시한다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence names a physical obstacle: materials that conduct electricity well also conduct heat well, which erases the temperature difference. That obstacle explains the low efficiency (under ten percent) mentioned in the next sentence and motivates the nanoscale research described at the end, so A is correct. B describes how the Seebeck effect works, but that is the job of the first sentence. C goes too far: the sentence points to a limitation, but the text never says the modules are unsuitable, and it actually goes on to describe efforts to fix the problem. D restates the final sentence; the underlined sentence presents the problem, not the solution.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.615Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"technology and engineering — Thermoelectric module Seebeck effect energy conversion from waste heat into electrical power generation","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"정답 A 검산 일치: 밑줄 문장은 \"Yet\"으로 전환해 전기전도-열전도 결합이라는 물리적 장애를 제시하고, 이어지는 \"For this reason\" 문장(10% 미만 효율)과 마지막 문장의 \"loosen this trade-off\"(연구 동기)로 직접 연결됨. B는 첫 문장 역할, D는 마지막 문장 역할로 위치 혼동 오답이며, C는 '제약'을 '부적합 단정'으로 과장한 오답으로 비교가 필요함. 과학 내용(Seebeck 효과, Wiedemann-Franz 유사 trade-off, 나노 결정립계 포논 산란, 상용 모듈 효율 <10%)은 사실과 부합. 한·영 해설 모두 결론·글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 원문 독창적 서술로 저작권 의심 없음. 두 단계 판단(장애 식별 + 뒤 문장과의 인과 연결) 요구로 medium 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"To pick A, the reader has to link the underlined sentence both to the efficiency limit that follows it and to the research at the end, which is two steps of reasoning. B and D each restate a different sentence (the first and the last), so a reader who checks where things are in the text can rule them out. Still, both use the same vocabulary as the passage, so a reader who skims could fall for them. C is the most tempting wrong answer: the underlined sentence does describe a limit on these uses, and C stretches that into \"unsuitable.\" Overall the item sits at the low end of medium.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-116","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-117","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"medium","skill":"text_structure_purpose","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Conventional microfluidic chips move fluids through networks of fixed channels, so each chip is effectively built for a single assay. Digital microfluidic devices take a different approach: they move discrete droplets across a grid of electrodes using electrowetting, in which an applied voltage changes how strongly a droplet wets the surface beneath it, pulling the droplet toward the energized electrode. __Because the path a droplet follows is set by the sequence of electrodes switched on rather than by etched channels, the same chip can be reprogrammed to split, merge, or route droplets for an entirely different experiment.__ Engineer Aaron Wheeler and colleagues have used this flexibility to isolate individual cells in separate droplets, expose each one to a different reagent, and then measure the cells' responses one at a time, an analysis that would have required several purpose-built channel chips.","question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined sentence in the text as a whole?","options":["It describes the physical mechanism by which an applied voltage causes a droplet to move toward an energized electrode.","It identifies a consequence of the way droplets are controlled that makes possible the single-cell work described afterward.","It presents a limitation of channel-based chips that Wheeler's team set out to overcome by isolating cells in droplets.","It offers evidence from Wheeler's experiments that digital devices measure cell responses more accurately than channel chips do."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"밑줄 문장은 앞 문장에서 설명한 전극 기반 제어 방식의 결과로 칩을 재프로그래밍할 수 있다는 점을 제시하고, 이 '유연성'이 다음 문장의 단일 세포 분석을 가능하게 하므로 B가 정답이다. A의 전압·젖음 메커니즘은 밑줄 문장이 아니라 바로 앞 문장의 내용이다. C는 채널 칩의 한계를 다루는 것처럼 보이지만, 밑줄 문장은 디지털 장치의 장점을 말하며 Wheeler 팀의 동기도 언급하지 않는다. D는 지문에 없는 '정확도' 비교를 주장하며, 밑줄 문장은 실험 증거도 아니다.","explanationEn":"The underlined sentence explains what follows from controlling droplets with electrodes: the chip can be reprogrammed. The next sentence then calls this \"flexibility\" and shows it making single-cell analysis possible, so B is correct. A describes the voltage-and-wetting mechanism, but that comes in the sentence before the underlined one. C may look right because channel chips come up, but the underlined sentence describes an advantage of digital devices, and the text never says what motivated Wheeler's team. D is wrong because the text never compares accuracy, and the underlined sentence isn't experimental evidence.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.615Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"technology and engineering — Microfluidic lab-on-chip device droplet manipulation and single-cell analysis through electrowetting actuation","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"밑줄 문장은 전극 기반 제어의 결과(재프로그래밍 가능)를 제시하고, 다음 문장이 'this flexibility'로 받아 단일 세포 분석을 설명하므로 B가 정확. A는 직전 문장의 메커니즘, C는 첫 문장의 채널 칩 한계, D는 지문에 없는 정확도 비교로 각각 배제됨. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 동일 결론과 글자 참조를 가지며 영어는 자연스럽고 한글 없음. Wheeler의 디지털 미세유체 연구 및 전기습윤 설명은 사실에 부합. 앞뒤 문장 연결(두 단계 판단)이 필요하고 오답 A·C가 인접 문장 내용을 차용한 부분적 근거를 가져 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"B만 정답으로 성립함. A는 앞 문장과 혼동하도록 만든 오답이고, C는 밑줄 문장이 채널 칩을 대비로 언급한다는 점을 이용한 부분 근거형 오답임. D는 정확도 비교라는 지문 밖 주장이라 배제됨. 중간 난이도에 맞음.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sv-text_structure_purpose-m-117","intendedSkill":"text_structure_purpose","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"st-rhetorical_synthesis-m-000","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"medium","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- \"The Weight of Harvest\" is a 2019 short story by Canadian writer Mara Lindqvist.\n- Its protagonist, Callum, operates a grain elevator in rural Saskatchewan.\n- At his sister Ingrid's wedding, Ingrid treasures a hand-carved wooden clock, believing Callum made it for her.\n- Callum later learns the clock was actually carved by their late father as a gift for a neighbor's daughter.\n- The story ends before Callum decides whether to tell Ingrid where the clock came from.\n- Critics have praised Lindqvist's spare descriptions of prairie landscapes.","question":"The student wants to present the central dilemma the protagonist faces in the story. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["In Mara Lindqvist's \"The Weight of Harvest,\" Callum must choose whether to tell Ingrid that the clock she cherishes, which she thinks he made, was actually carved by their father for someone else.","In Mara Lindqvist's \"The Weight of Harvest,\" Callum, a grain-elevator operator in Saskatchewan, attends the wedding of his sister, Ingrid, who treasures a hand-carved wooden clock.","In Mara Lindqvist's \"The Weight of Harvest,\" Callum learns that a wooden clock was carved by his late father as a gift for a neighbor's daughter.","In Mara Lindqvist's \"The Weight of Harvest,\" Callum works at a grain elevator amid prairie landscapes that critics say are described in spare, praised prose."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"주인공의 핵심 딜레마를 제시하려면 '잉그리드가 시계를 캘럼이 만든 것으로 믿는다'는 정보와 '실제로는 아버지가 다른 사람을 위해 만들었다'는 정보, 그리고 진실을 말할지 결정해야 한다는 상황을 결합해야 한다. A는 이 세 요소를 모두 연결하므로 정답이다. B는 결혼식과 시계를 언급하지만 진실이 무엇인지, 무엇을 선택해야 하는지는 빠져 있다. C는 시계의 진짜 출처는 밝히지만 잉그리드의 오해와 캘럼이 내려야 할 결정이 없어 딜레마가 드러나지 않는다. D는 배경과 비평가의 평가에 집중해 목표와 무관하다.","explanationEn":"To present the protagonist's central dilemma, you need to combine two facts: Ingrid believes Callum made the clock, but their father actually carved it for someone else. You also need the choice Callum faces about telling her the truth. Choice A connects all of these, so it is correct. Choice B mentions the wedding and the clock but leaves out the truth and the decision. Choice C gives the clock's real origin but leaves out Ingrid's mistaken belief and Callum's choice, so no dilemma comes through. Choice D focuses on the setting and the critics' praise, which has nothing to do with the goal.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.615Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Callum, a grain-elevator operator in Saskatchewan, discovers his sister's wedding gift was meant for someone else entirely, forcing him to decide whether to reveal the truth or let her keep the cherished misidentified object.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"A만이 '잉그리드의 오해 + 실제 출처 + 말할지 여부의 결정' 세 요소를 결합해 딜레마를 제시함. B·C는 관련 정보를 부분적으로 담아 비교가 필요하고 D는 배경·비평 중심으로 목표와 무관하나 말은 됨. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 정답 및 선택지 참조가 일치하고 모순 없음. 가상의 작품으로 저작권 문제 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B와 C는 각각 딜레마의 일부만 담고 있어 비교해야 배제된다. D는 명백한 오답이지만 말은 된다. A는 오해·진실·선택을 모두 담는다. 중간 난이도에 대체로 적합하다. 정답만 길이가 길어 단서가 될 수 있다는 점은 다소 아쉽다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"st-rhetorical_synthesis-m-000","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"st-rhetorical_synthesis-m-001","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"medium","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- The Last Lesson at Ushguli (2019) is a novel by Nino Kavtaradze.\n- It is set in a Svaneti village in the Georgian highlands during the 1970s.\n- Its main character, Giorgi, is a schoolteacher who will retire at the end of the term.\n- A district inspector from the Soviet education office requires every lesson to follow the state-issued textbook.\n- In the novel's central scene, Giorgi leaves the textbook closed and teaches using only a river stone, a hawk feather, and a sprig of wild thyme.\n- Each object is linked to a private memory that Giorgi never explains to his students.","question":"The student wants to show how what Giorgi does in the novel's central scene differs from what officials expected of him. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Although Giorgi will retire at the end of the term, he still teaches a lesson in the novel's central scene, using a river stone, a hawk feather, and a sprig of wild thyme.","Although a Soviet district inspector requires every lesson to follow the state textbook, Giorgi keeps the book closed and teaches with only a river stone, a hawk feather, and a sprig of wild thyme.","Although each object Giorgi brings to class is linked to a private memory, he never explains those memories to the students in his Svaneti village school.","Although The Last Lesson at Ushguli was published in 2019, Nino Kavtaradze sets the novel, which centers on a teacher named Giorgi, in the Georgian highlands of the 1970s."],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"목표는 장면 속 Giorgi의 행동이 당국의 기대와 어떻게 다른지 보여주는 것이므로, 장학관의 교과서 요구(기대)와 교과서를 덮고 자연물로 가르치는 행동을 함께 제시해야 한다. B는 이 두 메모를 결합해 대조를 분명히 드러낸다. A는 실제 행동은 언급하지만 대조 대상이 공식적 요구가 아니라 은퇴 시점이다. C는 개인적 기억과 침묵 사이의 대조일 뿐 당국의 기대가 빠져 있다. D는 출간 시기와 배경 시기를 대조할 뿐 Giorgi의 행동과 무관하다.","explanationEn":"Your goal is to show how Giorgi's actions in the central scene differ from what officials expected, so you need both the official expectation (the inspector's textbook rule) and what Giorgi actually does (closes the book and teaches with natural objects). B puts these two notes together and makes the contrast clear. A describes the lesson, but it sets it against Giorgi's retirement, not against any official demand. C contrasts his private memories with his silence and never mentions what officials expected. D contrasts the publication date with the setting and says nothing about Giorgi's behavior.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.615Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Giorgi, an aging schoolteacher in the Georgian highlands during the Soviet era, conducts one final lesson with his students using only objects from nature, each carrying a lifetime of quiet meaning.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"B가 유일하게 '당국의 기대(장학관의 교과서 규정)'와 'Giorgi의 실제 행동(교과서 덮고 자연물로 수업)'을 모두 결합해 목표를 달성한다. A는 실제 행동을 포함하지만 대조 대상이 은퇴이고, C는 자연물·기억만 다루어 공식 기대가 빠지며, D는 서지 정보 대조에 그친다. 해설(한·영) 모두 정답과 선택지 참조가 일치하고 영어도 자연스러우며 한글 혼입 없음. 가상의 소설이라 저작권 문제 없음. A·C가 부분적 근거를 가져 비교가 필요하므로 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["too_easy","eliminated:3"],"note":"관리(officials)·장학관의 요구를 언급하는 선택지는 B 하나뿐이라, 목표에 나온 'officials'라는 키워드만 맞춰 봐도 바로 정답이 나온다. A와 C는 장면을 다루긴 하지만 대조 축이 명백히 다르고, D는 장면과 무관해 쉽게 배제된다. 오답 중 공식적 기대를 부분적으로라도 담은 것이 없어서 비교해야만 배제되는 오답이 부족하다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"st-rhetorical_synthesis-m-001","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"st-rhetorical_synthesis-m-002","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"medium","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- Ruth Calloway's 2019 novel The Last Furrow is set on the Texas Panhandle in 1935.\n- Its protagonist, Pearl Haskins, is a farmwife whose wheat crop has failed for three straight years.\n- In one chapter, Pearl drives a mule wagon 31 miles through dust storms to the town of Dalhart.\n- Her aim is to pick up a single packet of drought-resistant sorghum seed mailed to her by her late mother's sister.\n- Calloway has said the chapter was inspired by her grandmother's diaries.\n- Reviewers have praised the chapter's spare, unsentimental prose.","question":"The student wants to explain the practical problem on Pearl's farm that motivates her journey in the chapter. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["In a chapter of The Last Furrow, Pearl Haskins drives a mule wagon 31 miles through dust storms to Dalhart, a journey Calloway based on her grandmother's diaries.","In a chapter of The Last Furrow, Pearl Haskins drives 31 miles to Dalhart through dust storms, an ordeal that reviewers say Calloway renders in spare, unsentimental prose.","In a chapter of The Last Furrow, Pearl Haskins, whose wheat has failed three years running, drives 31 miles through dust storms to Dalhart for a packet of drought-resistant sorghum seed.","In a chapter of The Last Furrow, Pearl Haskins drives 31 miles through dust storms to Dalhart to pick up a packet of seed mailed to her by her late mother's sister."],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"목표는 Pearl의 여정을 촉발한 농장의 실질적 문제를 설명하는 것이다. C는 3년 연속 밀 농사 실패라는 문제와 가뭄에 강한 수수 씨앗이라는 해결책을 연결해 여정의 동기를 분명히 보여 준다. A는 여정과 작가의 영감 출처만 말할 뿐 농장 문제는 언급하지 않는다. B는 평론가의 문체 평가에 초점을 둔다. D는 씨앗을 가지러 간다는 목적은 밝히지만 작물 실패나 씨앗의 가뭄 내성을 빠뜨려 그것이 어떤 문제를 해결하는지 보여 주지 못한다.","explanationEn":"Your goal is to explain the practical problem on the farm that drives Pearl's trip. C does this by linking two notes: her wheat has failed for three years, and the seed she is after is drought-resistant sorghum, so the trip is clearly a response to the failing crop. A covers the journey and where Calloway got the idea, but it never mentions any farm problem. B is about how reviewers judged the prose. D tells you she's going to get seed, but it leaves out the crop failure and the drought resistance, so you can't tell what problem the seed would solve.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.616Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Pearl, a Depression-era farmwife on the Texas panhandle, undertakes a grueling day-long wagon journey across dust storms to retrieve a single specific seed packet from a neighboring town.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"C가 유일하게 '3년 연속 밀 흉작'(문제)과 '가뭄 내성 수수 씨앗'(해결책)을 연결해 과제를 충족한다. D는 여정 목적(씨앗)을 담아 강한 부분 정답 오답이고, A·B는 여정은 서술하지만 농장 문제를 다루지 않는다. 선택지 내용은 모두 노트와 일치하며 해설(국·영)은 결론과 글자 참조가 일치한다. 가상 작품으로 저작권 문제 없음. 두 노트를 결합해야 정답이 도출되므로 medium에 적합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"C만 작물 실패(문제)와 가뭄 내성 씨앗(해결)을 연결함. D는 목적은 있으나 문제 정보가 없어 부분적으로 맞는 매력적 오답이고, A·B는 동기 정보가 없음. medium 난이도에 맞음. 가상의 작품이라 저작권 문제 없음.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"st-rhetorical_synthesis-m-002","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"st-rhetorical_synthesis-m-003","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"medium","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- \"The Keeper of the Hours\" is a short story by a fictional Scottish author, Eilidh Rankin.\n- It is set at a two-room primary school on a remote Hebridean island.\n- Morag, the story's nine-year-old protagonist, distrusts adults who claim to know things she cannot check for herself.\n- The school's clock, installed more than a century earlier, keeps perfect time even though no repairer has visited the island in decades.\n- Mr. Galbraith, the new janitor, quietly replaces the clock's worn gears with parts he carves from driftwood.\n- Of all the pupils and teachers, Morag alone discovers what Mr. Galbraith is doing.","question":"The student wants to show how the protagonist's personality relates to her role in the story's central discovery. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["In Eilidh Rankin's \"The Keeper of the Hours,\" a century-old school clock on a remote Hebridean island keeps perfect time, even though no repairer has visited in decades.","In Eilidh Rankin's \"The Keeper of the Hours,\" Morag, a nine-year-old who distrusts adults, attends a two-room primary school on a remote Hebridean island.","In Eilidh Rankin's \"The Keeper of the Hours,\" the new janitor, Mr. Galbraith, secretly keeps the school's century-old clock running by carving replacement gears from driftwood.","In Eilidh Rankin's \"The Keeper of the Hours,\" Morag, a nine-year-old unwilling to accept what she cannot verify herself, is the only person at her school to uncover the janitor's secret repairs to its clock."],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"목표는 주인공의 성격과 이야기의 핵심 발견에서 그녀가 맡는 역할을 연결하는 것이다. D는 스스로 확인할 수 없는 것을 믿지 않는 Morag의 성격과, 그녀만이 관리인의 비밀 수리를 알아낸다는 사실을 함께 제시하므로 정답이다. B는 Morag의 성격을 언급하지만 발견에 대한 내용이 없고, 배경 설명에 그친다. C는 발견의 내용(관리인의 수리)은 담고 있지만 Morag와 그녀의 성격이 빠져 있다. A는 시계의 수수께끼만 소개할 뿐 주인공을 전혀 다루지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The goal asks you to link the protagonist's personality to her part in the story's central discovery. D does this: it describes Morag's refusal to accept what she can't verify and states that she alone uncovers the janitor's secret repairs. B mentions Morag's distrust, but it only gives the setting and says nothing about the discovery. C describes what the janitor is secretly doing, but it leaves out Morag and her personality entirely. A presents only the mystery of the clock and never mentions the protagonist.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.616Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Morag, a skeptical nine-year-old at a remote Hebridean primary school, becomes the only person to notice that the new janitor is secretly maintaining the school's century-old clock with hand-carved wooden parts.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"D is the only choice combining Morag's personality (distrust of unverifiable claims, paraphrased accurately from the notes) with her role as sole discoverer. B (personality but no discovery) and C (discovery but no protagonist) are partially correct distractors requiring comparison; A is plausible but off-goal. Explanations in both languages match, reference correct letters, and contain no Korean in the English version. Fictional author/story clearly labeled, so no copyright concern. Difficulty matches medium."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":false,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:3"],"note":"D만 성격과 발견을 둘 다 담는다. B와 C는 각각 한 요소만 부분적으로 맞아서 비교해 봐야 배제되므로 medium 기준에 맞는다. 다만 D만 유독 길어 단서가 될 수 있다.","passed":false},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"st-rhetorical_synthesis-m-003","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"st-rhetorical_synthesis-m-004","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"medium","skill":"rhetorical_synthesis","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n- \"The Courtyard Gambit\" is a 2019 short story by Austrian writer Lena Hofbauer.\n- It follows Viktor and Mrs. Brenner, two elderly residents of a Vienna boarding house.\n- At first, the two neighbors exchange only curt nods and complaints about noise.\n- They begin a daily chess match, calling out moves across the shared courtyard from their windows.\n- By the story's end, Mrs. Brenner leaves a pot of soup outside Viktor's door when he falls ill.\n- Hofbauer has said she wanted to show how routine can quietly build intimacy.","question":"The student wants to describe how the relationship between the story's two main characters changes over time. Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","options":["Viktor and Mrs. Brenner, who initially share only curt nods and noise complaints, grow so close through their daily courtyard chess match that she brings him soup when he falls ill.","Viktor and Mrs. Brenner, two elderly residents of a Vienna boarding house, play a daily chess match by calling out moves across the shared courtyard from their windows.","Viktor and Mrs. Brenner, the central figures of Lena Hofbauer's 2019 story, reflect the author's stated aim of showing how routine can quietly build intimacy.","Viktor and Mrs. Brenner, neighbors in a Vienna boarding house, begin the story exchanging only curt nods and complaints about the noise in the building."],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"목표는 두 인물의 관계가 시간에 따라 어떻게 변하는지 설명하는 것이므로, 처음 상태와 나중 상태를 함께 보여 줘야 합니다. A는 처음의 냉담함(짧은 목례와 소음 불평)과 마지막의 애정(아플 때 수프를 가져다줌)을 체스 경기라는 계기로 연결하므로 정답입니다. B는 날마다 두는 체스라는 일과만 설명할 뿐 관계의 처음과 끝을 보여 주지 않습니다. C는 작가의 의도를 전할 뿐, 인물들의 관계가 실제로 어떻게 변하는지는 보여 주지 않습니다. D는 처음의 냉담한 관계만 제시하고 변화의 결과가 빠져 있습니다.","explanationEn":"Your goal is to show how the two characters' relationship changes over time, so the sentence needs both the starting point and the ending point. A does this: it gives their early coldness (curt nods and noise complaints) and their later affection (she brings him soup when he's sick), and it links the two through the chess match. B only describes the daily chess routine and never shows how the relationship started or ended up. C reports what the author meant to do, but it doesn't show the relationship actually changing. D gives only the cold beginning and leaves out the result of the change.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.616Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Viktor and Mrs. Brenner, elderly neighbors in a Vienna boarding house, engage in a daily chess match across their shared courtyard that gradually transforms their initial coldness into unexpected affection.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"A alone shows both the initial coldness and the later affection linked by the chess routine, matching the goal of describing change over time. B (routine only), D (beginning only) are partially relevant distractors requiring comparison; C (author's aim) is plausible but doesn't show the change. Korean and English explanations agree, letter references match, no Korean in the English explanation. Fictional story, no copyright issue."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"A의 'brings him soup'는 노트의 'leaves a pot of soup outside Viktor's door'를 약간 바꿔 쓴 표현이지만 허용 범위다. B, C, D는 각각 과정, 작가 의도, 시작 상태만 담고 있어 부분적인 근거를 가진 오답으로 잘 기능한다. 표준 중간 난이도에 적합하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"st-rhetorical_synthesis-m-004","intendedSkill":"rhetorical_synthesis","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"st-transitions-m-005","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"medium","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Each morning before the alley wakes, Thanh rubs wood ash into the aluminum pot her grandmother carried south out of Nam Dinh in 1954. A metalworker on Hang Dong Street once offered to hammer the pot smooth for almost nothing, and Thanh freely admits that its dents make it rock unsteadily on her charcoal stove. ______ she scrubs only around them, tracing with her thumb the deep crease left when her father dropped the pot while fleeing the bombing of 1972 and the shallow one from her own bus ride to the city.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Accordingly,","Still,","For example,","Similarly,"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"앞 문장은 수리 제안이 있었고 찌그러짐 때문에 냄비가 흔들린다는 점, 즉 냄비를 펴야 할 이유를 Thanh가 인정한다는 내용이다. 그런데 뒤 문장에서 그녀는 찌그러진 곳을 그대로 두고 그 주변만 닦는다. 이처럼 양보한 뒤 반전되는 관계이므로 B가 정답이다. A는 결과를 나타내는데, 앞 내용대로라면 냄비를 고쳐야 자연스러우므로 방향이 반대다. C는 뒤 문장이 앞 내용의 예시가 아니므로 맞지 않고, D는 두 행동이 서로 비슷하지 않고 대조되므로 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The previous sentence gives reasons to fix the pot: someone offered to repair it cheaply, and Thanh admits the dents make it rock on the stove. The next sentence shows her doing the opposite. She keeps the dents and cleans only around them. That is a concession followed by a reversal, so B is correct. A signals a result, but the logical result of those reasons would be fixing the pot, not keeping the dents. C doesn't work because the sentence isn't an example of what came before, and D doesn't work because her action contrasts with those reasons rather than resembling them.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.616Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Thanh, a noodle vendor in Hanoi's pre-dawn alley, restores a dented aluminum pot passed down through three generations, each dent marking a different family member's journey through war and displacement.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"앞 문장(저렴한 수리 제안 + 찌그러짐의 단점을 'freely admits'로 양보)과 뒤 문장(찌그러진 곳을 그대로 두고 주변만 닦음)은 양보-반전 관계이므로 'Still'이 유일하게 논리적이다. A(결과)는 훑어 읽으면 \"냄비 때문에 그렇게 한다\"로 오인할 수 있어 매력적 오답으로 기능하고, D는 두 개의 자국을 나열하는 뒤 문장 구조 때문에 표면적 유사성을 가진다. C는 예시 관계가 아니어서 배제된다. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 동일한 결론과 글자 참조(B 정답, A/C/D 배제 이유)를 제시하며 모순 없음. 영어 해설에 한글 없음. 1954 남하 이주, 1972 하노이 폭격, Hang Dong(동 세공 거리) 등 배경 사실도 무리 없음. 창작 지문으로 저작권 의심 없음. 두 문장의 관계를 연결해 판단해야 하는 표준 medium 수준에 부합."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"'freely admits' 양보 신호를 읽고 다음 행동과 대조됨을 확인해야 함. Accordingly는 그녀가 찌그러짐을 소중히 여긴다고 오독하면 매력적인 오답이 됨. 역사적 사실(1954년 남하, 1972년 폭격)도 문제없음.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"st-transitions-m-005","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"st-transitions-m-006","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"medium","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"On her first morning at the mountain bus station outside Oaxaca, Rosa assumed the elderly vendor's blankets were simply decorative, their zigzags and diamonds chosen for color alone. By the third day, after the woman had guided Rosa's hands through the first rows of a pattern on the small backstrap loom, Rosa understood that each zigzag marked a river crossing and each diamond a village her ancestors had left behind. ______ the bus she had been so impatient to board now seemed less like a rescue than an interruption.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Nevertheless,","For example,","As a result,","In other words,"],"correctIndex":2,"answers":null,"explanation":"앞 문장에서 Rosa는 무늬마다 가족의 이야기가 담겨 있다는 것을 깨닫고, 뒤 문장에서는 그 깨달음 때문에 버스가 더 이상 반갑지 않게 느껴진다. 따라서 원인과 결과를 잇는 C가 정답이다. A는 Rosa의 태도가 바뀌었다는 점 때문에 대조처럼 보이지만, 뒤 문장은 앞 문장의 깨달음과 충돌하는 것이 아니라 그 깨달음에서 자연스럽게 나온 결과이다. B는 뒤 문장이 무늬의 의미를 보여 주는 구체적 사례가 아니므로 맞지 않는다. D는 버스에 대한 느낌이 무늬의 의미를 다시 말한 것이 아니라 새로운 정보이므로 맞지 않는다.","explanationEn":"In the earlier sentence, Rosa realizes that each pattern holds part of her family's story. The final sentence then shows what that realization does to her: the bus no longer feels welcome. Since the second sentence is a consequence of the first, C is correct. A might be tempting because Rosa's attitude shifts, but the final sentence doesn't contradict her realization; it follows naturally from it. B doesn't work because how she feels about the bus isn't an example of what the patterns mean, and D doesn't work because that feeling is new information, not a restatement of the earlier point.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.616Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"C","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Rosa, a young woman waiting at a mountain bus station in Oaxaca, learns traditional weaving from an elderly vendor over several days, discovering that each pattern tells a story her family forgot.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"앞 문장의 깨달음(무늬의 조상 이야기) → 뒤 문장의 태도 변화(버스가 구원이 아닌 방해로 느껴짐)는 명확한 인과 관계이므로 C 'As a result'가 정답임을 직접 확인. A는 Rosa의 태도 전환 때문에 대조로 오인할 여지가 있고 D도 재진술로 오인할 수 있어 비교가 필요하며, B는 말은 되나 배제 가능. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 동일한 결론과 글자 참조를 가지며 모순 없음. 영어 해설에 한글 없음, 자연스러움. 빈칸 뒤 소문자 'the'와 선택지의 쉼표 형식 일치. 원창작 지문으로 보이며 사실 오류 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"두 문장 사이에는 인과 관계(깨달음 → 버스에 대한 인식 변화)가 분명하다. 'Nevertheless'는 첫날의 가정과 대비되어 보이므로 그럴듯한 오답이다. 'In other words'도 결과를 다른 말로 바꾼 것으로 착각할 여지가 있다. 중간 난이도에 적합하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"st-transitions-m-006","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"st-transitions-m-008","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Transitions","difficulty":"medium","skill":"transitions","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"In the winter of 1947, Dr. Feldman and Herr Richter waged a quiet war for the favor of Frau Hölzl, who ran the boarding house on Gumpendorfer Strasse. Feldman polished the brass doorknob of her sitting room each evening; Richter answered by reciting Rilke to her potted geraniums. Frau Hölzl, for her part, found both men exhausting and told them so plainly over breakfast. ______ the gestures continued, each more elaborate than the last, as though the two men needed the contest far more than they needed to win it.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","options":["Even so,","As a result,","Similarly,","In particular,"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"Frau Hölzl가 두 남자에게 지쳤다고 분명히 말했으므로 구애 행동은 멈추는 게 자연스럽다. 그런데도 행동이 오히려 더 정교해지며 계속되었으므로, 예상과 어긋나는 결과를 이어 주는 A가 정답이다. B는 행동이 이어진 것을 그녀의 거절이 낳은 결과로 만들어 버리는데, 마지막 구절이 경쟁 자체에 대한 두 남자의 욕구를 이유로 들기 때문에 인과 방향이 맞지 않는다. C는 앞 문장과 비슷한 내용을 덧붙일 때 쓰는 말인데, 이 문장은 거절과 비슷한 내용이 아니라 그에 반하는 내용이다. D는 앞 내용의 구체적인 사례를 들 때 쓰는 말이지만, 행동이 계속되었다는 것은 그녀의 불평을 구체화한 예가 아니다.","explanationEn":"Frau Hölzl plainly told both men they exhausted her, so you would expect the gestures to stop. Instead, they kept going and got more elaborate, so you need a transition that marks a result running against expectation, which is choice A. Choice B makes the continued gestures a consequence of her rebuke, but the final clause says they continued because the men needed the contest itself, so the cause-and-effect direction is wrong. Choice C signals an added point like the one before, but this sentence goes against her rebuke rather than echoing it. Choice D introduces a specific example, but the gestures continuing is not an example of her complaint.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.616Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Dr. Feldman and Herr Richter, rivals in a postwar Vienna boarding house, begin as adversaries competing for the landlady's favor through increasingly absurd gestures before recognizing their shared loneliness.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"직접 검산: 거절(지쳤다고 말함) → 그럼에도 행동 지속·심화 = 양보/반전 관계이므로 \"Even so,\" 정답 확실. B는 마지막 구절(\"needed the contest\")을 결과 해석으로 오독하면 끌릴 수 있는 매력적 오답, C·D는 비교적 쉽게 배제됨. 한국어·영어 해설 결론 및 선택지 글자 일치, 영어 해설 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 허구 설정의 창작 지문으로 저작권 의심 없음, 사실 오류 없음. 난이도는 medium 하단 수준(강한 오답이 B 하나뿐)이나 두 단계 판단(거절 확인 + 결과 반전 파악)이 필요해 적합으로 판정."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"거절 뒤에 행동이 계속되는 양보 관계라 정답은 A(Even so)로 확실하다. B는 인과로 착각할 여지가 있어 매력적인 오답 역할을 한다. C와 D는 쉽게 배제되지만 어색하지 않아 medium 범위 안에 든다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"st-transitions-m-008","intendedSkill":"transitions","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sq-boundaries-m-001","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Alemayehu poured the first round of coffee, the strong abol that her mother had always insisted be served to the eldest guest ______ envelope, its stamps faded and its corners softened by twenty years in a misdirected mailbag, lay unopened beside the incense burner, her sister's careful handwriting still visible through the dust.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":[", the",". The"," the",", and, the"],"correctIndex":1,"answers":null,"explanation":"빈칸 앞은 'Alemayehu poured the first round of coffee'라는 독립절에 긴 동격어구(the strong abol ... eldest guest)가 붙은 문장이고, 빈칸 뒤 'envelope ... lay unopened ...'도 주어와 동사를 갖춘 독립절이다. 두 독립절은 마침표로 나누어야 하므로 B가 정답이다. A는 쉼표가 동격어구를 닫아 주는 것처럼 보이지만, 쉼표 하나로 두 독립절을 이어 comma splice가 된다. C는 아무 문장부호 없이 두 절을 붙여 run-on 문장이 된다. D는 등위접속사 and를 쓴 점은 맞지만 and 뒤에 쉼표를 찍으면 안 되므로 틀렸다.","explanationEn":"Before the blank, you have an independent clause, \"Alemayehu poured the first round of coffee,\" followed by a long appositive (\"the strong abol ... eldest guest\"). After the blank comes another independent clause: \"envelope ... lay unopened ...\". Two independent clauses must be properly separated, and the period in B does exactly that. A seems to close off the appositive with a comma, but a single comma between two independent clauses makes a comma splice. C has no punctuation at all, so it creates a run-on sentence. D uses the conjunction \"and\" correctly, but you shouldn't put a comma after \"and,\" so D is also wrong.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.616Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"B","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Alemayehu receives a letter from her estranged sister during the Ethiopian coffee ceremony, arriving twenty years late, rekindling hope that forgiveness might still bloom across the distance that separated them.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"검산: 빈칸 앞 'Alemayehu poured the first round of coffee, the strong abol ... eldest guest'는 독립절+동격어구로 완결되고, 빈칸 뒤 'The envelope, its stamps faded ..., lay unopened ...'도 독립절이므로 마침표(B)가 유일하게 올바름. A는 comma splice, C는 run-on, D는 and 뒤 불필요한 쉼표로 오답. 긴 동격어구 때문에 A가 동격을 닫는 쉼표처럼 보이고 D는 접속사가 있어 부분적으로 그럴듯하므로 medium에 적합. 한·영 해설 모두 B를 일관되게 지지하며 글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 선택지 C의 선행 공백은 '문장부호 없음'을 나타내는 표기로 허용 범위."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"긴 동격어구와 삽입 수식어 때문에 절 경계를 찾기가 어려워 medium 수준에 맞다. A는 쉼표가 동격어구를 닫는 것처럼 보여 그럴듯한 오답이다. 반면 D(', and,')는 쉽게 배제되어 오답으로서의 힘이 약하다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sq-boundaries-m-001","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sq-boundaries-m-003","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"Cornelius had expected the half-starved mule he found wandering his Gold Rush camp to repay his kindness with labor. Instead, Duchess—having eaten three days of his oats, dozed through the morning heat, and stopped cold whenever the ore cart grew heavier than she ______ watched him strain at the sluice box with what looked unmistakably like pity.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["liked,","liked;","liked","liked—"],"correctIndex":3,"answers":null,"explanation":"주어 Duchess 뒤의 긴 삽입구는 대시로 시작했으므로 같은 부호인 대시로 닫아야 하고, 그래야 주어가 본동사 watched와 연결된다. 따라서 정답은 D이다. A는 삽입구를 닫는 쉼표처럼 보여 그럴듯하지만, 대시로 연 삽입구를 쉼표로 닫을 수 없다. B의 세미콜론은 주어 Duchess와 동사 watched 사이를 끊어 앞뒤 모두 완전한 절이 되지 못한다. C는 문장부호가 없어서 삽입구가 끝나는 곳이 표시되지 않고, she liked watched처럼 동사가 엉켜 읽힌다.","explanationEn":"The long interrupting phrase after the subject \"Duchess\" opens with a dash, so it has to close with a dash too. That closing dash lets the subject connect to its main verb, \"watched,\" which makes D correct. A looks reasonable because a comma could close an interruption, but you can't close a dash-opened interruption with a comma. B uses a semicolon that cuts the subject \"Duchess\" off from its verb \"watched,\" so neither side is a complete clause. C has no punctuation at all, so nothing marks where the interruption ends, and \"she liked watched\" reads as a jumble of verbs.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.616Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"D","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Prospector Cornelius finds a half-starved mule wandering his Gold Rush camp and names it Duchess, only to realize the stubborn creature's refusal to work harder than necessary contains more wisdom than any fortune.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"주어 Duchess 뒤 대시로 연 긴 삽입구(having eaten…, dozed…, and stopped cold… she liked)를 같은 부호인 대시로 닫아야 본동사 watched와 연결됨 — D 정답 검산 확인. A(쉼표)는 삽입구 닫기처럼 보이는 그럴듯한 오답, B(세미콜론)는 주어-동사 분리, C는 무부호로 동사 충돌. 한국어·영어 해설 모두 D를 일관되게 뒷받침하고 글자 참조 일치, 영어 자연스럽고 한글 없음. 삽입구가 길어 앞의 여는 대시를 되짚어 확인해야 하므로 두 단계 판단이 필요한 medium에 적합. 원창작 지문으로 저작권 의심 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"삽입구 안에 쉼표 목록과 'whenever' 종속절이 길게 들어 있어서 여는 대시를 놓치기 쉽고, 그래서 오답 A가 그럴듯해 보인다. medium 난이도에 맞는다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sq-boundaries-m-003","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}},{"gid":"sq-boundaries-m-004","subject":"SAT Reading & Writing","format":"mc","skillType":"Boundaries (Standard English Conventions)","difficulty":"medium","skill":"boundaries","examSystem":"sat_rw","createdVia":"ai_generated","subpattern":null,"group":null,"passage":"The letter had been written in the spring of 1941 and had wandered through three postal depots before it reached the village. Giorgi, who had not heard his son's voice in nearly thirty years, unfolded the brittle page beside the sheepfold______ a careful schoolboy hand, Levan had promised to come home when the snow left the pass, and the old man read the line aloud until the mountains seemed to answer.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","options":["; in",", in"," in",", which, in"],"correctIndex":0,"answers":null,"explanation":"빈칸 앞 \"Giorgi ... unfolded the brittle page beside the sheepfold\"는 삽입절이 있어도 완전한 독립절이고, 빈칸 뒤 \"in a careful schoolboy hand, Levan had promised...\"도 주어 Levan과 동사 had promised를 가진 독립절이다. 독립절 두 개는 세미콜론으로 이어야 하므로 A가 정답이다. B는 쉼표만으로 두 독립절을 이어 comma splice가 된다. C는 문장부호 없이 두 절을 붙인 run-on이며, \"sheepfold in a careful hand\"처럼 앞 절에 붙는 전치사구로 잘못 읽히게 된다. D는 which가 관계절을 만들지만 그 절 안에 Levan had promised라는 주어·동사가 따로 있어서 which가 들어갈 자리가 없으므로 문법적으로 성립하지 않는다.","explanationEn":"The words before the blank, \"Giorgi ... unfolded the brittle page beside the sheepfold,\" make a complete independent clause, even with the long \"who\" clause in the middle. The words after the blank, \"in a careful schoolboy hand, Levan had promised...,\" make a second independent clause with the subject Levan and the verb had promised. You need a semicolon to join two independent clauses, so A is correct. B joins them with only a comma, which is a comma splice. C uses no punctuation at all, which creates a run-on and makes the phrase look like it describes the sheepfold. D adds \"which,\" but the clause already has its own subject and verb (Levan had promised), so \"which\" has no role and the sentence falls apart.","figure":null,"statements":null,"evidenceTarget":null,"evidenceSpan":null,"answerRationale":null,"distractorErrorTypes":null,"renderCheck":{"ok":true,"renderer":"std-1","checkedAt":"2026-10-20T03:44:25.616Z","issues":[]},"publish":true,"quality":{"generatedBy":"claude-opus-5-5","levelTarget":"medium","targetLetter":"A","seed":"an excerpt of literary fiction (novel/short story scene) — Giorgi, an old shepherd in a Soviet Georgian village, receives a message from his son written before the war but delivered long after, its words becoming the mountain echo he needed to finally hear.","hardJudge":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:1"],"note":"빈칸 앞은 삽입 관계절을 포함한 완전한 독립절, 뒤는 전치사구가 앞에 놓인 독립절(Levan had promised)이므로 세미콜론(A)이 유일하게 적합함을 직접 확인. B는 comma splice, C는 run-on(또한 \"sheepfold in a careful hand\"로 오독 유도), D는 which가 기능할 자리가 없어 비문. 긴 삽입절과 도치된 전치사구 때문에 절 경계 파악에 두 단계 판단이 필요해 medium에 적합. 한·영 해설 모두 정답 및 선택지 글자와 일치하고 자연스러움. 선택지 C의 앞 공백 두 칸은 사소한 표기 문제로 판정에 영향 없음."},"advisory":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","fit":true,"correctOk":true,"complianceOk":true,"which":["fits","eliminated:2"],"note":"긴 삽입절과 도입 전치사구 때문에 절 경계를 찾으려면 두 단계 판단이 필요하다. B와 C는 그럴듯한 오답이다. D는 비교적 쉽게 배제된다.","passed":true},"mockExamGeneration":{"runId":"rw-supplement-medium","gid":"sq-boundaries-m-004","intendedSkill":"boundaries","recipeId":null,"recipeCheck":null,"hardBasis":null,"difficultyStatus":null,"review":null}}}]$satx$::jsonb;
  v_actor uuid := (select id from profiles where role = 'admin' order by created_at limit 1);
  r jsonb; v_pid uuid; v_vid uuid; v_n int := 0; v_skip int := 0;
begin
  if v_actor is null then raise exception 'No admin profile found.'; end if;
  for r in select * from jsonb_array_elements(v_items) loop
    if exists (select 1 from problem_versions where quality->'mockExamGeneration'->>'gid' = r->>'gid') then v_skip := v_skip + 1; continue; end if;
    v_pid := public.create_bank_problem(p_subject_id => (select id from subjects where name = r->>'subject' and archived_at is null), p_format => r->>'format', p_skill_type => r->>'skillType', p_topic => '',
      p_difficulty => r->>'difficulty', p_actor_id => v_actor, p_skill_code => r->>'skill', p_exam_system => r->>'examSystem', p_ap_subject => null, p_usage_scope => 'mock_exam');
    update problems set created_via = r->>'createdVia', subpattern = coalesce(r->>'subpattern', subpattern), similarity_group = coalesce(r->>'group', similarity_group) where id = v_pid;
    v_vid := public.save_problem_draft_version(p_problem_id => v_pid, p_passage => r->>'passage', p_options => nullif(r->'options', 'null'::jsonb), p_correct_index => (r->>'correctIndex')::int, p_explanation => r->>'explanation',
      p_difficulty => r->>'difficulty', p_actor_id => v_actor, p_answers => nullif(r->'answers', 'null'::jsonb), p_figure => nullif(r->'figure', 'null'::jsonb), p_figure_checked => false, p_statements => nullif(r->'statements', 'null'::jsonb),
      p_question => r->>'question', p_repair_status => null, p_explanation_en => r->>'explanationEn', p_evidence_target => r->>'evidenceTarget', p_evidence_span => r->>'evidenceSpan', p_answer_rationale => r->>'answerRationale',
      p_distractor_error_types => nullif(r->'distractorErrorTypes', 'null'::jsonb));
    perform public.set_problem_render_check(v_vid, r->'renderCheck');
    perform public.set_problem_quality(v_vid, r->'quality');
    if (r->>'publish')::boolean then perform public.confirm_and_publish_problem_version(v_vid, v_actor); end if;
    v_n := v_n + 1;
  end loop;
  raise notice 'SAT R&W import (27-30) 1/1: created=% skipped(existing)=%', v_n, v_skip;
end
$imp$;
